ps://api.github.com/users/endymion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/commits/2ddf18285035f9e01f4ad28098ef3854efd26062/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-01T03:16:36Z","email":"rap@endymion.com","name":"Ryan Alyn Porter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-01T03:16:36Z","email":"rap@endymion.com","name":"Ryan Alyn Porter"},"message":"feat(platform): Add centralized port registry and fix docs app rendering\n\nAdd @korporus/platform-config package as single source of truth for dev\nserver ports, eliminating 5+ hardcoded port references per app. All vite\nconfigs now import from the registry and use strictPort: true to fail\nfast on port conflicts instead of silently auto-incrementing.\n\nFix docs app rendering in the shell by injecting __DOCS_BASE_URL__ via\nVite''s define config, routing content fetches to the docs app''s own\norigin in dev mode. Add CORS headers to the docs plugin middleware,\ndirectory/index.md fallback resolution, URL hash-based deep linking\nacross documents, and correct code block styling for plain fenced blocks.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93ca03a48381446bb5e82da5cc4ce316ef394b8d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/git/trees/93ca03a48381446bb5e82da5cc4ce316ef394b8d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/git/commits/2ddf18285035f9e01f4ad28098ef3854efd26062","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/endymion","id":52344,"login":"endymion","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzQ0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/AnthusAI/Korporus/commit/2ddf18285035f9e01f4ad28098ef3854efd26062","node_id":"C_kwDORVGXi9oAKDJkZGYxODI4NTAzNWY5ZTAxZjRhZDI4MDk4ZWYzODU0ZWZkMjYwNjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/AnthusAI/Korporus/commit/8bde180b813d1c9778bbaf83deb36d306642c435","sha":"8bde180b813d1c9778bbaf83deb36d306642c435","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/commits/8bde180b813d1c9778bbaf83deb36d306642c435"}],"sha":"2ddf18285035f9e01f4ad28098ef3854efd26062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/commits/2ddf18285035f9e01f4ad28098ef3854efd26062"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/endymion","id":52344,"login":"endymion","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyMzQ0","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/commits/8bde180b813d1c9778bbaf83deb36d306642c435/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-28T21:18:34Z","email":"rap@endymion.com","name":"Ryan Alyn Porter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-28T21:18:34Z","email":"rap@endymion.com","name":"Ryan Alyn Porter"},"message":"feat(docs): Add documentation app with markdown rendering, search, and navigation\n\nNew federated Korporus app at packages/app-docs/ that renders markdown\ndocumentation from docs/ at the repo root.\n\nFeatures:\n- Vite plugin that scans docs/**/*.md at build time, generating a\n  docs-manifest.json with titles, headings, and search content\n- react-markdown + remark-gfm + rehype-slug for styled rendering\n  with GitHub-flavored markdown and header anchor IDs\n- Sidebar navigation tree built from the manifest\n- FlexSearch-powered full-text search in the settings slot\n- Breadcrumb navigation in the titlebar slot\n- Relative link resolution between docs (./sibling, ../other/doc)\n- Copy-to-clipboard anchor links on headings\n\nDocumentation content covering:\n- Getting started (installation, first app)\n- Architecture (module federation, web components, shell, manifests)\n- Guides (creating an app, state management, styling, deployment modes)\n- Reference (manifest schema, web-component-wrapper API, shell API)\n\nShell integration:\n- Manifest + icon registered in shell\n- Dev manifest rewrite for port 3002\n- Dockerfile and nginx.conf updated for /apps/docs/\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"834a54b0f372c50bebbceb7e55d944181fb18701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/git/trees/834a54b0f372c50bebbceb7e55d944181fb18701"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporu