om/users/endymion/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/commits/abe35477aa8ec4a48752df1470b2a6fc76b82ec5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-02-28T20:29:52Z","email":"rap@endymion.com","name":"Ryan Alyn Porter"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-02-28T20:29:52Z","email":"rap@endymion.com","name":"Ryan Alyn Porter"},"message":"feat: Working federated application platform POC\n\nImplements the full Korporus POC: a pnpm monorepo with a React/Vite shell\nthat loads independently-built apps at runtime via Module Federation 2.0\nand Web Components.\n\n- Monorepo: pnpm workspaces, shared tsconfig, ESLint, Prettier\n- Shell (apps/shell): React 19 + Vite 6 + Tailwind v4, manifest-based\n  app discovery, MF host runtime, three-slot layout (titlebar/main/settings)\n- Hello app (packages/app-hello): MF remote exposing 3 Web Components,\n  Zustand shared state across slots, dev manifest rewrite for cross-origin\n  MF loading in Vite dev mode\n- Shared packages: app-manifest (schema + validation), web-component-wrapper\n  (React → custom element bridge)\n- Demo apps: React and Angular hosts for third-party integration testing\n- Infrastructure: Dockerfile (multi-stage nginx), Terraform for ECR + App Runner\n- Kanbus task tracking updates\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"385b2e84230b8c17be896b38a1b14bcb12c38dcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/git/trees/385b2e84230b8c17be896b38a1b14bcb12c38dcd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/AnthusAI/Korporus/git/commits/abe35477aa8ec4a48752df1470b2a6fc76b82ec5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52344?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/endymion/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://a