/4d05846767973470f0ac0261edfe14560249b246"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72","sha":"a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72"}],"sha":"871e75bdae0fc5d2e73d4e9cfcb2aa0f920921fc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/871e75bdae0fc5d2e73d4e9cfcb2aa0f920921fc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:48:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T08:48:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs: brief guides and READMEs that point to yoltra.dev\n\nThe detailed documentation now lives on yoltra.dev, versioned by release. The repository keeps a\nbrief but complete version of every end-user document: what it is, how to install and use it,\nevery feature at least in a sentence, and a link to its full page (and each topic''s section) on\nthe site. English and Spanish stay parallel.\n\n- README (en, es): the pitch, three diagrams (where Yoltra sits, how a store works, the\n  packages), the packages, a complete quick start, DevTools, the demos, and a documentation table\n  pairing each brief document with its full page. The quick start says three steps everywhere.\n  The Spanish README links the Spanish package READMEs and contributor docs.\n- The guides (quick start, migration, testing, Next.js, decoration, request and reply), the 0.10\n  and 0.8 upgrade guides (now checklists), and the two design notes, each with its diagram. The\n  Spanish state-management comparison is rewritten from the English one, which it had drifted\n  from.\n- The package READMEs of core, react, ds and the devtools packages, each with its internals\n  diagram and, for core and ds, the size table unchanged.\n- Every diagram carries an accessible title and description.\n- tools/repo-tools/tests/docs-parity.test.ts holds every English and Spanish pair to the same\n  sections, diagrams and site pages, and every yoltra.dev link to the site''s URL scheme.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"e26fb6b320838dfa668f1ecfd855ac1bc8538387","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/e26fb6b320838dfa668f1ecfd855ac1bc8538387"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72","verification":{"payload":"tree e26fb6b320838dfa668f1ecfd855ac1bc8538387\nparent 2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791017290 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791017290 -0600\n\ndocs: brief guides and READMEs that point to yoltra.dev\n\nThe detailed documentation now lives on yoltra.dev, versioned by release. The repository keeps a\nbrief but complete version of every end-user document: what it is, how to install and use it,\nevery feature at least in a sentence, and a link to its full page (and each topic''s section) on\nthe site. English and Spanish stay parallel.\n\n- README (en, es): the pitch, three diagrams (where Yoltra sits, how a store works, the\n  packages), the packages, a complete quick start, DevTools, the demos, and a documentation table\n  pairing each brief document with its full page. The quick start says three steps everywhere.\n  The Spanish README links the Spanish package READMEs and contributor docs.\n- The guides (quick start, migration, testing, Next.js, decoration, request and reply), the 0.10\n  and 0.8 upgrade guides (now checklists), and the two design notes, each with its diagram. The\n  Spanish state-management comparison is rewritten from the English one, which it had drifted\n  from.\n- The package READMEs of core, react, ds and the devtools packages, each with its internals\n  diagram and, for core and ds, the size table unchanged.\n- Every diagram carries an accessible title and description.\n- tools/repo-tools/tests/docs-parity.test.ts holds every English and Spanish pair to the same\n  sections, diagrams and site pages, and every yoltra.dev link to the site''s URL scheme.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCasDBSgAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9e77AP9XkgiTQglCS1oPzUgf5kLIcrAdzBOCXOk9sb8AOFZfdwEAzjtpD3XWbZDZ\nc/xib/Zz6eqU85jsIbvvKzZktz4aDwI=\n=rVfU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:03:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGExOWYyNDViMTgyN2M4MjFjNDk5N2NjYzgwMmZjOWZkYjgyODljNzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63","sha":"2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63"}],"sha":"a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/a19f245b1827c821c4997ccc802fc9fdb8289c72"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T07:20:02Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T07:20:02Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"build(docs): generate the API reference as TypeDoc JSON, not committed Markdown\n\nThe API reference now lives on yoltra.dev, built from TypeDoc JSON generated at each release\ntag. The 440 Markdown pages under packages/*/docs and devtools/*/docs leave the repository, and\nthe tooling that only existed to keep them stamped and current goes with them.\n\n- Each package''s `docs` script runs TypeDoc once and writes JSON to its ignored .typedoc/\n  folder. @yoltra/ds produces that JSON for the first time.\n- typedoc-plugin-markdown is dropped, along with its overrides and the docs:md, docs:js and\n  docs:stamp scripts.\n- Source links use {gitRevision}, so a reference generated from a tag links to the source as it\n  was released rather than to whatever main holds later.\n- Cross-package symbol links point at their pages on yoltra.dev instead of committed files.\n- CI keeps `rush docs` as a check on the TSDoc: TypeDoc warns on a broken {@link} or a\n  malformed tag, and any warning fails the command. A clean tree afterwards proves nothing was\n  written outside .typedoc/.\n- docs-stamp.mjs and check-docs-current.mjs are removed with their tests, and the packages''\n  docs/ folders are ignored.\n- WORKFLOW (en, es) no longer asks contributors to commit generated files, and the protocol\n  README links the reference on yoltra.dev.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"90dd2a248a4ff7499eb3d4b61d2524666d7ee60c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/90dd2a248a4ff7499eb3d4b61d2524666d7ee60c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63","verification":{"payload":"tree 90dd2a248a4ff7499eb3d4b61d2524666d7ee60c\nparent 0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791012002 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791012002 -0600\n\nbuild(docs): generate the API reference as TypeDoc JSON, not committed Markdown\n\nThe API reference now lives on yoltra.dev, built from TypeDoc JSON generated at each release\ntag. The 440 Markdown pages under packages/*/docs and devtools/*/docs leave the repository, and\nthe tooling that only existed to keep them stamped and current goes with them.\n\n- Each package''s `docs` script runs TypeDoc once and writes JSON to its ignored .typedoc/\n  folder. @yoltra/ds produces that JSON for the first time.\n- typedoc-plugin-markdown is dropped, along with its overrides and the docs:md, docs:js and\n  docs:stamp scripts.\n- Source links use {gitRevision}, so a reference generated from a tag links to the source as it\n  was released rather than to whatever main holds later.\n- Cross-package symbol links point at their pages on yoltra.dev instead of committed files.\n- CI keeps `rush docs` as a check on the TSDoc: TypeDoc warns on a broken {@link} or a\n  malformed tag, and any warning fails the command. A clean tree afterwards proves nothing was\n  written outside .typedoc/.\n- docs-stamp.mjs and check-docs-current.mjs are removed with their tests, and the packages''\n  docs/ folders are ignored.\n- WORKFLOW (en, es) no longer asks contributors to commit generated files, and the protocol\n  README links the reference on yoltra.dev.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCasCsogAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9fK+AP9RNbUFJgxfnAtT0LVozT7LVgV+YH2YD9po6WdWVel2iQEA8jRjtUsZ3oYt\nWWFiNH39ccpZGAU8dSaD/EmLDOdGDAQ=\n=HRje\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T10:03:12Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDJjZDVkMzI5MzJlZDE1MzYzNWJkZWIzNzJmNTYzYWIzMDA3YTdhNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25","sha":"0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25"}],"sha":"2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2cd5d32932ed153635bdeb372f563ab3007a7a63"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:07:38Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:07:38Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"test(devtools-cli): wait for the Emit form to hold the keyboard\n\nThe Emit form test sent keys once the Emit tab''s label appeared, a render\nbefore the form takes the keyboard. On a loaded machine a [ then reached\nthe global binding and switched stores mid-payload, and the test timed\nout. It now waits for the form''s own hint and gives each frame''s effects\nlonger to run. Eight runs in a row pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"8c78674f97a8afa714d44a93f7d3b7fcd51cf04b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/8c78674f97a8afa714d44a93f7d3b7fcd51cf04b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25","verification":{"payload":"tree 8c78674f97a8afa714d44a93f7d3b7fcd51cf04b\nparent f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791000458 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791000458 -0600\n\ntest(devtools-cli): wait for the Emit form to hold the keyboard\n\nThe Emit form test sent keys once the Emit tab''s label appeared, a render\nbefore the form takes the keyboard. On a loaded machine a [ then reached\nthe global binding and switched stores mid-payload, and the test timed\nout. It now waits for the form''s own hint and gives each frame''s effects\nlonger to run. Eight runs in a row pass.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCasB/igAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9d5kAQDc6JVhV6zRIJGUtM4CUXRiYQ851GsLWns5Lh/3Tn1ZmwD/Xuh5h36qWQRn\nO7u48nS4BZp7skkBvitDcVm577oMhg8=\n=3dbA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T04:55:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDBkMmRiMTlmNjQzOTU2Mjk1ZDcxMWNlZjY3ZGNhYzRhMjhmMzJiMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f","sha":"f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f"}],"sha":"0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0d2db19f643956295d711cef67dcac4a28f32b25"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:03:41Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-03T04:03:41Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(devtools): tokens on every side, a fresh panel that updates, one connection per store\n\nBugs found while documenting the devtools, each reproduced first and each\nwith a test that fails without its fix:\n\n- Hub tokens worked for one agent only. The other store agent accepted\n  authToken and never sent it, and no panel could send one at all.\n  HubConnectionConfig gains authToken, sent in the handshake when set;\n  storeview passes it through; the extension stores it beside host and\n  port; both CLIs take --token or YOLTRA_DEVTOOLS_TOKEN, and the CLI''s\n  embedded hub hands the same token to its own panel. The hub''s log says\n  \"an extension handshake\".\n- A panel opened before a store''s first committed event froze on the\n  initial state: a version 0 snapshot counted as no snapshot, so every\n  later patch was buffered forever. useStoreState tracks whether it has a\n  snapshot separately from the version.\n- The CLI''s global keys fired while typing in the Emit form, so a q in a\n  payload quit. They are off while the form has focus; Esc leaves it.\n- Two stores with the same id: the hub silently replaced the first, so\n  their events merged and commands reached one. A second store with a\n  connected id is now refused, with one message shared by the hub and the\n  loopback broker; the agent retries, so it attaches once the first\n  leaves. The storeId docs give the real default, the store''s name.\n- Through the extension''s page bridge, every store on a page shared one\n  connection: only the first registered, and a command for one, time\n  travel included, was applied by all. Each page socket now has its own\n  connection, the relays carry the id unread, a closed socket is announced\n  so its id is free again, and older peers behave as before.\n\nCoverage floors for the CLI and storeview are raised to what the new panel\ntests measure; storeview''s branch floor is at its measured 76%.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"cc658a57c97015a690f03cd79b567d634a6ac8ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/cc658a57c97015a690f03cd79b567d634a6ac8ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f","verification":{"payload":"tree cc658a57c97015a690f03cd79b567d634a6ac8ac\nparent 6f22639abf7afadeeb41879ec36489c4cb60a8a5\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791000221 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1791000221 -0600\n\nfix(devtools): tokens on every side, a fresh panel that updates, one connection per store\n\nBugs found while documenting the devtools, each reproduced first and each\nwith a test that fails without its fix:\n\n- Hub tokens worked for one agent only. The other store agent accepted\n  authToken and never sent it, and no panel could send one at all.\n  HubConnectionConfig gains authToken, sent in the handshake when set;\n  storeview passes it through; the extension stores it beside host and\n  port; both CLIs take --token or YOLTRA_DEVTOOLS_TOKEN, and the CLI''s\n  embedded hub hands the same token to its own panel. The hub''s log says\n  \"an extension handshake\".\n- A panel opened before a store''s first committed event froze on the\n  initial state: a version 0 snapshot counted as no snapshot, so every\n  later patch was buffered forever. useStoreState tracks whether it has a\n  snapshot separately from the version.\n- The CLI''s global keys fired while typing in the Emit form, so a q in a\n  payload quit. They are off while the form has focus; Esc leaves it.\n- Two stores with the same id: the hub silently replaced the first, so\n  their events merged and commands reached one. A second store with a\n  connected id is now refused, with one message shared by the hub and the\n  loopback broker; the agent retries, so it attaches once the first\n  leaves. The storeId docs give the real default, the store''s name.\n- Through the extension''s page bridge, every store on a page shared one\n  connection: only the first registered, and a command for one, time\n  travel included, was applied by all. Each page socket now has its own\n  connection, the relays carry the id unread, a closed socket is announced\n  so its id is free again, and older peers behave as before.\n\nCoverage floors for the CLI and storeview are raised to what the new panel\ntests measure; storeview''s branch floor is at its measured 76%.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCasB+nQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9cEzAP97LICuEggNg1Yc7V2srk3puJaPkCtG7A0Z8A4skbvvgAD/R78sfxcrUcWH\njEMuEN/Zv1kDN3LOOVuK/IBUCxiOUw8=\n=cYxa\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T04:55:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGY2ZTZlOTAyNWY0NWM5ZWJmMGJkN2M2NDdlOGVhMzQ5NDhiMjQ3NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6f22639abf7afadeeb41879ec36489c4cb60a8a5","sha":"6f22639abf7afadeeb41879ec36489c4cb60a8a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6f22639abf7afadeeb41879ec36489c4cb60a8a5"}],"sha":"f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/f6e6e9025f45c9ebf0bd7c647e8ea34948b2474f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6f22639abf7afadeeb41879ec36489c4cb60a8a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:48:41Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T09:48:41Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs: add architecture diagrams, and focus the docs on browser and React\n\nMermaid diagrams in the style of the README''s \"How a store works\", each\nchecked against the source, in English and Spanish alike:\n\n- README: where Yoltra sits in an application, and how the packages\n  depend on each other.\n- core, react and ds READMEs: the store''s internals and the persistence\n  flow, how each hook reaches the store, how themes and tokens fit.\n- Guides: re-entrant draining and every emit() outcome, a whole\n  store.call(), the two Next.js patterns, and what replace* does with\n  each registration.\n- devtools READMEs: the protocol client and handshake, the hub''s gates,\n  the agent''s pipeline, the panel and time travel; the extension''s ASCII\n  figure becomes a diagram that includes its page bridge.\n\nThe documentation now covers browser and React applications, workers and\ntests. Two guides and one agent''s documentation leave the public docs; the\nagent itself is unchanged and still released. Source changes are comment\nwording only, and the API reference is regenerated from them.\n\nCorrections found while drawing: effects run for every committed event,\nincluding one a slice refused; the agent''s storeId defaults to the store''s\nname; the CLI binds no number keys and has a Time Travel tab; and inside a\nDevTools panel the extension always uses its page bridge.\n\nAdds the documentation-only change files the README changes need for the\ndevtools cli, protocol, server and ui packages and for ds.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"7e6619b53226e044a3255f7c34e8a971457d45c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/7e6619b53226e044a3255f7c34e8a971457d45c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/6f22639abf7afadeeb41879ec36489c4cb60a8a5","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e6619b53226e044a3255f7c34e8a971457d45c6\nparent 4381647b782b6c1ba1469e6dbf615f65acaf985e\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790934521 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790934521 -0600\n\ndocs: add architecture diagrams, and focus the docs on browser and React\n\nMermaid diagrams in the style of the README''s \"How a store works\", each\nchecked against the source, in English and Spanish alike:\n\n- README: where Yoltra sits in an application, and how the packages\n  depend on each other.\n- core, react and ds READMEs: the store''s internals and the persistence\n  flow, how each hook reaches the store, how themes and tokens fit.\n- Guides: re-entrant draining and every emit() outcome, a whole\n  store.call(), the two Next.js patterns, and what replace* does with\n  each registration.\n- devtools READMEs: the protocol client and handshake, the hub''s gates,\n  the agent''s pipeline, the panel and time travel; the extension''s ASCII\n  figure becomes a diagram that includes its page bridge.\n\nThe documentation now covers browser and React applications, workers and\ntests. Two guides and one agent''s documentation leave the public docs; the\nagent itself is unchanged and still released. Source changes are comment\nwording only, and the API reference is regenerated from them.\n\nCorrections found while drawing: effects run for every committed event,\nincluding one a slice refused; the agent''s storeId defaults to the store''s\nname; the CLI binds no number keys and has a Time Travel tab; and inside a\nDevTools panel the extension always uses its page bridge.\n\nAdds the documentation-only change files the README changes need for the\ndevtools cli, protocol, server and ui packages and for ds.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCasBwlQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9Y1hAQDqFZ9HQpkP6sJSWAByvTVDv6CUNWUJvbC/0QmOf6jGEAEAqW/+h3cXGLKp\nFHa2dCoAidDG9tjjYQG1pORDBAOsAAc=\n=CQSn\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-03T04:55:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6f22639abf7afadeeb41879ec36489c4cb60a8a5","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDZmMjI2MzlhYmY3YWZhZGVlYjQxODc5ZWMzNjQ4OWM0Y2I2MGE4YTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/