ttps://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1475a527281106394dd02f4d1197078046c94f40/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:56:40Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:56:40Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"chore(release): v0.9.0\n\nApply the pending change files with rush version --bump: the lock-step yoltra\nsuite (core, react, devtools-*) moves from 0.8.0 to 0.9.0, @yoltra/ds moves\nfrom 0.3.0 to 0.4.0 under its own policy, and the CHANGELOGs are written. The\npeer range on @yoltra/core moves to ^0.9.0 in react and both devtools agents.\n\nThis commit is published through a manual run of the Release workflow, not a\ntag. The examples resolve @yoltra/* from npm, so they cannot move to 0.9.0 and\nds 0.4.0 until both are published. The v0.9.0 tag goes on the follow-up commit\nthat bumps them.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"0511c0ee0c3d52553834964fd1faa9d80a1da191","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/0511c0ee0c3d52553834964fd1faa9d80a1da191"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/1475a527281106394dd02f4d1197078046c94f40","verification":{"payload":"tree 0511c0ee0c3d52553834964fd1faa9d80a1da191\nparent 1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790744200 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790744200 -0600\n\nchore(release): v0.9.0\n\nApply the pending change files with rush version --bump: the lock-step yoltra\nsuite (core, react, devtools-*) moves from 0.8.0 to 0.9.0, @yoltra/ds moves\nfrom 0.3.0 to 0.4.0 under its own policy, and the CHANGELOGs are written. The\npeer range on @yoltra/core moves to ^0.9.0 in react and both devtools agents.\n\nThis commit is published through a manual run of the Release workflow, not a\ntag. The examples resolve @yoltra/* from npm, so they cannot move to 0.9.0 and\nds 0.4.0 until both are published. The v0.9.0 tag goes on the follow-up commit\nthat bumps them.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaryWiAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9RZXAQD7k4eqvu6azHZ94txRW0iVyl5fs/QVMC5O2Nx6ENalygD/ZX/GUx39FpdE\niP3qljniF71wao1TOqPTJ0oQUqqUuQg=\n=33zl\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1475a527281106394dd02f4d1197078046c94f40","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDE0NzVhNTI3MjgxMTA2Mzk0ZGQwMmY0ZDExOTcwNzgwNDZjOTRmNDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8","sha":"1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8"}],"sha":"1475a527281106394dd02f4d1197078046c94f40","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1475a527281106394dd02f4d1197078046c94f40"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:50:53Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:50:53Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(ds): storageKey no longer points at a key the provider cannot take\n\n`NoFlashScriptOptions.storageKey` said it must match whatever `ThemeProvider`\nwas given. The provider takes no key: it always reads and writes\n`THEME_STORAGE_KEY`. Following the documentation, a reader passing a custom key\nto both would find the prop does not exist and keep it on the script alone,\nwhich then restores nothing and says nothing. It now says to leave it unset\nbeside the provider, and that it is for an application persisting the theme\nitself through `applyTheme`.\n\n`#0F172A` was \"ink\" in the brand line and \"carbon\" in the dark theme. Since\n0.4.0 `ink` names the always-dark surface code sits on, so the brand colour is\ncarbon everywhere, in both READMEs and the token module''s documentation.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"b2dd3662e68768890de9a384054bffc380f16f24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/b2dd3662e68768890de9a384054bffc380f16f24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8","verification":{"payload":"tree b2dd3662e68768890de9a384054bffc380f16f24\nparent 6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743853 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743853 -0600\n\ndocs(ds): storageKey no longer points at a key the provider cannot take\n\n`NoFlashScriptOptions.storageKey` said it must match whatever `ThemeProvider`\nwas given. The provider takes no key: it always reads and writes\n`THEME_STORAGE_KEY`. Following the documentation, a reader passing a custom key\nto both would find the prop does not exist and keep it on the script alone,\nwhich then restores nothing and says nothing. It now says to leave it unset\nbeside the provider, and that it is for an application persisting the theme\nitself through `applyTheme`.\n\n`#0F172A` was \"ink\" in the brand line and \"carbon\" in the dark theme. Since\n0.4.0 `ink` names the always-dark surface code sits on, so the brand colour is\ncarbon everywhere, in both READMEs and the token module''s documentation.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaryVLQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9XMUAQDH0nMqNd04sQ00USQMBYykL9DJQ9rlfePQ3dB5ZEIy8gEA1GKORLt3ifGo\n/jHU4+b54qTFbCi2GvPZPhDjcTmb2Ao=\n=hP4e\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDFkZjMxM2M2MDllZTA1NDk3NTg0NTNhMjQ2NDMzNTg5NDcyNDc2Yzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9","sha":"6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9"}],"sha":"1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1df313c609ee0549758453a246433589472476c8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:47:40Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:47:40Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(ds): the density change, and a ThemeProvider README that matches the code\n\n\"Upgrading from 0.3.x\" covered the token renames and not the change a codemod\ncannot make: the default density is one step tighter, a `md` button 36px\nrather than 44px. It says so now, and how to ask for the old size.\n\nThe ThemeProvider README said the no-flash script does not ship. It has shipped\nsince this release, as `noFlashScript()`, and the README now shows it along with\n`defaultTheme` and what happens when storage is blocked.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"8526f058f3bab0801f9e7b8e2dbd71f091ac2930","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/8526f058f3bab0801f9e7b8e2dbd71f091ac2930"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9","verification":{"payload":"tree 8526f058f3bab0801f9e7b8e2dbd71f091ac2930\nparent 01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743660 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743660 -0600\n\ndocs(ds): the density change, and a ThemeProvider README that matches the code\n\n\"Upgrading from 0.3.x\" covered the token renames and not the change a codemod\ncannot make: the default density is one step tighter, a `md` button 36px\nrather than 44px. It says so now, and how to ask for the old size.\n\nThe ThemeProvider README said the no-flash script does not ship. It has shipped\nsince this release, as `noFlashScript()`, and the README now shows it along with\n`defaultTheme` and what happens when storage is blocked.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaryUbQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9dgBAQDvWTIYFXqDsIJ1NiemB5ZeKN8CTln6bG9mwdarihSYGAEAvKUqYjhiqMgU\nD+S4UdU72NvA0VE95t7PW91ek2xJ/gk=\n=USTh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDYyOTVkYjVhODYxYzFkMjEyNTg4NmJkMmEwNTRjZDA3MGU3NDY4ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e","sha":"01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e"}],"sha":"6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6295db5a861c1d2125886bd2a054cd070e7468e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:47:40Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:47:40Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(react): say what the useAtomicProps guard does, frozen state included\n\nThe development guard throws on an undeclared read and names the path, and since\n0.9.0 it does so over frozen state too, which is what immer''s `produce` and\ncore''s `deepFreeze` hand it. Neither README mentioned the guard at all.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"3e1dfe31447bc42a1214545a2de921f0f934d8a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/3e1dfe31447bc42a1214545a2de921f0f934d8a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e","verification":{"payload":"tree 3e1dfe31447bc42a1214545a2de921f0f934d8a0\nparent abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743660 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743660 -0600\n\ndocs(react): say what the useAtomicProps guard does, frozen state included\n\nThe development guard throws on an undeclared read and names the path, and since\n0.9.0 it does so over frozen state too, which is what immer''s `produce` and\ncore''s `deepFreeze` hand it. Neither README mentioned the guard at all.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaryUbAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9Yz9AQDWSExzfZCniYzBS9Ck9Rx188UOJhOodXBDKz5UAT8EXgD/RWl3KjYlvNLq\nUqd0JPaxIRybj+s1WywtCWX7hcM3cQQ=\n=50Dg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDAxNzg3ZWUzZjllMjRiODAwNDJkMTEwYmMxYzU2Nzc2ZWZjOGNjM2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8","sha":"abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8"}],"sha":"01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/01787ee3f9e24b80042d110bc1c56776efc8cc3e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:47:39Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:47:39Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(core): the Spanish README says everything the English one does\n\nSix passages existed only in English, most of them from the 0.8.0 cycle: the\n`written` phase example and why `all` does not include it, the responder paced\nby its reader, two notes in the call table, the wildcard `immediate` delivery,\nand the `parentId`/`depth` example. \"Giving up\" had been translated as\n\"Retroceso\", which means a setback; it is now \"Rendirse\", as in the call guide.\n\nThe English README gains the three section rules the Spanish one already had, and\nboth agree on \"v1.0.0\". The decoration guide''s channel-targeting section sat one\nlevel too deep under React; it is its own section in both languages.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"6a290cfd0e9dff52b7237392e7bc279ed0e14cad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/6a290cfd0e9dff52b7237392e7bc279ed0e14cad"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8","verification":{"payload":"tree 6a290cfd0e9dff52b7237392e7bc279ed0e14cad\nparent b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743659 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743659 -0600\n\ndocs(core): the Spanish README says everything the English one does\n\nSix passages existed only in English, most of them from the 0.8.0 cycle: the\n`written` phase example and why `all` does not include it, the responder paced\nby its reader, two notes in the call table, the wildcard `immediate` delivery,\nand the `parentId`/`depth` example. \"Giving up\" had been translated as\n\"Retroceso\", which means a setback; it is now \"Rendirse\", as in the call guide.\n\nThe English README gains the three section rules the Spanish one already had, and\nboth agree on \"v1.0.0\". The decoration guide''s channel-targeting section sat one\nlevel too deep under React; it is its own section in both languages.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaryUbAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9S5TAP9xEn85HP061lqcH31oLV5bxZGxjWe8N2vVnyfWlPcj+AD7BgRIC489CqpK\nTG3QPuPH/AroT8QJVXcqpuBTN1PBRgk=\n=AX2n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGFiZDkxMmExM2ZiNTk5MTBjNDJkODcxMDM2MTFiMGIwYjY4MzU0ZDg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db","sha":"b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db"}],"sha":"abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/abd912a13fb59910c42d87103611b0b0b68354d8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:40:33Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:40:33Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(ds): the README names everything 0.4.0 ships\n\n`MenuItem`, `MenuSeparator`, `focusableWithin` and `resolvePlacement` are\nexported and appeared nowhere in the inventory. Authoring described the three\nmixins that predate the SASS restructure and a template literal that no longer\nexists; it now describes the shared entry, all ten mixins, and the stylelint\nrule that turns a hardcoded colour or type value into an error. The tokens\nsection introduces the interactive track role, and the Spanish README gains the\n`ThemeProvider` note it was missing.\n\nThe tabs change file said a typical import lands at 0.7 KB under a 1 KB\nbudget. The measured figure is 0.9 KB and the budget is 1.2 KB, so the\nCHANGELOG entry now agrees with the size table beside it.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"b4eb30f40cd38061a4298eb5f11b900f6171ba0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/b4eb30f40cd38061a4298eb5f11b900f6171ba0c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db","verification":{"payload":"tree b4eb30f40cd38061a4298eb5f11b900f6171ba0c\nparent 9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743233 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743233 -0600\n\ndocs(ds): the README names everything 0.4.0 ships\n\n`MenuItem`, `MenuSeparator`, `focusableWithin` and `resolvePlacement` are\nexported and appeared nowhere in the inventory. Authoring described the three\nmixins that predate the SASS restructure and a template literal that no longer\nexists; it now describes the shared entry, all ten mixins, and the stylelint\nrule that turns a hardcoded colour or type value into an error. The tokens\nsection introduces the interactive track role, and the Spanish README gains the\n`ThemeProvider` note it was missing.\n\nThe tabs change file said a typical import lands at 0.7 KB under a 1 KB\nbudget. The measured figure is 0.9 KB and the budget is 1.2 KB, so the\nCHANGELOG entry now agrees with the size table beside it.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarySwQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9RO+AP9dQI/yKQOT2LUChe5rvWi50VUNnpBpzrMVWcY50d00uwEA036cXt7FPBab\nwYXJ5gYGxEn9sEC8AkDkdb6Qb4kcVQk=\n=4OhD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGI0OWNlMTAyNjIyMWExNzM3MjVlN2Q1M2RmYzgzNWI5ODJlMzM2ZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e","sha":"9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e"}],"sha":"b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/b49ce1026221a173725e7d53dfc835b982e336db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:40:32Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:40:32Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(react): the Spanish README keeps the English order\n\n\"Colecciones normalizadas\" sat after \"Estado\", just before the licence. It now\nsits where \"Normalised collections\" does, ahead of React 18+ compatibility.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"936075c8086a1418d85c07737025c9cc676b9492","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/936075c8086a1418d85c07737025c9cc676b9492"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e","verification":{"payload":"tree 936075c8086a1418d85c07737025c9cc676b9492\nparent 88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743232 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743232 -0600\n\ndocs(react): the Spanish README keeps the English order\n\n\"Colecciones normalizadas\" sat after \"Estado\", just before the licence. It now\nsits where \"Normalised collections\" does, ahead of React 18+ compatibility.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarySwAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9epKAP9ZmCYKYVofEjF41ERJOXR88TArfiRyfprexmoq8LupTwEAsAkHQW6TPCIj\nEXDP11zcJOzOjB4J+MuGdtIFU+6+HAk=\n=cvuq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDlhYjVlNzQ0NzU3YWUyY2E2ZGExY2E1YmJkZDMzOTFiZjAzYTk0NGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e","sha":"88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e"}],"sha":"9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/9ab5e744757ae2ca6da1ca5bbdd3391bf03a944e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:40:31Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:40:31Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(core): the README describes the 0.9.0 surface\n\nFour of the five minor changes in 0.9.0 had no line in either README:\n`channelPattern` in `When`, `reason` and `vetoedBy` on instrumented events,\nthe normalized `when` on each registration change, and castless\n`registerReducer`. The README ships in the tarball, so this has to land before\nthe bump or npm shows the 0.8.0 text for the whole release.\n\nThe size prose quoted deltas from when the table read 9.2 / 10.7 / 12.1. The\ncheck only regenerates the lines between the markers, so it never noticed:\npersistence adds 1.3 KB and the barrel 2.7 KB, not 1.5 and 2.9.\n\nThe Spanish README catches up on two paragraphs it never received, and the\nSpanish decoration guide loses a typo and a cross-reference to a heading that\nhad been renamed.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"02523afc832bf80bc2a7d70549d737d2c187d485","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/02523afc832bf80bc2a7d70549d737d2c187d485"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e","verification":{"payload":"tree 02523afc832bf80bc2a7d70549d737d2c187d485\nparent ce7f96f7d52821ae86c513cc5cd5c98f9985300f\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743231 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790743231 -0600\n\ndocs(core): the README describes the 0.9.0 surface\n\nFour of the five minor changes in 0.9.0 had no line in either README:\n`channelPattern` in `When`, `reason` and `vetoedBy` on instrumented events,\nthe normalized `when` on each registration change, and castless\n`registerReducer`. The README ships in the tarball, so this has to land before\nthe bump or npm shows the 0.8.0 text for the whole release.\n\nThe size prose quoted deltas from when the table read 9.2 / 10.7 / 12.1. The\ncheck only regenerates the lines between the markers, so it never noticed:\npersistence adds 1.3 KB and the barrel 2.7 KB, not 1.5 and 2.9.\n\nThe Spanish README catches up on two paragraphs it never received, and the\nSpanish decoration guide loses a typo and a cross-reference to a heading that\nhad been renamed.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarySvwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9a+LAP9PmuYg4Hrd5nTj2KtrRLQzBj5B7V5JSwDgDy+1UryZaAEAvxkCdogc5cK3\nWBpeA97mjHltkUWQ6KvD1YihP+s5UgI=\n=h/Pf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDg4ZGE0NzhlMjY5ZWNlNDU0N2RiOTQxOGZhMTkyMDEzZTUyY2JiNmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/ce7f96f7d52821ae86c513cc5cd5c98f9985300f","sha":"ce7f96f7d52821ae86c513cc5cd5c98f9985300f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ce7f96f7d52821ae86c513cc5cd5c98f9985300f"}],"sha":"88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/88da478e269ece4547db9418fa192013e52cbb6e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ce7f96f7d52821ae86c513cc5cd5c98f9985300f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T06:08:55Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-30T04:05:59Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"ci: fail the build when a lock-step suite comes apart\n\nA `lockStepVersion` policy is a promise that a set of packages moves as one.\nNine of them share a version because they are released, installed and supported\ntogether, and a consumer pinning one has to be able to reason about the rest.\n\nNothing enforced it. The policy is a declaration in `version-policies.json`, and\nwhat actually ships is whatever sits in each `package.json` — two facts free to\ndisagree in a commit nobody reads closely because it is called\n`chore(release)`.\n\nThey come apart through a command that looks right. `rush version --bump`\napplies the policy and moves the whole set; `rush publish --apply` bumps each\npackage from its own change files and does not consult the policy. On the 0.9.0\ntree that difference is live: core carries `minor` entries and `@yoltra/react`,\n`devtools-cli` and `devtools-server` carry only `patch` ones, so a `rush publish`\npreview puts core at 0.9.0 and those three at 0.8.1. It exits zero.\n\n`RELEASING.md` already specified the right command, which is the point: the\ndocumentation was correct and would not have stopped anyone. So this checks the\n**state** rather than the command, and catches a hand-edited manifest, a bad\nmerge or a half-applied bump on the same footing.\n\nThe policy''s own `version` field is part of the comparison. A set that agrees\nwith itself but not with the policy means the bump was applied by something that\ndid not know the policy existed, and comparing members only to each other would\ncall that healthy.\n\nWired into CI, and again into the release workflow immediately before publish.\nThe second placement is the one that matters: that job publishes whatever\nversions the tagged commit carries, npm does not take a package back, and a\n`git push --follow-tags` starts both workflows without the release job waiting\nfor CI.\n\nVerified by simulating the exact split — react moved to 0.8.1 — and confirming\nthe check names it and exits non-zero. Five tests cover the split, the\nagrees-with-itself-but-not-the-policy case, packages outside any lock-step\npolicy, and a member whose manifest is missing. The config reader is\nstring-aware, because both files it reads are JSONC and one of them contains\nURLs with `//` in them.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"0233e29b04648b40f3fca401036352e024fcb931","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/0233e29b04648b40f3fca401036352e024fcb931"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/ce7f96f7d52821ae86c513cc5cd5c98f9985300f","verification":{"payload":"tree 0233e29b04648b40f3fca401036352e024fcb931\nparent ee9494648f22020aefa0194c33202b2fdc018d1d\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790662135 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790741159 -0600\n\nci: fail the build when a lock-step suite comes apart\n\nA `lockStepVersion` policy is a promise that a set of packages moves as one.\nNine of them share a version because they are released, installed and supported\ntogether, and a consumer pinning one has to be able to reason about the rest.\n\nNothing enforced it. The policy is a declaration in `version-policies.json`, and\nwhat actually ships is whatever sits in each `package.json` — two facts free to\ndisagree in a commit nobody reads closely because it is called\n`chore(release)`.\n\nThey come apart through a command that looks right. `rush version --bump`\napplies the policy and moves the whole set; `rush publish --apply` bumps each\npackage from its own change files and does not consult the policy. On the 0.9.0\ntree that difference is live: core carries `minor` entries and `@yoltra/react`,\n`devtools-cli` and `devtools-server` carry only `patch` ones, so a `rush publish`\npreview puts core at 0.9.0 and those three at 0.8.1. It exits zero.\n\n`RELEASING.md` already specified the right command, which is the point: the\ndocumentation was correct and would not have stopped anyone. So this checks the\n**state** rather than the command, and catches a hand-edited manifest, a bad\nmerge or a half-applied bump on the same footing.\n\nThe policy''s own `version` field is part of the comparison. A set that agrees\nwith itself but not with the policy means the bump was applied by something that\ndid not know the policy existed, and comparing members only to each other would\ncall that healthy.\n\nWired into CI, and again into the release workflow immediately before publish.\nThe second placement is the one that matters: that job publishes whatever\nversions the tagged commit carries, npm does not take a package back, and a\n`git push --follow-tags` starts both workflows without the release job waiting\nfor CI.\n\nVerified by simulating the exact split — react moved to 0.8.1 — and confirming\nthe check names it and exits non-zero. Five tests cover the split, the\nagrees-with-itself-but-not-the-policy case, packages outside any lock-step\npolicy, and a member whose manifest is missing. The config reader is\nstring-aware, because both files it reads are JSONC and one of them contains\nURLs with `//` in them.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaryKpwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9TISAP9HxsjFTjWQao33vxC/g4rrAErBASqaKqVQuG+L2EvFAAD+L3rcNCFRaFSO\nGqHhP8i/ABTxtOslrOxTzGcfhLv40QY=\n=6kpL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-30T04:58:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"pu