s/a758ddb2b2046dfb0304e1cf8631d7774205615d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/ed0a4162e47031dae5201e39956469632af0a3d7","verification":{"payload":"tree a758ddb2b2046dfb0304e1cf8631d7774205615d\nparent 351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790519776 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790519776 -0600\n\nchore(core): refresh the measured size table\n\n0.2 KB on each of the three entries: the channel-pattern matcher, the\ndevelopment-only key-collision check, and two fields on the instrumentation\npayload. A typical import is 11.7 KB against a 14 KB budget.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkp4AAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9WyZAQDmpo8aagnB2KoHa0set5TpuWya3WGIR0XaSD6GuiOVNwD/fqkCuhtRA0pF\nExgB7y6p1+bwb/7ACKtu5BTL3VA5VQo=\n=ZtXd\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:02:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/ed0a4162e47031dae5201e39956469632af0a3d7","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGVkMGE0MTYyZTQ3MDMxZGFlNTIwMWUzOTk1NjQ2OTYzMmFmMGEzZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83","sha":"351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83"}],"sha":"ed0a4162e47031dae5201e39956469632af0a3d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ed0a4162e47031dae5201e39956469632af0a3d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:32:52Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:32:52Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(core): the call declarations are the call surface, and nothing else\n\nA consuming runtime''s review listed `isReplyTo(event, requestId, correlationId)`\namong the things 0.8.0 shipped, marked \"exported\". It is not exported: it carries\n`@internal` and is absent from the barrel. They read it in\n`dist/types/store/call.d.ts`, where it was, because being `@internal` does not\nkeep a declaration out of the emitted types — only out of the reference, via\nTypeDoc''s `excludeInternal`. The two disagreed, and the consumer believed the one\nthat ships.\n\nBoth helpers now live beside their only caller in `performCall.ts`, unexported,\nso they cannot reach the declarations at all. `call.d.ts` carries exactly\n`ReplySpec`, `CallOptions`, `CallHandle`, `CallTimeoutError` and\n`CallAbortedError`, with no `@internal` left in it. Nothing at runtime changes.\n\n**On stripping `@internal` from the published types generally: it cannot be done\nas things stand, and I measured rather than assumed it.** Enabling TypeScript''s\n`stripInternal` for core fails the build immediately, because both devtools\nagents call `__devtoolsIntrospect`, `__replayEvents` and `__applyExternalState`,\nall three of which are tagged `@internal` on `StoreInstance`. They resolve core''s\ntypes through the published declarations — the workspace link goes through\n`exports.types` — so hiding those members breaks our own packages, and would\nbreak any third-party devtools integration too. `devtools-protocol` even\nadvertises `__replayEvents` support as a capability.\n\nThe underlying problem is that `@internal` currently means two different things\nhere: genuinely private helpers, and a devtools contract plus type-level\nmachinery that public signatures reference — `EMFromReducersStrict` alone appears\nthirteen times in the emitted declarations. Separating those is a real change to\nthe public reference and wants a decision of its own, so this commit does the\npart that is unambiguous and leaves the rest recorded.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"37a11e77dfe758363418efe6130175c24676fbf9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/37a11e77dfe758363418efe6130175c24676fbf9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83","verification":{"payload":"tree 37a11e77dfe758363418efe6130175c24676fbf9\nparent b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790519572 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790519572 -0600\n\nfix(core): the call declarations are the call surface, and nothing else\n\nA consuming runtime''s review listed `isReplyTo(event, requestId, correlationId)`\namong the things 0.8.0 shipped, marked \"exported\". It is not exported: it carries\n`@internal` and is absent from the barrel. They read it in\n`dist/types/store/call.d.ts`, where it was, because being `@internal` does not\nkeep a declaration out of the emitted types — only out of the reference, via\nTypeDoc''s `excludeInternal`. The two disagreed, and the consumer believed the one\nthat ships.\n\nBoth helpers now live beside their only caller in `performCall.ts`, unexported,\nso they cannot reach the declarations at all. `call.d.ts` carries exactly\n`ReplySpec`, `CallOptions`, `CallHandle`, `CallTimeoutError` and\n`CallAbortedError`, with no `@internal` left in it. Nothing at runtime changes.\n\n**On stripping `@internal` from the published types generally: it cannot be done\nas things stand, and I measured rather than assumed it.** Enabling TypeScript''s\n`stripInternal` for core fails the build immediately, because both devtools\nagents call `__devtoolsIntrospect`, `__replayEvents` and `__applyExternalState`,\nall three of which are tagged `@internal` on `StoreInstance`. They resolve core''s\ntypes through the published declarations — the workspace link goes through\n`exports.types` — so hiding those members breaks our own packages, and would\nbreak any third-party devtools integration too. `devtools-protocol` even\nadvertises `__replayEvents` support as a capability.\n\nThe underlying problem is that `@internal` currently means two different things\nhere: genuinely private helpers, and a devtools contract plus type-level\nmachinery that public signatures reference — `EMFromReducersStrict` alone appears\nthirteen times in the emitted declarations. Separating those is a real change to\nthe public reference and wants a decision of its own, so this commit does the\npart that is unambiguous and leaves the rest recorded.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkpFAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9TohAQCFrd8nXG3b+XJtvB01Rl8erOyLx/WJEfEzrMnobS8RLwEA8UsJhSpIi4Sl\n6jtkCj7e6E2BC/BILcvX3uyEPGMtvw8=\n=Fgf3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:02:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDM1MWY1ZWU4MmI1MGZjMzg1NTZiNDdmN2I3Y2QwZDBkNjVhMDljODM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd","sha":"b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd"}],"sha":"351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/351f5ee82b50fc38556b47f7b7cd0d0d65a09c83"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:20:32Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:20:32Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(core): name the key collision, and stop mangling namespaced channels\n\nThe store joins a channel and a type into one key and dispatches, deduplicates\nand introspects on it. Nothing checked the join was unambiguous.\n\n`(\"a::b\", \"c\")` and `(\"a\", \"b::c\")` both become `\"a::b::c\"`. Demonstrated against\nthe published package before writing any of this: two subscribers, one registered\nfor each pair, and both received both events. With a dedup window, one pair\nsilently drops the other.\n\nA consuming runtime''s own source asserted the store \"structurally forbids `::` in\na local channel name\". It does not. They are correcting their sentence; this is\nthe half that is ours.\n\n**The first design of this warned on `::` and was wrong.** M4''s own test tripped\nit, which was the useful accident: `alias::channel` is how a federated peer''s\nchannel is namespaced, so a store bridging peers is full of legitimate `::` and a\nwarning on the separator would have fired constantly for correct code. A warning\nnobody can act on is a warning everybody mutes.\n\nSo the rule is the precise one. A `::` in a channel is fine on its own; what is\nnot fine is two pairs collapsing together, and that is what is reported, naming\nboth pairs, because either one alone looks blameless. It warns once per colliding\nkey rather than once per event, and costs one `includes` before it touches a map.\n\nIt warns rather than throws. The separator has been accepted since the first\nrelease and the store cannot know who relies on it, so refusing it on a minor\nupgrade would break working applications. A hard rule stays available at 1.0.\n\n**Second half, which nobody filed.** The four paths that split the key back apart\ntook the *first* separator, so an effect on `(\"bb::plan\", \"go\")` was reported as\nchannel `bb`, type `plan`, with the rest discarded — a registration against a\nchannel that does not exist, while the real one went missing. One of them\nmanufactured a `When` from the mis-split behind `key.split(\"::\") as [string,\nstring]`, a cast asserting a two-element tuple for a three-element array, and\nthat value then flowed to every registration observer.\n\nAll four now go through one helper that splits on the last separator, which is\ncorrect because no path the store controls puts `::` in a type. Federation''s\nnamespaced channels therefore introspect honestly rather than as a channel nobody\nregistered.\n\nAlso removes a `node:process` import I had added to the new module: core is a\nbrowser library, and every other file there reads the bundler-replaced global.\nThe build caught it as an externalization warning.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"f87635a88fbd581d754fbbb7f05ee5b932ec72a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/f87635a88fbd581d754fbbb7f05ee5b932ec72a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd","verification":{"payload":"tree f87635a88fbd581d754fbbb7f05ee5b932ec72a8\nparent ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790518832 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790518832 -0600\n\nfix(core): name the key collision, and stop mangling namespaced channels\n\nThe store joins a channel and a type into one key and dispatches, deduplicates\nand introspects on it. Nothing checked the join was unambiguous.\n\n`(\"a::b\", \"c\")` and `(\"a\", \"b::c\")` both become `\"a::b::c\"`. Demonstrated against\nthe published package before writing any of this: two subscribers, one registered\nfor each pair, and both received both events. With a dedup window, one pair\nsilently drops the other.\n\nA consuming runtime''s own source asserted the store \"structurally forbids `::` in\na local channel name\". It does not. They are correcting their sentence; this is\nthe half that is ours.\n\n**The first design of this warned on `::` and was wrong.** M4''s own test tripped\nit, which was the useful accident: `alias::channel` is how a federated peer''s\nchannel is namespaced, so a store bridging peers is full of legitimate `::` and a\nwarning on the separator would have fired constantly for correct code. A warning\nnobody can act on is a warning everybody mutes.\n\nSo the rule is the precise one. A `::` in a channel is fine on its own; what is\nnot fine is two pairs collapsing together, and that is what is reported, naming\nboth pairs, because either one alone looks blameless. It warns once per colliding\nkey rather than once per event, and costs one `includes` before it touches a map.\n\nIt warns rather than throws. The separator has been accepted since the first\nrelease and the store cannot know who relies on it, so refusing it on a minor\nupgrade would break working applications. A hard rule stays available at 1.0.\n\n**Second half, which nobody filed.** The four paths that split the key back apart\ntook the *first* separator, so an effect on `(\"bb::plan\", \"go\")` was reported as\nchannel `bb`, type `plan`, with the rest discarded — a registration against a\nchannel that does not exist, while the real one went missing. One of them\nmanufactured a `When` from the mis-split behind `key.split(\"::\") as [string,\nstring]`, a cast asserting a two-element tuple for a three-element array, and\nthat value then flowed to every registration observer.\n\nAll four now go through one helper that splits on the last separator, which is\ncorrect because no path the store controls puts `::` in a type. Federation''s\nnamespaced channels therefore introspect honestly rather than as a channel nobody\nregistered.\n\nAlso removes a `node:process` import I had added to the new module: core is a\nbrowser library, and every other file there reads the bundler-replaced global.\nThe build caught it as an externalization warning.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkmMAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9QZWAQD2zG9Ri4av18zWLjBlOXXiIwET6sslTh2zLDX6EfyvjQEA5h5vwK83w4AV\n9banoz9EBR6fruP1q3Ziq3g0nji25g8=\n=4bvy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:02:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGIwN2RiOTM2ZmY3NjllMTFlOTM0NzNjNjUzZTNkZGY0YTU4YzE5ZmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e","sha":"ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e"}],"sha":"b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/b07db936ff769e11e93473c653e3ddf4a58c19fd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:09:15Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:09:15Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core): target a channel you cannot name, and report the matcher you have\n\nTwo halves of the same complaint: what a matcher can express, and what a matcher\ntells an observer.\n\n**Expressing it.** `when` compares exactly, so `{ channel: \"plan\" }` matches\n`plan` and nothing else. A guard whose channels arrive namespaced — a federated\npeer''s `bb::plan` beside a local `plan` — cannot use `when` at all, because the\naliases are invented by whoever federates and no list can be written in advance.\nIt has to match every event and filter in its own body, which costs the pre-call\nskip and, more quietly, tells every observer it matches the entire store.\n\n`{ channelPattern }` covers it, with `*` standing for zero or more characters so\none rule reaches a channel and its namespaced forms together. Zero rather than\none deliberately: `\"*plan\"` has to match bare `plan` as well as `bb::plan`, which\nis the whole case. The cost is the usual glob one, that it also matches `replan`,\nand a store with both wants `\"*::plan\"` plus a rule for the local channel.\n\n`*` is the only metacharacter and everything else is escaped, so a pattern cannot\nbecome an expression that backtracks, and compiled patterns are cached because a\nmatcher runs once per middleware per event. It stays a string rather than a\npredicate: a matcher is reported to observers and travels to a devtools panel,\nand a function would make every one of them opaque — which is precisely the\nproblem the other half of this commit fixes.\n\nThe guide records the trap beside the feature, which is the more useful half of\nwhat was reported. A guard already filtering in its body on a stripped base\nchannel looks like it would be faster with `when`, and converting it silently\nstops it seeing every namespaced channel. Nothing throws; it keeps running,\nkeeps returning true, and no longer guards what it was written for.\n\n**Reporting it.** `RegistrationChange.when` is documented as \"the normalized\nmatcher, as `matchesWhen` will actually use it\", and for a keyed slice it was\nabsent. Both producers read `patternReducers`, which holds only pattern-based\nslices — a keyed slice dispatches through the reducer bus and is deliberately\nkept out of that map, because that map is what the emit loop re-tests per event.\nSo the most common slice form reported how it dispatches and nothing about what\nit matches, in `onRegistrationChange` and `__devtoolsIntrospect` alike. Two\nconsumers wanted this to publish a store''s live topology.\n\nFixed with a second map that records the reported matcher for every slice,\nseparate from the runtime one so dispatch behaviour is untouched. Function-form\nmiddleware had the mirror defect, reporting `undefined` where the effects path\nreports `{ any: true }` for the same meaning; they now agree.\n\nOne existing test asserted `when: undefined` for a keyed reducer, pinning the\ndefect. Updated, with a note saying which way round it now is.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"ab6e4d05e6389466a7a2fd8bca67df58c0f6f0a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/ab6e4d05e6389466a7a2fd8bca67df58c0f6f0a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e","verification":{"payload":"tree ab6e4d05e6389466a7a2fd8bca67df58c0f6f0a1\nparent 77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790518155 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790518155 -0600\n\nfeat(core): target a channel you cannot name, and report the matcher you have\n\nTwo halves of the same complaint: what a matcher can express, and what a matcher\ntells an observer.\n\n**Expressing it.** `when` compares exactly, so `{ channel: \"plan\" }` matches\n`plan` and nothing else. A guard whose channels arrive namespaced — a federated\npeer''s `bb::plan` beside a local `plan` — cannot use `when` at all, because the\naliases are invented by whoever federates and no list can be written in advance.\nIt has to match every event and filter in its own body, which costs the pre-call\nskip and, more quietly, tells every observer it matches the entire store.\n\n`{ channelPattern }` covers it, with `*` standing for zero or more characters so\none rule reaches a channel and its namespaced forms together. Zero rather than\none deliberately: `\"*plan\"` has to match bare `plan` as well as `bb::plan`, which\nis the whole case. The cost is the usual glob one, that it also matches `replan`,\nand a store with both wants `\"*::plan\"` plus a rule for the local channel.\n\n`*` is the only metacharacter and everything else is escaped, so a pattern cannot\nbecome an expression that backtracks, and compiled patterns are cached because a\nmatcher runs once per middleware per event. It stays a string rather than a\npredicate: a matcher is reported to observers and travels to a devtools panel,\nand a function would make every one of them opaque — which is precisely the\nproblem the other half of this commit fixes.\n\nThe guide records the trap beside the feature, which is the more useful half of\nwhat was reported. A guard already filtering in its body on a stripped base\nchannel looks like it would be faster with `when`, and converting it silently\nstops it seeing every namespaced channel. Nothing throws; it keeps running,\nkeeps returning true, and no longer guards what it was written for.\n\n**Reporting it.** `RegistrationChange.when` is documented as \"the normalized\nmatcher, as `matchesWhen` will actually use it\", and for a keyed slice it was\nabsent. Both producers read `patternReducers`, which holds only pattern-based\nslices — a keyed slice dispatches through the reducer bus and is deliberately\nkept out of that map, because that map is what the emit loop re-tests per event.\nSo the most common slice form reported how it dispatches and nothing about what\nit matches, in `onRegistrationChange` and `__devtoolsIntrospect` alike. Two\nconsumers wanted this to publish a store''s live topology.\n\nFixed with a second map that records the reported matcher for every slice,\nseparate from the runtime one so dispatch behaviour is untouched. Function-form\nmiddleware had the mirror defect, reporting `undefined` where the effects path\nreports `{ any: true }` for the same meaning; they now agree.\n\nOne existing test asserted `when: undefined` for a keyed reducer, pinning the\ndefect. Updated, with a note saying which way round it now is.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkjiwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9Vh8AP92q+LbZcm1qhbslKcjdJXaOqFjufHFlmRyTMjeBM0b4gEAksUJbUqVm6Rx\ng4wI2YZhiNoq1hGYY0p5CxZZBryHjg8=\n=85t5\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:02:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGViYWIxODU4MzkwNTA3ZjAzODc3OTZhZTM2N2I5N2NmNDk5MjExOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1","sha":"77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1"}],"sha":"ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ebab1858390507f0387796ae367b97cf4992118e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:01:01Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T14:01:01Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core): a decoration can register a reducer without a cast\n\n`registerReducer` was the one member of the decoration family a decorator could\nnot satisfy. A consuming project reported keeping exactly one named cast for it,\nand the report was right about the mechanism.\n\nThe parameter was `ReducerSpec<any, EM>` — the store''s own event map — so a spec\nnaming a channel the application does not have could not typecheck. Neither\ndirection of assignability holds, which is why no variance annotation rescues it:\nthe forward direction fails on `reducer`, a property holding a function type\nrather than a method declaration, so `strictFunctionTypes` checks its parameters\ncontravariantly; the reverse fails on `when`, whose `EventKey<EM>` is not\nassignable to a concrete key tuple. Different members, opposite directions.\n\n`registerSlice` never had the problem because its constraint is\n`ReducerSpec<any, any>`, under which a concrete key tuple is fine, and the\ncontributed event map is recovered from the spec''s brand in value position rather\nthan from the type. `registerReducer` now has the same shape, and the\nimplementation already delegated to `registerSlice`, so this is the signature\ncatching up with the behaviour.\n\nThe same report''s claim about `registerMiddleware` is out of date: the generic\noverload added in 0.8.0 made it castless already. Only this one was left.\n\nSecond half, which nobody filed: the `Store` class''s public signatures narrowed\nevery decoration member back to the store''s own `EM`, shadowing the permissive\nones on `StoreDecoration`. `createStore` returns `StoreInstance`, so decorators\nwritten against that were fine, but `Store` is exported too and anyone typed\nagainst the class lost castless decoration entirely. Widened to match.\n\nThe type tests assert the cast is gone, and were checked against the old\nsignature first to confirm they fail with exactly the reported error rather than\npassing vacuously.\n\nAlso documents the pattern behind the request. A decorator that owns a\nlifecycle, a connection or a credential cannot put it in reduced state, because\nstate is snapshotted, frozen and shipped to a devtools panel. Three independent\nlibraries needed to hand something else back and all three returned\n`{ store, handle }`. The guide stated the contract as absolute; it now describes\nthe pattern, states plainly that it costs nesting and dependency-by-constraint,\nand says when not to reach for it.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"2d8df180f81aef72becb9c0b196a14cff0d33a80","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/2d8df180f81aef72becb9c0b196a14cff0d33a80"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1","verification":{"payload":"tree 2d8df180f81aef72becb9c0b196a14cff0d33a80\nparent 2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790517661 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790517661 -0600\n\nfeat(core): a decoration can register a reducer without a cast\n\n`registerReducer` was the one member of the decoration family a decorator could\nnot satisfy. A consuming project reported keeping exactly one named cast for it,\nand the report was right about the mechanism.\n\nThe parameter was `ReducerSpec<any, EM>` — the store''s own event map — so a spec\nnaming a channel the application does not have could not typecheck. Neither\ndirection of assignability holds, which is why no variance annotation rescues it:\nthe forward direction fails on `reducer`, a property holding a function type\nrather than a method declaration, so `strictFunctionTypes` checks its parameters\ncontravariantly; the reverse fails on `when`, whose `EventKey<EM>` is not\nassignable to a concrete key tuple. Different members, opposite directions.\n\n`registerSlice` never had the problem because its constraint is\n`ReducerSpec<any, any>`, under which a concrete key tuple is fine, and the\ncontributed event map is recovered from the spec''s brand in value position rather\nthan from the type. `registerReducer` now has the same shape, and the\nimplementation already delegated to `registerSlice`, so this is the signature\ncatching up with the behaviour.\n\nThe same report''s claim about `registerMiddleware` is out of date: the generic\noverload added in 0.8.0 made it castless already. Only this one was left.\n\nSecond half, which nobody filed: the `Store` class''s public signatures narrowed\nevery decoration member back to the store''s own `EM`, shadowing the permissive\nones on `StoreDecoration`. `createStore` returns `StoreInstance`, so decorators\nwritten against that were fine, but `Store` is exported too and anyone typed\nagainst the class lost castless decoration entirely. Widened to match.\n\nThe type tests assert the cast is gone, and were checked against the old\nsignature first to confirm they fail with exactly the reported error rather than\npassing vacuously.\n\nAlso documents the pattern behind the request. A decorator that owns a\nlifecycle, a connection or a credential cannot put it in reduced state, because\nstate is snapshotted, frozen and shipped to a devtools panel. Three independent\nlibraries needed to hand something else back and all three returned\n`{ store, handle }`. The guide stated the contract as absolute; it now describes\nthe pattern, states plainly that it costs nesting and dependency-by-constraint,\nand says when not to reach for it.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkhngAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9Uo+AQDU0dtaOOEJYNb2yn5HXdUXwUO/WvlUoVbRhTsOxWC/5gEAsCF/O4Nktfje\nlj8hfvEClqZqc+o8ggJmku9yb0MkIAw=\n=XjHU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:02:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDc3ZmU0NTcxZjVlYmJmNzBmY2M2ZmU3MzE3NTJiOTYzZTUyMDhiYjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3","sha":"2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3"}],"sha":"77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/77fe4571f5ebbf70fcc6fe731752b963e5208bb1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:45:47Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:45:47Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core): an uncommitted event now tells the observer why, and who\n\n0.8.0 gave attribution to the emitter and withheld it from the observer.\n`EmitResult` gained `reason` and `vetoedBy`; the instrumentation path computed\nboth and dropped them on the floor.\n\nSo a consumer tapping `store.instrument` could report `committed: false` and\ncould not say whether a guard had refused the action, a double-click had been\ndeduplicated, or a cascade had breached its ceiling. Those want three different\nresponses, which is the argument 0.8.0 itself made for putting the fields on\n`EmitResult`: \"a caller could not tell a guard refusing an action from a\ndouble-click being deduplicated.\" The observer was left in exactly the position\nthe caller was rescued from.\n\nInstrumentation is the only seam that sees every event, uncommitted ones\nincluded, without the observer joining the pipeline. Gathering reasons at emit\nsites instead would mean touching every call site and would still miss whatever\nan effect emits, so there was nowhere else for a consuming runtime to get this.\n\n`InstrumentedEvent` now carries both, spread conditionally beside `rejected` so\nthe object stays byte-identical in shape when they are absent. No value is\nrecomputed: `emitInstrumentation` already receives the `EmitResult`.\n\nDocumented with the limit rather than implying three values are reachable: a\ndeduplicated event is dropped at `emit` before it is ever queued, and a cascade\nrefusal returns before the drain reaches instrumentation, so `reason` reads\n\"vetoed\" or nothing today. The type is wider because it is shared with\n`EmitResult`, not because the other values arrive.\n\nCarried through to the panel, which is where the distinction is read by eye:\n`STORE_EVENT` gains both fields, both agents forward them, and the event\ntimeline labels a bounced row with what stopped it and, where the middleware had\na name, who. Previously a refusal, a deduplication and a cascade breach were one\nred dot. Every field is optional, so an older agent against a newer panel and\nthe reverse both keep working.\n\nOne caveat found while testing and left in a comment: `vetoedBy` comes from\n`Function.name`, and a bundler renames a named function expression assigned to a\nbinding of its own name. It is a strong hint, not an identifier.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"c9554a2037293c881344ecd110bad431ee1b8550","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/c9554a2037293c881344ecd110bad431ee1b8550"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3","verification":{"payload":"tree c9554a2037293c881344ecd110bad431ee1b8550\nparent 451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790516747 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790516747 -0600\n\nfeat(core): an uncommitted event now tells the observer why, and who\n\n0.8.0 gave attribution to the emitter and withheld it from the observer.\n`EmitResult` gained `reason` and `vetoedBy`; the instrumentation path computed\nboth and dropped them on the floor.\n\nSo a consumer tapping `store.instrument` could report `committed: false` and\ncould not say whether a guard had refused the action, a double-click had been\ndeduplicated, or a cascade had breached its ceiling. Those want three different\nresponses, which is the argument 0.8.0 itself made for putting the fields on\n`EmitResult`: \"a caller could not tell a guard refusing an action from a\ndouble-click being deduplicated.\" The observer was left in exactly the position\nthe caller was rescued from.\n\nInstrumentation is the only seam that sees every event, uncommitted ones\nincluded, without the observer joining the pipeline. Gathering reasons at emit\nsites instead would mean touching every call site and would still miss whatever\nan effect emits, so there was nowhere else for a consuming runtime to get this.\n\n`InstrumentedEvent` now carries both, spread conditionally beside `rejected` so\nthe object stays byte-identical in shape when they are absent. No value is\nrecomputed: `emitInstrumentation` already receives the `EmitResult`.\n\nDocumented with the limit rather than implying three values are reachable: a\ndeduplicated event is dropped at `emit` before it is ever queued, and a cascade\nrefusal returns before the drain reaches instrumentation, so `reason` reads\n\"vetoed\" or nothing today. The type is wider because it is shared with\n`EmitResult`, not because the other values arrive.\n\nCarried through to the panel, which is where the distinction is read by eye:\n`STORE_EVENT` gains both fields, both agents forward them, and the event\ntimeline labels a bounced row with what stopped it and, where the middleware had\na name, who. Previously a refusal, a deduplication and a cascade breach were one\nred dot. Every field is optional, so an older agent against a newer panel and\nthe reverse both keep working.\n\nOne caveat found while testing and left in a comment: `vetoedBy` comes from\n`Function.name`, and a bundler renames a named function expression assigned to a\nbinding of its own name. It is a strong hint, not an identifier.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkeCwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9TlYAP9pnCQeeZgOxxZt3usIH+6h68X03QnB90J41dvhOpU+jAEAxO/F3F5RZF+/\nEIqMYYvXN51lHFWdM1jZjQOIBfuHBQo=\n=JLY/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:02:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDJlYmZmY2Y4NmRmMjBkNDBmMzk3ZDA0NTY5MDYwNmY2ZGM5ZDNmYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f","sha":"451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f"}],"sha":"2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2ebffcf86df20d40f397d045690606f6dc9d3fa3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:38:00Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T13:38:00Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(core): the documentation that contradicted the code\n\nA consuming runtime reviewed 0.8.0 and filed eight asks. Two of them are\ndocumentation, and reading the source to answer them turned up two more that\nnobody had filed.\n\n**Replay.** `__replayEvents` still said it runs \"reducers and event subscribers\nONLY\" in both `types.ts` and `Store.ts`. 0.8.0 stopped notifying subscribers\nunless one opts in per subscription, and shipped a documentation-correction patch\nin the same release that reached `onEvent` and missed this. The phrase is the one\nthat tells a reader replay is subscriber-visible, so it read as a promise rather\nthan a stale list. Correct text already existed in the replay loop''s own comment\na hundred lines below.\n\n**Correlation.** Two defects nobody filed, found while answering a third ask.\n`store.call()` matches a reply on `event.parentId === requestId` — the immediate\nparent — while the prose in three places claimed anything \"causally descended\",\nwhich overstates it by a degree: a reply emitted a further hop down a cascade\ncarries the intermediate event''s id and is not seen. And `CallOptions.correlationId`\nopened by saying it correlates \"instead of on causality\", then said eleven lines\nlater that a reply matches on the echoed id *or* the causal link. The second is\nwhat the code does. The parent check runs first and unconditionally, so the option\nwidens the match and there is deliberately no way to match on the echoed id alone.\nBoth now say what happens.\n\n**The slice boundary.** A reducer receives exactly one slice and returns exactly\none slice. It is handed no `getState`, no store reference and no sibling, and\n`commitStaged` writes back only under the name the reducer was mounted as, so it\ncannot reach another slice even by returning a whole-store-shaped object. That is\nstructural, and no prose anywhere said so — grepping for it finds only *error*\nisolation, a different property. Two consumers built mechanisms around intra-slice\nwrite authorisation before establishing that inside one slice there is no second\nwriter and so no question to answer.\n\n**Finding `store.call()` at all.** The review asked for release notes describing a\n0.8.0 rebuild. There was no rebuild: the diff across the three call source files\nbetween the 0.7.0 and 0.8.0 tags is empty, the whole surface shipped in 0.6.0 with\na fifteen-line changelog entry, and the Request and Reply guide landed in the same\ncommit as the feature. The reviewer''s own version range already contained every\nfeature they concluded was missing.\n\nThe discoverability failure behind it is ours, though. The package README''s call\nsection ended without linking its own 243-line guide. `correlationId` — the one\noption a responder across a boundary needs — appeared in no hand-written document,\nonly in generated reference. And the upgrade guide listed `store.call` under\n\"nothing to do\" without saying where it is documented, which reads as absence. All\nthree are fixed, and the guide gains the section on replying when the reply cannot\nbe a direct child.\n\nAlso repoints seven links in Spanish indexes that pointed at English pages with\nSpanish equivalents.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"fb6a29c891aff95d9779c2e0b81907a2db098227","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/fb6a29c891aff95d9779c2e0b81907a2db098227"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f","verification":{"payload":"tree fb6a29c891aff95d9779c2e0b81907a2db098227\nparent 6b65bc82db1a0fec6433d2bc23d733bbc79b97f4\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790516280 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790516280 -0600\n\ndocs(core): the documentation that contradicted the code\n\nA consuming runtime reviewed 0.8.0 and filed eight asks. Two of them are\ndocumentation, and reading the source to answer them turned up two more that\nnobody had filed.\n\n**Replay.** `__replayEvents` still said it runs \"reducers and event subscribers\nONLY\" in both `types.ts` and `Store.ts`. 0.8.0 stopped notifying subscribers\nunless one opts in per subscription, and shipped a documentation-correction patch\nin the same release that reached `onEvent` and missed this. The phrase is the one\nthat tells a reader replay is subscriber-visible, so it read as a promise rather\nthan a stale list. Correct text already existed in the replay loop''s own comment\na hundred lines below.\n\n**Correlation.** Two defects nobody filed, found while answering a third ask.\n`store.call()` matches a reply on `event.parentId === requestId` — the immediate\nparent — while the prose in three places claimed anything \"causally descended\",\nwhich overstates it by a degree: a reply emitted a further hop down a cascade\ncarries the intermediate event''s id and is not seen. And `CallOptions.correlationId`\nopened by saying it correlates \"instead of on causality\", then said eleven lines\nlater that a reply matches on the echoed id *or* the causal link. The second is\nwhat the code does. The parent check runs first and unconditionally, so the option\nwidens the match and there is deliberately no way to match on the echoed id alone.\nBoth now say what happens.\n\n**The slice boundary.** A reducer receives exactly one slice and returns exactly\none slice. It is handed no `getState`, no store reference and no sibling, and\n`commitStaged` writes back only under the name the reducer was mounted as, so it\ncannot reach another slice even by returning a whole-store-shaped object. That is\nstructural, and no prose anywhere said so — grepping for it finds only *error*\nisolation, a different property. Two consumers built mechanisms around intra-slice\nwrite authorisation before establishing that inside one slice there is no second\nwriter and so no question to answer.\n\n**Finding `store.call()` at all.** The review asked for release notes describing a\n0.8.0 rebuild. There was no rebuild: the diff across the three call source files\nbetween the 0.7.0 and 0.8.0 tags is empty, the whole surface shipped in 0.6.0 with\na fifteen-line changelog entry, and the Request and Reply guide landed in the same\ncommit as the feature. The reviewer''s own version range already contained every\nfeature they concluded was missing.\n\nThe discoverability failure behind it is ours, though. The package README''s call\nsection ended without linking its own 243-line guide. `correlationId` — the one\noption a responder across a boundary needs — appeared in no hand-written document,\nonly in generated reference. And the upgrade guide listed `store.call` under\n\"nothing to do\" without saying where it is documented, which reads as absence. All\nthree are fixed, and the guide gains the section on replying when the reply cannot\nbe a direct child.\n\nAlso repoints seven links in Spanish indexes that pointed at English pages with\nSpanish equivalents.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkcOQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9U5GAQCCIsqx0NudOeYLk80K0Th3X51wT1tbkW/UsBAyyIjepwD/YxiLVFUUsAQq\nuFIPg2xGuqeMKVMo0XNOfNSl2mEOjw8=\n=itG/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T21:02:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDQ1MWUwMjUxODI2MDcxZjM1OWY0YWFkNTcxMGE2ZWNmMWExOWE2NGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6b65bc82db1a0fec6433d2bc23d733bbc79b97f4","sha":"6b65bc82db1a0fec6433d2bc23d733bbc79b97f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6b65bc82db1a0fec6433d2bc23d733bbc79b97f4"}],"sha":"451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/451e0251826071f359f4aad5710a6ecf1a19a64f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/8f54042797ac1533ec6ab5771aede96cff3ab89b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:59:24Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:59:24Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"chore(repo): recompute the Rush state hash after the rebase\n\n`repo-state.json` holds a hash of the lockfile, so rebasing this branch onto a\nmain that had itself changed the lockfile left the two disagreeing. It is the\none file that conflicted across all thirteen commits, and it is generated, so\nthe conflict was resolved by letting `rush update` recompute it rather than by\npicking a side.\n\nIts own commit because it belongs to none of the others.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"11e2026e090d4d98dc88deef7e633e105bf280f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/11e2026e090d4d98dc88deef7e633e105bf280f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/8f54042797ac1533ec6ab5771aede96cff3ab89b","verification":{"payload":"tree 11e2026e090d4d98dc88deef7e633e105bf280f1\nparent 0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513964 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513964 -0600\n\nchore(repo): recompute the Rush state hash after the rebase\n\n`repo-state.json` holds a hash of the lockfile, so rebasing this branch onto a\nmain that had itself changed the lockfile left the two disagreeing. It is the\none file that conflicted across all thirteen commits, and it is generated, so\nthe conflict was resolved by letting `rush update` recompute it rather than by\npicking a side.\n\nIts own commit because it belongs to none of the others.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkTLAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9elAAPwIYKNVvw6ICrA9KGTdGyN+2DZVEliWtdhbtWCcKMJg+QEAu6tdlmpL+UB9\nJEO1PYaANynnfPmVy7q9J8uBOd1efQ8=\n=R2sk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/8f54042797ac1533ec6ab5771aede96cff3ab89b","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDhmNTQwNDI3OTdhYzE1MzNlYzZhYjU3NzFhZWRlOTZjZmYzYWI4OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00","sha":"0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00"}],"sha":"8f54042797ac1533ec6ab5771aede96cff3ab89b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/8f54042797ac1533ec6ab5771aede96cff3ab89b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:50:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:35Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(ds): describe the evidence without naming the project it came from\n\nTwo TSDoc comments quoted a consuming project''s own class names as the evidence\nfor a component existing. The prose around them was already generic, but the\nnames carried that project''s prefix, and both comments ship: to npm inside the\ntype declarations, and to the committed API reference. The evidence is the same\nwithout them, so they are gone and the sentences say what happened instead.\n\nWhile in the file, `CardElevation` gets the doc comment that had been sitting\nabove `CardTone` describing it. Two published pages were wrong as a result: one\nexplained a card''s lift under the heading for its surface, and the other had no\ndescription at all.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"4fc6cd67687e8157f1ecd179f5d23a9be8723b7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/4fc6cd67687e8157f1ecd179f5d23a9be8723b7f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00","verification":{"payload":"tree 4fc6cd67687e8157f1ecd179f5d23a9be8723b7f\nparent ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513428 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513915 -0600\n\ndocs(ds): describe the evidence without naming the project it came from\n\nTwo TSDoc comments quoted a consuming project''s own class names as the evidence\nfor a component existing. The prose around them was already generic, but the\nnames carried that project''s prefix, and both comments ship: to npm inside the\ntype declarations, and to the committed API reference. The evidence is the same\nwithout them, so they are gone and the sentences say what happened instead.\n\nWhile in the file, `CardElevation` gets the doc comment that had been sitting\nabove `CardTone` describing it. Two published pages were wrong as a result: one\nexplained a card''s lift under the heading for its surface, and the other had no\ndescription at all.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS+wAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9QA1AQCbq+wMpy52SYeY7dCr6rQ/iCT2UlviCdRVIZLe48lFlwD/bC6ea4sFFx+8\ncP2BudWUEFtLhjBjHSi9hsidb+dkfA8=\n=VZB9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDBjNGU1NWM1ZTNiMWFmYmI2NGVhNTE1ZWQ2YzVkMGI0MDJiZDhhMDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9","sha":"ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9"}],"sha":"0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0c4e55c5e3b1afbb64ea515ed6c5d0b402bd8a00"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:47:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:34Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(react): reading a nested object from frozen state no longer throws\n\n`useAtomicProps` threw a `TypeError` raised by the engine as soon as a selector\nhanded back an object and the component read an object out of it.\n\nThe development guard against undeclared reads wraps each nested value in its\nown proxy, so a read two levels down is still checked. A `get` trap may not do\nthat over an own data property that is both non-writable and non-configurable,\nwhich is exactly the pair `Object.freeze` produces: the specification requires\nthe trap to return that value itself, and V8 checks it. The message names the\nproperty and the two descriptors and nothing else, and it is raised before any\ncode in this package runs, so the stack trace pointed at the component that did\nthe reading with nothing in it to suggest where to look.\n\nFrozen state is the ordinary case rather than an exotic one. Immer auto-freezes\nwhatever `produce` returns unless a program calls `setAutoFreeze(false)`, and\nthis repository ships a `deepFreeze` in core for the same purpose, so a reducer\nwritten the usual way hands the store frozen objects and any selector returning\na container hit this.\n\nThe guard is now built over a shallow, extensible copy when its subject is\nfrozen, which is what makes returning a nested guard legal. Nested values stay\nthe frozen originals and are copied in turn only if a read goes through them.\nAn undeclared read is still refused at every depth.\n\nEvery test for this guard built its state from a plain object literal and never\nfroze it, so the suite agreed with itself for two releases. Four tests now\nfreeze it, one of them pinning the engine''s message so the failure mode is\nrecognisable if it ever returns.\n\nThe other proxy in this package, the typed-path recorder, is unaffected: its\ntarget is a function, whose `length` and `name` are non-writable but\nconfigurable, so the invariant does not apply.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"3566812872f77bbeafa952fc4e607488d9fec08a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/3566812872f77bbeafa952fc4e607488d9fec08a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9","verification":{"payload":"tree 3566812872f77bbeafa952fc4e607488d9fec08a\nparent 3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513230 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513914 -0600\n\nfix(react): reading a nested object from frozen state no longer throws\n\n`useAtomicProps` threw a `TypeError` raised by the engine as soon as a selector\nhanded back an object and the component read an object out of it.\n\nThe development guard against undeclared reads wraps each nested value in its\nown proxy, so a read two levels down is still checked. A `get` trap may not do\nthat over an own data property that is both non-writable and non-configurable,\nwhich is exactly the pair `Object.freeze` produces: the specification requires\nthe trap to return that value itself, and V8 checks it. The message names the\nproperty and the two descriptors and nothing else, and it is raised before any\ncode in this package runs, so the stack trace pointed at the component that did\nthe reading with nothing in it to suggest where to look.\n\nFrozen state is the ordinary case rather than an exotic one. Immer auto-freezes\nwhatever `produce` returns unless a program calls `setAutoFreeze(false)`, and\nthis repository ships a `deepFreeze` in core for the same purpose, so a reducer\nwritten the usual way hands the store frozen objects and any selector returning\na container hit this.\n\nThe guard is now built over a shallow, extensible copy when its subject is\nfrozen, which is what makes returning a nested guard legal. Nested values stay\nthe frozen originals and are copied in turn only if a read goes through them.\nAn undeclared read is still refused at every depth.\n\nEvery test for this guard built its state from a plain object literal and never\nfroze it, so the suite agreed with itself for two releases. Four tests now\nfreeze it, one of them pinning the engine''s message so the failure mode is\nrecognisable if it ever returns.\n\nThe other proxy in this package, the typed-path recorder, is unaffected: its\ntarget is a function, whose `length` and `name` are non-writable but\nconfigurable, so the invariant does not apply.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS+gAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ZFWAP9p+AMWe0PbmNKafBam2SDTQKsa7gCt6Rvryi7l0ig34AEA8FuByPkKXHiH\n1adF2NuOxXvmaOBEFt6UZPhjnnzuZwc=\n=gsfy\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGVjNjVhNGVmMTEzYmQ2MzA3NDVmMDM1OWM4OTQ4YmI3MWQwMDhiYTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9","sha":"3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9"}],"sha":"ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/ec65a4ef113bd630745f0359c8948bb71d008ba9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:13:27Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:34Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(ds): the examples now demonstrate the design system they document\n\nM6 was meant to be a rename pass over the five in-repo examples. The renames\nwere the smallest part of it.\n\nThe mechanical half went as planned. `scripts/codemod-tokens.mjs` rewrote 38\nproperties across both the CSS and the SCSS, flagged the six uses of\n`--yl-color-brand` it is not allowed to decide, and those were settled by hand:\ntext takes `fg-brand`, a slider thumb takes `interactive-bg`, an active nav\nunderline takes the same role as the label above it. Every `--yl-*` reference in\nevery example now resolves against the emitted sheet, verified by extracting the\nproperty names from `themeCss()` and diffing.\n\nThe rest was what the survey had already said and nobody had acted on.\n\n**Two examples rendered the design system''s components unstyled.** The React and\nNext.js examples import `Button`, `Input`, `Select`, `Badge`, `Callout` and\n`CodeBlock`, and imported not one component stylesheet between them. They\ninjected `themeCss()`, which emits custom properties and no rules at all, so\nevery one of those components rendered as a bare element carrying class names\nthat nothing defined. The React example''s CSS bundle went from nothing to 11.9\nKB when the sheets were added, which is the size of the bug.\n\n**Two examples had no 10px root.** Every `--yl-*` length is a rem against the\nroot `base.css` establishes, and without it `--yl-space-2` is 12.8px rather than\n8px. Both apps used spacing tokens anyway, so every gap in them was out by the\nsame factor. The Next.js example sets its own root, which is the case\n`base-no-root.css` was written for and had no users of until now.\n\n**Mission control declared a whole palette beside the system''s.** Eleven colours,\n15 hex literals, 53 lengths in device pixels, zero tokens, under a comment in\n`main.tsx` claiming the telemetry visuals were \"built from the same tokens\".\nThey were not. They are now: no palette, 92 token references, and the four\nhand-picked accents replaced by the four status roles, which is the same\nvocabulary a `Badge` or a `Callout` uses for the same meanings. The hand-rolled\nvalues turn out to have been eyeballed from the dark theme all along, matching\n`fg-default` and `fg-muted` to within a point or two of each channel, so naming\nthe roles changes almost nothing about how it looks and everything about whether\nit follows a change to them.\n\nThree badges there were `variant=\"brand\"` because `error`, `warning` and\n`success` did not exist when they were written. M4 added them.\n\nThe floating panels in the kinetic-logo demo moved onto the ink roles —\n`bg-ink`, `fg-on-ink`, `border-on-ink` — which were defined in the first release\nand used by nothing. Their section headings and note were mid-greys on a\nnear-black surface, 3.3 to 1 and 2.4 to 1 at 10px, both under the 4.5 to 1 that\nsmall text has to clear; the muted role is 6.1 to 1 there.\n\nEvery remaining literal in the examples is a blur radius or a gradient extent,\nboth of which belong in device pixels, and every one of them says so.\n\nTwo package fixes fell out of doing the work:\n\n**The upgrade codemod was not published.** `files` listed `dist/`, `LICENSE` and\n`README.md`, and the README has documented\n`node node_modules/@yoltra/ds/scripts/codemod-tokens.mjs` since the rename\nlanded. The one command a consumer needs in order to move to this release was\nthe one command that could not run. Verified now by unpacking a real tarball and\nrunning it against a file.\n\n**The README omitted the tokens people actually reinvent.** A table of them now:\nz-index, elevation, motion, breakpoints, containers, tabular figures, font\nweights, border widths. Not one had a single use across the projects surveyed\nfor this release, and every example in this commit was rewriting them by hand.\nThe authoring section also still described the flat stylesheet layout that M2\nreplaced.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"ceadc8194c287d9e7baf1356db448c3d0d38d8a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/ceadc8194c287d9e7baf1356db448c3d0d38d8a5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9","verification":{"payload":"tree ceadc8194c287d9e7baf1356db448c3d0d38d8a5\nparent 787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790511207 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513914 -0600\n\nfeat(ds): the examples now demonstrate the design system they document\n\nM6 was meant to be a rename pass over the five in-repo examples. The renames\nwere the smallest part of it.\n\nThe mechanical half went as planned. `scripts/codemod-tokens.mjs` rewrote 38\nproperties across both the CSS and the SCSS, flagged the six uses of\n`--yl-color-brand` it is not allowed to decide, and those were settled by hand:\ntext takes `fg-brand`, a slider thumb takes `interactive-bg`, an active nav\nunderline takes the same role as the label above it. Every `--yl-*` reference in\nevery example now resolves against the emitted sheet, verified by extracting the\nproperty names from `themeCss()` and diffing.\n\nThe rest was what the survey had already said and nobody had acted on.\n\n**Two examples rendered the design system''s components unstyled.** The React and\nNext.js examples import `Button`, `Input`, `Select`, `Badge`, `Callout` and\n`CodeBlock`, and imported not one component stylesheet between them. They\ninjected `themeCss()`, which emits custom properties and no rules at all, so\nevery one of those components rendered as a bare element carrying class names\nthat nothing defined. The React example''s CSS bundle went from nothing to 11.9\nKB when the sheets were added, which is the size of the bug.\n\n**Two examples had no 10px root.** Every `--yl-*` length is a rem against the\nroot `base.css` establishes, and without it `--yl-space-2` is 12.8px rather than\n8px. Both apps used spacing tokens anyway, so every gap in them was out by the\nsame factor. The Next.js example sets its own root, which is the case\n`base-no-root.css` was written for and had no users of until now.\n\n**Mission control declared a whole palette beside the system''s.** Eleven colours,\n15 hex literals, 53 lengths in device pixels, zero tokens, under a comment in\n`main.tsx` claiming the telemetry visuals were \"built from the same tokens\".\nThey were not. They are now: no palette, 92 token references, and the four\nhand-picked accents replaced by the four status roles, which is the same\nvocabulary a `Badge` or a `Callout` uses for the same meanings. The hand-rolled\nvalues turn out to have been eyeballed from the dark theme all along, matching\n`fg-default` and `fg-muted` to within a point or two of each channel, so naming\nthe roles changes almost nothing about how it looks and everything about whether\nit follows a change to them.\n\nThree badges there were `variant=\"brand\"` because `error`, `warning` and\n`success` did not exist when they were written. M4 added them.\n\nThe floating panels in the kinetic-logo demo moved onto the ink roles —\n`bg-ink`, `fg-on-ink`, `border-on-ink` — which were defined in the first release\nand used by nothing. Their section headings and note were mid-greys on a\nnear-black surface, 3.3 to 1 and 2.4 to 1 at 10px, both under the 4.5 to 1 that\nsmall text has to clear; the muted role is 6.1 to 1 there.\n\nEvery remaining literal in the examples is a blur radius or a gradient extent,\nboth of which belong in device pixels, and every one of them says so.\n\nTwo package fixes fell out of doing the work:\n\n**The upgrade codemod was not published.** `files` listed `dist/`, `LICENSE` and\n`README.md`, and the README has documented\n`node node_modules/@yoltra/ds/scripts/codemod-tokens.mjs` since the rename\nlanded. The one command a consumer needs in order to move to this release was\nthe one command that could not run. Verified now by unpacking a real tarball and\nrunning it against a file.\n\n**The README omitted the tokens people actually reinvent.** A table of them now:\nz-index, elevation, motion, breakpoints, containers, tabular figures, font\nweights, border widths. Not one had a single use across the projects surveyed\nfor this release, and every example in this commit was rewriting them by hand.\nThe authoring section also still described the flat stylesheet layout that M2\nreplaced.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS+gAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ZQkAQDbj3auW5NJzcuA7E/gE9MxoYOJ3kyjQkzPX9QlelydiwD/btCIQVGavYco\n4R+SSQofWQGoRDKEgW15fBIHYvg8NQI=\n=9w4J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDM3MjJiMTNmZmM1NGE1NTJiOGJjYTY3OTRiMzc0ZjY3ZDQ0Y2I1Zjk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5","sha":"787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5"}],"sha":"3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3722b13ffc54a552b8bca6794b374f67d44cb5f9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T11:45:57Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:34Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(ds): the components the consuming projects had already written\n\nFive components, none of them invented here. Each one was found in a project\nthat depends on this package, built locally because the design system did not\nship it, and in two cases built twice in two applications that could not import\nfrom one another.\n\n`Stat` and `StatGrid` for a labelled figure. It renders a real zero rather than\na dash: \"unavailable\" and \"none\" are different facts, and a component written\nwith `value && ...` quietly tells the reader the wrong one.\n\n`Chip` for a compact tag. Squared off where `Badge` is a pill, so the two do not\nread as the same thing at a glance.\n\n`ProgressBar`, the determinate counterpart to `Spinner`. It clamps its value,\nbecause a bar past its end is a layout bug that arrives with production data\nlong after the component was reviewed. `label` is required: a bar with no name\nis announced as a percentage with no subject. The fill is a transform rather\nthan a width, and its origin follows the writing direction, so it does not run\nbackwards in a right-to-left interface.\n\n`AuthCard`, pure composition over `Card`, `Stack` and `Heading`, rendering as\n`main` unless told otherwise. Two `main` landmarks say nothing about which holds\nthe content, so the escape hatch is documented rather than implied.\n\nWith them, `useControllableState`, for a value that is either the caller''s or\nthe component''s, and `noFlashScript()`, the inline script this package has\ndocumented since its first release and never shipped. It shares\n`THEME_STORAGE_KEY` with `ThemeProvider` from one module, so a provider writing\none key while the script reads another cannot happen.\n\nPutting those two halves side by side exposed a defect in the older one.\n`ThemeProvider` restored the theme through a guard that produced `false` when\n`localStorage` was absent, and `false ?? system` keeps the `false`, so the root\nwas set to `data-theme=\"false\"` and every colour fell back to its light-theme\ndefault. Reading also threw outright where site data is blocked, which inside an\neffect takes the tree down, and a stored value naming no theme was applied\nverbatim. Reading is now guarded and validated; persisting is allowed to fail on\nits own, because a theme the reader chose and can see is worth more than the\npromise of remembering it.\n\nThat whole path was untested, at 19% when this milestone began. It is at 100%\nnow, and the package at 99.8/96.7/100/99.8.\n\nAlso: every component''s README, the two package READMEs now listing the real\nexport surface rather than a table that had been missing seven components since\nbefore this work started, and 20 new snapshots.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"31cbcd4585c85bd72513d60e9615e03c0621eb78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/31cbcd4585c85bd72513d60e9615e03c0621eb78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5","verification":{"payload":"tree 31cbcd4585c85bd72513d60e9615e03c0621eb78\nparent 2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790509557 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513914 -0600\n\nfeat(ds): the components the consuming projects had already written\n\nFive components, none of them invented here. Each one was found in a project\nthat depends on this package, built locally because the design system did not\nship it, and in two cases built twice in two applications that could not import\nfrom one another.\n\n`Stat` and `StatGrid` for a labelled figure. It renders a real zero rather than\na dash: \"unavailable\" and \"none\" are different facts, and a component written\nwith `value && ...` quietly tells the reader the wrong one.\n\n`Chip` for a compact tag. Squared off where `Badge` is a pill, so the two do not\nread as the same thing at a glance.\n\n`ProgressBar`, the determinate counterpart to `Spinner`. It clamps its value,\nbecause a bar past its end is a layout bug that arrives with production data\nlong after the component was reviewed. `label` is required: a bar with no name\nis announced as a percentage with no subject. The fill is a transform rather\nthan a width, and its origin follows the writing direction, so it does not run\nbackwards in a right-to-left interface.\n\n`AuthCard`, pure composition over `Card`, `Stack` and `Heading`, rendering as\n`main` unless told otherwise. Two `main` landmarks say nothing about which holds\nthe content, so the escape hatch is documented rather than implied.\n\nWith them, `useControllableState`, for a value that is either the caller''s or\nthe component''s, and `noFlashScript()`, the inline script this package has\ndocumented since its first release and never shipped. It shares\n`THEME_STORAGE_KEY` with `ThemeProvider` from one module, so a provider writing\none key while the script reads another cannot happen.\n\nPutting those two halves side by side exposed a defect in the older one.\n`ThemeProvider` restored the theme through a guard that produced `false` when\n`localStorage` was absent, and `false ?? system` keeps the `false`, so the root\nwas set to `data-theme=\"false\"` and every colour fell back to its light-theme\ndefault. Reading also threw outright where site data is blocked, which inside an\neffect takes the tree down, and a stored value naming no theme was applied\nverbatim. Reading is now guarded and validated; persisting is allowed to fail on\nits own, because a theme the reader chose and can see is worth more than the\npromise of remembering it.\n\nThat whole path was untested, at 19% when this milestone began. It is at 100%\nnow, and the package at 99.8/96.7/100/99.8.\n\nAlso: every component''s README, the two package READMEs now listing the real\nexport surface rather than a table that had been missing seven components since\nbefore this work started, and 20 new snapshots.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS+gAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9VcuAQDXqFCt0T+r+2TyNqR6KD/ZC1zmD6GhTBMIcgupkkOFMQEAxJjDwN8/PYzl\nNzn/sKU+10Rrgp0FxfxQsxTWkaDAxgs=\n=2bgg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDc4N2Y1OWU1NGJiZTI5OWE4MWRkMGRhZWJhYjU5N2ZkODkzYmEyZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3","sha":"2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3"}],"sha":"787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/787f59e54bbe299a81dd0daebab597fd893ba2f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:58:55Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:33Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(ds): the fixes consuming projects had been working around\n\nEvery item here was found by reading what four projects had built locally rather than\nby reviewing this package, which is the useful thing about having read them.\n\n**Button.** A `danger` variant, because a consuming project''s build was red over\n`variant=\"danger\"` and had been shipped that way. It uses `error[600]`, where a white\nlabel is 4.83 to 1; `[500]` is 3.76 and would have repeated the brand colour''s\nmistake. An `lg` size at 44px, the touch target a control used standing up at a\ncounter needs, and the same padding `md` had before the density pass. A `loading`\nstate, hand-rolled as `{busy ? \"Saving…\" : \"Save\"}` at ten or more call sites across\ntwo projects. And `pressed`, for the toggle idiom copied verbatim three times.\n\n`loading` sets `aria-busy` and `aria-disabled` rather than `disabled`: the real\nattribute drops the control out of the tab order mid-action and throws the reader\nsomewhere else. The label stays in the layout at zero opacity, which holds the width\n**and** keeps the accessible name, where `visibility: hidden` and `display: none`\nboth hold the width and take the name away. The spinner is drawn in `button.css`\nrather than borrowed from `Spinner`, so importing one stylesheet stays enough.\n\n**Badge** gains the four status kinds, using the words `Callout` already used. Two\nprojects added these independently, and one passed raw light-mode hex through a\n`style` prop to get them, which was wrong in the dark theme.\n\n**Card** gains `tone=\"subtle\"`. One project added the same thing locally and two of\nits screens gave up on `Card` entirely and inlined a border.\n\n**Label** ships, and `.yl-label` is styled on its own rather than as\n`.yl-field > .yl-label`. This package''s own TSDoc showed a bare\n`<label className=\"yl-label\">`, a project copied that example sixteen times, and\nevery one of them received no styling. The example now shows `Label`, so the class\nname is not something anyone needs to know.\n\n**Table** cells take `numeric`, which right-aligns and switches on tabular figures so\na column stops shuffling sideways as values change width; it was written out six\ntimes across three projects. `TableScroll` is the horizontal scroll region one\nproject carried as eight call sites of a class defined in a runtime `<style>` tag. It\nis a separate component rather than a prop on `Table`, because wrapping every table\nwould change the layout of every table that did not need it, and its `label` is\nrequired: the region is focusable so it can be scrolled from the keyboard, and a\nfocusable region with no name is a tab stop that announces nothing.\n\n**Tooltip** supplies `tabIndex: 0` to its trigger. A button is focusable already; a\nspan is not, and without it that tooltip opens for a pointer and never for a\nkeyboard. One project added it at three separate call sites before noticing it was\nthe same omission each time.\n\n**The five overlay hooks are exported.** They were implemented, shipped inside the\nbundle and exported by neither entry point, so nothing could reach them and nothing\nfailed. One project consequently hand-rolled a `role=\"dialog\"` overlay with no focus\ntrap, no Escape handling, no scroll lock and no focus restore, which is exactly the\nset those hooks already provided. There is now a test for the export surface,\nbecause a missing export is invisible to every other kind of test: the code\ncompiles, the suite passes, and the feature does not exist.\n\n**An unclassed anchor reads the link colour.** `--yl-color-fg-link` was defined from\nthe first release and applied to nothing, so prose links fell back to the user\nagent''s blue, which is unreadable on a dark background. A project patched it with\n`a:not(.yl-btn):not(.yl-link)` and recorded the trap in that approach: `:not()`\ntakes its argument''s specificity, so the chain out-specifies a bare `.yl-link` and\nevery future classed anchor has to join it. `:not([class])` avoids the problem\nentirely.\n\nThe typical-import budget moves 1 KB to 1.2 KB, measured rather than guessed: the\nadditions take it from 0.7 KB to 0.9 KB, and the tree-shaking regression it exists\nto catch now lands at 1.5 KB. Verified in both directions.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"0ba09aaa3d7ea5ff4a0175cb818f8ff733204dec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/0ba09aaa3d7ea5ff4a0175cb818f8ff733204dec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3","verification":{"payload":"tree 0ba09aaa3d7ea5ff4a0175cb818f8ff733204dec\nparent 5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790503135 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513913 -0600\n\nfeat(ds): the fixes consuming projects had been working around\n\nEvery item here was found by reading what four projects had built locally rather than\nby reviewing this package, which is the useful thing about having read them.\n\n**Button.** A `danger` variant, because a consuming project''s build was red over\n`variant=\"danger\"` and had been shipped that way. It uses `error[600]`, where a white\nlabel is 4.83 to 1; `[500]` is 3.76 and would have repeated the brand colour''s\nmistake. An `lg` size at 44px, the touch target a control used standing up at a\ncounter needs, and the same padding `md` had before the density pass. A `loading`\nstate, hand-rolled as `{busy ? \"Saving…\" : \"Save\"}` at ten or more call sites across\ntwo projects. And `pressed`, for the toggle idiom copied verbatim three times.\n\n`loading` sets `aria-busy` and `aria-disabled` rather than `disabled`: the real\nattribute drops the control out of the tab order mid-action and throws the reader\nsomewhere else. The label stays in the layout at zero opacity, which holds the width\n**and** keeps the accessible name, where `visibility: hidden` and `display: none`\nboth hold the width and take the name away. The spinner is drawn in `button.css`\nrather than borrowed from `Spinner`, so importing one stylesheet stays enough.\n\n**Badge** gains the four status kinds, using the words `Callout` already used. Two\nprojects added these independently, and one passed raw light-mode hex through a\n`style` prop to get them, which was wrong in the dark theme.\n\n**Card** gains `tone=\"subtle\"`. One project added the same thing locally and two of\nits screens gave up on `Card` entirely and inlined a border.\n\n**Label** ships, and `.yl-label` is styled on its own rather than as\n`.yl-field > .yl-label`. This package''s own TSDoc showed a bare\n`<label className=\"yl-label\">`, a project copied that example sixteen times, and\nevery one of them received no styling. The example now shows `Label`, so the class\nname is not something anyone needs to know.\n\n**Table** cells take `numeric`, which right-aligns and switches on tabular figures so\na column stops shuffling sideways as values change width; it was written out six\ntimes across three projects. `TableScroll` is the horizontal scroll region one\nproject carried as eight call sites of a class defined in a runtime `<style>` tag. It\nis a separate component rather than a prop on `Table`, because wrapping every table\nwould change the layout of every table that did not need it, and its `label` is\nrequired: the region is focusable so it can be scrolled from the keyboard, and a\nfocusable region with no name is a tab stop that announces nothing.\n\n**Tooltip** supplies `tabIndex: 0` to its trigger. A button is focusable already; a\nspan is not, and without it that tooltip opens for a pointer and never for a\nkeyboard. One project added it at three separate call sites before noticing it was\nthe same omission each time.\n\n**The five overlay hooks are exported.** They were implemented, shipped inside the\nbundle and exported by neither entry point, so nothing could reach them and nothing\nfailed. One project consequently hand-rolled a `role=\"dialog\"` overlay with no focus\ntrap, no Escape handling, no scroll lock and no focus restore, which is exactly the\nset those hooks already provided. There is now a test for the export surface,\nbecause a missing export is invisible to every other kind of test: the code\ncompiles, the suite passes, and the feature does not exist.\n\n**An unclassed anchor reads the link colour.** `--yl-color-fg-link` was defined from\nthe first release and applied to nothing, so prose links fell back to the user\nagent''s blue, which is unreadable on a dark background. A project patched it with\n`a:not(.yl-btn):not(.yl-link)` and recorded the trap in that approach: `:not()`\ntakes its argument''s specificity, so the chain out-specifies a bare `.yl-link` and\nevery future classed anchor has to join it. `:not([class])` avoids the problem\nentirely.\n\nThe typical-import budget moves 1 KB to 1.2 KB, measured rather than guessed: the\nadditions take it from 0.7 KB to 0.9 KB, and the tree-shaking regression it exists\nto catch now lands at 1.5 KB. Verified in both directions.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS+QAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9TwAAQC64cGkdoVM430miSPVJWZiFx6kiKG31c9ArQAzthxtvgEA6wmbAbK9SaOn\nAUyeIybUiEGpSagMI/0rAJDMNqKbKwc=\n=de1d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDJlNGJlNmI4ZWFmNDgzODhmNzU0ODAyMjI5M2E5OGRjMWM0NzdlYTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09","sha":"5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09"}],"sha":"2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2e4be6b8eaf48388f7548022293a98dc1c477ea3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:40:41Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:33Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(ds)!: the ARIA tabs pattern, a shakeable token graph, and the pairing audit landed\n\nThe three things the tracker was carrying, all closed.\n\n**Tabs implements the pattern now.** It set the four roles and `aria-selected` for four\nreleases and nothing else: every tab its own tab stop, arrow keys inert, and no\nattribute connecting a tab to the panel it controlled. It gains a roving `tabIndex`\nso the set is one stop, arrow keys that read the computed writing direction rather\nthan assuming left-to-right, `Home` and `End`, wrapping at both ends,\n`aria-controls` and `aria-labelledby` in both directions, and a focusable panel so\nTab from the selected tab reaches the content it selected.\n\nSelection follows focus by default, which is what the practices recommend when a\npanel is cheap. A new `activation=\"manual\"` moves focus only, for the case they\ncarve out: a panel expensive enough that arrowing past three to reach the fourth\nwould fetch three things nobody asked for. Sixteen behavioural tests, including the\nright-to-left inversion and two instances on one page keeping distinct ids.\n\n**A typical import drops from 2.8 KB to 0.7 KB.** The cause was not what the\nprevious two commits guessed. `/*#__PURE__*/` annotations were already working and\nthe `.join()` on the font stacks cost 37 bytes. The real mechanism is that a member\nexpression at module scope is something a bundler must assume could invoke a getter,\nso `const p = foundationTokens.palette` and every `p.primary[500]` inside a theme\nobject literal made both themes unconditional side effects. An application importing\none component shipped 6.3 KB where 0.3 KB was needed.\n\nFixed by hoisting the palette to its own binding, so `./themes` imports it instead\nof reading it off an object, and by building each theme inside a function whose call\nis annotated pure: inside a function body those reads are ordinary. `DARK_BASE`\nmoved in with them, because an annotation promises the call is side-effect free and\nsays nothing about the arguments passed to it. Measured through package resolution,\nthe way a consumer imports, not by absolute path.\n\nThe typical-import budget tightens from 4 KB to 1 KB. Thin on purpose: the\nregression measures 1.4 KB and would have passed at 1.5. Proved by hoisting\n`DARK_BASE` back out and watching `rush size` fail, then restoring.\n\n**The pairing audit is a test.** It reads the compiled CSS, resolves each `color`\nthrough the custom properties, walks up to the background the element actually sits\non, and measures. 106 assertions across both themes. It exists because a switch knob\nat 1.48:1 got past both existing suites, and it is committed only now because the\nfirst two attempts at it were wrong in ways that would have hidden a defect:\ncompositing translucent colours over white regardless of theme, pairing a resting\ncolour with a `:hover` background, and missing descendant selectors so `.yl-code pre`\nlooked like light text on a white page. Proved by injecting white-on-light into Badge\nand watching exactly two assertions fail with the real resolved values.\n\nIt still does not cover a background against a background, which is what the switch\nknob was. That stays asserted explicitly, and the suite says so in its own remarks.\n\n**One thing found on the way.** React''s `useId` counter is global to the module, so\ngiving Tabs its ARIA wiring renumbered every id generated after it: nineteen snapshot\nfailures, two of them the change and seventeen noise. A serializer renumbers them per\nsnapshot, keeping the relationships visible while dropping the counter''s value.\nSnapshots that churn for unrelated reasons stop being read. Proved by adding a\n`useId` to Badge and watching nothing else move.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"347662ed8f5c13520450c35302eb183d8111b718","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/347662ed8f5c13520450c35302eb183d8111b718"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09","verification":{"payload":"tree 347662ed8f5c13520450c35302eb183d8111b718\nparent a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790502041 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513913 -0600\n\nfeat(ds)!: the ARIA tabs pattern, a shakeable token graph, and the pairing audit landed\n\nThe three things the tracker was carrying, all closed.\n\n**Tabs implements the pattern now.** It set the four roles and `aria-selected` for four\nreleases and nothing else: every tab its own tab stop, arrow keys inert, and no\nattribute connecting a tab to the panel it controlled. It gains a roving `tabIndex`\nso the set is one stop, arrow keys that read the computed writing direction rather\nthan assuming left-to-right, `Home` and `End`, wrapping at both ends,\n`aria-controls` and `aria-labelledby` in both directions, and a focusable panel so\nTab from the selected tab reaches the content it selected.\n\nSelection follows focus by default, which is what the practices recommend when a\npanel is cheap. A new `activation=\"manual\"` moves focus only, for the case they\ncarve out: a panel expensive enough that arrowing past three to reach the fourth\nwould fetch three things nobody asked for. Sixteen behavioural tests, including the\nright-to-left inversion and two instances on one page keeping distinct ids.\n\n**A typical import drops from 2.8 KB to 0.7 KB.** The cause was not what the\nprevious two commits guessed. `/*#__PURE__*/` annotations were already working and\nthe `.join()` on the font stacks cost 37 bytes. The real mechanism is that a member\nexpression at module scope is something a bundler must assume could invoke a getter,\nso `const p = foundationTokens.palette` and every `p.primary[500]` inside a theme\nobject literal made both themes unconditional side effects. An application importing\none component shipped 6.3 KB where 0.3 KB was needed.\n\nFixed by hoisting the palette to its own binding, so `./themes` imports it instead\nof reading it off an object, and by building each theme inside a function whose call\nis annotated pure: inside a function body those reads are ordinary. `DARK_BASE`\nmoved in with them, because an annotation promises the call is side-effect free and\nsays nothing about the arguments passed to it. Measured through package resolution,\nthe way a consumer imports, not by absolute path.\n\nThe typical-import budget tightens from 4 KB to 1 KB. Thin on purpose: the\nregression measures 1.4 KB and would have passed at 1.5. Proved by hoisting\n`DARK_BASE` back out and watching `rush size` fail, then restoring.\n\n**The pairing audit is a test.** It reads the compiled CSS, resolves each `color`\nthrough the custom properties, walks up to the background the element actually sits\non, and measures. 106 assertions across both themes. It exists because a switch knob\nat 1.48:1 got past both existing suites, and it is committed only now because the\nfirst two attempts at it were wrong in ways that would have hidden a defect:\ncompositing translucent colours over white regardless of theme, pairing a resting\ncolour with a `:hover` background, and missing descendant selectors so `.yl-code pre`\nlooked like light text on a white page. Proved by injecting white-on-light into Badge\nand watching exactly two assertions fail with the real resolved values.\n\nIt still does not cover a background against a background, which is what the switch\nknob was. That stays asserted explicitly, and the suite says so in its own remarks.\n\n**One thing found on the way.** React''s `useId` counter is global to the module, so\ngiving Tabs its ARIA wiring renumbered every id generated after it: nineteen snapshot\nfailures, two of them the change and seventeen noise. A serializer renumbers them per\nsnapshot, keeping the relationships visible while dropping the counter''s value.\nSnapshots that churn for unrelated reasons stop being read. Proved by adding a\n`useId` to Badge and watching nothing else move.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS+QAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9fjiAQC4HMzAAup+aTCFoC9ZydejpCghTurWtaVfTGWRsl2wkgEAzwZiJGCZl/Yt\nH0PAXtnnCGtwEkU/iaWKJhubNa42PAQ=\n=Q1Oz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDViN2YzMjA1NTNiZjk0MGU4NDZhYTRmMWU5MzA5OWUyMjkzNGVkMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2","sha":"a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2"}],"sha":"5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/5b7f320553bf940e846aa4f1e93099e22934ed09"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T09:15:51Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:33Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(ds)!: every component reads tokens, and stylelint keeps it that way\n\n121 hardcoded values become 12. The twelve that remain are each deliberate: two\n`em` values that must scale with the text around them, the spinner''s documented\nfallback, four breakpoints a media query cannot read from a custom property, the\none-pixel clip-rect idiom, and a SASS default argument.\n\nThe target was never zero literals. A dialog''s max-width is not a design-system\ndecision, and pretending it is would put twenty measures in the token sheet that\nno other component will ever read. The rule this settles on is narrower and\nenforceable: a literal is a defect wherever a token exists, and a **named**\ncomponent property is the answer wherever one does not. So `--dialog-width-md`,\n`--switch-track-width`, `--tooltip-max-width` and a dozen others now say what they\nare, and can be overridden from a stylesheet without reaching into a class.\n\n**The type scale reaches CSS for the first time.** It was emitted by nothing for\nfour releases, so `Typography.scss` grew its own and the two drifted: headings\nrendered 3.2rem where the scale said 3.6rem, and `Text` rendered 1.5rem where it\nsaid 1.6rem. Reconciled toward the components, not the tokens, because those are\nthe sizes users have seen and because the alternative was making everything\nlarger in the same release that tightened the spacing. `h5` and `h6` were missing\nfrom the scale entirely and are now there. A `type()` mixin applies a whole role,\nwhich is what makes twelve roles usable from five-declaration blocks.\nTypography.scss drops from 26 literals to 4.\n\n**CodeBlock''s copy button changes with the theme now.** Its five `rgba()` literals\nwere palette values copied by hand, so the header and the button stayed put while\nthe surface under them flipped. Both washes derive from the ink foreground, and the\nhover is twice the resting state rather than the two-hundredths of alpha that\nderiving them from the border role first produced.\n\n**stylelint closes the milestone**, wired into `rushx lint`. A hex, an `rgba()`, a\nliteral font size, a literal font weight, a raw font stack or a `px` border width\nis an error. Proved by breaking a stylesheet four ways and watching it catch all\nfour. This is why it moved here from M2: the rule cannot pass until the values it\nrejects are gone, and landing it earlier would have meant shipping it as a warning\nand tightening it later.\n\nVerified by resolving every declaration in every compiled stylesheet against the\ntoken sheet, before and after, per selector rather than positionally so the\nmixin''s reordering did not mask anything. Forty differences, of which three are\n`calc()` rewrites of the same arithmetic, two add `letter-spacing: normal` where\nthe initial value already applied, and ten are intended: Callout''s icon loses a\npixel with the body role, the modal title adopts h3''s weight and leading, `.yl-text`\nnow states its own weight instead of inheriting, and CodeBlock''s five.\n\nThat comparison also caught a regression I had introduced. `Heading` emits *either*\na level class or a size class, never both, so moving the shared axes onto the level\nmodifiers left `<Heading size=\"xs\">` with no weight and no leading. They are back\non the base.\n\nThe 134 DOM snapshots are unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"d745d0bccb6c955a862b2469912eba19d165420d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/d745d0bccb6c955a862b2469912eba19d165420d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2","verification":{"payload":"tree d745d0bccb6c955a862b2469912eba19d165420d\nparent fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790500551 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513913 -0600\n\nfeat(ds)!: every component reads tokens, and stylelint keeps it that way\n\n121 hardcoded values become 12. The twelve that remain are each deliberate: two\n`em` values that must scale with the text around them, the spinner''s documented\nfallback, four breakpoints a media query cannot read from a custom property, the\none-pixel clip-rect idiom, and a SASS default argument.\n\nThe target was never zero literals. A dialog''s max-width is not a design-system\ndecision, and pretending it is would put twenty measures in the token sheet that\nno other component will ever read. The rule this settles on is narrower and\nenforceable: a literal is a defect wherever a token exists, and a **named**\ncomponent property is the answer wherever one does not. So `--dialog-width-md`,\n`--switch-track-width`, `--tooltip-max-width` and a dozen others now say what they\nare, and can be overridden from a stylesheet without reaching into a class.\n\n**The type scale reaches CSS for the first time.** It was emitted by nothing for\nfour releases, so `Typography.scss` grew its own and the two drifted: headings\nrendered 3.2rem where the scale said 3.6rem, and `Text` rendered 1.5rem where it\nsaid 1.6rem. Reconciled toward the components, not the tokens, because those are\nthe sizes users have seen and because the alternative was making everything\nlarger in the same release that tightened the spacing. `h5` and `h6` were missing\nfrom the scale entirely and are now there. A `type()` mixin applies a whole role,\nwhich is what makes twelve roles usable from five-declaration blocks.\nTypography.scss drops from 26 literals to 4.\n\n**CodeBlock''s copy button changes with the theme now.** Its five `rgba()` literals\nwere palette values copied by hand, so the header and the button stayed put while\nthe surface under them flipped. Both washes derive from the ink foreground, and the\nhover is twice the resting state rather than the two-hundredths of alpha that\nderiving them from the border role first produced.\n\n**stylelint closes the milestone**, wired into `rushx lint`. A hex, an `rgba()`, a\nliteral font size, a literal font weight, a raw font stack or a `px` border width\nis an error. Proved by breaking a stylesheet four ways and watching it catch all\nfour. This is why it moved here from M2: the rule cannot pass until the values it\nrejects are gone, and landing it earlier would have meant shipping it as a warning\nand tightening it later.\n\nVerified by resolving every declaration in every compiled stylesheet against the\ntoken sheet, before and after, per selector rather than positionally so the\nmixin''s reordering did not mask anything. Forty differences, of which three are\n`calc()` rewrites of the same arithmetic, two add `letter-spacing: normal` where\nthe initial value already applied, and ten are intended: Callout''s icon loses a\npixel with the body role, the modal title adopts h3''s weight and leading, `.yl-text`\nnow states its own weight instead of inheriting, and CodeBlock''s five.\n\nThat comparison also caught a regression I had introduced. `Heading` emits *either*\na level class or a size class, never both, so moving the shared axes onto the level\nmodifiers left `<Heading size=\"xs\">` with no weight and no leading. They are back\non the base.\n\nThe 134 DOM snapshots are unchanged.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS+QAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9c+wAQDwJKhpbUOV/pBlr+IzECfGBRzNi5iXjQnjPwYgh6jemQEA6Sw6+XqxDmTe\n8cQQSeWpoTeDNhFzplLkMeylI5mI3g0=\n=7+BS\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGE5NmEzNTFkYjkxMWUzZGIyMWFiZGNmOWIxOWQ5YmEyN2E2ZDBiYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0","sha":"fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0"}],"sha":"a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/a96a351db911e3db21abdcf9b19d9ba27a6d0ba2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:57:05Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(ds): a README for every component, and a test that keeps it that way\n\nEighteen READMEs, one per component directory, each with what the component is for,\nits import including whether that is the main entry or `/client`, examples covering\nthe variants, a props table and the accessibility contract. They sit beside the\nsource rather than under `docs/`, because `docs/` is TypeDoc output and is rewritten\non every `rushx docs`.\n\nA test enforces it. It checks that a component directory has a README, that the\nREADME is titled after it, that it shows an import and balanced code fences, and that\nits examples name something the module actually exports. That last check is against\nthe export list rather than the directory name, because five of these are families:\nFeedback exports Spinner, Field exports Input, Modal exports Dialog. Requiring the\ndirectory name would have failed all five and taught the next person to rename a\nheading rather than write an example.\n\nThe test is deliberately shallow and says so in its own remarks. It cannot tell\nwhether a README is *true*. Four of the first thirteen were not: Card''s defaults are\n`elevation=\"xs\"` and `bordered={true}`, and I had written the opposite of both;\nEmptyState defaults to an `h3`; and Menu has no typeahead. Verifying the prose against\nthe source is still a reviewer''s job, and no assertion of this shape replaces it.\n\nWriting them surfaced four gaps in the components themselves, now documented where\nsomebody choosing a component will see them rather than after adopting one:\n\nTabs sets `role=\"tablist\"`, `role=\"tab\"`, `aria-selected` and `role=\"tabpanel\"` and\nimplements none of the rest of the pattern. No arrow-key navigation, no\n`aria-controls`, no `aria-labelledby` on the panel, no roving `tabIndex`, so every tab\nis its own tab stop. Everything is reachable and operable, which makes it a gap rather\nthan a defect, but it is not what an assistive technology user expects.\n\nMenu roves with ArrowUp, ArrowDown, Home and End, and has no typeahead. Table has no\nresponsive overflow container and no numeric alignment, both of which a consuming\nproject added locally. There is no accordion beside Tabs.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"abc4cb8fea3b5b2ebdfdd3a11ccc78b650a9fc28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/abc4cb8fea3b5b2ebdfdd3a11ccc78b650a9fc28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0","verification":{"payload":"tree abc4cb8fea3b5b2ebdfdd3a11ccc78b650a9fc28\nparent 405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790499425 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513890 -0600\n\ndocs(ds): a README for every component, and a test that keeps it that way\n\nEighteen READMEs, one per component directory, each with what the component is for,\nits import including whether that is the main entry or `/client`, examples covering\nthe variants, a props table and the accessibility contract. They sit beside the\nsource rather than under `docs/`, because `docs/` is TypeDoc output and is rewritten\non every `rushx docs`.\n\nA test enforces it. It checks that a component directory has a README, that the\nREADME is titled after it, that it shows an import and balanced code fences, and that\nits examples name something the module actually exports. That last check is against\nthe export list rather than the directory name, because five of these are families:\nFeedback exports Spinner, Field exports Input, Modal exports Dialog. Requiring the\ndirectory name would have failed all five and taught the next person to rename a\nheading rather than write an example.\n\nThe test is deliberately shallow and says so in its own remarks. It cannot tell\nwhether a README is *true*. Four of the first thirteen were not: Card''s defaults are\n`elevation=\"xs\"` and `bordered={true}`, and I had written the opposite of both;\nEmptyState defaults to an `h3`; and Menu has no typeahead. Verifying the prose against\nthe source is still a reviewer''s job, and no assertion of this shape replaces it.\n\nWriting them surfaced four gaps in the components themselves, now documented where\nsomebody choosing a component will see them rather than after adopting one:\n\nTabs sets `role=\"tablist\"`, `role=\"tab\"`, `aria-selected` and `role=\"tabpanel\"` and\nimplements none of the rest of the pattern. No arrow-key navigation, no\n`aria-controls`, no `aria-labelledby` on the panel, no roving `tabIndex`, so every tab\nis its own tab stop. Everything is reachable and operable, which makes it a gap rather\nthan a defect, but it is not what an assistive technology user expects.\n\nMenu roves with ArrowUp, ArrowDown, Home and End, and has no typeahead. Table has no\nresponsive overflow container and no numeric alignment, both of which a consuming\nproject added locally. There is no accordion beside Tabs.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS4gAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ZsvAP0QSmTjwlZakGWUDpkEoTuW8qDQr3lOy8F+pH2ehNj+hAD7B/CvGTM72HRM\nJDwvAsyvOAG0X7VCmb7XUMFbw+0pdwE=\n=K1GF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGZiMWExMzllNjA0ZjU3NWJhMDFhODc4OWE1ZGJlNWE5NDY0Zjc2YzA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3","sha":"405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3"}],"sha":"fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/fb1a139e604f575ba01a8789a5dbe5a9464f76c0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:51:03Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"refactor(ds): a directory per component\n\nEach component now owns a directory holding its source and its stylesheet, so\n`src/primitives/Button/` has `Button.tsx` and `Button.scss` and has somewhere to\nput the README that follows. Eighteen of them, plus the support modules that are\nnot components and stay where they are: the overlay hooks, the placement maths and\nthe anchored-position hook.\n\nThe published import paths are unchanged, which was the constraint that made the\nmove safe to do at all. `build-styles.mjs` derives an output name from the\nstylesheet''s basename, so `Button/Button.scss` still emits `button.css`; naming it\n`index.scss` would have emitted `index.css` and broken every documented import.\nVerified by diffing the contents of `dist/styles/` before and after.\n\nBoth scanners become recursive, and the test helper now sorts the way the build\nscript already did, by basename across both tiers. That difference had been\ninvisible while the directories were flat and became visible the moment they were\nnot, which is why the hardcoded sheet list in the snapshot suite needed reordering.\n\nThe evidence that this is only a move: 421 tests pass with **no snapshot written**.\nAll twenty compiled stylesheets and all one hundred and thirty-four DOM snapshots\nmatched what was recorded before the files changed place, and six of the built\nsheets were diffed against their snapshots afterwards for good measure.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"76f535237764fd17f4035ff59f95b29f67a07719","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/76f535237764fd17f4035ff59f95b29f67a07719"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3","verification":{"payload":"tree 76f535237764fd17f4035ff59f95b29f67a07719\nparent 3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790499063 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513890 -0600\n\nrefactor(ds): a directory per component\n\nEach component now owns a directory holding its source and its stylesheet, so\n`src/primitives/Button/` has `Button.tsx` and `Button.scss` and has somewhere to\nput the README that follows. Eighteen of them, plus the support modules that are\nnot components and stay where they are: the overlay hooks, the placement maths and\nthe anchored-position hook.\n\nThe published import paths are unchanged, which was the constraint that made the\nmove safe to do at all. `build-styles.mjs` derives an output name from the\nstylesheet''s basename, so `Button/Button.scss` still emits `button.css`; naming it\n`index.scss` would have emitted `index.css` and broken every documented import.\nVerified by diffing the contents of `dist/styles/` before and after.\n\nBoth scanners become recursive, and the test helper now sorts the way the build\nscript already did, by basename across both tiers. That difference had been\ninvisible while the directories were flat and became visible the moment they were\nnot, which is why the hardcoded sheet list in the snapshot suite needed reordering.\n\nThe evidence that this is only a move: 421 tests pass with **no snapshot written**.\nAll twenty compiled stylesheets and all one hundred and thirty-four DOM snapshots\nmatched what was recorded before the files changed place, and six of the built\nsheets were diffed against their snapshots afterwards for good measure.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS4gAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9Rw2AP9jl/j5TXARAeHIf+Ltj6tY+ZCymKPsvR7ry46AHPhz+QD/f+1buUBj2yiv\nLF89Uu5z0XM+O55MlVp11gduLM9AEAg=\n=aVHz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDQwNTgwMjQ4NmEyOTgzNDMzZWRiZGQ1ODY2NDM1ZmFhNjZiZTgwZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2","sha":"3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2"}],"sha":"405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/405802486a2983433edbdd5866435faa66be80d3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:46:16Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"refactor(ds): one shared entry for the stylesheets, and mixins for what was copied\n\nSix of fifteen component sheets imported the mixins partial. The other nine\nreimplemented whatever they needed, which is how the same media query came to be\nwritten three times and the same elevated-surface treatment twice, with the same\nexplanatory comment in both copies.\n\nThere is now one entry partial. A component writes `@use \"../styles\" as *` and\nstops needing to know which file a shared fragment lives in. Five mixins cover\nwhat was being copied. The reduced-motion media query, where the condition is\nshared and what it suppresses is not, so that part stays with the component. Two\ndisabled treatments, because a field recolours its text while a switch is painted\nby the user agent from `accent-color` and can only fade. The house transition,\nwritten out at five sites with both tokens repeated per property. And the surface\ntreatment the modal and anchored tiers had a placeholder each for, where position\nand border legitimately differ and the background, foreground, shadow and focus\nreset did not.\n\n`form.css` is self-sufficient now. `.yl-field` was defined in Field.scss while its\n`__required`, `__hint` and `__error` children were defined in Form.scss, so a\nconsumer importing `form.css` for `FormField` also needed `field.css` for the\nwrapper''s layout, and nothing said so. The block moves to the file whose component\nrenders the class. Field.scss is left styling only the controls.\n\nOne deliberate behaviour change. A disabled checkbox changed its cursor and\nnothing else, so it looked enabled to anyone not hovering it, while the switch and\nthe slider beside it faded. It fades too now.\n\nThe snapshots are the evidence this is a refactor. Button, Feedback and CodeBlock\nare byte-identical, so the transition and reduced-motion mixins emit exactly what\nthey replaced. Modal and Popover changed declaration order only, verified by\ncomparing their sorted declaration sets. Field and Form together differ by one\nline, the checkbox''s new opacity. Nothing else in the compiled CSS moved.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"d850ba01553937394992a2e8bec0510d3e71b33d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/d850ba01553937394992a2e8bec0510d3e71b33d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2","verification":{"payload":"tree d850ba01553937394992a2e8bec0510d3e71b33d\nparent 134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790498776 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513890 -0600\n\nrefactor(ds): one shared entry for the stylesheets, and mixins for what was copied\n\nSix of fifteen component sheets imported the mixins partial. The other nine\nreimplemented whatever they needed, which is how the same media query came to be\nwritten three times and the same elevated-surface treatment twice, with the same\nexplanatory comment in both copies.\n\nThere is now one entry partial. A component writes `@use \"../styles\" as *` and\nstops needing to know which file a shared fragment lives in. Five mixins cover\nwhat was being copied. The reduced-motion media query, where the condition is\nshared and what it suppresses is not, so that part stays with the component. Two\ndisabled treatments, because a field recolours its text while a switch is painted\nby the user agent from `accent-color` and can only fade. The house transition,\nwritten out at five sites with both tokens repeated per property. And the surface\ntreatment the modal and anchored tiers had a placeholder each for, where position\nand border legitimately differ and the background, foreground, shadow and focus\nreset did not.\n\n`form.css` is self-sufficient now. `.yl-field` was defined in Field.scss while its\n`__required`, `__hint` and `__error` children were defined in Form.scss, so a\nconsumer importing `form.css` for `FormField` also needed `field.css` for the\nwrapper''s layout, and nothing said so. The block moves to the file whose component\nrenders the class. Field.scss is left styling only the controls.\n\nOne deliberate behaviour change. A disabled checkbox changed its cursor and\nnothing else, so it looked enabled to anyone not hovering it, while the switch and\nthe slider beside it faded. It fades too now.\n\nThe snapshots are the evidence this is a refactor. Button, Feedback and CodeBlock\nare byte-identical, so the transition and reduced-motion mixins emit exactly what\nthey replaced. Modal and Popover changed declaration order only, verified by\ncomparing their sorted declaration sets. Field and Form together differ by one\nline, the checkbox''s new opacity. Nothing else in the compiled CSS moved.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS4gAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9XZMAP9ZVOrQlfvY4AFk+eGxL9CA2uOG9fgDAHAmN1yF7Em9fAEAwqB3/otHbusV\nvGHQS/DO/tL40dAUl8Bpy+fu5qpmwgs=\n=Iwbz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDNmOWIxMDI1NmNmYTkyMzZkMzdiYjYwNDFkNzE1MTdiYTEzMmY4ZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd","sha":"134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd"}],"sha":"3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3f9b10256cfa9236d37bb6041d71517ba132f8e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:36:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:09Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(ds)!: tighter density, a visible switch, and dark surfaces built from the brand\n\nThree things, all reported from looking at the rendered result rather than at the\ncode, which is the half the test suite could not reach.\n\n**Density comes down one step.** A primary button was 44px tall against 15px\ntext, which is generous for anything but a touch target. It is 36px now, and card\npadding, modal padding, popover padding, table cells, the empty state and the\ndefault Stack, Inline and Grid gaps all come down one step on the same 4px grid.\nThe scale itself is untouched, deliberately: --yl-space-4 is still 16px, because\nconsumers build layouts against those numbers and moving them would change every\napplication silently. What changed is which step each component chooses.\n\n**A switch knob nobody could see.** It was fg.inverse on border.strong, so in the\nlight theme a white dot sat on a pale grey groove at 1.48 to 1. A knob''s position\nis the state, so WCAG 1.4.11 asks for 3 to 1, and using a *text* token as a knob\nbackground was the error underneath the symptom.\n\nFixed with a role rather than a one-off value, because a slider and the progress\nbar that is planned want the same surface. interactive.track is the unfilled part\nof a control, dark enough in the light theme that a pale knob reads against it and\nlight enough in the dark theme that a dark one does. The knob becomes bg.panel, a\nbackground token for a background. All four combinations now clear 3 to 1, the\nworst being 4.76.\n\nWorth recording how this was found, because the contrast suite added yesterday\nmissed it. That suite checks *token pairings* and says so in its own remarks; this\nwas a component pairing two rules apart, and a background against a background\nrather than text against a background. A prototype audit that resolves every\ndeclared colour against its effective backdrop, walking BEM ancestry and\ncompositing translucent layers, found it once the audit''s own bugs were fixed. It\nalso produced a dozen false positives before that, from compositing over white\nregardless of theme and from pairing a resting colour with a hover background, so\nit is recorded for M3 rather than committed half-right. The switch pairings are\nasserted explicitly in the meantime.\n\n**The dark theme is the brand now.** Its five surfaces were hand-picked hexes, the\none part of the theme file the palette could not explain, and the exception I had\nto write into the module docs. They are mixed from carbon and the deepest brand\nblue instead: the panel is carbon with 16% blue, and the rest step from there\ntoward black or toward neutral[800]. A dark interface reads as blue-black rather\nthan neutral grey, which is what makes it look like Yoltra, and a brand change\nmoves the theme instead of leaving it behind. The light theme keeps the brand in\nits accents, where it belongs on a white page, and its canvas is now a tint of\nprimary[50] rather than a fourth literal.\n\nAll 75 contrast assertions pass against the derived surfaces, which is the point\nof having built them first.\n\nThe 134 DOM snapshots are unchanged again. 12 CSS snapshots carry the diff.\n\nA typical import grows 2.7 KB to 2.8 KB. That a component-only import moved at\nall on a change to the theme objects is the clearest evidence yet that they are\nnot being tree-shaken, so the note from the previous commit is now a finding\nrather than a suspicion.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"e9b0dd17b126cd6a57f1fbd651e76d64200c99af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/e9b0dd17b126cd6a57f1fbd651e76d64200c99af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd","verification":{"payload":"tree e9b0dd17b126cd6a57f1fbd651e76d64200c99af\nparent 2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790498188 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513889 -0600\n\nfeat(ds)!: tighter density, a visible switch, and dark surfaces built from the brand\n\nThree things, all reported from looking at the rendered result rather than at the\ncode, which is the half the test suite could not reach.\n\n**Density comes down one step.** A primary button was 44px tall against 15px\ntext, which is generous for anything but a touch target. It is 36px now, and card\npadding, modal padding, popover padding, table cells, the empty state and the\ndefault Stack, Inline and Grid gaps all come down one step on the same 4px grid.\nThe scale itself is untouched, deliberately: --yl-space-4 is still 16px, because\nconsumers build layouts against those numbers and moving them would change every\napplication silently. What changed is which step each component chooses.\n\n**A switch knob nobody could see.** It was fg.inverse on border.strong, so in the\nlight theme a white dot sat on a pale grey groove at 1.48 to 1. A knob''s position\nis the state, so WCAG 1.4.11 asks for 3 to 1, and using a *text* token as a knob\nbackground was the error underneath the symptom.\n\nFixed with a role rather than a one-off value, because a slider and the progress\nbar that is planned want the same surface. interactive.track is the unfilled part\nof a control, dark enough in the light theme that a pale knob reads against it and\nlight enough in the dark theme that a dark one does. The knob becomes bg.panel, a\nbackground token for a background. All four combinations now clear 3 to 1, the\nworst being 4.76.\n\nWorth recording how this was found, because the contrast suite added yesterday\nmissed it. That suite checks *token pairings* and says so in its own remarks; this\nwas a component pairing two rules apart, and a background against a background\nrather than text against a background. A prototype audit that resolves every\ndeclared colour against its effective backdrop, walking BEM ancestry and\ncompositing translucent layers, found it once the audit''s own bugs were fixed. It\nalso produced a dozen false positives before that, from compositing over white\nregardless of theme and from pairing a resting colour with a hover background, so\nit is recorded for M3 rather than committed half-right. The switch pairings are\nasserted explicitly in the meantime.\n\n**The dark theme is the brand now.** Its five surfaces were hand-picked hexes, the\none part of the theme file the palette could not explain, and the exception I had\nto write into the module docs. They are mixed from carbon and the deepest brand\nblue instead: the panel is carbon with 16% blue, and the rest step from there\ntoward black or toward neutral[800]. A dark interface reads as blue-black rather\nthan neutral grey, which is what makes it look like Yoltra, and a brand change\nmoves the theme instead of leaving it behind. The light theme keeps the brand in\nits accents, where it belongs on a white page, and its canvas is now a tint of\nprimary[50] rather than a fourth literal.\n\nAll 75 contrast assertions pass against the derived surfaces, which is the point\nof having built them first.\n\nThe 134 DOM snapshots are unchanged again. 12 CSS snapshots carry the diff.\n\nA typical import grows 2.7 KB to 2.8 KB. That a component-only import moved at\nall on a change to the theme objects is the clearest evidence yet that they are\nnot being tree-shaken, so the note from the previous commit is now a finding\nrather than a suspicion.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS4QAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9YI4AP9kZbBhBfKj8vrO3NzSt6Qm//2gvcsJusqetxTWk3LjGQD9Hw4V6s4SK7hg\n76q8eC8B4FQAawMuK3OS9hoqyMQ8zwY=\n=U4tV\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDEzNGYwYmI0ZjcyYWM5NDlmM2YxYjEwZjM1ZDY1OTYxODIwMTg1ZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56","sha":"2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56"}],"sha":"134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/134f0bb4f72ac949f3f1b10f35d65961820185dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T08:12:03Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:09Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(ds)!: token tiers, an exhaustive emitter, and contrast that is asserted\n\nThe token layer had the right shape and the wrong guarantees. Three things were\ntrue at once: the emitter named every property it emitted, the dark theme\nrestated palette steps as literals, and nothing had ever computed a contrast\nratio. Each hid a defect the other two made hard to see.\n\n**The emitter is exhaustive.** It listed twenty-seven properties by hand, so a\ntoken could be added to the TypeScript and never reach CSS. Five had:\ninteractive.primary.border, all of interactive.ghost.*, motion.duration.slow,\ntwo of the three easings, and the entire twelve-style type scale. Nothing failed,\nbecause nothing compared the two, and Typography.scss hardcoded twenty-five\nvalues that had tokens all along. Now every leaf is walked and a namespace\ndeclares only its prefix, its formatting and any leaf renames. 86 properties\nbecame 160, most of that the type scale, emitted one axis at a time so a caller\ncan take a size without inheriting a weight.\n\nThe converse is now a test. It counts leaves rather than re-deriving names,\nbecause a test that repeats the emitter''s own kebab-casing cannot disagree with\nit.\n\n**No component name survives in the global namespace.** btn became interactive,\nghost became interactive-quiet, and code became the ink surface. Naming a global\ntoken after one component makes that component''s internals public API, which is\nhow Modal and Popover ended up borrowing a button''s ghost colours.\n\n**The contrast failure is fixed with a step that already existed.** Brand text\nand button fills move from primary[500] to primary[600]. White on [500] measures\n4.06 to 1, so every primary button label in the system failed AA, and both\nconsumers who reported the badge case missed that. On [600] it is 5.38 to 1. No\ncolour was invented. brand.primary stays #1A7FE2 for identity, where 4.06:1 is enough, and\nfg.brand exists for everything smaller. The dark theme''s button inverts instead:\na dark fill on a dark canvas is 3.48:1 against its own background and reads as\ndisabled, where a bright fill with an ink label is 6.74:1 both ways.\n\ntests/contrast.test.ts computes sixty-nine pairings across both themes,\ncompositing the translucent ones over what sits behind them, because measuring\nrgba as if it were opaque reports a ratio no reader sees. It found two defects in\ntokens added in this same change. Status solid accents at palette[500] measure\n2.55 to 1 for success and 2.29 to 1 for warning, below the 3 to 1 an indicator\nneeds, so light uses [600]. Disabled text is asserted to stay *below* the threshold, since\nWCAG 1.4.3 exempts it and darkening it would make disabled copy look enabled.\n\n**The dark theme derives from the palette.** An alpha() helper replaces a dozen\nrgba literals that were palette steps said in a way nobody could grep for.\n\nThis also brings in the tokens consumers had to invent because they did not\nexist. Content\nmeasures, a weight ramp, tabular figures, and a solid accent per status, all of\nwhich were found hardcoded or aliased in projects that consume this package.\n\nRenames are mechanical except one. --yl-color-brand maps to brand-primary, which\nis right for decoration and wrong for text, so the codemod prints every site it\ntouched and what to use instead. Ten sites here needed that judgement: four were\ntext and took fg-brand or fg-link, three were control fills and took\ninteractive-bg, one was a focus ring that had been borrowing the brand colour\nbecause no role said focus, and one is a spinner that is genuinely decorative.\n\nThe 134 DOM snapshots are unchanged, which is the useful part: this moves no\nmarkup. The 20 CSS snapshots carry the whole diff.\n\nA typical import grows 2.3 KB to 2.7 KB against a 4 KB budget. One thing to check\nlater, because alpha() may have made the theme objects opaque to tree-shaking: if\nso, a consumer importing one component now ships the whole palette.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"51b1e0b00585f7ab906111cc8339884cf0361660","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/51b1e0b00585f7ab906111cc8339884cf0361660"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56","verification":{"payload":"tree 51b1e0b00585f7ab906111cc8339884cf0361660\nparent 9c0510771c37104d69f88e787e5c19d311d04c24\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790496723 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513889 -0600\n\nfeat(ds)!: token tiers, an exhaustive emitter, and contrast that is asserted\n\nThe token layer had the right shape and the wrong guarantees. Three things were\ntrue at once: the emitter named every property it emitted, the dark theme\nrestated palette steps as literals, and nothing had ever computed a contrast\nratio. Each hid a defect the other two made hard to see.\n\n**The emitter is exhaustive.** It listed twenty-seven properties by hand, so a\ntoken could be added to the TypeScript and never reach CSS. Five had:\ninteractive.primary.border, all of interactive.ghost.*, motion.duration.slow,\ntwo of the three easings, and the entire twelve-style type scale. Nothing failed,\nbecause nothing compared the two, and Typography.scss hardcoded twenty-five\nvalues that had tokens all along. Now every leaf is walked and a namespace\ndeclares only its prefix, its formatting and any leaf renames. 86 properties\nbecame 160, most of that the type scale, emitted one axis at a time so a caller\ncan take a size without inheriting a weight.\n\nThe converse is now a test. It counts leaves rather than re-deriving names,\nbecause a test that repeats the emitter''s own kebab-casing cannot disagree with\nit.\n\n**No component name survives in the global namespace.** btn became interactive,\nghost became interactive-quiet, and code became the ink surface. Naming a global\ntoken after one component makes that component''s internals public API, which is\nhow Modal and Popover ended up borrowing a button''s ghost colours.\n\n**The contrast failure is fixed with a step that already existed.** Brand text\nand button fills move from primary[500] to primary[600]. White on [500] measures\n4.06 to 1, so every primary button label in the system failed AA, and both\nconsumers who reported the badge case missed that. On [600] it is 5.38 to 1. No\ncolour was invented. brand.primary stays #1A7FE2 for identity, where 4.06:1 is enough, and\nfg.brand exists for everything smaller. The dark theme''s button inverts instead:\na dark fill on a dark canvas is 3.48:1 against its own background and reads as\ndisabled, where a bright fill with an ink label is 6.74:1 both ways.\n\ntests/contrast.test.ts computes sixty-nine pairings across both themes,\ncompositing the translucent ones over what sits behind them, because measuring\nrgba as if it were opaque reports a ratio no reader sees. It found two defects in\ntokens added in this same change. Status solid accents at palette[500] measure\n2.55 to 1 for success and 2.29 to 1 for warning, below the 3 to 1 an indicator\nneeds, so light uses [600]. Disabled text is asserted to stay *below* the threshold, since\nWCAG 1.4.3 exempts it and darkening it would make disabled copy look enabled.\n\n**The dark theme derives from the palette.** An alpha() helper replaces a dozen\nrgba literals that were palette steps said in a way nobody could grep for.\n\nThis also brings in the tokens consumers had to invent because they did not\nexist. Content\nmeasures, a weight ramp, tabular figures, and a solid accent per status, all of\nwhich were found hardcoded or aliased in projects that consume this package.\n\nRenames are mechanical except one. --yl-color-brand maps to brand-primary, which\nis right for decoration and wrong for text, so the codemod prints every site it\ntouched and what to use instead. Ten sites here needed that judgement: four were\ntext and took fg-brand or fg-link, three were control fills and took\ninteractive-bg, one was a focus ring that had been borrowing the brand colour\nbecause no role said focus, and one is a spinner that is genuinely decorative.\n\nThe 134 DOM snapshots are unchanged, which is the useful part: this moves no\nmarkup. The 20 CSS snapshots carry the whole diff.\n\nA typical import grows 2.3 KB to 2.7 KB against a 4 KB budget. One thing to check\nlater, because alpha() may have made the theme objects opaque to tree-shaking: if\nso, a consumer importing one component now ships the whole palette.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS4QAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ePTAQDeDKp3MxZqkkguNzOs+qys9l/SwaUAa51CJhUS/vNUqAD+MZsVxh2ZtNyW\nChgh+dNMJ+gx+nIR8MtgIjss5Z2mUwk=\n=oeHp\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDJkMzkzOTBjNjJkNWI1OGJhYjg5NTM0NDI4ZjcxOTMxNGZiYmNhNTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/9c0510771c37104d69f88e787e5c19d311d04c24","sha":"9c0510771c37104d69f88e787e5c19d311d04c24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/9c0510771c37104d69f88e787e5c19d311d04c24"}],"sha":"2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2d39390c62d5b58bab89534428f719314fbbca56"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/9c0510771c37104d69f88e787e5c19d311d04c24/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T05:46:42Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T12:58:09Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"test(ds): snapshot the compiled CSS and the rendered DOM\n\nThe behavioural suites ask whether a role is right or a class is present, which\nis the correct question and a narrow one. It passes just as happily when a\nwrapper element appears, an aria-describedby stops being emitted, or a modifier\nclass is renamed. And jsdom applies no stylesheet, so nothing in the package\ncould see a styling change at all.\n\nTwo suites, because neither half is sufficient and the gap between them is where\nthis package''s styling bugs have actually lived. The CSS snapshots are written as\nreal .css files rather than into a .snap: a stylesheet escaped onto one line is\nnot reviewable, and review is the whole point. Their names match dist/styles/,\nand each one is byte-identical to the artefact published under that name, which\nis why the compile here trims exactly as build-styles.mjs does. A snapshot is the\npublished file, not something resembling it.\n\nThe DOM half covers 108 variants across the server-safe surface and 26 across the\nclient and overlay tier. Overlays are recorded through the data-yl-portal marker\nrather than document.body, so the testing library''s own container is not captured\nbeside the subject and cannot churn the snapshots when the harness changes.\n\nOn strictness, vitest resolves updateSnapshot to \"none\" only when CI is set, so a\nmissing snapshot fails there and is written locally, which is the split we want.\nNothing needed configuring, since snapshotOptions is not settable from\ndefineConfig. What that leaves uncovered is deletion, so the sheet list is\nhardcoded rather than discovered: adding or removing a stylesheet is a deliberate\nedit to the test, not a silently self-satisfying count.\n\nThe sass compile moves into tests/support so the two suites share one memoized\nrun instead of doubling the slowest part of the package''s tests.\n\nCoverage rises to 99.26/96.28/98.91/99.26 against gates of 97/97/95/96, and\nThemeProvider goes from 19.35% of statements and none of its functions to\n77.41/66.66/66.66 purely by being rendered. It was the one real hole here.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"14c7ec3d1d2d0b07cb361baf3401ca9b9f194e7e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/14c7ec3d1d2d0b07cb361baf3401ca9b9f194e7e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/9c0510771c37104d69f88e787e5c19d311d04c24","verification":{"payload":"tree 14c7ec3d1d2d0b07cb361baf3401ca9b9f194e7e\nparent 6b65bc82db1a0fec6433d2bc23d733bbc79b97f4\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790488002 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790513889 -0600\n\ntest(ds): snapshot the compiled CSS and the rendered DOM\n\nThe behavioural suites ask whether a role is right or a class is present, which\nis the correct question and a narrow one. It passes just as happily when a\nwrapper element appears, an aria-describedby stops being emitted, or a modifier\nclass is renamed. And jsdom applies no stylesheet, so nothing in the package\ncould see a styling change at all.\n\nTwo suites, because neither half is sufficient and the gap between them is where\nthis package''s styling bugs have actually lived. The CSS snapshots are written as\nreal .css files rather than into a .snap: a stylesheet escaped onto one line is\nnot reviewable, and review is the whole point. Their names match dist/styles/,\nand each one is byte-identical to the artefact published under that name, which\nis why the compile here trims exactly as build-styles.mjs does. A snapshot is the\npublished file, not something resembling it.\n\nThe DOM half covers 108 variants across the server-safe surface and 26 across the\nclient and overlay tier. Overlays are recorded through the data-yl-portal marker\nrather than document.body, so the testing library''s own container is not captured\nbeside the subject and cannot churn the snapshots when the harness changes.\n\nOn strictness, vitest resolves updateSnapshot to \"none\" only when CI is set, so a\nmissing snapshot fails there and is written locally, which is the split we want.\nNothing needed configuring, since snapshotOptions is not settable from\ndefineConfig. What that leaves uncovered is deletion, so the sheet list is\nhardcoded rather than discovered: adding or removing a stylesheet is a deliberate\nedit to the test, not a silently self-satisfying count.\n\nThe sass compile moves into tests/support so the two suites share one memoized\nrun instead of doubling the slowest part of the package''s tests.\n\nCoverage rises to 99.26/96.28/98.91/99.26 against gates of 97/97/95/96, and\nThemeProvider goes from 19.35% of statements and none of its functions to\n77.41/66.66/66.66 purely by being rendered. It was the one real hole here.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarkS4QAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9VMsAQCG9QogrDyhgsLqLSgLmJpUia+/p5jjyNhZG3+cPuejugD/dYx8u7zsphK3\nplqC+7u8lA0GfFNGO8m+9mE99OG+/Ak=\n=yQeB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T05:51:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","grav