id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/248d5c5163fa103ceee3a584c090480cf57a62f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:11:37Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:11:37Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(devtools): publish the licence with the code\n\nSeven devtools packages shipped MIT-licensed code with no licence text. Their\n`files` field listed only `dist` (and `bin`), and npm does not force-include a\nlicence the way it force-includes a README, so nothing carried it. Confirmed\nagainst the published artefact rather than inferred: the tarball for\ndevtools-protocol 0.7.0 contains package.json, README.md and README.es.md, and\nno LICENSE.\n\nThe other five published packages already solve this, so this is the same\npattern rather than a new one: `LICENSE` joins `files`, and a `prepublishOnly`\nhook copies the root licence into the package directory at publish time. The\ncopied file is deliberately not committed, which is why none of the five carry\none in the tree either.\n\nVerified in two halves, because `npm pack` does not run `prepublishOnly` and so\ncannot prove this on its own. The copy script resolves correctly from the\ndevtools directory depth, and once the file exists the tarball carries\n`package/LICENSE`. That the hook itself fires on a real publish is already\nevidenced by core 0.7.0, whose published tarball contains the licence it never\ncommits.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"b9e17d509096d36d445c0a93cd16a17fde975c72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/b9e17d509096d36d445c0a93cd16a17fde975c72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/248d5c5163fa103ceee3a584c090480cf57a62f7","verification":{"payload":"tree b9e17d509096d36d445c0a93cd16a17fde975c72\nparent 4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790493097 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790493097 -0600\n\nfix(devtools): publish the licence with the code\n\nSeven devtools packages shipped MIT-licensed code with no licence text. Their\n`files` field listed only `dist` (and `bin`), and npm does not force-include a\nlicence the way it force-includes a README, so nothing carried it. Confirmed\nagainst the published artefact rather than inferred: the tarball for\ndevtools-protocol 0.7.0 contains package.json, README.md and README.es.md, and\nno LICENSE.\n\nThe other five published packages already solve this, so this is the same\npattern rather than a new one: `LICENSE` joins `files`, and a `prepublishOnly`\nhook copies the root licence into the package directory at publish time. The\ncopied file is deliberately not committed, which is why none of the five carry\none in the tree either.\n\nVerified in two halves, because `npm pack` does not run `prepublishOnly` and so\ncannot prove this on its own. The copy script resolves correctly from the\ndevtools directory depth, and once the file exists the tarball carries\n`package/LICENSE`. That the hook itself fires on a real publish is already\nevidenced by core 0.7.0, whose published tarball contains the licence it never\ncommits.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarjBqQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9TUCAQCmvQ2pyGsdIvCair13/tzlX9o//ruumb8YpNvuafhurQEA8AyjyuDTOTID\n0iiQbw2GOWLUPJr6nkiGCUH7DJ6kHgk=\n=saPX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T07:21:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/248d5c5163fa103ceee3a584c090480cf57a62f7","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDI0OGQ1YzUxNjNmYTEwM2NlZWUzYTU4NGMwOTA0ODBjZjU3YTYyZjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3","sha":"4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3"}],"sha":"248d5c5163fa103ceee3a584c090480cf57a62f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/248d5c5163fa103ceee3a584c090480cf57a62f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:04:41Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T07:04:41Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs: badges on every published package, and links that survive npm\n\nTwelve packages are published and only three carried badges, so nine package\npages said nothing about their own version, licence or typings. The set is now\nuniform: version, monthly downloads, types and licence, on both language\nREADMEs, plus a CI badge on the repository root where it belongs rather than\nrepeated twelve times.\n\nEvery URL was checked against the live service before being committed, because\na badge fails in a way that looks like success: shields answers 200 and renders\nthe word \"invalid\" or \"not found\" inside the SVG, so status codes prove nothing.\nFour candidates were rejected on that evidence. npm/dt redirects (301) and is\ndeprecated. bundlephobia renders \"rate limited by upstream service\".\ngithub/license renders \"license not identifiable by github\", where npm/l reads\nMIT correctly. npm/node/v renders \"404 badge not found\" because the path is\nnode/v, not under npm. All 47 distinct URLs now in the tree render real values.\n\nSize badges are deliberately absent. `rushx size --check-readme` already\npublishes a generated, gated figure, and bundlejs reports core at 11.4 kB where\nthat table says 11.5 KB ships. A second unverified number that can contradict\nthe reviewed one is worse than no number, and bundlejs already times out on ds.\n\nbadgen is dropped rather than kept alongside shields. Two providers meant two\nvisual styles and two independent outage risks, and badgen carried the\nper-package badges while the root used shields.\n\nThe link half is the same problem seen from npm. Every relative link that leaves\na package directory, 78 of them across 20 files, resolves on GitHub and breaks\non npm, because without repository.directory npm treats the package root as the\nrepository root and ../../README.md escapes above it. Setting directory on all\ntwelve packages fixes the 68 that point at files, including the Versión en\nEspañol toggle on every page.\n\nThe remaining 10 pointed at directories, and those cannot be fixed that way:\nnpm rewrites relative links as blob URLs, and blob on a directory is a 404. They\nbecome absolute tree URLs instead.\n\nNo link in any published README is broken on GitHub, before or after.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"905044131eaac96fe190ce3e2f6e0cb4682ce88e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/905044131eaac96fe190ce3e2f6e0cb4682ce88e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 905044131eaac96fe190ce3e2f6e0cb4682ce88e\nparent 367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790492681 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790492681 -0600\n\ndocs: badges on every published package, and links that survive npm\n\nTwelve packages are published and only three carried badges, so nine package\npages said nothing about their own version, licence or typings. The set is now\nuniform: version, monthly downloads, types and licence, on both language\nREADMEs, plus a CI badge on the repository root where it belongs rather than\nrepeated twelve times.\n\nEvery URL was checked against the live service before being committed, because\na badge fails in a way that looks like success: shields answers 200 and renders\nthe word \"invalid\" or \"not found\" inside the SVG, so status codes prove nothing.\nFour candidates were rejected on that evidence. npm/dt redirects (301) and is\ndeprecated. bundlephobia renders \"rate limited by upstream service\".\ngithub/license renders \"license not identifiable by github\", where npm/l reads\nMIT correctly. npm/node/v renders \"404 badge not found\" because the path is\nnode/v, not under npm. All 47 distinct URLs now in the tree render real values.\n\nSize badges are deliberately absent. `rushx size --check-readme` already\npublishes a generated, gated figure, and bundlejs reports core at 11.4 kB where\nthat table says 11.5 KB ships. A second unverified number that can contradict\nthe reviewed one is worse than no number, and bundlejs already times out on ds.\n\nbadgen is dropped rather than kept alongside shields. Two providers meant two\nvisual styles and two independent outage risks, and badgen carried the\nper-package badges while the root used shields.\n\nThe link half is the same problem seen from npm. Every relative link that leaves\na package directory, 78 of them across 20 files, resolves on GitHub and breaks\non npm, because without repository.directory npm treats the package root as the\nrepository root and ../../README.md escapes above it. Setting directory on all\ntwelve packages fixes the 68 that point at files, including the Versión en\nEspañol toggle on every page.\n\nThe remaining 10 pointed at directories, and those cannot be fixed that way:\nnpm rewrites relative links as blob URLs, and blob on a directory is a 404. They\nbecome absolute tree URLs instead.\n\nNo link in any published README is broken on GitHub, before or after.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarjACgAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9XyfAP9r5AsIGQWKJ98Ac4E+vwZXQKcQnB4boVyALOMynWGVUAEAkPWkznq7SAFy\nnvpyg7EFLeBQJ11rltIgDTemzyxhDg8=\n=Kayf\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T07:21:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDRlYjNiM2E0NmQyY2VkOGJhYmRlMGU4YjQwODhkNDcwNjZhNzQzZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126","sha":"367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126"}],"sha":"4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/4eb3b3a46d2ced8babde0e8b4088d47066a743e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T05:52:26Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T05:52:26Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(core): onEvent gets its documentation back, and the registration seam its own\n\nrush docs exits 1 on a warning, and TypeDoc was emitting four: the signature\nStore.onRegistrationChange carried @param tags for channel, type, handler and\nphase, none of which it takes. That failed the \"Verify docs are current\" job\nbefore the diff it exists to check ever ran.\n\nThe cause is placement, not wording. onRegistrationChange was inserted between\nonEvent''s doc comment and onEvent itself, so the comment bound to the new method\nand onEvent, sixty lines further down, was left with none at all. The published\nreference has been describing the wrong method under the wrong name and omitting\none of the store''s oldest hooks.\n\nonEvent''s comment moves back to onEvent, unchanged. onRegistrationChange gets a\ncomment of its own, in the shape the other public methods here use: a summary,\nthe batching rule and the queueing rule, its two parameters, and an example.\nThe long-form rationale stays on the interface in types.ts, which is where a\nreader following the type lands.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"c9003036d7f3a0ab94de012335eef86837958889","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/c9003036d7f3a0ab94de012335eef86837958889"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126","verification":{"payload":"tree c9003036d7f3a0ab94de012335eef86837958889\nparent aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790488346 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790488346 -0600\n\ndocs(core): onEvent gets its documentation back, and the registration seam its own\n\nrush docs exits 1 on a warning, and TypeDoc was emitting four: the signature\nStore.onRegistrationChange carried @param tags for channel, type, handler and\nphase, none of which it takes. That failed the \"Verify docs are current\" job\nbefore the diff it exists to check ever ran.\n\nThe cause is placement, not wording. onRegistrationChange was inserted between\nonEvent''s doc comment and onEvent itself, so the comment bound to the new method\nand onEvent, sixty lines further down, was left with none at all. The published\nreference has been describing the wrong method under the wrong name and omitting\none of the store''s oldest hooks.\n\nonEvent''s comment moves back to onEvent, unchanged. onRegistrationChange gets a\ncomment of its own, in the shape the other public methods here use: a summary,\nthe batching rule and the queueing rule, its two parameters, and an example.\nThe long-form rationale stays on the interface in types.ts, which is where a\nreader following the type lands.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarivGgAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ZXlAP9nnmG9VHF4oY4bndYJIaNOSrNaDjv3ntf8zcAsC0GlLAEAuhHNrV5JViJa\n1Wc5EtLUROkc1E3ACMlt42+StpPd/Aw=\n=ERJH\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDM2N2E0OTY2ZjE2Mzk3MTA3MGVlZGQxNmExMWY3NTI3MjZiMDQxMjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06","sha":"aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06"}],"sha":"367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/367a4966f163971070eedd16a11f752726b04126"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T05:45:24Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T05:45:24Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(repo): unblock CI - lockfile, size table, coverage and reference\n\nFour gates were failing and only the first was visible, because rush install\nstops before the others run.\n\nThe shrinkwrap was out of date because the example apps were bumped to ^0.8.0\nwithout a rush update, and no rush update could have repaired it: the examples\nresolve @yoltra/* from the published registry by design, and 0.8.0 is not\npublished yet. So the bump deadlocked the release. CI could not install until\n0.8.0 existed, and 0.8.0 could not be tagged until CI passed.\n\nThey now ask for ^0.7.0, which does exist, and get bumped once the release is\nout. Locally this costs nothing: every example already aliases @yoltra/* to the\nworkspace dist through its vite config and tsconfig paths, so the declared range\nonly describes what a plain npm install or StackBlitz would fetch. The one real\ncost is temporary, and only there - until 0.8.0 publishes, a visitor installing\nmission-control gets a react without the duringReplay option its MissionLog\npasses.\n\nCore''s published size table was 0.1 KB stale in both READMEs.\n\ndevtools-node-agent''s branch coverage had fallen to 51.85% against its 54% gate,\nbecause the per-event byte cap arrived without a test. That cap is what keeps one\noversized payload from ending a session, so it is worth covering rather than\nworth lowering the gate for. A new suite drives a real hub over real sockets and\nasserts both halves: a payload under the cap is forwarded whole with no flag\nadded, and one over it is replaced by the truncation marker with event.truncated\nand patchesTruncated set and the socket still open. Absent rather than false is\nthe contract, so a panel can treat the flag''s presence as the signal. Branches\nare back to 59.64%.\n\nThe committed reference had drifted for the protocol additions this release made.\n\nencodeState was left imported but unused in both agents when the bounded encoder\nreplaced every call, which was the only warning rush build emitted.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"7baa6c79b0375f7eefa12ffb326551ef6d12f813","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/7baa6c79b0375f7eefa12ffb326551ef6d12f813"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06","verification":{"payload":"tree 7baa6c79b0375f7eefa12ffb326551ef6d12f813\nparent 21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790487924 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790487924 -0600\n\nfix(repo): unblock CI - lockfile, size table, coverage and reference\n\nFour gates were failing and only the first was visible, because rush install\nstops before the others run.\n\nThe shrinkwrap was out of date because the example apps were bumped to ^0.8.0\nwithout a rush update, and no rush update could have repaired it: the examples\nresolve @yoltra/* from the published registry by design, and 0.8.0 is not\npublished yet. So the bump deadlocked the release. CI could not install until\n0.8.0 existed, and 0.8.0 could not be tagged until CI passed.\n\nThey now ask for ^0.7.0, which does exist, and get bumped once the release is\nout. Locally this costs nothing: every example already aliases @yoltra/* to the\nworkspace dist through its vite config and tsconfig paths, so the declared range\nonly describes what a plain npm install or StackBlitz would fetch. The one real\ncost is temporary, and only there - until 0.8.0 publishes, a visitor installing\nmission-control gets a react without the duringReplay option its MissionLog\npasses.\n\nCore''s published size table was 0.1 KB stale in both READMEs.\n\ndevtools-node-agent''s branch coverage had fallen to 51.85% against its 54% gate,\nbecause the per-event byte cap arrived without a test. That cap is what keeps one\noversized payload from ending a session, so it is worth covering rather than\nworth lowering the gate for. A new suite drives a real hub over real sockets and\nasserts both halves: a payload under the cap is forwarded whole with no flag\nadded, and one over it is replaced by the truncation marker with event.truncated\nand patchesTruncated set and the socket still open. Absent rather than false is\nthe contract, so a panel can treat the flag''s presence as the signal. Branches\nare back to 59.64%.\n\nThe committed reference had drifted for the protocol additions this release made.\n\nencodeState was left imported but unused in both agents when the bounded encoder\nreplaced every call, which was the only warning rush build emitted.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarithgAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ckcAP0WWUGTolm3KHXYvAWpDkDoykG+NRviHKnhrzQNIs9X0wEA5vmAKY12KA89\nObj3IdAK8K5so0TPXxNHHVtnmjghqAg=\n=nq42\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGFlZDUzNTk5YjVlYzJiMTNlNjE0OWEzMGFmZjdmMmQ4ZjRhODRlMDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e","sha":"21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e"}],"sha":"aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/aed53599b5ec2b13e6149a30aff7f2d8f4a84e06"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:56:17Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:56:17Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(react): a glob covering a container and its children no longer throws\n\nFound by checking whether the example apps still work, which the build passing\ndid not answer.\n\n`satellites.**` expands to the container path and the paths beneath it, so the\nprojection assigned the store''s real array at `satellites` and then tried to\nwrite `satellites.0` into it. State is frozen in development, so that threw\nCannot assign to read only property ''0''. In production it would have silently\nmutated the store''s own state, which is the worse of the two. A container\nborrowed from state is now shallow-copied before anything is written into it.\n\nThis was latent until the declared-path guard moved into createHooks. The\nprojection only ever ran in the package-level copy of the hook, and no test\ncombined a glob with an array, so nothing exercised it. The mission-control\nexample does exactly that in its header, and would have crashed on render.\n\nTwo example changes follow from the release rather than from a bug:\n\nMissionLog opts into duringReplay. It derives a log purely from the event\nstream and performs no I/O, which is the case the opt-in exists for, and\nmission-control is the example that demonstrates time travel. Left as it was,\nthe log would freeze while you dragged the timeline, which defeats the demo.\n\nEvery example declared ^0.2.0 for core and react, six minors behind, and ^0.1.0\nfor ds which is at 0.3.0. They build because Rush resolves to the workspace, so\nnothing caught it, but these are the files people copy when starting a project.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"bbd49fd5c0199518aa57772470d0279f15d6103a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/bbd49fd5c0199518aa57772470d0279f15d6103a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e","verification":{"payload":"tree bbd49fd5c0199518aa57772470d0279f15d6103a\nparent 1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790481377 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790481377 -0600\n\nfix(react): a glob covering a container and its children no longer throws\n\nFound by checking whether the example apps still work, which the build passing\ndid not answer.\n\n`satellites.**` expands to the container path and the paths beneath it, so the\nprojection assigned the store''s real array at `satellites` and then tried to\nwrite `satellites.0` into it. State is frozen in development, so that threw\nCannot assign to read only property ''0''. In production it would have silently\nmutated the store''s own state, which is the worse of the two. A container\nborrowed from state is now shallow-copied before anything is written into it.\n\nThis was latent until the declared-path guard moved into createHooks. The\nprojection only ever ran in the package-level copy of the hook, and no test\ncombined a glob with an array, so nothing exercised it. The mission-control\nexample does exactly that in its header, and would have crashed on render.\n\nTwo example changes follow from the release rather than from a bug:\n\nMissionLog opts into duringReplay. It derives a log purely from the event\nstream and performs no I/O, which is the case the opt-in exists for, and\nmission-control is the example that demonstrates time travel. Left as it was,\nthe log would freeze while you dragged the timeline, which defeats the demo.\n\nEvery example declared ^0.2.0 for core and react, six minors behind, and ^0.1.0\nfor ds which is at 0.3.0. They build because Rush resolves to the workspace, so\nnothing caught it, but these are the files people copy when starting a project.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarithQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9bZ5AP9Va+hnprSlWbVjWQ5jMZi3fY2WTMz1SPfF4azXhJKD5QEAmD22vCCEptr8\nabPlY2/jWkZLR8gyqMR9ksJOQEMvhgk=\n=bCJZ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDIxYTgwNzU4NTRjOWE0MTYxYzczNDgxNWE2YmFjY2QyNzEyNWFlMGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac","sha":"1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac"}],"sha":"21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/21a8075854c9a4161c734815a6baccd27125ae0e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:29:46Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:29:46Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(react): require core 0.8.0, which the code already did\n\nThe peer range said ^0.7.0 while the shipped source calls store.registerSlice,\npasses onEvent a fifth argument, and imports six types that exist only in\n0.8.0. So npm would happily install react 0.8.0 against core 0.7.x and the\nresult fails at runtime: store.registerSlice is not a function on any withSlice\ncall, and the replay opt-in quietly dropped by a core that takes four arguments.\n\nThe two devtools agents were bumped when they gained the same requirement; this\none was missed, and nothing catches it because the workspace always resolves to\nthe local core.\n\nAlso removes the hardcoded version from the Status section of both root READMEs.\n\"Release Candidate stage (v0.7.0)\" would have been wrong the moment this shipped,\nwith nothing to notice, which is the same failure mode as the size table that\n0.7.0 fixed by generating it. A version badge takes its place, so the number\ncomes from the registry rather than from prose.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"6931b88d4062c87fd1dc71f84132f930b5af0c12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/6931b88d4062c87fd1dc71f84132f930b5af0c12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac","verification":{"payload":"tree 6931b88d4062c87fd1dc71f84132f930b5af0c12\nparent 4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790479786 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790479786 -0600\n\nfix(react): require core 0.8.0, which the code already did\n\nThe peer range said ^0.7.0 while the shipped source calls store.registerSlice,\npasses onEvent a fifth argument, and imports six types that exist only in\n0.8.0. So npm would happily install react 0.8.0 against core 0.7.x and the\nresult fails at runtime: store.registerSlice is not a function on any withSlice\ncall, and the replay opt-in quietly dropped by a core that takes four arguments.\n\nThe two devtools agents were bumped when they gained the same requirement; this\none was missed, and nothing catches it because the workspace always resolves to\nthe local core.\n\nAlso removes the hardcoded version from the Status section of both root READMEs.\n\"Release Candidate stage (v0.7.0)\" would have been wrong the moment this shipped,\nwith nothing to notice, which is the same failure mode as the size table that\n0.7.0 fixed by generating it. A version badge takes its place, so the number\ncomes from the registry rather than from prose.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarithQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9YGeAQC1qBfSu+JeTGqdidjy2tuce9Q670O1wlXSmpfbxwGWegEAthNcqZgQaa42\n9Q6jS+L3RLAx7FT39tPAFTz6K6w/WAs=\n=1WQO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDFlYjIzNmIwOWUzZmU2OWQ3ODVkYTYzYmRjZTUzOTJiNzU3ZTcxYWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef","sha":"4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef"}],"sha":"1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1eb236b09e3fe69d785da63bdce5392b757e71ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:21:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T03:21:10Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs: bring the Spanish documentation level with 0.8.0\n\nThe Spanish root README, which lives at docs/es/README.md, was missing the\nstore diagram entirely. It now carries both Mermaid flowcharts translated, the\npipeline and the when matcher, plus the niceties table. Heading counts match the\nEnglish at 25, and the Spanish charts validate the same way: 25 and 9 nodes, no\ndangling references, no brackets inside labels.\n\nIts documentation list was missing three entries, two of them written during\nthis release: the upgrade guide, the decoration guide, and request/reply, which\nhad been absent since that guide was added. Its quick-start link also pointed at\nthe English file although a Spanish translation exists.\n\nThe audit turned up a gap that was not a translation problem. Neither React\nREADME documented anything from 0.8.0, in either language: no replay opt-in on\nuseEvent, no `written` phase, and nothing about the chainable surface. Both now\ncover all three, with the rules that make the chain safe, module scope and once,\nand the note that the store and context are the same objects so providers and\nthe Suspense cache are shared across views.\n\nBoth React READMEs also still quoted \"useStore must be used inside\n<StoreProvider>\", a message the hook collapse replaced.\n\nEvery EN/ES pair now matches on heading count: the four READMEs and all ten\nguides. Every relative link in the Spanish files resolves.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"4029b6c68b4a900cd74bec71d4a88ff764c1b7a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/4029b6c68b4a900cd74bec71d4a88ff764c1b7a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef","verification":{"payload":"tree 4029b6c68b4a900cd74bec71d4a88ff764c1b7a8\nparent 2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790479270 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790479270 -0600\n\ndocs: bring the Spanish documentation level with 0.8.0\n\nThe Spanish root README, which lives at docs/es/README.md, was missing the\nstore diagram entirely. It now carries both Mermaid flowcharts translated, the\npipeline and the when matcher, plus the niceties table. Heading counts match the\nEnglish at 25, and the Spanish charts validate the same way: 25 and 9 nodes, no\ndangling references, no brackets inside labels.\n\nIts documentation list was missing three entries, two of them written during\nthis release: the upgrade guide, the decoration guide, and request/reply, which\nhad been absent since that guide was added. Its quick-start link also pointed at\nthe English file although a Spanish translation exists.\n\nThe audit turned up a gap that was not a translation problem. Neither React\nREADME documented anything from 0.8.0, in either language: no replay opt-in on\nuseEvent, no `written` phase, and nothing about the chainable surface. Both now\ncover all three, with the rules that make the chain safe, module scope and once,\nand the note that the store and context are the same objects so providers and\nthe Suspense cache are shared across views.\n\nBoth React READMEs also still quoted \"useStore must be used inside\n<StoreProvider>\", a message the hook collapse replaced.\n\nEvery EN/ES pair now matches on heading count: the four READMEs and all ten\nguides. Every relative link in the Spanish files resolves.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarithQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9VHmAQDNHqTAYz/t57aOAk9nE+cmBE35zfVSrtC1JdVvyGbNpAD+IvwFYGpg8ljK\nffK19AQ3hWSgPSkSDcLkYsNlsWWQBQo=\n=Iy96\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDQ5MzFjZjA0NWUyZDkyYWEwNTI2YzcwYTQ4YTQ3YTNiMGMxZmVkZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7","sha":"2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7"}],"sha":"4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/4931cf045e2d92aa0526c70a48a47a3b0c1fedef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:29:09Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:29:09Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core): say why an emit did not commit, and report subscriber errors\n\nTwo diagnostics and an upgrade guide. No new capability: the release already\ncarries a feature, and what it needed at the tail was for what shipped to be\nlegible.\n\ncommitted: false arrived from three unrelated causes through one shared frozen\nobject. A caller could not tell a guard refusing an action from a double-click\nbeing collapsed by dedup, and those want opposite responses: surface the\nrefusal, say nothing about the duplicate. EmitResult gains reason, one of\nvetoed, deduped or cascade.\n\nIt also gains vetoedBy. That closes an asymmetry worth naming: a reducer\nrefusal has always named its slice, through rejectedBy and onRejected, while a\nmiddleware veto named nobody at all. \"The event vanished\" had no author. Both\nfields are absent when the event committed, so nothing existing changes shape.\n\nonSubscriberError is the fourth of a set. Reducers, effects, rejections and\ncascades each had a hook; event subscribers had console.error and nothing else,\nso an application could not route a failing one to its own reporting.\nSubscribers are the seam a decoration is told to use, which makes the gap more\nvisible than it was.\n\nThe upgrade guide is the part I would keep if only one survived. The existing\nmigration guide is about arriving from Redux, Zustand or Jotai and says nothing\nabout moving between Yoltra versions, and this release changes when middleware\nvetoes, when replay notifies, what replace* removes and whether an undeclared\nread throws. That is hard to extract from thirty changelog entries, so each\nsection leads with how you would notice rather than with what changed.\n\nIt also corrects the migration guide, which still told Redux users that Yoltra\nmiddleware \"returns a boolean\".\n\nTypeDoc regenerated; the reference carries the new fields and NotCommittedReason\nhas a page.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"8ebe24f48c8697a0c309cc0af062fd6b1f4de3b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/8ebe24f48c8697a0c309cc0af062fd6b1f4de3b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7","verification":{"payload":"tree 8ebe24f48c8697a0c309cc0af062fd6b1f4de3b3\nparent 6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790465349 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790465349 -0600\n\nfeat(core): say why an emit did not commit, and report subscriber errors\n\nTwo diagnostics and an upgrade guide. No new capability: the release already\ncarries a feature, and what it needed at the tail was for what shipped to be\nlegible.\n\ncommitted: false arrived from three unrelated causes through one shared frozen\nobject. A caller could not tell a guard refusing an action from a double-click\nbeing collapsed by dedup, and those want opposite responses: surface the\nrefusal, say nothing about the duplicate. EmitResult gains reason, one of\nvetoed, deduped or cascade.\n\nIt also gains vetoedBy. That closes an asymmetry worth naming: a reducer\nrefusal has always named its slice, through rejectedBy and onRejected, while a\nmiddleware veto named nobody at all. \"The event vanished\" had no author. Both\nfields are absent when the event committed, so nothing existing changes shape.\n\nonSubscriberError is the fourth of a set. Reducers, effects, rejections and\ncascades each had a hook; event subscribers had console.error and nothing else,\nso an application could not route a failing one to its own reporting.\nSubscribers are the seam a decoration is told to use, which makes the gap more\nvisible than it was.\n\nThe upgrade guide is the part I would keep if only one survived. The existing\nmigration guide is about arriving from Redux, Zustand or Jotai and says nothing\nabout moving between Yoltra versions, and this release changes when middleware\nvetoes, when replay notifies, what replace* removes and whether an undeclared\nread throws. That is hard to extract from thirty changelog entries, so each\nsection leads with how you would notice rather than with what changed.\n\nIt also corrects the migration guide, which still told Redux users that Yoltra\nmiddleware \"returns a boolean\".\n\nTypeDoc regenerated; the reference carries the new fields and NotCommittedReason\nhas a page.\n\nSigned-off-by: pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarithAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9fAuAQDNszb7Jfq9T1NYVV3Y0gd+z6fkp5rNcx4wxNUj5b92gwEAjxyYjNUMroip\nLrw+kpVmD33uEwoC8FcJ12O/85bScQY=\n=XqVB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDJmNDRmOTk2OTUwYTE4Mzg0N2QwYjkxMjUxYzM1MjY4NGUzYzQyYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b","sha":"6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b"}],"sha":"2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/2f44f996950a183847d0b91251c352684e3c42a7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:28:36Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:28:36Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs: a diagram of the store in the root README\n\nThe README described what a store gives you and never showed how one works.\nTwo Mermaid flowcharts: one event end to end, and how `when` decides whether a\nhandler is found by an O(1) lookup or matched on every event.\n\nThe pipeline diagram is the one place the ordering is visible at a glance: that\nthe reduce phase is synchronous and effects are not, that slices stage before\nany of them writes so a late refusal can still stop the first write, and that\nthe fan-out has four distinct destinations rather than one.\n\nA short table follows for the parts that are cross-cutting and therefore have\nno place in a flow: the codec, persistence, devtools, runtime registration and\nthe cascade guard.\n\nFirst Mermaid in the repo; GitHub renders it natively. The labels avoid\nbrackets and braces, which the parser reads as shape syntax even inside quotes,\nand every edge uses the piped-label form.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"af37d2ab1e4559e41f6f1e2ba251f254a7096446","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/af37d2ab1e4559e41f6f1e2ba251f254a7096446"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b","verification":{"payload":"tree af37d2ab1e4559e41f6f1e2ba251f254a7096446\nparent 31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790461716 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790461716 -0600\n\ndocs: a diagram of the store in the root README\n\nThe README described what a store gives you and never showed how one works.\nTwo Mermaid flowcharts: one event end to end, and how `when` decides whether a\nhandler is found by an O(1) lookup or matched on every event.\n\nThe pipeline diagram is the one place the ordering is visible at a glance: that\nthe reduce phase is synchronous and effects are not, that slices stage before\nany of them writes so a late refusal can still stop the first write, and that\nthe fan-out has four distinct destinations rather than one.\n\nA short table follows for the parts that are cross-cutting and therefore have\nno place in a flow: the codec, persistence, devtools, runtime registration and\nthe cascade guard.\n\nFirst Mermaid in the repo; GitHub renders it natively. The labels avoid\nbrackets and braces, which the parser reads as shape syntax even inside quotes,\nand every edge uses the piped-label form.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarithAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9f6EAPwO9+3vQwDyO/SeRT+Tf5hBg7cJiVvt1efvWJTiyU3L9AEA4Ug5c+HFdcbU\nj7Wawht7U8oM+qy1qcBOoAnILpCC2AA=\n=yWnD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDY2MjU2NTlkNDc3ZjMxMzU3OGI4NTExNTU1YzBkYmUwNzliNTU5OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416","sha":"31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416"}],"sha":"6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6625659d477f313578b8511555c0dbe079b5599b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:12:21Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:12:21Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix: three findings from the project analysis, folded into this release\n\nAll three are either bugs users hit or things this release caused, so they\nbelong in it rather than in a follow-up. The coverage debt in devtools-storeview\nand devtools-cli, and the dispose() semantics, are deliberately left out: one is\na milestone of test-writing for debt that predates this work, the other is a\npre-existing behaviour change that deserves its own decision.\n\nuseAtomicProps had two implementations, and the declared-path guard lived in\nonly one of them: the package-level copy, which the barrel deliberately steers\npeople away from. Through createYoltra, which the documentation recommends, a\nselector could read state it never declared, receive the right value once, and\nthen never re-render, because the component is subscribed to the declared paths\nonly. A silent failure, in the release whose theme is removing them.\n\nPatching the one instance would have left the cause. The two implementations\nare collapsed: hooks.ts is now typed faces over the same set createHooks\nreturns, so a fix cannot land in one copy and miss the other. That drift has\nalready bitten twice, once when the written phase left three copies claiming a\nhandler could see only two, and once here. hooks.ts drops from 517 lines to\n388, and the dead useAtomicPropImpl it left behind goes with it.\n\nThe shared instance is built lazily. createHooks reaches the Suspense hooks,\nwhich reach this module, so building it at import time left whichever loaded\nfirst looking at the others half-initialized, and ten test files failed to load\nat all. By first render everything is settled.\n\nEvent payloads were unbounded while snapshots were carefully capped. The hub\nlimits a frame to 8 MiB and ws answers an oversized one by closing the\nconnection, not by dropping the message, so one large emit ended the session.\nThis release made it reachable in ordinary use: CORE-3 turned an ArrayBuffer\nfrom `{}` into its full base64. New maxEventBytes, 512 KiB by default, far below\nthe snapshot cap because events are frequent and a snapshot is not, with a wire\nflag so a panel can say \"truncated\" rather than showing nothing.\n\nThe disposed-slice diagnostic I added is bounded at 64. It is development-only\nand holds strings, but a long session of mount-and-dispose cycles grew it for\nthe lifetime of the store.\n\nTwo messages become one: the package-level useStore carried its own terser\nwording, and the surviving message names the fix rather than only the rule.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"484d99bf1ad9a1757db8711749d0d8166adef69f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/484d99bf1ad9a1757db8711749d0d8166adef69f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416","verification":{"payload":"tree 484d99bf1ad9a1757db8711749d0d8166adef69f\nparent 1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790460741 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790460741 -0600\n\nfix: three findings from the project analysis, folded into this release\n\nAll three are either bugs users hit or things this release caused, so they\nbelong in it rather than in a follow-up. The coverage debt in devtools-storeview\nand devtools-cli, and the dispose() semantics, are deliberately left out: one is\na milestone of test-writing for debt that predates this work, the other is a\npre-existing behaviour change that deserves its own decision.\n\nuseAtomicProps had two implementations, and the declared-path guard lived in\nonly one of them: the package-level copy, which the barrel deliberately steers\npeople away from. Through createYoltra, which the documentation recommends, a\nselector could read state it never declared, receive the right value once, and\nthen never re-render, because the component is subscribed to the declared paths\nonly. A silent failure, in the release whose theme is removing them.\n\nPatching the one instance would have left the cause. The two implementations\nare collapsed: hooks.ts is now typed faces over the same set createHooks\nreturns, so a fix cannot land in one copy and miss the other. That drift has\nalready bitten twice, once when the written phase left three copies claiming a\nhandler could see only two, and once here. hooks.ts drops from 517 lines to\n388, and the dead useAtomicPropImpl it left behind goes with it.\n\nThe shared instance is built lazily. createHooks reaches the Suspense hooks,\nwhich reach this module, so building it at import time left whichever loaded\nfirst looking at the others half-initialized, and ten test files failed to load\nat all. By first render everything is settled.\n\nEvent payloads were unbounded while snapshots were carefully capped. The hub\nlimits a frame to 8 MiB and ws answers an oversized one by closing the\nconnection, not by dropping the message, so one large emit ended the session.\nThis release made it reachable in ordinary use: CORE-3 turned an ArrayBuffer\nfrom `{}` into its full base64. New maxEventBytes, 512 KiB by default, far below\nthe snapshot cap because events are frequent and a snapshot is not, with a wire\nflag so a panel can say \"truncated\" rather than showing nothing.\n\nThe disposed-slice diagnostic I added is bounded at 64. It is development-only\nand holds strings, but a long session of mount-and-dispose cycles grew it for\nthe lifetime of the store.\n\nTwo messages become one: the package-level useStore carried its own terser\nwording, and the surviving message names the fix rather than only the rule.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCarithAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9bCJAQDGeRponfGUpZ/xltJYsg6xiMbiYMgotKg/DglSJETrvwEAijM9yR7lTRDx\nxL9DAZG3LGkYKQxKwFILeYNKZDzo2Qc=\n=VAqG\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDMxMzY1ZjQ1ODM3MTMzNDliMTczNzcwNzMyZGZlMTBiZmFmM2E0MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae","sha":"1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae"}],"sha":"31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/31365f4583713349b173770732dfe10bfaf3a416"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:40:55Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:40:55Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix: nine defects found reviewing this release\n\nA review of the whole branch turned up ten findings. Nine were real and are\nfixed here; each has a regression test, and the devtools one was verified by\nreverting the fix and watching the test fail.\n\nThe worst is mine from the codec work. Resolving a binary tag''s kind from\nconstructor.name meant Node''s Buffer, a Uint8Array subclass and everywhere,\nencoded as kind \"Buffer\", which the decoder''s allow-list rejects. It came back\nundefined and nothing reported it: through persist as much as through time\ntravel, a silent total loss of the value. That is the exact failure the module\nexists to prevent, reintroduced by the fix for it. Kinds resolve by instanceof\nnow, a subclass round-trips as its base, and the path is reported because\nlosing the subclass is still a loss.\n\nhotReplace half-applied: replaceReducers refuses to take over a slice a library\nowns, and that refusal fired after middleware and effects were already swapped.\nThe check is a pre-flight across the whole call now.\n\nThe rest: encodeStateBounded base64-encoded a buffer before noticing it had\nblown the budget; disposing one effect registration stripped the metadata of\nothers sharing its function; both new disposers were non-idempotent and the\nmiddleware one announced the removal before performing it; a registration made\nfrom inside an emitCurrent snapshot was re-entered instead of queued; an encode\nthat was both truncated and lossy reported only the truncation; and the\ndevtools agent pushed two whole-store snapshots per store.call(), because the\ninternal reply listener''s mount and unmount both reached the observer.\n\nThe tenth finding, that announceMountedSlice only reaches top-level paths, is\nnot a defect. An ordinary commit behaves identically: detectChangedProps\nreports a newly-appearing subtree at its root, so a connect on \"deep.n\" does\nnot fire when deep first appears, whether the slice was mounted late or not.\nDiverging here would have made the mount path inconsistent with every other\nwrite. The doc comment overclaimed and now states the scope.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"e5acec314ff28c9515db9c773381febf837395c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/e5acec314ff28c9515db9c773381febf837395c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae","verification":{"payload":"tree e5acec314ff28c9515db9c773381febf837395c6\nparent 6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790455255 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790455255 -0600\n\nfix: nine defects found reviewing this release\n\nA review of the whole branch turned up ten findings. Nine were real and are\nfixed here; each has a regression test, and the devtools one was verified by\nreverting the fix and watching the test fail.\n\nThe worst is mine from the codec work. Resolving a binary tag''s kind from\nconstructor.name meant Node''s Buffer, a Uint8Array subclass and everywhere,\nencoded as kind \"Buffer\", which the decoder''s allow-list rejects. It came back\nundefined and nothing reported it: through persist as much as through time\ntravel, a silent total loss of the value. That is the exact failure the module\nexists to prevent, reintroduced by the fix for it. Kinds resolve by instanceof\nnow, a subclass round-trips as its base, and the path is reported because\nlosing the subclass is still a loss.\n\nhotReplace half-applied: replaceReducers refuses to take over a slice a library\nowns, and that refusal fired after middleware and effects were already swapped.\nThe check is a pre-flight across the whole call now.\n\nThe rest: encodeStateBounded base64-encoded a buffer before noticing it had\nblown the budget; disposing one effect registration stripped the metadata of\nothers sharing its function; both new disposers were non-idempotent and the\nmiddleware one announced the removal before performing it; a registration made\nfrom inside an emitCurrent snapshot was re-entered instead of queued; an encode\nthat was both truncated and lossy reported only the truncation; and the\ndevtools agent pushed two whole-store snapshots per store.call(), because the\ninternal reply listener''s mount and unmount both reached the observer.\n\nThe tenth finding, that announceMountedSlice only reaches top-level paths, is\nnot a defect. An ordinary commit behaves identically: detectChangedProps\nreports a newly-appearing subtree at its root, so a connect on \"deep.n\" does\nnot fire when deep first appears, whether the slice was mounted late or not.\nDiverging here would have made the mount path inconsistent with every other\nwrite. The doc comment overclaimed and now states the scope.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9eggAP9NU9f1CiSWNz6Sdy387YsCNzhgqGcc9KbtbyP8YfQLNAD/XOER3WFuOeqR\nGfva4n8KdwbQP13HcTpQe/kMxl4THwE=\n=KtY9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDFiODEzM2FmYmU4YTc4OTRiYTZhMTBlMDBkZjliNWRjMDdjM2M3YWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c","sha":"6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c"}],"sha":"1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1b8133afbe8a7894ba6a10e00df9b5dc07c3c7ae"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:01:51Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T20:01:51Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"test(core): silence the intentional reducer error in the replay suite\n\nThe isReplaying-restored test throws from a reducer on purpose, and core\nreports that through its own error path, so a clean run printed a stack trace\nand rush reported SUCCESS WITH WARNINGS. Every other test here that provokes an\nerror already spies on console; this one did not. An intentional failure should\nnot read as a broken suite.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"7e0b99688a5b05ce5b74baf8371e810fded2fe43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/7e0b99688a5b05ce5b74baf8371e810fded2fe43"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e0b99688a5b05ce5b74baf8371e810fded2fe43\nparent 57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790452911 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790452911 -0600\n\ntest(core): silence the intentional reducer error in the replay suite\n\nThe isReplaying-restored test throws from a reducer on purpose, and core\nreports that through its own error path, so a clean run printed a stack trace\nand rush reported SUCCESS WITH WARNINGS. Every other test here that provokes an\nerror already spies on console; this one did not. An intentional failure should\nnot read as a broken suite.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9dI/AP9/MC5CZTJn9LcYB3ly1GgXKi2IeafcKMAGWcdLOXS4swD8DyKt1OwNRBw2\n8M542CkJtS6KQVtri/5jZONt9tQqnwM=\n=kEyX\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDZmNmEyZDEyNTEyZDg3NGJkNDA5YzkxNTUzYjE3ODI3NTFmYTRmNGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0","sha":"57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0"}],"sha":"6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/6f6a2d12512d874bd409c91553b1782751fa4f4c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:59:00Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:59:00Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs: a decoration guide, and corrections to what drifted\n\nThe decoration feature spans core and react, a contract, a lifecycle seam and\na set of rules that only make sense together: why the builders exist, why\nnesting rather than piping, what survives a hot reload, and why withSlice hands\nback no disposer. Reference pages cannot carry that, so it is a guide, in\nEnglish and Spanish.\n\nIt leads with the failure rather than the API. Before 0.8.0 a decoration needed\na cast at every registration site and then lost its slice, and its state, on the\nfirst hot reload, because core''s own documented HMR line deleted it. Someone\nreaching for this feature has probably hit that.\n\nSeparately, three docstrings had drifted from the code. The onEvent phase list\nomitted ''written'' in both the interface and the implementation, though the\nphase has existed and been handled in both for a release, and neither said\nreplay no longer notifies. ReducerSpec''s remark recommended `when` over an\n`events` property that had already been removed. replaceReducers documented\nonly preserveState and still implied it replaced everything.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"108d5d3a9d4c5c839efebc334f71c9590de88fd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/108d5d3a9d4c5c839efebc334f71c9590de88fd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0","verification":{"payload":"tree 108d5d3a9d4c5c839efebc334f71c9590de88fd0\nparent 59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790452740 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790452740 -0600\n\ndocs: a decoration guide, and corrections to what drifted\n\nThe decoration feature spans core and react, a contract, a lifecycle seam and\na set of rules that only make sense together: why the builders exist, why\nnesting rather than piping, what survives a hot reload, and why withSlice hands\nback no disposer. Reference pages cannot carry that, so it is a guide, in\nEnglish and Spanish.\n\nIt leads with the failure rather than the API. Before 0.8.0 a decoration needed\na cast at every registration site and then lost its slice, and its state, on the\nfirst hot reload, because core''s own documented HMR line deleted it. Someone\nreaching for this feature has probably hit that.\n\nSeparately, three docstrings had drifted from the code. The onEvent phase list\nomitted ''written'' in both the interface and the implementation, though the\nphase has existed and been handled in both for a release, and neither said\nreplay no longer notifies. ReducerSpec''s remark recommended `when` over an\n`events` property that had already been removed. replaceReducers documented\nonly preserveState and still implied it replaced everything.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9R5eAQCNJ/N35kpzR41K32jR8awv074QswAXzwOcmUk8TwrYgwD8DXnNydSc+ZKb\n1mVDbVqt9v0QfF8MlZ6K7nWVUedcXwM=\n=JZus\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDU3ZmY5YmI3MTkzMjRkYzAyMWU2MjEyMWFhZDdmM2ZmYWFlMmVkYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341","sha":"59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341"}],"sha":"57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/57ff9bb719324dc021e62121aad7f3ffaae2edb0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:55:04Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:55:04Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(devtools): push subscriptions when registrations change\n\n__devtoolsIntrospect() is a pull, so the panel''s subscription list went stale\nthe moment anything was registered at runtime: a decoration mounting a slice, a\nhot reload, an onEvent added by a component. The panel had no way to know and\nno reason to ask again, so it showed a topology that had already moved on.\n\nThe agent subscribes to onRegistrationChange and sends STORE_SUBSCRIPTIONS\nunprompted. No connection check: the transport already buffers while\ndisconnected, and each frame is a full snapshot, so if several queue up only\nthe last carries anything the earlier ones did not. REQUEST_SUBSCRIPTIONS now\nanswers from the same builder rather than a second copy of it.\n\nPeer ranges move to @yoltra/core ^0.8.0 on both agents.\n\nThe e2e test drives a real agent against the loopback hub and asserts the frame\narrives without the panel asking, carrying the new slice with the provenance a\npanel needs to attribute it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"ba064a1749e2d88c73cc8d4666b4aac03c8ab0c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/ba064a1749e2d88c73cc8d4666b4aac03c8ab0c6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341","verification":{"payload":"tree ba064a1749e2d88c73cc8d4666b4aac03c8ab0c6\nparent 620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790420104 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790420104 -0600\n\nfeat(devtools): push subscriptions when registrations change\n\n__devtoolsIntrospect() is a pull, so the panel''s subscription list went stale\nthe moment anything was registered at runtime: a decoration mounting a slice, a\nhot reload, an onEvent added by a component. The panel had no way to know and\nno reason to ask again, so it showed a topology that had already moved on.\n\nThe agent subscribes to onRegistrationChange and sends STORE_SUBSCRIPTIONS\nunprompted. No connection check: the transport already buffers while\ndisconnected, and each frame is a full snapshot, so if several queue up only\nthe last carries anything the earlier ones did not. REQUEST_SUBSCRIPTIONS now\nanswers from the same builder rather than a second copy of it.\n\nPeer ranges move to @yoltra/core ^0.8.0 on both agents.\n\nThe e2e test drives a real agent against the loopback hub and asserts the frame\narrives without the panel asking, carrying the new slice with the provenance a\npanel needs to attribute it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritggAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9VPcAPsFtpley/ww3HIVI/bF5wfdNqrduFVSH/cQF00Fe8qqRwD/XGEZvBnsF84B\nWawuHjwqxZ3DZdAFlt3QM/oACZ6A+gI=\n=pDmz\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDU5NjUxZGQwZTk5NDc2Njg0NTAyMjUxMWM3ZjBjNjJjNTdiODEzNDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6","sha":"620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6"}],"sha":"59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/59651dd0e994766845022511c7f0c62c57b81341"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:55:03Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:55:03Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(react): chainable hooks for a decorated store\n\ncreateYoltra bound R, S and EM at creation, so a slice mounted afterwards was\ninvisible to every hook: useAtomicProp on it returned unknown and useSelector\ncould not see it at all. withSlice, withMiddleware and withEffect now return a\nYoltra whose types have grown, and free-function forms exist for a library\nhanded a Yoltra it did not create.\n\nThe context object is re-typed, never recreated. That is what lets a\nStoreProvider from any view in a chain serve the hooks of every other, and it\nis also why the Suspense cache is shared rather than split: the cache keys on\nstore identity through a WeakMap, and the widened store is the same object.\n\ncreateHooks allocates fresh function objects per call, so these belong at\nmodule scope, called once, before the first render. That is documented rather\nthan enforced, because nothing at the type level can enforce it.\n\nWriting the free function''s return as ReturnType<Yoltra[...]> sent the compiler\ninto unbounded inference and overflowed its stack: resolving the return of a\ngeneric method on a self-referential interface. It is written out explicitly.\n\nAlso strengthens the public-export test. It was a one-way toHaveProperty loop,\nwhich catches a removal and not an addition, and it had drifted: createYoltra\nand the three entity hooks were exported and absent from the asserted list. It\nnow asserts the set both ways.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"eb673ca57d0be3c6fd5dad5f3d76110c853d744e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/eb673ca57d0be3c6fd5dad5f3d76110c853d744e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6","verification":{"payload":"tree eb673ca57d0be3c6fd5dad5f3d76110c853d744e\nparent 643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790420103 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790420103 -0600\n\nfeat(react): chainable hooks for a decorated store\n\ncreateYoltra bound R, S and EM at creation, so a slice mounted afterwards was\ninvisible to every hook: useAtomicProp on it returned unknown and useSelector\ncould not see it at all. withSlice, withMiddleware and withEffect now return a\nYoltra whose types have grown, and free-function forms exist for a library\nhanded a Yoltra it did not create.\n\nThe context object is re-typed, never recreated. That is what lets a\nStoreProvider from any view in a chain serve the hooks of every other, and it\nis also why the Suspense cache is shared rather than split: the cache keys on\nstore identity through a WeakMap, and the widened store is the same object.\n\ncreateHooks allocates fresh function objects per call, so these belong at\nmodule scope, called once, before the first render. That is documented rather\nthan enforced, because nothing at the type level can enforce it.\n\nWriting the free function''s return as ReturnType<Yoltra[...]> sent the compiler\ninto unbounded inference and overflowed its stack: resolving the return of a\ngeneric method on a self-referential interface. It is written out explicitly.\n\nAlso strengthens the public-export test. It was a one-way toHaveProperty loop,\nwhich catches a removal and not an addition, and it had drifted: createYoltra\nand the three entity hooks were exported and absent from the asserted list. It\nnow asserts the set both ways.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritggAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ahmAP0eAjegduPS7Vs1FHWnL8dPNY3iViqtm9ODVls44bLccgEAnbtoKmQDOcOs\nPRet8OtHIff0QBm4DoDAQLkc1DopGAw=\n=4/eL\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDYyMGM4NjQwMDFmMzJkZWIxZTJjZDhmYThmMGIxNDA0ZmU3MDQ3ZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558","sha":"643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558"}],"sha":"620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/620c864001f32deb1e2cd8fa8f0b1404fe7047e6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:54:48Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:54:48Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core): onRegistrationChange, a push seam for the registration lifecycle\n\n__devtoolsIntrospect() is a pull, so a devtools panel''s subscription list went\nstale the moment anything was registered at runtime, and a library that needed\nto react to another library had nothing to wait on. It cannot ride instrument:\nInstrumentedEvent is event-flow shaped, with changedPaths, prevValues and\nreduceTimeMs, and topology is not an event.\n\nChanges arrive as an array, one batch per public call. replaceReducers updates\na slice by unmounting and remounting it, so a per-change observer would watch\nsomething merely being updated disappear; hotReplace delivers one batch across\nall three kinds rather than three views of a topology mid-rebuild.\n\nEach change is self-sufficient, so an observer never needs a follow-up pull:\nkind, op, name, origin, owner, the normalized matcher rather than the raw spec,\nand for a reducer a four-valued state. That fourth value is the point:\n\"retained\" distinguishes a slice whose state survived an unmount from one whose\ndid not, and an observer treating every unmount as destruction would tear down\na subscription it is about to need.\n\nemitCurrent closes the late-subscriber gap. Spec-time registrations happen\ninside createStore, so a decorator applied afterwards never saw them arrive;\nthe snapshot is delivered synchronously before subscribe returns, which is one\nshape rather than two and no race to reason about. The synthesized changes\ncarry their real origins, never a synthetic marker, because filtering on\nprovenance is the main thing an observer does.\n\nObservers run after the state broadcast, so the view layer learns a fact before\na library gets to react to it. A registration made by an observer is the\nlegitimate ordering-dependency case, so it is queued rather than delivered\nre-entrantly: depth-first work, breadth-first notification, bounded at 64\nrounds like the reduce depth. Overflow logs rather than throws, because the\ntopology is correct at that point and throwing would truncate the stream and\nunwind a caller that did nothing wrong.\n\nReplay produces no changes, which the docstring states so nobody adds a\nduringReplay option here by analogy with onEvent. dispose is terminal and\nsilent. A throwing observer does not stop the others. An observer returning a\nPromise is reported in development and deliberately not awaited or adopted.\nNothing is allocated when nobody is observing, which matters because these\ncall sites run inside createStore.\n\nFixes a slice registered with a pattern matcher never being reported at all:\nmountSlice returns early for one, so a notification at the end of its body\nfired only for key-dispatched slices. Caught by a test written for the seam.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"4558dac6c228171f177694dc2c67573fe6e8faa6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/4558dac6c228171f177694dc2c67573fe6e8faa6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558","verification":{"payload":"tree 4558dac6c228171f177694dc2c67573fe6e8faa6\nparent c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790420088 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790420088 -0600\n\nfeat(core): onRegistrationChange, a push seam for the registration lifecycle\n\n__devtoolsIntrospect() is a pull, so a devtools panel''s subscription list went\nstale the moment anything was registered at runtime, and a library that needed\nto react to another library had nothing to wait on. It cannot ride instrument:\nInstrumentedEvent is event-flow shaped, with changedPaths, prevValues and\nreduceTimeMs, and topology is not an event.\n\nChanges arrive as an array, one batch per public call. replaceReducers updates\na slice by unmounting and remounting it, so a per-change observer would watch\nsomething merely being updated disappear; hotReplace delivers one batch across\nall three kinds rather than three views of a topology mid-rebuild.\n\nEach change is self-sufficient, so an observer never needs a follow-up pull:\nkind, op, name, origin, owner, the normalized matcher rather than the raw spec,\nand for a reducer a four-valued state. That fourth value is the point:\n\"retained\" distinguishes a slice whose state survived an unmount from one whose\ndid not, and an observer treating every unmount as destruction would tear down\na subscription it is about to need.\n\nemitCurrent closes the late-subscriber gap. Spec-time registrations happen\ninside createStore, so a decorator applied afterwards never saw them arrive;\nthe snapshot is delivered synchronously before subscribe returns, which is one\nshape rather than two and no race to reason about. The synthesized changes\ncarry their real origins, never a synthetic marker, because filtering on\nprovenance is the main thing an observer does.\n\nObservers run after the state broadcast, so the view layer learns a fact before\na library gets to react to it. A registration made by an observer is the\nlegitimate ordering-dependency case, so it is queued rather than delivered\nre-entrantly: depth-first work, breadth-first notification, bounded at 64\nrounds like the reduce depth. Overflow logs rather than throws, because the\ntopology is correct at that point and throwing would truncate the stream and\nunwind a caller that did nothing wrong.\n\nReplay produces no changes, which the docstring states so nobody adds a\nduringReplay option here by analogy with onEvent. dispose is terminal and\nsilent. A throwing observer does not stop the others. An observer returning a\nPromise is reported in development and deliberately not awaited or adopted.\nNothing is allocated when nobody is observing, which matters because these\ncall sites run inside createStore.\n\nFixes a slice registered with a pattern matcher never being reported at all:\nmountSlice returns early for one, so a notification at the end of its body\nfired only for key-dispatched slices. Caught by a test written for the seam.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritggAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9UDUAP97EYh+t8tTQPGxsjMNpHM59uPt4TzFQNvPLFwPODwPEQEAzqaYpM0rNfSU\nB7BQPgJrxO4ejdtGdCtSM/9jAid9LwI=\n=c4SF\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDY0MzQ5MzEwM2Y0NjYzZDhiYjMyMjU4N2JkNzhmYzI0MTNkMmQ1NTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3","sha":"c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3"}],"sha":"643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/643493103f4663d8bb322587bd78fc2413d2d558"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:01:17Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T10:01:17Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core): typed growth for a store decorated after construction\n\nregisterReducer took a plain string and returned a bare disposer, so a slice a\nlibrary mounted was invisible to the type system: nothing downstream knew it\nexisted or what shape it had, and a spec targeting a channel the application''s\nevent map did not contain needed a cast at every registration site.\n\nregisterSlice, withSlice, withMiddleware and withEffect return the store\nre-typed. Decoration is type-level only: the same runtime object comes back, so\nsubscriptions, effects, middleware, the dedup cache, both buses and any\nin-flight call() are untouched and nothing re-subscribes. The cast lives in one\nplace, so no call site needs one, which is the whole point.\n\nDecorators compose by nesting in either order. That falls out of StoreDecorator\nbeing generic over the incoming store rather than from any variance rule: R, S\nand EM are inference sites, so an events-only decorator nested inside one that\nadds a slice infers the already-widened values and carries them through. There\nis no pipe, because every decorator takes (store, config) and each step would\nneed a lambda to become unary, making a pipe longer than the nesting it\nreplaces.\n\nThe register* family now returns a callable object carrying .store and\n.dispose, so an existing bare-disposer call site compiles and runs unchanged.\nwithSlice returns no disposer on purpose: after one runs the widened type still\npromises a slice that is gone, and no type system can express \"valid until that\ncall\". Reading a disposed slice through connect throws a named error in\ndevelopment instead of returning undefined from a type that promised a value.\n\nAlso fixes a slice mounted after construction never waking connect. It\nbroadcast to subscribe listeners but emitted nothing on the connector bus, so\nuseAtomicProp and the Suspense hooks never learned it existed and a component\nwatching a path inside it never re-rendered. Without this the feature would\nhave shipped a documented path that does not work.\n\nOne catch worth recording: the type-level suite briefly went vacuous. Built\nwith the inferring createStore overload, an unannotated spec literal gives\nEMOfSpec nothing to infer from, EM lands on EventMapBase, and its index\nsignatures accept any channel and payload, so every negative assertion passed\nfor the wrong reason. It uses the explicit overload now.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"9cf9a722e1e04101e8d29b93e0d92e7d0111a41a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/9cf9a722e1e04101e8d29b93e0d92e7d0111a41a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3","verification":{"payload":"tree 9cf9a722e1e04101e8d29b93e0d92e7d0111a41a\nparent 8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790416877 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790416877 -0600\n\nfeat(core): typed growth for a store decorated after construction\n\nregisterReducer took a plain string and returned a bare disposer, so a slice a\nlibrary mounted was invisible to the type system: nothing downstream knew it\nexisted or what shape it had, and a spec targeting a channel the application''s\nevent map did not contain needed a cast at every registration site.\n\nregisterSlice, withSlice, withMiddleware and withEffect return the store\nre-typed. Decoration is type-level only: the same runtime object comes back, so\nsubscriptions, effects, middleware, the dedup cache, both buses and any\nin-flight call() are untouched and nothing re-subscribes. The cast lives in one\nplace, so no call site needs one, which is the whole point.\n\nDecorators compose by nesting in either order. That falls out of StoreDecorator\nbeing generic over the incoming store rather than from any variance rule: R, S\nand EM are inference sites, so an events-only decorator nested inside one that\nadds a slice infers the already-widened values and carries them through. There\nis no pipe, because every decorator takes (store, config) and each step would\nneed a lambda to become unary, making a pipe longer than the nesting it\nreplaces.\n\nThe register* family now returns a callable object carrying .store and\n.dispose, so an existing bare-disposer call site compiles and runs unchanged.\nwithSlice returns no disposer on purpose: after one runs the widened type still\npromises a slice that is gone, and no type system can express \"valid until that\ncall\". Reading a disposed slice through connect throws a named error in\ndevelopment instead of returning undefined from a type that promised a value.\n\nAlso fixes a slice mounted after construction never waking connect. It\nbroadcast to subscribe listeners but emitted nothing on the connector bus, so\nuseAtomicProp and the Suspense hooks never learned it existed and a component\nwatching a path inside it never re-rendered. Without this the feature would\nhave shipped a documented path that does not work.\n\nOne catch worth recording: the type-level suite briefly went vacuous. Built\nwith the inferring createStore overload, an unannotated spec literal gives\nEMOfSpec nothing to infer from, EM lands on EventMapBase, and its index\nsignatures accept any channel and payload, so every negative assertion passed\nfor the wrong reason. It uses the explicit overload now.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9eZXAP94Tt/i3+LrlVhMnmSisiobjmAsbKOzffATFbEfK2w/AAEAq/mvIvTCaGrt\n1T9xz8uoKdshIKZuS8UaL2JENKFHoA4=\n=z8DB\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGM5YzI5MmJkNDk2ZDllY2E3N2U5M2NmZDRhMTg0NzE1NTZjYmJlZDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e","sha":"8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e"}],"sha":"c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/c9c292bd496d9eca77e93cfd4a18471556cbbed3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:48:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:48:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core)!: registrations made after construction survive replace*\n\nreplace* exists to replace what the application authored. A reducer, middleware\nor effect a library installed with registerReducer, registerMiddleware or\nregisterEffect was never part of that set, and no caller of\nreplaceReducers(myReducers) means \"and also delete the slice devtools mounted,\nalong with its state\".\n\nThe old reading was the literal one and the useful one is \"replace mine\". It\nmade the HMR line core''s own docstring recommends delete a library''s slice and\nits state on the first file save, with no error, no warning and no diagnostic:\nthe feature worked until the developer saved a file.\n\nProvenance is recorded internally on every registration. No public signature\ntakes it and no library declares it, because correctness must not depend on\nanyone remembering to pass a string. That is also why owner is introspection\nonly: a library that forgot to pass one would otherwise lose its state.\n\nThe in-repo victim is store.call(). Its reply listener is a pattern effect\nregistered for the lifetime of the call, and replaceEffects cleared both\nregistries wholesale, so a reload mid-call did not fail the call, it hung to the\nidle timeout with nothing pointing at the file save. That listener is now the\nstore''s own and survives even { scope: \"all\" }, because a harness resetting a\nstore never means \"and abandon the call awaiting a reply\". Both regression\ntests hang for five seconds against the old behaviour rather than merely\nasserting a flag.\n\n{ scope: \"all\" } restores the previous semantics exactly. hotReplace forwards\nit to all three, since it is the documented HMR entry point and one flag should\nbe enough.\n\nA collision throws before anything is mutated, naming the slice and its owner. An\napplication authoring a slice a library owns is a real mistake, a silent takeover\nis the worst outcome, and a half-applied replace would be worse than a refusal.\n\nMiddleware order after a preserving replace is reproduced rather than incidental:\nnew spec entries first, retained ones after, matching where they sat before. A\ndynamic auth guard moving from first to last changes which events get vetoed.\n\nreplaceReducers now broadcasts when the state root changed, which registerReducer\nhas always done and this never did, so a React tree stopped rendering stale state\nafter a reload. Gated on root identity.\n\nThree smaller fixes fall out: effectMeta is pruned per dropped effect instead of\nnever, the registerMiddleware disposer splices by entry identity instead of\nindexOf on the function, and a snapshot that predates a runtime slice no longer\nwarns about a slice it could not have known about.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"dee3beb7f9e9184715a9043311a570793c8f0455","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/dee3beb7f9e9184715a9043311a570793c8f0455"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e","verification":{"payload":"tree dee3beb7f9e9184715a9043311a570793c8f0455\nparent 05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790416108 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790416108 -0600\n\nfeat(core)!: registrations made after construction survive replace*\n\nreplace* exists to replace what the application authored. A reducer, middleware\nor effect a library installed with registerReducer, registerMiddleware or\nregisterEffect was never part of that set, and no caller of\nreplaceReducers(myReducers) means \"and also delete the slice devtools mounted,\nalong with its state\".\n\nThe old reading was the literal one and the useful one is \"replace mine\". It\nmade the HMR line core''s own docstring recommends delete a library''s slice and\nits state on the first file save, with no error, no warning and no diagnostic:\nthe feature worked until the developer saved a file.\n\nProvenance is recorded internally on every registration. No public signature\ntakes it and no library declares it, because correctness must not depend on\nanyone remembering to pass a string. That is also why owner is introspection\nonly: a library that forgot to pass one would otherwise lose its state.\n\nThe in-repo victim is store.call(). Its reply listener is a pattern effect\nregistered for the lifetime of the call, and replaceEffects cleared both\nregistries wholesale, so a reload mid-call did not fail the call, it hung to the\nidle timeout with nothing pointing at the file save. That listener is now the\nstore''s own and survives even { scope: \"all\" }, because a harness resetting a\nstore never means \"and abandon the call awaiting a reply\". Both regression\ntests hang for five seconds against the old behaviour rather than merely\nasserting a flag.\n\n{ scope: \"all\" } restores the previous semantics exactly. hotReplace forwards\nit to all three, since it is the documented HMR entry point and one flag should\nbe enough.\n\nA collision throws before anything is mutated, naming the slice and its owner. An\napplication authoring a slice a library owns is a real mistake, a silent takeover\nis the worst outcome, and a half-applied replace would be worse than a refusal.\n\nMiddleware order after a preserving replace is reproduced rather than incidental:\nnew spec entries first, retained ones after, matching where they sat before. A\ndynamic auth guard moving from first to last changes which events get vetoed.\n\nreplaceReducers now broadcasts when the state root changed, which registerReducer\nhas always done and this never did, so a React tree stopped rendering stale state\nafter a reload. Gated on root identity.\n\nThree smaller fixes fall out: effectMeta is pruned per dropped effect instead of\nnever, the registerMiddleware disposer splices by entry identity instead of\nindexOf on the function, and a snapshot that predates a runtime slice no longer\nwarns about a slice it could not have known about.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9XjcAQCRQCyDJjXmSy2AxR2XD1NlajymeZeQNOGYnhDXLgKpgwEAuT56mUWjKHPd\ndfzZKDVMwjPHxab86TSbDT7k7fdgpgc=\n=8KpM\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDg2MTdmYzA5MzBlMmY1MTEzMWFkNjdjMDhmNjhhMTdjMGU1NmJjOGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d","sha":"05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d"}],"sha":"8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/8617fc0930e2f51131ad67c08f68a17c0e56bc8e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:34:54Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:34:54Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"test(react): pin that useEvent is unaffected by subscription identity\n\nCore now stores an entry per onEvent subscription rather than the bare handler\nin a Set. React never hit the old dedup, because useEvent registers a fresh\narrow created inside the effect callback rather than the caller''s function, so\ntwo calls have always produced two distinct references. This keeps it that way:\nif the wrapper were ever hoisted or memoised, two calls sharing a handler would\nsilently collapse into one subscription and one of the disposers would take the\nother''s with it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"ed8accf9354081b6513f77beba15b0b8534a2979","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/ed8accf9354081b6513f77beba15b0b8534a2979"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d","verification":{"payload":"tree ed8accf9354081b6513f77beba15b0b8534a2979\nparent 0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790415294 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790415294 -0600\n\ntest(react): pin that useEvent is unaffected by subscription identity\n\nCore now stores an entry per onEvent subscription rather than the bare handler\nin a Set. React never hit the old dedup, because useEvent registers a fresh\narrow created inside the effect callback rather than the caller''s function, so\ntwo calls have always produced two distinct references. This keeps it that way:\nif the wrapper were ever hoisted or memoised, two calls sharing a handler would\nsilently collapse into one subscription and one of the disposers would take the\nother''s with it.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgQAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9aMLAQDHeN6odaNlkXHJsUIJDONoJk5EzQrbB8XG/faz1WuamgD/Sk/Co2e8OHQ1\nE0kRMgWcLA4zIVkleFRJnI1OaXzUYgM=\n=2B1g\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDA1ZGZhZDhhOGRmMmNlOTI3YzYwZDkwYWUwMjFiZGNmOWMyOTg0NWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd","sha":"0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd"}],"sha":"05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/05dfad8a8df2ce927c60d90ae021bdcf9c29845d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:15:55Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:15:55Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"chore(core): refresh the published size table\n\nThe replay opt-in adds a subscriber entry per subscription and the isReplaying\ngetter, so { createStore } moves from 10.1 KB to 10.2 KB gated and 9.3 to 9.5\nshipped. The table is gated, so a stale one fails the build rather than\nquietly publishing a number that is no longer true.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"98c1be123082bfef89242fb61da5dc4dbf0fbd4e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/98c1be123082bfef89242fb61da5dc4dbf0fbd4e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd","verification":{"payload":"tree 98c1be123082bfef89242fb61da5dc4dbf0fbd4e\nparent d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790414155 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790414155 -0600\n\nchore(core): refresh the published size table\n\nThe replay opt-in adds a subscriber entry per subscription and the isReplaying\ngetter, so { createStore } moves from 10.1 KB to 10.2 KB gated and 9.3 to 9.5\nshipped. The table is gated, so a stale one fails the build rather than\nquietly publishing a number that is no longer true.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9RpVAQCxnpEtiRg5aTR63IykJlN9qzzbcAaUwAO7aYQ3xNdjQgD/TMyC9VLN6Dpm\nuMSLlepV+Zj1FMoLeeaB7HFBVQ5c1Ak=\n=XXAx\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDBhOGNhMGY5NTA2ODc4MTA3MzYwYTU0OTQwMDFjMzQwYTZmOGEyZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7","sha":"d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7"}],"sha":"0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0a8ca0f9506878107360a5494001c340a6f8a2dd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:15:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:15:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(react): useEvent forwards the replay opt-in, and a real store proves it\n\nCore stopped notifying event subscribers during replay, and useEvent had no\nway to pass the opt-in through, so a component that legitimately derives view\nstate from the event stream could not ask for replayed events at all.\n\nThe effect''s dependency array takes options?.duringReplay, never options. An\nobject literal is a new reference on every render, so depending on it would\nunsubscribe and resubscribe each time. That loop leaves the subscription\nlooking correct at every point you might inspect it, which is why it gets its\nown regression test rather than being left to the others to notice.\n\nAdds tests/integration/replay-useEvent.test.tsx against a real store. This is\nthe only test in the package that would catch a regression in core''s\nnotification rule. createMockStore is a structural cast that reimplements\nphase matching locally, so it neither fails to compile when StoreInstance grows\nnor reflects what core actually does: all 366 lines of mock-based useEvent\ntests would stay green while core went back to notifying on every scrub. The\nmock is the thing being bypassed, so it cannot be the thing that verifies it.\n\nThe mock is still taught the rule, so it can show the hook forwards the flag,\nand gains the isReplaying member rather than leaving it undefined behind the\ncast. Existing assertions on onEvent''s arity are updated for the new argument.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"d21bd1c31a692d9f8fd7e9e9c9c86dae8467ec2e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/d21bd1c31a692d9f8fd7e9e9c9c86dae8467ec2e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7","verification":{"payload":"tree d21bd1c31a692d9f8fd7e9e9c9c86dae8467ec2e\nparent 0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790414128 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790414128 -0600\n\nfeat(react): useEvent forwards the replay opt-in, and a real store proves it\n\nCore stopped notifying event subscribers during replay, and useEvent had no\nway to pass the opt-in through, so a component that legitimately derives view\nstate from the event stream could not ask for replayed events at all.\n\nThe effect''s dependency array takes options?.duringReplay, never options. An\nobject literal is a new reference on every render, so depending on it would\nunsubscribe and resubscribe each time. That loop leaves the subscription\nlooking correct at every point you might inspect it, which is why it gets its\nown regression test rather than being left to the others to notice.\n\nAdds tests/integration/replay-useEvent.test.tsx against a real store. This is\nthe only test in the package that would catch a regression in core''s\nnotification rule. createMockStore is a structural cast that reimplements\nphase matching locally, so it neither fails to compile when StoreInstance grows\nnor reflects what core actually does: all 366 lines of mock-based useEvent\ntests would stay green while core went back to notifying on every scrub. The\nmock is the thing being bypassed, so it cannot be the thing that verifies it.\n\nThe mock is still taught the rule, so it can show the hook forwards the flag,\nand gains the isReplaying member rather than leaving it undefined behind the\ncast. Existing assertions on onEvent''s arity are updated for the new argument.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9brWAQCvRl7g4PWrBYyTdn0S1F2TjG6+0Kbx7EuTq3HwHH1mFQEA/lWhaLq8Hvos\nt+Nszcji1z7iVCihb/jzUz96PRV35w4=\n=M8Mv\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGQ2MGVjYjk3MmE5M2Q5YjVlZDhjYjcwZDVhZGM5ZDg5YTgzYzljYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3","sha":"0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3"}],"sha":"d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d60ecb972a93d9b5ed8cb70d5adc9d89a83c9ca7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:15:16Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:15:16Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core)!: replay no longer notifies event subscribers unless opted in\n\n__replayEvents ran every onEvent handler exactly as a live event would. The\nreplay loop''s own comment enumerates what it skips, middleware, effects, dedup\nand DevTools logging, and event subscribers were simply missing from that list.\n\nSo in any application configured with devtools: { allowReplay: true },\nscrubbing the timeline re-published to peers, re-wrote to sockets and re-fired\nanalytics for events that were not happening again. Nothing inside a handler\ncould tell the difference: the replay flag was private, no flag was stamped on\nthe event, and the handler signature had nowhere to carry one.\n\nA subscriber that legitimately wants replayed events, meaning one deriving view\nstate purely from the event stream and performing no I/O, opts in with\n{ duringReplay: true }. isReplaying is added for anything that must branch\nrather than skip.\n\nThe flag is saved and restored rather than set and cleared to false, because\n__replayEvents calls __applyExternalState first and clearing on the inner\ncall''s way out would unset it for the whole event loop that follows. It is\nrestored in a finally: left stuck at true by a throwing reducer, the store\nwould silence every subscriber from then on, a debugging operation permanently\nbreaking the application it was debugging.\n\nState fidelity is untouched. Reducers produce state, and coarse subscribe\nlisteners and connect subscriptions keep firing so a UI can follow the scrub.\nThe connect gap is deliberate and documented: silencing it would stop\ntime-travel showing anything.\n\nRegistries now store an entry per subscription rather than the bare handler.\nThat is where the opt-in lives, and it incidentally fixes two subscriptions\nsharing one handler function being a single Set member, where disposing either\nremoved both.\n\nOne existing test asserted the old behaviour and is inverted.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"2a7717e71cf2343cb4fc240d805441a5e5b4e04b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/2a7717e71cf2343cb4fc240d805441a5e5b4e04b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a7717e71cf2343cb4fc240d805441a5e5b4e04b\nparent 3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790414116 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790414116 -0600\n\nfeat(core)!: replay no longer notifies event subscribers unless opted in\n\n__replayEvents ran every onEvent handler exactly as a live event would. The\nreplay loop''s own comment enumerates what it skips, middleware, effects, dedup\nand DevTools logging, and event subscribers were simply missing from that list.\n\nSo in any application configured with devtools: { allowReplay: true },\nscrubbing the timeline re-published to peers, re-wrote to sockets and re-fired\nanalytics for events that were not happening again. Nothing inside a handler\ncould tell the difference: the replay flag was private, no flag was stamped on\nthe event, and the handler signature had nowhere to carry one.\n\nA subscriber that legitimately wants replayed events, meaning one deriving view\nstate purely from the event stream and performing no I/O, opts in with\n{ duringReplay: true }. isReplaying is added for anything that must branch\nrather than skip.\n\nThe flag is saved and restored rather than set and cleared to false, because\n__replayEvents calls __applyExternalState first and clearing on the inner\ncall''s way out would unset it for the whole event loop that follows. It is\nrestored in a finally: left stuck at true by a throwing reducer, the store\nwould silence every subscriber from then on, a debugging operation permanently\nbreaking the application it was debugging.\n\nState fidelity is untouched. Reducers produce state, and coarse subscribe\nlisteners and connect subscriptions keep firing so a UI can follow the scrub.\nThe connect gap is deliberate and documented: silencing it would stop\ntime-travel showing anything.\n\nRegistries now store an entry per subscription rather than the bare handler.\nThat is where the opt-in lives, and it incidentally fixes two subscriptions\nsharing one handler function being a single Set member, where disposing either\nremoved both.\n\nOne existing test asserted the old behaviour and is inverted.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9d9bAQCz5lZHvngBYpkRsQ7op/fgXmhnY7iIO2gGdOrokAd0lAEA7u78VDftix9t\nDC3vULNjDKMKbIqmIn9HDb6DA3G6ugE=\n=1Vxg\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDBkMjcwYmM4NmY4YTcwZWQyMmVjMTdmNjk0NmQ2MGJhNDg3MDVhZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f","sha":"3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f"}],"sha":"0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/0d270bc86f8a70ed22ec17f6946d60ba48705ae3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:05:34Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T09:05:34Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"docs(core): regenerate the reference, and correct what the veto change made untrue\n\nThe API reference is committed, so a signature change leaves it stating\nsomething false until it is regenerated. MiddlewareFunction now reads\nboolean | void with the reasoning attached, PersistencePhase carries its new\n\"encode\" member, and the fifteen new type and builder exports have pages.\n\nTwo prose claims were wrong rather than merely stale. The testing guide said\nmiddleware \"returns a boolean\", and the core README said the same in an inline\ncomment; under the new rule returning nothing is both legal and the right thing\nfor middleware that only observes. Both now say only an explicit false vetoes,\nin English and Spanish.\n\nThe guide also gained a line about testing the allow path. A guard that stops\nrejecting is a silent failure, and so is one that rejects everything, and the\nold text only prompted for the second.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"8796563ed429cbfadb2e8be73cc40311bf6ddc9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/8796563ed429cbfadb2e8be73cc40311bf6ddc9d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f","verification":{"payload":"tree 8796563ed429cbfadb2e8be73cc40311bf6ddc9d\nparent 1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790413534 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790413534 -0600\n\ndocs(core): regenerate the reference, and correct what the veto change made untrue\n\nThe API reference is committed, so a signature change leaves it stating\nsomething false until it is regenerated. MiddlewareFunction now reads\nboolean | void with the reasoning attached, PersistencePhase carries its new\n\"encode\" member, and the fifteen new type and builder exports have pages.\n\nTwo prose claims were wrong rather than merely stale. The testing guide said\nmiddleware \"returns a boolean\", and the core README said the same in an inline\ncomment; under the new rule returning nothing is both legal and the right thing\nfor middleware that only observes. Both now say only an explicit false vetoes,\nin English and Spanish.\n\nThe guide also gained a line about testing the allow path. A guard that stops\nrejecting is a silent failure, and so is one that rejects everything, and the\nold text only prompted for the second.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritgAAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ZtWAQCQQvA3a5+IkcXh9/aYkm5nlPfo5ZcRSJG3qP2Df6ZOcQEA19fOzsW7mn3T\n8DaWxAz3A0vqKr4K9kMXhzTU/Nxfiw4=\n=qD3j\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDNjYzc4MzBlMTQ2ZmI2N2FlZTY0ODIwNzAxOTI3ZmY3YzRkMzc3N2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97","sha":"1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97"}],"sha":"3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/3cc7830e146fb67aee64820701927ff7c4d3777f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:25:56Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:25:56Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(core): dedup fingerprints route through the codec\n\nJSON.stringify produced two opposite failures on the one path whose whole job\nis deciding whether two payloads are the same. A Map, Set, ArrayBuffer or typed\narray stringified to {}, so distinct payloads collided and the second event was\nsilently swallowed, which is precisely what the README says Yoltra refuses to\ndo by default. A BigInt or a cyclic payload threw, hit a timestamp-and-random\nfallback, and was never deduplicated however identical.\n\nTwo further collisions on the primitive fast path: null and undefined both\nproduced ::null, and String(payload) made the number 1 and the string \"1\" the\nsame event, as it did true and \"true\".\n\nPlain-object keys are sorted, because insertion order is not content. Array and\nMap order is left alone: their order is semantic, and normalising it would make\ngenuinely different payloads collide, which drops real events rather than\nmerely failing to dedupe. That is the worse direction, so the sort is deliberate\nin what it does not touch.\n\nA payload past the fingerprint node budget is never deduplicated. Two large\npayloads differing only past the cutoff would otherwise collide; refusing costs\na duplicate, which is the safe failure and matches what already happened to\npayloads the old code could not serialize.\n\nExtracted to store/fingerprint.ts following the matching.ts and paths.ts\nprecedent. The walk runs only when dedupWindowMs is above zero, which is off by\ndefault, and an explicit dedupKey bypasses fingerprinting entirely.\n\nBundle cost is not opt-in, though: { createStore } grows 9.0 KB to 10.1 KB\ngated, 8.3 to 9.3 shipped, because the codec is now reachable from the store\nrather than only from persistence and the barrel. Size tables regenerated.\n\nOne existing test asserted that a cyclic payload is never deduped, which is the\ndefect this fixes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"993edcbf51d28406d3812fa54c9ff4b0ca2d0a72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/993edcbf51d28406d3812fa54c9ff4b0ca2d0a72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97","verification":{"payload":"tree 993edcbf51d28406d3812fa54c9ff4b0ca2d0a72\nparent 21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790411156 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790411156 -0600\n\nfix(core): dedup fingerprints route through the codec\n\nJSON.stringify produced two opposite failures on the one path whose whole job\nis deciding whether two payloads are the same. A Map, Set, ArrayBuffer or typed\narray stringified to {}, so distinct payloads collided and the second event was\nsilently swallowed, which is precisely what the README says Yoltra refuses to\ndo by default. A BigInt or a cyclic payload threw, hit a timestamp-and-random\nfallback, and was never deduplicated however identical.\n\nTwo further collisions on the primitive fast path: null and undefined both\nproduced ::null, and String(payload) made the number 1 and the string \"1\" the\nsame event, as it did true and \"true\".\n\nPlain-object keys are sorted, because insertion order is not content. Array and\nMap order is left alone: their order is semantic, and normalising it would make\ngenuinely different payloads collide, which drops real events rather than\nmerely failing to dedupe. That is the worse direction, so the sort is deliberate\nin what it does not touch.\n\nA payload past the fingerprint node budget is never deduplicated. Two large\npayloads differing only past the cutoff would otherwise collide; refusing costs\na duplicate, which is the safe failure and matches what already happened to\npayloads the old code could not serialize.\n\nExtracted to store/fingerprint.ts following the matching.ts and paths.ts\nprecedent. The walk runs only when dedupWindowMs is above zero, which is off by\ndefault, and an explicit dedupKey bypasses fingerprinting entirely.\n\nBundle cost is not opt-in, though: { createStore } grows 9.0 KB to 10.1 KB\ngated, 8.3 to 9.3 shipped, because the codec is now reachable from the store\nrather than only from persistence and the barrel. Size tables regenerated.\n\nOne existing test asserted that a cyclic payload is never deduped, which is the\ndefect this fixes.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritfwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9ZMKAP9QUMk6cI/f0Kl8r9u4IPFAS/sOA0++Q01ZrOZWuZ4k8wEAxz6yuELAEjex\njDr5v6dfXdUS5jZILRS3bLXNxx5bjww=\n=GH6T\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDFjMGUzMjMwODcyYmI2YTg0ZmVhNTM0MmMyYzM1NmEyZmQ2ZjBmOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939","sha":"21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939"}],"sha":"1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/1c0e3230872bb6a84fea5342c2c356a2fd6f0f97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:25:19Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:25:19Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(core): codec tags binary values and refuses exotic prototypes loudly\n\nThe walker fell through to Object.entries with no prototype guard, so a\nUint8Array encoded as {\"0\":1,\"1\":2}, an ArrayBuffer as {}, and a class instance\nas a plain object with its prototype gone. None of it appeared in\nEncodeReport.unsupported, so nothing anywhere said a value had been lost. Both\nconsumers were exposed: persistence encodes on write, and time-travel applies\ndecoded state to the live store.\n\nAll nine typed arrays plus DataView and ArrayBuffer now round-trip through one\nbinary tag carrying the constructor name. Base64 rather than a number array:\none node against 100,000, and about 1.37 JSON characters per byte against 3.5,\nwhich is what decides whether a bounded snapshot fits. Encoding covers the\nview''s own window, not its whole backing buffer, so a decoded view no longer\nshares a buffer with its former siblings.\n\nDecoding resolves the constructor through a frozen null-prototype allow-list\nread with hasOwnProperty.call. Avoiding globalThis[kind] is not sufficient on\nits own: kind arrives off a socket, and a frozen object literal still answers\n\"constructor\" from Object.prototype, so new Object(buffer) handed the buffer\nstraight back. Six hostile kinds are pinned.\n\nAn unrecognised exotic is reported and tagged with its constructor name while\nkeeping its own enumerable properties. A bare marker would decode to undefined,\nwhich is more destructive than the bug: a class instance already round-tripped\nas a plain object carrying its props, and a data-loss fix should not lose more\nthan what it fixes.\n\nfreezeState now passes binary views through. Object.freeze on a view with\nelements is a TypeError by language rule, so the development freeze threw at\nstore construction and bytes could not be kept in slice state at all. There is\nnothing to deep-freeze either way: the contents are numbers, not a reachable\nobject graph. Immutability for a view is reference-level, as it already is for\nMap and Set.\n\nPersistence stops discarding the encode report. Losses reach onError under a\nnew \"encode\" phase, its own rather than \"write\" because a serialization loss\nand a full disk need different responses. Reporting never blocks the write.\n\nNote for a rollback: state written here containing binary carries a tag 0.7.x\ndoes not recognise, and its decoder returns undefined for an unknown tag, so\ndowngrading loses that slice silently.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"6fbf7f5e57e849026597c0dbbaa60847f5b00214","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/6fbf7f5e57e849026597c0dbbaa60847f5b00214"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939","verification":{"payload":"tree 6fbf7f5e57e849026597c0dbbaa60847f5b00214\nparent d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790411119 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790411119 -0600\n\nfix(core): codec tags binary values and refuses exotic prototypes loudly\n\nThe walker fell through to Object.entries with no prototype guard, so a\nUint8Array encoded as {\"0\":1,\"1\":2}, an ArrayBuffer as {}, and a class instance\nas a plain object with its prototype gone. None of it appeared in\nEncodeReport.unsupported, so nothing anywhere said a value had been lost. Both\nconsumers were exposed: persistence encodes on write, and time-travel applies\ndecoded state to the live store.\n\nAll nine typed arrays plus DataView and ArrayBuffer now round-trip through one\nbinary tag carrying the constructor name. Base64 rather than a number array:\none node against 100,000, and about 1.37 JSON characters per byte against 3.5,\nwhich is what decides whether a bounded snapshot fits. Encoding covers the\nview''s own window, not its whole backing buffer, so a decoded view no longer\nshares a buffer with its former siblings.\n\nDecoding resolves the constructor through a frozen null-prototype allow-list\nread with hasOwnProperty.call. Avoiding globalThis[kind] is not sufficient on\nits own: kind arrives off a socket, and a frozen object literal still answers\n\"constructor\" from Object.prototype, so new Object(buffer) handed the buffer\nstraight back. Six hostile kinds are pinned.\n\nAn unrecognised exotic is reported and tagged with its constructor name while\nkeeping its own enumerable properties. A bare marker would decode to undefined,\nwhich is more destructive than the bug: a class instance already round-tripped\nas a plain object carrying its props, and a data-loss fix should not lose more\nthan what it fixes.\n\nfreezeState now passes binary views through. Object.freeze on a view with\nelements is a TypeError by language rule, so the development freeze threw at\nstore construction and bytes could not be kept in slice state at all. There is\nnothing to deep-freeze either way: the contents are numbers, not a reachable\nobject graph. Immutability for a view is reference-level, as it already is for\nMap and Set.\n\nPersistence stops discarding the encode report. Losses reach onError under a\nnew \"encode\" phase, its own rather than \"write\" because a serialization loss\nand a full disk need different responses. Reporting never blocks the write.\n\nNote for a rollback: state written here containing binary carries a tag 0.7.x\ndoes not recognise, and its decoder returns undefined for an unknown tag, so\ndowngrading loses that slice silently.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritfwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9Rv1AP0aNQckH9GSjn+mm0SDiIHyG6t6xbpCVgPPG1+L2gAmUAD/SCwLcgvMPWWQ\nFztITSNKqqy8WWew7BUOwcHlAaGw1AU=\n=VRek\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKDIxODU1YzdkMGVmMTU3ZWM4NGZjYmZlYjFhMjAxMjQ1NWM4OWI5Mzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014","sha":"d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014"}],"sha":"21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/21855c7d0ef157ec84fcbfeb1a2012455c89b939"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:24:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T08:24:28Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"fix(core)!: middleware vetoes only on an explicit false\n\nThe veto test was `!result`, so `undefined`, `0`, `\"\"`, `null` and `NaN` all\nvetoed. Middleware that did its work and fell off the end silently swallowed\nevery event it matched, and the symptom is reducers quietly stopping for one\nchannel, which reads as a routing, `when` or registration-order problem. Nothing\nabout it points at the missing return.\n\nThe documented contract already said `false`, so this makes the documentation\ntrue rather than changing what it promises.\n\nMiddlewareFunction returns boolean | void to match: under the new rule an\nomitted return is correct, so making the compiler demand one would be wrong. It\nwas boolean only because any falsy value used to veto.\n\nA middleware that throws still vetoes, on the grounds that a guard which crashed\nhas not decided the event is safe, but the log now names the event and states\nthe consequence. One existing test pinned the old message string.\n\nAlso exports EmptyEventMap, which the empty-map branch of EMAddOf needs: the\nbare {} type accepts any non-nullish value, including 0 and \"\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"e5e7275c62a72782e723b7f92317ca61b5131f2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/e5e7275c62a72782e723b7f92317ca61b5131f2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014","verification":{"payload":"tree e5e7275c62a72782e723b7f92317ca61b5131f2f\nparent d844d0a7b193daf9d9b07c586246b43f66fbaab3\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790411068 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790411068 -0600\n\nfix(core)!: middleware vetoes only on an explicit false\n\nThe veto test was `!result`, so `undefined`, `0`, `\"\"`, `null` and `NaN` all\nvetoed. Middleware that did its work and fell off the end silently swallowed\nevery event it matched, and the symptom is reducers quietly stopping for one\nchannel, which reads as a routing, `when` or registration-order problem. Nothing\nabout it points at the missing return.\n\nThe documented contract already said `false`, so this makes the documentation\ntrue rather than changing what it promises.\n\nMiddlewareFunction returns boolean | void to match: under the new rule an\nomitted return is correct, so making the compiler demand one would be wrong. It\nwas boolean only because any falsy value used to veto.\n\nA middleware that throws still vetoes, on the grounds that a guard which crashed\nhas not decided the event is safe, but the log now names the event and states\nthe consequence. One existing test pinned the old message string.\n\nAlso exports EmptyEventMap, which the empty-map branch of EMAddOf needs: the\nbare {} type accepts any non-nullish value, including 0 and \"\".\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritfwAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9Z/5AQDUhoUO9N/4KUlxx/c91C3wZ4CYukeMbeIQuPfICaBuAwD/YMFXlkGNpqVg\n63ZMwO1/DGjTYvfGYFXMhoxSf2zCkgU=\n=eTq3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGQ4MGQ4NGNiNjYxNmJiYTU0ZmQ4MzJjMDg0ZjA1NzEyM2JmZTIwMTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/d844d0a7b193daf9d9b07c586246b43f66fbaab3","sha":"d844d0a7b193daf9d9b07c586246b43f66fbaab3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d844d0a7b193daf9d9b07c586246b43f66fbaab3"}],"sha":"d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d80d84cb6616bba54fd832c084f057123bfe2014"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/commits/d844d0a7b193daf9d9b07c586246b43f66fbaab3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:12:20Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T07:12:20Z","email":"manu@erael.com.mx","name":"pixerael"},"message":"feat(core): spec builders and the type machinery for post-construction registration\n\nA store decorated after construction currently loses the types of whatever it\ngained: registerReducer takes a plain string and returns a bare disposer, so a\nslice mounted by a library is invisible to every hook, and a spec targeting a\nchannel the application''s event map does not contain needs a cast at each site.\n\nThe obstacle is that the added event map cannot be inferred from a spec''s `when`,\nwhich carries channel and type strings and no payload types, and TypeScript has\nno partial type-argument inference. defineSlice, defineMiddleware and defineEffect\npark it in a value position instead, where inference works, so a registration site\nneeds no type argument and no cast. They are identity at runtime.\n\nAdds the widening types this rests on, with declare-only registration surfaces in\nboth packages so the machinery is proven before anything implements it. No public\nbehaviour changes; nothing yet returns a widened store.\n\nSatisfiesSlices intersects with unknown rather than any. Satisfying the\nS extends Record<R, any> constraint with any collapsed every slice''s state to any\nwhile still compiling, which is the class of silent failure the feature exists to\nremove. The compiler cannot derive the constraint itself: WidenState and WidenNames\nboth branch on `string extends N` and it checks each in isolation.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>","tree":{"sha":"42368fda5ccf9fd70d42c1b2b746a62e5dcb3896","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/trees/42368fda5ccf9fd70d42c1b2b746a62e5dcb3896"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/yoltra/yoltra/git/commits/d844d0a7b193daf9d9b07c586246b43f66fbaab3","verification":{"payload":"tree 42368fda5ccf9fd70d42c1b2b746a62e5dcb3896\nparent edcad20975050f6b9db42383f4b55d2fd934b75f\nauthor pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790406740 -0600\ncommitter pixerael <manu@erael.com.mx> 1790406740 -0600\n\nfeat(core): spec builders and the type machinery for post-construction registration\n\nA store decorated after construction currently loses the types of whatever it\ngained: registerReducer takes a plain string and returns a bare disposer, so a\nslice mounted by a library is invisible to every hook, and a spec targeting a\nchannel the application''s event map does not contain needs a cast at each site.\n\nThe obstacle is that the added event map cannot be inferred from a spec''s `when`,\nwhich carries channel and type strings and no payload types, and TypeScript has\nno partial type-argument inference. defineSlice, defineMiddleware and defineEffect\npark it in a value position instead, where inference works, so a registration site\nneeds no type argument and no cast. They are identity at runtime.\n\nAdds the widening types this rests on, with declare-only registration surfaces in\nboth packages so the machinery is proven before anything implements it. No public\nbehaviour changes; nothing yet returns a widened store.\n\nSatisfiesSlices intersects with unknown rather than any. Satisfying the\nS extends Record<R, any> constraint with any collapsed every slice''s state to any\nwhile still compiling, which is the class of silent failure the feature exists to\nremove. The compiler cannot derive the constraint itself: WidenState and WidenNames\nboth branch on `string extends N` and it checks each in isolation.\n\nSigned-off-by: Manu <manu@erael.com.mx>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niHUEABYKAB0WIQRM+b+qhsfVhele/BlcnB4y1kQ39QUCaritfgAKCRBcnB4y1kQ3\n9dt9AP9wKSlmk2mq77qqscTF5/lIllqrwTnOQKNpdljuCGfmkgD/T5VCUU32qF4D\nmQjpe82g88p8el/6oBAOgYUznpK2LA0=\n=LuLh\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-27T06:05:41Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/228319905?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/pixerael","id":228319905,"login":"pixerael","node_id":"U_kgDODZvioQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/pixerael","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/d844d0a7b193daf9d9b07c586246b43f66fbaab3","node_id":"C_kwDORVItEtoAKGQ4NDRkMGE3YjE5M2RhZjlkOWIwN2M1ODYyNDZiNDNmNjZmYmFhYjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/yoltra/yoltra/commit/edcad20975050f6b9db42383f4b55d2fd934b75f","sha":"e