712d43f8eae53180e0cea5ddb302aee08b7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jensenbox/ha-arctic-spa/commits/ed987712d43f8eae53180e0cea5ddb302aee08b7"}],"sha":"395a752311142592b10b33ec2f6722eb5268a285","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jensenbox/ha-arctic-spa/commits/395a752311142592b10b33ec2f6722eb5268a285"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/189265?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jensenbox","id":189265,"login":"jensenbox","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4OTI2NQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jensenbox","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jensenbox/ha-arctic-spa/commits/ed987712d43f8eae53180e0cea5ddb302aee08b7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T18:47:20Z","email":"christian@closient.com","name":"Christian Jensen"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T18:47:20Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Fix HACS review findings: raise HA version floor to 2024.8.0, stop persisting API key material in unique_id (#55)\n\nHome Assistant 2024.1.0 predates entry.runtime_data (2024.6) and the\nconfig_entry param on DataUpdateCoordinator (2024.8), used in\n__init__.py and coordinator.py respectively -- an install on the\ndeclared floor would hard-fail at setup. Raise hacs.json''s floor to\n2024.8.0 to match.\n\nThe config flow persisted the first 16 characters of the user''s API\nkey as the config entry''s unique_id, exposing partial credential\nmaterial anywhere entry metadata is shown. Hash the full key instead;\nsame dedup behavior, no credential material retained.","tree":{"sha":"ba970902b9d924c9ef048f5cfa1a91ed3a608710","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jensenbox/ha-arctic-spa/git/trees/ba970902b9d924c9ef048f5cfa1a91ed3a608710"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jensenbox/ha-arctic-spa/git/commits/ed987712d43f8eae53180e0cea5ddb302aee08b7","verification":{"payload":"tree ba970902b9d924c9ef048f5cfa1a91ed3a608710\nparent 16436f466fe3891f5fbe781f8b2c738a70ce0716\nauthor Christian Jensen <christian@closient.com> 1789584440 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789584440 -0700\n\nFix HACS review findings: raise HA version floor to 2024.8.0, stop persisting API key material in unique_id (#55)\n\nHome Assistant 2024.1.0 predates entry.runtime_data (2024.6) and the\nconfig_entry param on DataUpdateCoordinator (2024.8), used in\n__init__.py and coordinator.py respectively -- an install on the\ndeclared floor would hard-fail at setup. Raise hacs.json''s floor to\n2024.8.0 to match.\n\nThe config flow persisted the first 16 characters of the user''s API\nkey as the config entry''s unique_id, exposing partial credential\nmaterial anywhere entry metadata is shown. Hash the full key instead;\nsame dedup behavior, no credential material retained.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqquQ4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAU5MQACnFbQR1aJ0dhqocV2vaitTQ\nwFUxiP4CQAW3uNV2f/vIpdeHTEzEBv9kUfiKDlp2rmLPsPaj/7k4zhP0esigdHcJ\nLC49aaf1bZA9nC9aAcQT1TdQMbOocueTQKhtbVA6EHLonNbtWpYowQEg3UGUb0MX\nEfG6LipZ3+LnsgCXeJApmeemD8oQvXRef2mo1TCJ2Pi9eoRWvk00Ne5fbrGvLu4Z\n1DvHWPOGy6ERhm5XAEiIjoMMX0RC0690oYpFswANId00zTc7h2DjpB3B50jWv5Vu\nAcucVmw3OX4jPmvMXFQpfCHElR882r5QmC/xajHqW51U45Z1mGgFW+xfulYn9srd\nIafpOQjb7t9QheRbdaOZPvnfgIjYu1f3+Yik6yFhDbcWNYpu9f