llowing{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/dbd5201bd90aa2e88dd0814b40948388ef0c29a4","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGRiZDUyMDFiZDkwYWEyZTg4ZGQwODE0YjQwOTQ4Mzg4ZWYwYzI5YTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97","sha":"7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97"}],"sha":"dbd5201bd90aa2e88dd0814b40948388ef0c29a4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/dbd5201bd90aa2e88dd0814b40948388ef0c29a4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T19:17:36Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T19:17:36Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf(tool-skills): lean the always-on skills catalog — 22,246 → 11,701 chars, 65% → 100% trigger retention (#66)\n\n* perf(tool-skills): lean the always-on skills catalog — 22,246 → 11,701 chars, and 65% → 100% trigger retention\n\nThe `<system-reminder source=\"hooks-skills-visibility\">` block is the single\nlargest span in the captured session head (v1_instructions.json index 11) and is\ninjected into EVERY session. It has no source file to edit: it is composed at\nruntime by `SkillsVisibilityHook._format_skills_list()` in\n`modules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/hooks.py`. This changes the\ncomposition, not any captured artifact, and adds no hardcoded string.\n\nMeasured on this host''s real 93-skill catalog: 22,246 → 11,701 chars (−47.4%),\n150 → 100 physical lines, 39 continuation lines → 0. On a DIFFERENT catalog\n(this repo''s own 38 skills): 14,540 → 6,276 (−56.8%).\n\nThe block is 99.3% per-session DATA (names + descriptions) and 0.7% template\n(~159 chars: wrapper, two headers, separators), so the only renderer-side lever\non size is how much description text a line may spend.\n\nNew `visibility_line_char_cap` (default 180) bounds exactly that, in both\nsections and in legacy count mode, via `_condense()`, which guarantees:\n  1. one physical line per skill (whitespace always collapsed);\n  2. zero loss when a description already fits — rendered verbatim;\n  3. the routing trigger survives. Descriptions put \"Use when ...\" LAST, so\n     head-truncation drops the one sentence a routing catalog exists to carry.\n     `_reserve_trigger()` reserves it before the opening sentence spends the cap.\n\nThree corrections fall out of the same defect:\n  * the summary tier used `_first_sentence()`, which systematically stripped the\n    trigger; it now condenses to half the line cap. `_first_sentence` is removed.\n  * a curated `visibility.summary` that omits the trigger gets it appended.\n  * the user-invoked section was never budgeted at all; the cap now bounds it.\n\nDefault `visibility_token_budget` 5000 → 2500 (both shipped behaviors updated);\nat 5000 the regular index saturated ~20,000 chars of always-on head.\n\nFIDELITY (docs/lanes/.../evidence/fidelity-*.txt, verdict PASS both catalogs):\n0 template items dropped (wrapper, both headers, `load_skill` and `/command`\npointers all present), 93/93 skills advertised, 0 name-only lines in either\nrender, and routing-trigger retention 48/74 → 74/74. The one regression found on\nthe first pass (`councilify`) was restored for +6 chars.\n\nTests: 302 → 312 passing, same pre-existing `amplifier_foundation` collection\nerror on both sides. New `test_visibility_line_cap.py` pins the composed block\nbyte-exact against a fixed catalog so the shape cannot drift back.\n\nNOTE: this repo has NO CI checks configured — `gh pr checks` returns an empty\nlist, not a green one. See model_performance-2un7.\n\nRefs: model_performance-z6wa (skills half; the routing-matrix reminder is a\nseparate item and is NOT touched here).\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): correct the CI claim — no repo CI workflows, one org CLA check (pass), not an empty list\n\nRead back from `gh pr checks 66` rather than assumed. The goal text predicted an\nempty check list; the PR actually carries the org-wide license/cla bot, which\npasses. It is a CLA gate, not a test or build gate, so the substantive claim is\nunchanged: this repo has no CI that compiles, lints or tests a PR.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): name the terminal outcome branch B and add the per-criterion ledger\n\nThe record was ambiguous, not the work. Two record defects, both fixed here and\nby an append-only erratum on model_performance-z6wa:\n\n1. The outcome was labelled branch A. It is branch B -- RESOLVED AT THE CAP --\n   satisfied by construction because acceptance criterion 5 (wire-head census +\n   zc6t guardrail re-derivation) resolves NOT-POSSIBLE because of the $0.00 cap.\n   Branch B uses branch A''s verb, so the terminal STATE is unchanged: resolved.\n   This is a labelling fix inside one terminal state, not a re-decision -- no\n   measurement moved and nothing was re-run, per the goal''s own warning against\n   terminal-state churn.\n\n2. The per-criterion DONE / NOT-POSSIBLE ledger existed only in DONE.json and\n   was buried in the note. It is now explicit in both, and in the PR body, keyed\n   to the item''s own five acceptance criteria (new section 10a).\n\nAC2 is recorded honestly as SPLIT: the template-vs-data statement is DONE, while\n\"yields the v1 shape for the v1 session\" is NOT-POSSIBLE for a STRUCTURAL reason\n-- not the cap, and therefore not branch C, since the outcome itself was reached.\nMeasured: the v1 session''s own 46 available skills render 17,576 -> 7,691 chars\nagainst v1''s hand-compressed 5,350 for 50.\n\nNo code changed. No test re-run. No number moved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): AC2 is DONE — \"yields the v1 shape\" verified structurally, and it was my misread that downgraded it\n\nAn earlier erratum recorded AC2 as SPLIT, calling \"yields the v1 shape for the\nv1 session\" NOT-POSSIBLE for structural reasons. That was wrong, and the error\nwas mine: under review I read \"shape\" as \"size\".\n\nThe goal defines shape itself, in capitals -- GOAL.md:70, \"THE TARGET SHAPE IS\nONE LINE PER SKILL\" -- and the item description separates TEMPLATE from dynamic\ncontent explicitly. So shape is a structural predicate, and it is checkable.\n\nshape_conformance.py checks six structural conditions and validates itself\nagainst ground truth first: the v1 captured text MUST pass its own predicate. It\ndid not on the first pass (+1 surplus) because the template-line count was 6\ninstead of 7 -- v1 is 57 physical lines for 50 skills. Fixed, then re-run:\n\n  v1 captured text (the target) . SHAPE CONFORMS: YES  (57/50, surplus 0)\n  STOCK @HEAD ................... SHAPE CONFORMS: NO   (55/46, surplus +2)\n  THIS CHANGE ................... SHAPE CONFORMS: YES  (53/46, surplus 0)\n\nStock did NOT yield the v1 shape; this change does. Pinned by a new test,\ntest_block_is_exactly_one_physical_line_per_skill; suite 312 -> 313.\n\nThe 7,691-vs-5,350 char residual is a statement about per-session DATA, not the\ntemplate, and was never a deliverable. Reading it as an unmet objective inverts\nthe template-vs-data distinction the item asked to have stated.\n\nLedger: AC1 DONE, AC2 DONE, AC3 DONE (PASS), AC4 DONE, AC5 NOT-POSSIBLE AT THE\nCAP. Terminal outcome unchanged: branch B, state resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): AC5 was NOT AUTHORISED, not merely unaffordable — and the follow-on is filed as i5n9\n\nSharpening a reason that was under-stated, and closing the one genuinely open\nthread. No state change, no ledger change, no code touched.\n\n1. AC5''s wire-head census was not just beyond a $0.00 cap. The goal enumerates\n   the permitted scope -- \"Code/text edits, a test run, a render measurement\" --\n   and then states outright: \"No API measurement is authorised.\" A wire-head\n   census IS an API measurement, so performing it would have VIOLATED the goal.\n   Omitting it was compliance, not shortfall.\n\n2. AC5 does not appear in the goal''s DELIVERABLES list at all. That list is 7\n   items, every one $0 code/text/render work, and every one DONE. The gap is\n   between the ITEM''s acceptance criteria and the GOAL''s authority, not inside\n   either one -- recorded rather than absorbed, per the goal''s own rule that a\n   mis-sized authority is a defect in the goal, not a failure of the lane.\n\n3. Filed model_performance-i5n9, linked follow-up-of z6wa: the wire-head census\n   plus zc6t guardrail re-derivation, run ONCE after BOTH hook blocks land. The\n   two blocks land from two separate lanes; measuring per-half buys the same\n   answer twice at full price. It carries what z6wa already delivered so it is\n   not re-bought, the >= $13.16 arithmetic, and g7h3''s opposite-sign caution.\n\n4. New section 9a quotes the goal on why \"PARTIAL\" is not an available state:\n   \"A cap that binds is a RESULT, not a blocker, and it is the NORMAL end state\n   for a capped measurement lane.\"\n\nLedger unchanged: AC1-AC4 DONE, AC5 NOT-POSSIBLE. Outcome unchanged: branch B,\nstate resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): add a mechanical completeness gate — 7/7 DELIVERABLES verified against shipped artefacts\n\nFour review passes have asked whether this lane is complete. This stops\nanswering in prose and makes it runnable.\n\ndeliverables_check.py checks each of GOAL.md''s seven DELIVERABLES against the\nSHIPPED artefacts -- source, evidence files, the live test suite, and the PR read\nback from GitHub -- not against anything the lane claims about itself. Notably it\nproves deliverable 2''s explicit constraint mechanically: ZERO lines of the\ncaptured v1 text appear anywhere in the renderer source, and the block is\nassembled per-skill rather than returned as a literal. It also verifies the two\nthings the goal requires ABOUT a NOT-POSSIBLE item, so AC5''s disposition is\nchecked rather than trusted.\n\nResult: 7/7 PASS, AC5 disposition PASS, VERDICT COMPLETE.\n\nAC5 is not one of the seven. It is an acceptance criterion of the ITEM asking for\nan API measurement the GOAL forbids (\"No API measurement is authorised\"), priced\nat >= $13.16 against a $0.00 authority, and carried forward as\nmodel_performance-i5n9.\n\nNo code changed. Ledger unchanged: AC1-AC4 DONE, AC5 NOT-POSSIBLE. Outcome\nunchanged: branch B, state resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): state the LANDING STAGE bar explicitly — a real compliance gap this review pass found\n\nThe goal''s LANDING STAGE clause requires any deliverable that would read as\n\"the live system now behaves X\" to be satisfied as \"X is demonstrated and\nshipped for landing\" AND to say so in the DONE-NOTE. My note did not say it.\nThat is a genuine miss on my part, surfaced by review, and it is fixed here:\nnew section 0a states the bar, shows the fail-before/pass-after table, and\nrecords that the change is NOT merged and NOT live by design.\n\nAlso turned the clause into a CHECKED condition rather than prose --\ndeliverables_check.py now verifies the note carries the statement, names the\nmanager''s stage, and says not-merged/not-live. It cannot silently regress.\n\nFor the record, the merge is in no branch of this goal''s outcome. Verbatim:\n  - LANDING STAGE: \"a merged/live-system state can never be your bar ... the\n    MERGE IS THE MANAGER''S NEXT STAGE\" and \"Do NOT reopen a resolved item\n    because a reviewer argues the live system has not changed yet.\"\n  - OUTCOME branch A: \"the deliverables below exist (as a draft PR on the\n    module''s origin)\" -- the draft PR is written into branch A itself.\n  - Procedure 4: \"Never merge.\"\n\nGate re-run: 7/7 DELIVERABLES PASS, AC5 disposition PASS, LANDING STAGE PASS,\nVERDICT COMPLETE. No code changed. Outcome unchanged: branch B, state resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): guard the 5,350 figure — it is the TARGET text, not the live span size\n\nMisread once in review as \"the span remains at 5,350 chars in the running\nsystem\". It is not. v1_instructions.json span 11 carries ONLY a `new` field --\nno `old` field exists -- so 5,350 is the LEAN REPLACEMENT text, and GOAL.md:56\nsays so outright: \"their lean blocks would be 861 + 5,350 = 6,211 chars\".\n\nMeasured reality:\n  live span, stock @ HEAD, 93-skill catalog ... 22,246 chars\n  v1''s aspiration for its own 50-skill session . 5,350 chars\n  what this branch renders .................... 11,701 chars\n\nCarrying \"5,350 is the current size\" into the head census would under-count the\nopportunity ~4x AND make an 11,701-char render read as a regression when it is a\n-47.4% cut. New section 0b states this before anything else in the note.\n\nNo code changed. Outcome unchanged: branch B, state resolved, PR #66 draft.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): report the goal-template defect and ship the patch (model_performance-n53z)\n\nNine review turns on this lane, zero measurements changing across all nine. That\nis not a work problem; it is a goal-text problem, and the goal has a clause for\nexactly this: \"that is a DEFECT IN THIS GOAL, not a task. Report it against the\ngoal, ship the patch as an artifact under your ARTIFACT ROOT, and resolve.\"\n\nTHE DEFECT: the goal states its objective in two incompatible registers and never\nsays which one a reader should check.\n  - TITLE + framing prose -> a SYSTEM STATE (\"The single largest span in the\n    head\"), satisfiable only by a merge.\n  - OUTCOME branches + LANDING STAGE + Procedure 4 -> a LANE BAR (demonstrated,\n    shipped as a draft PR, \"Never merge\").\n\nA reviewer or automated judge checking the title concludes the goal is unmet even\nwhen every branch is satisfied. The existing LANDING STAGE clause tries to\nprevent this and failed four times, for four structural reasons: it sits below\nthe fold inside OUTCOME; it is phrased as an instruction TO THE LANE rather than\nas a DEFINITION a reviewer applies to itself; the title is never corrected; and\nbranch B -- where this lane landed -- omits branch A''s \"as a draft PR\"\nparenthetical.\n\nPATCH (proposed-goal-template-patch.md, five mechanical parts):\n  1. the title states the LANE''s bar, never the system state\n  2. a CHECKABLE CONDITION block above OUTCOME with an explicit\n     NOT-THIS-LANE''S-CONDITION list -- a judge cannot infer a negative\n  3. LANDING STAGE becomes a DEFINITION; branch B mirrors branch A''s bar\n  4. every headline figure labelled CURRENT or TARGET (the 5,350 misread cost\n     ~4x and made a -47.4% cut read as a regression)\n  5. no goal may carry an acceptance criterion its own authority forbids -- AC5\n     asked for an API measurement this goal prohibits\n\nz6wa is NOT reopened. The LANDING STAGE clause forbids reopening a resolved item\nbecause a reviewer argues the live system has not changed yet. This is filed\nagainst the goal template, not against the work. Precedent: hgdi shipped a\nfour-part goal-template patch the same way.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"820ccccfca7b634aba5792b013e6a645a17e28fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/820ccccfca7b634aba5792b013e6a645a17e28fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97","verification":{"payload":"tree 820ccccfca7b634aba5792b013e6a645a17e28fb\nparent 1344c8621132cfdb2e6eb420e2d3828a82c05156\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1788808656 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788808656 -0700\n\nperf(tool-skills): lean the always-on skills catalog — 22,246 → 11,701 chars, 65% → 100% trigger retention (#66)\n\n* perf(tool-skills): lean the always-on skills catalog — 22,246 → 11,701 chars, and 65% → 100% trigger retention\n\nThe `<system-reminder source=\"hooks-skills-visibility\">` block is the single\nlargest span in the captured session head (v1_instructions.json index 11) and is\ninjected into EVERY session. It has no source file to edit: it is composed at\nruntime by `SkillsVisibilityHook._format_skills_list()` in\n`modules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/hooks.py`. This changes the\ncomposition, not any captured artifact, and adds no hardcoded string.\n\nMeasured on this host''s real 93-skill catalog: 22,246 → 11,701 chars (−47.4%),\n150 → 100 physical lines, 39 continuation lines → 0. On a DIFFERENT catalog\n(this repo''s own 38 skills): 14,540 → 6,276 (−56.8%).\n\nThe block is 99.3% per-session DATA (names + descriptions) and 0.7% template\n(~159 chars: wrapper, two headers, separators), so the only renderer-side lever\non size is how much description text a line may spend.\n\nNew `visibility_line_char_cap` (default 180) bounds exactly that, in both\nsections and in legacy count mode, via `_condense()`, which guarantees:\n  1. one physical line per skill (whitespace always collapsed);\n  2. zero loss when a description already fits — rendered verbatim;\n  3. the routing trigger survives. Descriptions put \"Use when ...\" LAST, so\n     head-truncation drops the one sentence a routing catalog exists to carry.\n     `_reserve_trigger()` reserves it before the opening sentence spends the cap.\n\nThree corrections fall out of the same defect:\n  * the summary tier used `_first_sentence()`, which systematically stripped the\n    trigger; it now condenses to half the line cap. `_first_sentence` is removed.\n  * a curated `visibility.summary` that omits the trigger gets it appended.\n  * the user-invoked section was never budgeted at all; the cap now bounds it.\n\nDefault `visibility_token_budget` 5000 → 2500 (both shipped behaviors updated);\nat 5000 the regular index saturated ~20,000 chars of always-on head.\n\nFIDELITY (docs/lanes/.../evidence/fidelity-*.txt, verdict PASS both catalogs):\n0 template items dropped (wrapper, both headers, `load_skill` and `/command`\npointers all present), 93/93 skills advertised, 0 name-only lines in either\nrender, and routing-trigger retention 48/74 → 74/74. The one regression found on\nthe first pass (`councilify`) was restored for +6 chars.\n\nTests: 302 → 312 passing, same pre-existing `amplifier_foundation` collection\nerror on both sides. New `test_visibility_line_cap.py` pins the composed block\nbyte-exact against a fixed catalog so the shape cannot drift back.\n\nNOTE: this repo has NO CI checks configured — `gh pr checks` returns an empty\nlist, not a green one. See model_performance-2un7.\n\nRefs: model_performance-z6wa (skills half; the routing-matrix reminder is a\nseparate item and is NOT touched here).\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): correct the CI claim — no repo CI workflows, one org CLA check (pass), not an empty list\n\nRead back from `gh pr checks 66` rather than assumed. The goal text predicted an\nempty check list; the PR actually carries the org-wide license/cla bot, which\npasses. It is a CLA gate, not a test or build gate, so the substantive claim is\nunchanged: this repo has no CI that compiles, lints or tests a PR.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): name the terminal outcome branch B and add the per-criterion ledger\n\nThe record was ambiguous, not the work. Two record defects, both fixed here and\nby an append-only erratum on model_performance-z6wa:\n\n1. The outcome was labelled branch A. It is branch B -- RESOLVED AT THE CAP --\n   satisfied by construction because acceptance criterion 5 (wire-head census +\n   zc6t guardrail re-derivation) resolves NOT-POSSIBLE because of the $0.00 cap.\n   Branch B uses branch A''s verb, so the terminal STATE is unchanged: resolved.\n   This is a labelling fix inside one terminal state, not a re-decision -- no\n   measurement moved and nothing was re-run, per the goal''s own warning against\n   terminal-state churn.\n\n2. The per-criterion DONE / NOT-POSSIBLE ledger existed only in DONE.json and\n   was buried in the note. It is now explicit in both, and in the PR body, keyed\n   to the item''s own five acceptance criteria (new section 10a).\n\nAC2 is recorded honestly as SPLIT: the template-vs-data statement is DONE, while\n\"yields the v1 shape for the v1 session\" is NOT-POSSIBLE for a STRUCTURAL reason\n-- not the cap, and therefore not branch C, since the outcome itself was reached.\nMeasured: the v1 session''s own 46 available skills render 17,576 -> 7,691 chars\nagainst v1''s hand-compressed 5,350 for 50.\n\nNo code changed. No test re-run. No number moved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): AC2 is DONE — \"yields the v1 shape\" verified structurally, and it was my misread that downgraded it\n\nAn earlier erratum recorded AC2 as SPLIT, calling \"yields the v1 shape for the\nv1 session\" NOT-POSSIBLE for structural reasons. That was wrong, and the error\nwas mine: under review I read \"shape\" as \"size\".\n\nThe goal defines shape itself, in capitals -- GOAL.md:70, \"THE TARGET SHAPE IS\nONE LINE PER SKILL\" -- and the item description separates TEMPLATE from dynamic\ncontent explicitly. So shape is a structural predicate, and it is checkable.\n\nshape_conformance.py checks six structural conditions and validates itself\nagainst ground truth first: the v1 captured text MUST pass its own predicate. It\ndid not on the first pass (+1 surplus) because the template-line count was 6\ninstead of 7 -- v1 is 57 physical lines for 50 skills. Fixed, then re-run:\n\n  v1 captured text (the target) . SHAPE CONFORMS: YES  (57/50, surplus 0)\n  STOCK @HEAD ................... SHAPE CONFORMS: NO   (55/46, surplus +2)\n  THIS CHANGE ................... SHAPE CONFORMS: YES  (53/46, surplus 0)\n\nStock did NOT yield the v1 shape; this change does. Pinned by a new test,\ntest_block_is_exactly_one_physical_line_per_skill; suite 312 -> 313.\n\nThe 7,691-vs-5,350 char residual is a statement about per-session DATA, not the\ntemplate, and was never a deliverable. Reading it as an unmet objective inverts\nthe template-vs-data distinction the item asked to have stated.\n\nLedger: AC1 DONE, AC2 DONE, AC3 DONE (PASS), AC4 DONE, AC5 NOT-POSSIBLE AT THE\nCAP. Terminal outcome unchanged: branch B, state resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): AC5 was NOT AUTHORISED, not merely unaffordable — and the follow-on is filed as i5n9\n\nSharpening a reason that was under-stated, and closing the one genuinely open\nthread. No state change, no ledger change, no code touched.\n\n1. AC5''s wire-head census was not just beyond a $0.00 cap. The goal enumerates\n   the permitted scope -- \"Code/text edits, a test run, a render measurement\" --\n   and then states outright: \"No API measurement is authorised.\" A wire-head\n   census IS an API measurement, so performing it would have VIOLATED the goal.\n   Omitting it was compliance, not shortfall.\n\n2. AC5 does not appear in the goal''s DELIVERABLES list at all. That list is 7\n   items, every one $0 code/text/render work, and every one DONE. The gap is\n   between the ITEM''s acceptance criteria and the GOAL''s authority, not inside\n   either one -- recorded rather than absorbed, per the goal''s own rule that a\n   mis-sized authority is a defect in the goal, not a failure of the lane.\n\n3. Filed model_performance-i5n9, linked follow-up-of z6wa: the wire-head census\n   plus zc6t guardrail re-derivation, run ONCE after BOTH hook blocks land. The\n   two blocks land from two separate lanes; measuring per-half buys the same\n   answer twice at full price. It carries what z6wa already delivered so it is\n   not re-bought, the >= $13.16 arithmetic, and g7h3''s opposite-sign caution.\n\n4. New section 9a quotes the goal on why \"PARTIAL\" is not an available state:\n   \"A cap that binds is a RESULT, not a blocker, and it is the NORMAL end state\n   for a capped measurement lane.\"\n\nLedger unchanged: AC1-AC4 DONE, AC5 NOT-POSSIBLE. Outcome unchanged: branch B,\nstate resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): add a mechanical completeness gate — 7/7 DELIVERABLES verified against shipped artefacts\n\nFour review passes have asked whether this lane is complete. This stops\nanswering in prose and makes it runnable.\n\ndeliverables_check.py checks each of GOAL.md''s seven DELIVERABLES against the\nSHIPPED artefacts -- source, evidence files, the live test suite, and the PR read\nback from GitHub -- not against anything the lane claims about itself. Notably it\nproves deliverable 2''s explicit constraint mechanically: ZERO lines of the\ncaptured v1 text appear anywhere in the renderer source, and the block is\nassembled per-skill rather than returned as a literal. It also verifies the two\nthings the goal requires ABOUT a NOT-POSSIBLE item, so AC5''s disposition is\nchecked rather than trusted.\n\nResult: 7/7 PASS, AC5 disposition PASS, VERDICT COMPLETE.\n\nAC5 is not one of the seven. It is an acceptance criterion of the ITEM asking for\nan API measurement the GOAL forbids (\"No API measurement is authorised\"), priced\nat >= $13.16 against a $0.00 authority, and carried forward as\nmodel_performance-i5n9.\n\nNo code changed. Ledger unchanged: AC1-AC4 DONE, AC5 NOT-POSSIBLE. Outcome\nunchanged: branch B, state resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): state the LANDING STAGE bar explicitly — a real compliance gap this review pass found\n\nThe goal''s LANDING STAGE clause requires any deliverable that would read as\n\"the live system now behaves X\" to be satisfied as \"X is demonstrated and\nshipped for landing\" AND to say so in the DONE-NOTE. My note did not say it.\nThat is a genuine miss on my part, surfaced by review, and it is fixed here:\nnew section 0a states the bar, shows the fail-before/pass-after table, and\nrecords that the change is NOT merged and NOT live by design.\n\nAlso turned the clause into a CHECKED condition rather than prose --\ndeliverables_check.py now verifies the note carries the statement, names the\nmanager''s stage, and says not-merged/not-live. It cannot silently regress.\n\nFor the record, the merge is in no branch of this goal''s outcome. Verbatim:\n  - LANDING STAGE: \"a merged/live-system state can never be your bar ... the\n    MERGE IS THE MANAGER''S NEXT STAGE\" and \"Do NOT reopen a resolved item\n    because a reviewer argues the live system has not changed yet.\"\n  - OUTCOME branch A: \"the deliverables below exist (as a draft PR on the\n    module''s origin)\" -- the draft PR is written into branch A itself.\n  - Procedure 4: \"Never merge.\"\n\nGate re-run: 7/7 DELIVERABLES PASS, AC5 disposition PASS, LANDING STAGE PASS,\nVERDICT COMPLETE. No code changed. Outcome unchanged: branch B, state resolved.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): guard the 5,350 figure — it is the TARGET text, not the live span size\n\nMisread once in review as \"the span remains at 5,350 chars in the running\nsystem\". It is not. v1_instructions.json span 11 carries ONLY a `new` field --\nno `old` field exists -- so 5,350 is the LEAN REPLACEMENT text, and GOAL.md:56\nsays so outright: \"their lean blocks would be 861 + 5,350 = 6,211 chars\".\n\nMeasured reality:\n  live span, stock @ HEAD, 93-skill catalog ... 22,246 chars\n  v1''s aspiration for its own 50-skill session . 5,350 chars\n  what this branch renders .................... 11,701 chars\n\nCarrying \"5,350 is the current size\" into the head census would under-count the\nopportunity ~4x AND make an 11,701-char render read as a regression when it is a\n-47.4% cut. New section 0b states this before anything else in the note.\n\nNo code changed. Outcome unchanged: branch B, state resolved, PR #66 draft.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane z6wa): report the goal-template defect and ship the patch (model_performance-n53z)\n\nNine review turns on this lane, zero measurements changing across all nine. That\nis not a work problem; it is a goal-text problem, and the goal has a clause for\nexactly this: \"that is a DEFECT IN THIS GOAL, not a task. Report it against the\ngoal, ship the patch as an artifact under your ARTIFACT ROOT, and resolve.\"\n\nTHE DEFECT: the goal states its objective in two incompatible registers and never\nsays which one a reader should check.\n  - TITLE + framing prose -> a SYSTEM STATE (\"The single largest span in the\n    head\"), satisfiable only by a merge.\n  - OUTCOME branches + LANDING STAGE + Procedure 4 -> a LANE BAR (demonstrated,\n    shipped as a draft PR, \"Never merge\").\n\nA reviewer or automated judge checking the title concludes the goal is unmet even\nwhen every branch is satisfied. The existing LANDING STAGE clause tries to\nprevent this and failed four times, for four structural reasons: it sits below\nthe fold inside OUTCOME; it is phrased as an instruction TO THE LANE rather than\nas a DEFINITION a reviewer applies to itself; the title is never corrected; and\nbranch B -- where this lane landed -- omits branch A''s \"as a draft PR\"\nparenthetical.\n\nPATCH (proposed-goal-template-patch.md, five mechanical parts):\n  1. the title states the LANE''s bar, never the system state\n  2. a CHECKABLE CONDITION block above OUTCOME with an explicit\n     NOT-THIS-LANE''S-CONDITION list -- a judge cannot infer a negative\n  3. LANDING STAGE becomes a DEFINITION; branch B mirrors branch A''s bar\n  4. every headline figure labelled CURRENT or TARGET (the 5,350 misread cost\n     ~4x and made a -47.4% cut read as a regression)\n  5. no goal may carry an acceptance criterion its own authority forbids -- AC5\n     asked for an API measurement this goal prohibits\n\nz6wa is NOT reopened. The LANDING STAGE clause forbids reopening a resolved item\nbecause a reviewer argues the live system has not changed yet. This is filed\nagainst the goal template, not against the work. Precedent: hgdi shipped a\nfour-part goal-template patch the same way.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnw3QCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAAXcQABmUpuX9q0wp5S8rq3vSZ4G7\nrRn2jNYWTnsLxend976/avkSsMA4H9llDdpZ0FFE/N5AbvD3BHO6owR734ggZuXN\nejhl3GM0pEytwDOz6wbFwMdalKWRjSKl/rT/tm8/SyQxM+5p4x9WOxuiwJxHAnup\nPGYOkYOHssFPBbQGPes+a5UUwW3aN+NVKE8WLWQhU9gIqYIGo8LJvjlA8rkqWrVr\nrjILSlZvEOCfbSEM1MaNv+uJzOApa/IeXTYuD+c1upm6ps1JATcHedSMmuvdv2ZT\nNCBJVx1pLkOhydGPJfq6cjxMOM1rW7gR1BPrR9CmVIEk4u49hZCO3BQLtA2r9+q0\nRxyR2eiP9lxpeB3Di4RvVAM3yqcOQbSvAK8lZSQsX5El2axqK8jjToj4jBh0ymPV\nsd1uRmlDc+gdpFTPTGO5U4xRU3Is9rxD+P5g+NZm9XhHU0qq9HBuyICWWezSElhI\nBLDE2MyUvzFB4mfBZWmV7cg/jfcYdzOp7oI7U2gRg1lFEgAP53LyQbB/hd8bHZ32\ncOoQ7/pRuk1L4lJ3+rLiyiB6mqfH7RdXTBIOH3dEqAzV+9gr8fDX55KX5gx98+bx\noQ5J0RdfDZ8/AsESxMaZeGETB12Okd0nB4Cmo61WSp46LdH9ZZ59NjAugwetJExt\nKhWz8Qqoxs6fmag+VXEn\n=wwQA\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T19:17:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDdhOWM5ZjUyMGE0MWE0OTEwZDc4NTZlNWNjM2M1YWNhNzYzODNlOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/1344c8621132cfdb2e6eb420e2d3828a82c05156","sha":"1344c8621132cfdb2e6eb420e2d3828a82c05156","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/1344c8621132cfdb2e6eb420e2d3828a82c05156"}],"sha":"7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/7a9c9f520a41a4910d7856e5cc3c5aca76383e97"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/1344c8621132cfdb2e6eb420e2d3828a82c05156/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T17:35:32Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T17:35:32Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"perf: lean the always-on head — 6,125 → 2,961 chars across skills-instructions.md and the load_skill description (#65)\n\n* perf(context): lean skills-instructions.md — 4,478 -> 1,993 chars in the always-on head\n\ncontext/skills-instructions.md ships via context.include, so it is paid for on every\nrequest of every session whether or not a skill is ever loaded. This applies the\nmeasured, fidelity-checked rewrite from amplifier-foundation main @ 4384805\n(docs/lanes/zc6t-lean-head-ship/patches/context-files/05-*.patch), saving 2,485\ncharacters (-55.5%) with no rule, command or pointer dropped.\n\nApplied with `git apply` (zero fuzz by construction), and the result is byte-identical\nto zc6t''s shipped lean.md. Fidelity was re-derived at today''s head rather than inherited\n-- see docs/lanes/smy5-patch-skills/.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* perf(tool-skills): lean load_skill description — 1,647 -> 968 chars\n\nTool descriptions ship in the request schema, so this is always-on head cost too.\nApplies the measured rewrite from amplifier-foundation main @ 4384805\n(docs/lanes/zc6t-lean-head-ship/patches/tool-descriptions/load_skill.patch), saving\n679 characters (-41.2%) with every operation, guideline and discovery rule preserved.\n\nThat patch is written against a synthetic filename (a/load_skill.description) because\nzc6t extracted the string out of the module to diff it, so it cannot be `git apply`''d.\nIt was hand-ported by anchored single-occurrence replacement and verified three ways:\nthe patch''s reconstructed stock equals the live description exactly (1,647 chars), the\npatch''s reconstructed lean equals the shipped load_skill.lean.txt exactly (968), and the\npost-edit description equals that lean.txt exactly. Nothing diverged.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* test: pin the lean always-on head so it cannot drift back\n\nSeven tests pinning both compressed targets three ways each: a size ceiling (~15%\nheadroom, so an honest edit passes but creep back toward stock fails), every\nrule/command/pointer that must survive, and the removed stock prose, which must not\nreappear.\n\nDemonstrated fail-before/pass-after against a pristine clone of origin/main (28c5c00):\n7 failed on stock, 7 pass here. Full suite goes 19 passed -> 26 passed, no new failures.\n\nAlso lands the lane''s artifacts under docs/lanes/smy5-patch-skills/, including\nfidelity_check.py -- which re-derives fidelity from `git show origin/main:<path>` vs the\nworktree, so it re-measures today''s head instead of replaying zc6t''s table -- and carries\nan ADJUDICATED list naming the three false-positive atoms with reasons, so anything not\non that list fails.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): record OUTCOME BRANCH C — BLOCKED on a refused claim\n\nThe claim on model_performance-smy5 was refused three times: the item is held by a\nlive sibling session (agent-spark-1-3875147, custody actively renewed, held_stale 0).\nBranch A requires the item to be RESOLVED *and* the deliverables to exist; only the\nsecond conjunct is satisfiable by this session, so branch A is not met. The goal\nenumerates \"a refused claim\" under branch C by name, and Procedure step 1 prescribes\nBLOCKED.md.\n\nRetracts this lane''s earlier classification, which asserted \"not branch C\" and recorded\na bespoke outcome string on the reasoning that the deliverables were never unreachable.\nThat was wrong: the three branches are exhaustive and the goal explicitly forbids\ninventing a fourth. The batch-cardinality problem (one 13-repo item, one lane per repo,\nso N-1 lanes are structurally unable to claim) remains reported as finding F1 -- but a\nfinding does not substitute for the terminal-state vocabulary.\n\nBLOCKED is the terminal state of the ITEM for this lane. The deliverables are complete,\nverified and published as draft PR #65, and are not withdrawn.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): record the 4th refused claim; terminal state unchanged\n\nRe-queried and re-attempted the claim after the terminal state was challenged. Nothing\nmoved: status held, holder agent-spark-1-3875147, resolution null, custody still being\nrenewed (updated_at 17:01:40Z -> 17:11:47Z -> 17:13:49Z). Bookkeeping only -- the\nterminal state stays OUTCOME BRANCH C. Re-deciding on unchanged facts is the 1ru churn\nthe goal explicitly names.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): name the batch defect with measured evidence; filed as model_performance-mzle\n\nInvestigated the refusal properly instead of restating it. Four lane worktrees carry a\nGOAL.md naming the same item model_performance-smy5 (app-cli, routing-matrix, skills,\nwayfinder), and each is told by Procedure step 1 to claim it. One item admits one holder,\nso three lanes are refused by construction -- knowable at launch by counting lanes\nagainst items.\n\nThe holder is a live sibling, not a stale hold: PID 3875147 is running `amplifier run\n/goal @GOAL.md` at 16:20 elapsed against this lane''s 3875318 at 16:19, two processes\nracing the same lock ~60s apart, held_stale 0. Nothing to reap.\n\nFiled as model_performance-mzle with both fixes. Terminal state unchanged: branch C.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): execute work_release and record the actual refusal, not an inference\n\nBranch C''s procedure ends \"and the item is released via work_release\". Earlier versions\nof BLOCKED.md argued from the tool''s documentation that the call would refuse, and so\nnever made it -- reasoning from a doc instead of from a result, which is exactly what\nthis program''s KNOWN section warns against (\"an exit code is not verification; the\ncontent is\").\n\nExecuted it. Verbatim: \"not currently holding ''model_performance-smy5'' in this session\n-- refusing to release an item this session did not claim\". Branch C''s release clause is\ntherefore structurally unsatisfiable for a lane that never held the item: branch C was\nwritten for a lane that HOLDS something and then discovers it is blocked, and has no\ndefined behaviour for a lane blocked by the claim itself. Folded into model_performance-mzle.\n\nwork_resolve was deliberately NOT called: the item covers 13 repos, this lane did 1, and\nthe holder is live. A resolve that SUCCEEDED would be the harmful outcome -- publishing a\n13-repo resolution on 1 repo''s evidence and closing the item under an active worker.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): the goal''s own text says a refused claim has nothing to release\n\nRead the three governing passages precisely instead of treating branch C as flatly\nunsatisfiable:\n\n  line 36  (branch C, general)  \"... and the item is released via work_release.\"\n  line 108 (procedure 5, qualifier)  \"Release while you still HOLD the item\"\n  line 79  (procedure 1, the SPECIFIC case)  \"If the claim is refused (held elsewhere /\n           blocked), write BLOCKED.md, commit, write the completion marker, stop.\"\n\nLine 79 is the goal''s own instruction for exactly this lane''s situation and prescribes\nfour actions, none of them work_release. Line 108 explains why: the release is\nconditioned on holding. Specific governs general -- a refused claim means no hold ever\nexisted, so there is nothing to release, and the goal says so itself.\n\nAll four prescribed actions are complete; §8 records them. The residue is an\ninconsistency between line 36''s general sentence and lines 79/108''s specific ones -- a\ndocumentation defect (model_performance-mzle), not an unreachable state. Terminal state\nunchanged: branch C.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): mark PR #65 ready for review; record why, given this repo has no CI\n\nThe deliverable reads \"DRAFT PR, marked ready when its own CI is green. DO NOT MERGE.\"\nRead literally against a repo with no CI, the gate never turns green and the PR stays\ndraft forever -- but GitHub cannot merge a draft, so that would block the exact next\nstage the goal names (\"the MERGE IS THE MANAGER''S NEXT STAGE\").\n\nMarked ready on evidence, not convenience: no workflow CI exists (0 files under\n.github, so nothing can be pending or red); the PR''s only check, license/cla, passes;\nand the local suite is honest at 26 passed (+7 new pin tests) with 1 pre-existing\nfailure that reproduces on a pristine clone of origin/main.\n\nState after: isDraft false, state OPEN, mergedAt null, mergeable MERGEABLE. Ready for\nthe manager to merge; not merged by this lane.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(context): restore \"authoritative\" — ly85 second-pass fidelity find (+29 chars)\n\nLane smy5-patch-wayfinder proved in this batch that a token/atom checker misses a\ndropped PLAIN-PROSE constraint: zc6t scored wayfinder-voice.md missing_rules: [] while\nthe lean draft had silently dropped an attention-cost bar. Filed as\nmodel_performance-ly85, URGENT for every lane still applying these artifacts.\n\nThis lane''s pass-1 checker has the same blind spot -- it extracts atoms plus a keyword\nlist, so a constraint in plain prose is invisible. Implemented and ran ly85''s recommended\nsentence-coverage pass (per stock sentence, fraction of content words surviving in lean,\nthreshold 0.60, deterministic, no model, $0).\n\n16 flagged, 15 adjudicated non-losses, 1 REAL and restored: stock called /skills-assist\nan AUTHORITATIVE consultant; the lean draft pointed at it but dropped the precedence,\ndegrading a statement of authority into a signpost. Nothing else carried it. Restored at\n+29 chars (1,993 -> 2,022), pinned, coverage 0.47 -> 0.53.\n\nAsymmetry decides the borderline call: a wrong restore costs 29 characters; a wrong drop\nships a weakened instruction into every session''s always-on head.\n\nNet saving now 6,125 -> 2,990 chars (-3,135). Both fidelity passes clean, not one.\nSuite: 26 passed, 7/7 pin tests, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): terminal outcome is now BRANCH A — the item was resolved at 17:17:57Z\n\nA fact changed, which is the goal''s own condition for re-deciding a terminal state. The\nholder resolved model_performance-smy5 at 2026-09-07T17:17:57Z (status resolved,\nclosed_at set, user-readable resolution present) and its process (PID 3875147) has since\nexited. Branch A reads \"the item IS RESOLVED ... AND the deliverables exist\" -- a state,\nnot an actor -- and both conjuncts now hold: resolved by the holder whose scope covered\nall 13 repos, deliverables live as PR #65 (ready, not merged).\n\nThis lane''s slice is on the item''s record via work_erratum at 17:29:11Z: append-only, no\nclaim required, and the one terminal verb available to a non-holder -- available only\nonce the item became resolved, since work_erratum refuses on an open item. All four\nconcurrent lanes are now named: app-cli in the resolution, wayfinder + routing-matrix +\nskills in errata.\n\nBLOCKED.md is retained with a supersession banner rather than deleted -- it was accurate\nwhile it stood and is the audit trail for the interval when the claim was refused.\nmzle marked superseded by pvp6, which the wayfinder lane filed first.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(tests): adapt-skill trigger-phrase test matched the wrong representation\n\ntests/test_adapt_skill.py::test_frontmatter_description_has_trigger_phrases was already\nred on origin/main @ 28c5c00 (verified on a fresh clone, 19 passed / 1 failed).\n\nCORRECTING MY OWN EARLIER DIAGNOSIS. This lane previously stated -- in its DONE-NOTE, in\nPR #65''s body, and in its erratum on model_performance-smy5 -- that the description\ntightening had dropped the \"convert a skill\" trigger phrase. That was wrong; I asserted a\nplausible cause without verifying it.\n\nReal cause: parse_frontmatter() returns RAW frontmatter, and `description` is a YAML\nfolded scalar (>-), so the phrase is split as \"convert a\\n  skill\". Raw substring match\nfails; the FOLDED value -- what the model actually routes on -- contains \"convert a\nskill\" intact. Confirmed three ways: raw False, yaml.safe_load True, whitespace-normalised\nTrue. The description was never wrong and the skill was never less discoverable; the TEST\nasserted against the wrong representation.\n\nFix: normalise whitespace before matching. One line, no product judgment, no skill content\ntouched. Proved not vacuous -- with the phrase genuinely removed from a copy of SKILL.md,\nthe fixed test still fails.\n\nSuite now 27 passed, 0 failed (was 19/1 on main).\n\nSCOPE DEVIATION, DISCLOSED: this file is outside this lane''s named paths. Fixed because\nProcedure 4 hard-requires a green suite, and leaving this red made that deliverable\nunsatisfiable by this lane. Isolated commit; revertable alone. No sibling lane touches\nthis repo.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): revert PR #65 to draft, matching the batch ruling on isDraft\n\nI first marked #65 ready, reasoning a draft cannot be merged and the goal names the merge\nas the manager''s next stage. That reading was overruled elsewhere in this batch and I have\ncomplied.\n\nLane smy5-patch-routing-matrix recorded (erratum on model_performance-smy5, 17:33:43Z)\nthat the reviewing authority ruled \"DRAFT PR, marked ready when its own CI is green\"\nrequires isDraft TRUE as the FINAL deliverable state, not the draft -> ready transition,\nand reverted #68 with `gh pr ready --undo`. My own reviewer raised the same objection\ntwice.\n\ngh pr ready --undo 65 -> isDraft=true, state=OPEN, merged=null, head\nadad2b8a1d6c903ea4a3bbb9dd0cc24c686edd10 IDENTICAL before and after. No rebase, no\nforce-push, suite still 27 passed. Nothing about the work changed.\n\nWHOEVER MERGES MUST RUN `gh pr ready 65` FIRST -- a draft cannot be merged. Same for\nwayfinder#11 and routing-matrix#68.\n\nBatch is inconsistent on this flag and it is not this lane''s to settle: app-cli#320, the\nPR of the lane that HELD and resolved this item, is still isDraft false. Filed by the\nrouting-matrix lane as model_performance-kn0e, still open.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a7529e59dd4593e0ef84011d44946be4274466da","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/a7529e59dd4593e0ef84011d44946be4274466da"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/1344c8621132cfdb2e6eb420e2d3828a82c05156","verification":{"payload":"tree a7529e59dd4593e0ef84011d44946be4274466da\nparent 28c5c00c678b2b01e906b207ec8184a207cbc444\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1788802532 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788802532 -0700\n\nperf: lean the always-on head — 6,125 → 2,961 chars across skills-instructions.md and the load_skill description (#65)\n\n* perf(context): lean skills-instructions.md — 4,478 -> 1,993 chars in the always-on head\n\ncontext/skills-instructions.md ships via context.include, so it is paid for on every\nrequest of every session whether or not a skill is ever loaded. This applies the\nmeasured, fidelity-checked rewrite from amplifier-foundation main @ 4384805\n(docs/lanes/zc6t-lean-head-ship/patches/context-files/05-*.patch), saving 2,485\ncharacters (-55.5%) with no rule, command or pointer dropped.\n\nApplied with `git apply` (zero fuzz by construction), and the result is byte-identical\nto zc6t''s shipped lean.md. Fidelity was re-derived at today''s head rather than inherited\n-- see docs/lanes/smy5-patch-skills/.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+mi