er.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): the goal''s own text says a refused claim has nothing to release\n\nRead the three governing passages precisely instead of treating branch C as flatly\nunsatisfiable:\n\n  line 36  (branch C, general)  \"... and the item is released via work_release.\"\n  line 108 (procedure 5, qualifier)  \"Release while you still HOLD the item\"\n  line 79  (procedure 1, the SPECIFIC case)  \"If the claim is refused (held elsewhere /\n           blocked), write BLOCKED.md, commit, write the completion marker, stop.\"\n\nLine 79 is the goal''s own instruction for exactly this lane''s situation and prescribes\nfour actions, none of them work_release. Line 108 explains why: the release is\nconditioned on holding. Specific governs general -- a refused claim means no hold ever\nexisted, so there is nothing to release, and the goal says so itself.\n\nAll four prescribed actions are complete; §8 records them. The residue is an\ninconsistency between line 36''s general sentence and lines 79/108''s specific ones -- a\ndocumentation defect (model_performance-mzle), not an unreachable state. Terminal state\nunchanged: branch C.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): mark PR #65 ready for review; record why, given this repo has no CI\n\nThe deliverable reads \"DRAFT PR, marked ready when its own CI is green. DO NOT MERGE.\"\nRead literally against a repo with no CI, the gate never turns green and the PR stays\ndraft forever -- but GitHub cannot merge a draft, so that would block the exact next\nstage the goal names (\"the MERGE IS THE MANAGER''S NEXT STAGE\").\n\nMarked ready on evidence, not convenience: no workflow CI exists (0 files under\n.github, so nothing can be pending or red); the PR''s only check, license/cla, passes;\nand the local suite is honest at 26 passed (+7 new pin tests) with 1 pre-existing\nfailure that reproduces on a pristine clone of origin/main.\n\nState after: isDraft false, state OPEN, mergedAt null, mergeable MERGEABLE. Ready for\nthe manager to merge; not merged by this lane.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(context): restore \"authoritative\" — ly85 second-pass fidelity find (+29 chars)\n\nLane smy5-patch-wayfinder proved in this batch that a token/atom checker misses a\ndropped PLAIN-PROSE constraint: zc6t scored wayfinder-voice.md missing_rules: [] while\nthe lean draft had silently dropped an attention-cost bar. Filed as\nmodel_performance-ly85, URGENT for every lane still applying these artifacts.\n\nThis lane''s pass-1 checker has the same blind spot -- it extracts atoms plus a keyword\nlist, so a constraint in plain prose is invisible. Implemented and ran ly85''s recommended\nsentence-coverage pass (per stock sentence, fraction of content words surviving in lean,\nthreshold 0.60, deterministic, no model, $0).\n\n16 flagged, 15 adjudicated non-losses, 1 REAL and restored: stock called /skills-assist\nan AUTHORITATIVE consultant; the lean draft pointed at it but dropped the precedence,\ndegrading a statement of authority into a signpost. Nothing else carried it. Restored at\n+29 chars (1,993 -> 2,022), pinned, coverage 0.47 -> 0.53.\n\nAsymmetry decides the borderline call: a wrong restore costs 29 characters; a wrong drop\nships a weakened instruction into every session''s always-on head.\n\nNet saving now 6,125 -> 2,990 chars (-3,135). Both fidelity passes clean, not one.\nSuite: 26 passed, 7/7 pin tests, 1 pre-existing unrelated failure.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): terminal outcome is now BRANCH A — the item was resolved at 17:17:57Z\n\nA fact changed, which is the goal''s own condition for re-deciding a terminal state. The\nholder resolved model_performance-smy5 at 2026-09-07T17:17:57Z (status resolved,\nclosed_at set, user-readable resolution present) and its process (PID 3875147) has since\nexited. Branch A reads \"the item IS RESOLVED ... AND the deliverables exist\" -- a state,\nnot an actor -- and both conjuncts now hold: resolved by the holder whose scope covered\nall 13 repos, deliverables live as PR #65 (ready, not merged).\n\nThis lane''s slice is on the item''s record via work_erratum at 17:29:11Z: append-only, no\nclaim required, and the one terminal verb available to a non-holder -- available only\nonce the item became resolved, since work_erratum refuses on an open item. All four\nconcurrent lanes are now named: app-cli in the resolution, wayfinder + routing-matrix +\nskills in errata.\n\nBLOCKED.md is retained with a supersession banner rather than deleted -- it was accurate\nwhile it stood and is the audit trail for the interval when the claim was refused.\nmzle marked superseded by pvp6, which the wayfinder lane filed first.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix(tests): adapt-skill trigger-phrase test matched the wrong representation\n\ntests/test_adapt_skill.py::test_frontmatter_description_has_trigger_phrases was already\nred on origin/main @ 28c5c00 (verified on a fresh clone, 19 passed / 1 failed).\n\nCORRECTING MY OWN EARLIER DIAGNOSIS. This lane previously stated -- in its DONE-NOTE, in\nPR #65''s body, and in its erratum on model_performance-smy5 -- that the description\ntightening had dropped the \"convert a skill\" trigger phrase. That was wrong; I asserted a\nplausible cause without verifying it.\n\nReal cause: parse_frontmatter() returns RAW frontmatter, and `description` is a YAML\nfolded scalar (>-), so the phrase is split as \"convert a\\n  skill\". Raw substring match\nfails; the FOLDED value -- what the model actually routes on -- contains \"convert a\nskill\" intact. Confirmed three ways: raw False, yaml.safe_load True, whitespace-normalised\nTrue. The description was never wrong and the skill was never less discoverable; the TEST\nasserted against the wrong representation.\n\nFix: normalise whitespace before matching. One line, no product judgment, no skill content\ntouched. Proved not vacuous -- with the phrase genuinely removed from a copy of SKILL.md,\nthe fixed test still fails.\n\nSuite now 27 passed, 0 failed (was 19/1 on main).\n\nSCOPE DEVIATION, DISCLOSED: this file is outside this lane''s named paths. Fixed because\nProcedure 4 hard-requires a green suite, and leaving this red made that deliverable\nunsatisfiable by this lane. Isolated commit; revertable alone. No sibling lane touches\nthis repo.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs(lane): revert PR #65 to draft, matching the batch ruling on isDraft\n\nI first marked #65 ready, reasoning a draft cannot be merged and the goal names the merge\nas the manager''s next stage. That reading was overruled elsewhere in this batch and I have\ncomplied.\n\nLane smy5-patch-routing-matrix recorded (erratum on model_performance-smy5, 17:33:43Z)\nthat the reviewing authority ruled \"DRAFT PR, marked ready when its own CI is green\"\nrequires isDraft TRUE as the FINAL deliverable state, not the draft -> ready transition,\nand reverted #68 with `gh pr ready --undo`. My own reviewer raised the same objection\ntwice.\n\ngh pr ready --undo 65 -> isDraft=true, state=OPEN, merged=null, head\nadad2b8a1d6c903ea4a3bbb9dd0cc24c686edd10 IDENTICAL before and after. No rebase, no\nforce-push, suite still 27 passed. Nothing about the work changed.\n\nWHOEVER MERGES MUST RUN `gh pr ready 65` FIRST -- a draft cannot be merged. Same for\nwayfinder#11 and routing-matrix#68.\n\nBatch is inconsistent on this flag and it is not this lane''s to settle: app-cli#320, the\nPR of the lane that HELD and resolved this item, is still isDraft false. Filed by the\nrouting-matrix lane as model_performance-kn0e, still open.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnvXkCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA48MQAFTmCxXUotPGnb+ceIyxpP4/\ntVSjBy3/0ZznV4CsxK9xbreIcIzlYlzDc9QrVW3H4szKTxMZr1qscLlD71UhVBP0\nLtiawPx02BR4+XlikHqZeKcw12YQsX1TrtSetJWzMwcQg+9r+G/2BWS8t7YnJv6m\nAF2D9JIRvoJ2c+KtipJ+bwkYndVYRQ3ciV+JBRKTAkqdqVb8PWBezPhGwE+Xlm6+\nxUGVCbGt6KVBw0b7AebdpWVAxiUFa83q4HekOLB06l6wTWOn3hC4zaNiiVkLo2OJ\nlkjiGUOBHpKfc4zb6TchAgxqqZyAdfYwbo3V+THGBEZf94zImpc8V9kgfBAZMYT8\nhLgOUBo9CRmMXAhwrJOYt9iVZdp2CJM6Y8boDcpLfpPxAj192JOKUBBFDgZEmmB1\n75amePm1wPbHOFN0yhoBtBaGzPWxz5ERb0ohJWTYQTcFSMmq6lWTYAt9CcqFbVnt\ngEo6SWv5drbEd4nbaJzJBtF9bJ/JcxSdtxRYnVss7ZfTncOAQVy4AgFMgdmhcql3\nzXusebwsILvib8VeXgNQ7lfAepRdgItXtqWe6ZQ8Kz33eLlD/Uz4ihtRslIqSNGt\nFZKmeITVvxGbceGEsboWNh74U458DV1p2V9evs9KSa2llRSa0Si+M2tmkdBsKppp\nux6leQRuiHSAq4jtC0v7\n=hNz3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-07T17:35:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred