","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T15:50:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs(skills-assist): note the shared description-token budget (#64)\n\nAdds a description token-ceiling reference to the progressive-\ndisclosure table''s Metadata row (pointing at the canonical\nfoundation:context/shared/description-authoring-principles.md), and\none paragraph noting that skill metadata visibility is a SHARED,\ncapped budget, not a per-skill allowance: the visibility hook renders\nunder visibility_token_budget (default 5000 tokens) or, in legacy\ncount-cap mode, max_skills_visible (default 50, see\nmodules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/hooks.py). At the\ndefault 50-skill cap, the current curated collection''s top-50 already\nruns ~8k tokens/session at full detail before the budget renderer\nstarts trimming to name-only. No other content in this guide changed\n-- it is otherwise the model for description authoring in this repo.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"db446c0e634ccd1a4e5bca4ae27599030a7389b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/db446c0e634ccd1a4e5bca4ae27599030a7389b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/28c5c00c678b2b01e906b207ec8184a207cbc444","verification":{"payload":"tree db446c0e634ccd1a4e5bca4ae27599030a7389b1\nparent e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1788105022 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788105022 -0700\n\ndocs(skills-assist): note the shared description-token budget (#64)\n\nAdds a description token-ceiling reference to the progressive-\ndisclosure table''s Metadata row (pointing at the canonical\nfoundation:context/shared/description-authoring-principles.md), and\none paragraph noting that skill metadata visibility is a SHARED,\ncapped budget, not a per-skill allowance: the visibility hook renders\nunder visibility_token_budget (default 5000 tokens) or, in legacy\ncount-cap mode, max_skills_visible (default 50, see\nmodules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/hooks.py). At the\ndefault 50-skill cap, the current curated collection''s top-50 already\nruns ~8k tokens/session at full detail before the budget renderer\nstarts trimming to name-only. No other content in this guide changed\n-- it is otherwise the model for description authoring in this repo.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlFE+CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAeIgQAGsdJGscGgV2h073DPpN9uCA\nSyKXx5rk+qZmAD6yDP7Xb7BzKbBrFddCLiqzoBICh0p5YbF7+7yU+feoaO0uwXlG\n7k4PQbByEUToWsIcWHLiRf1m4YQRgDWmFGidKT+mwopsqlQs24uiexekR9e1PeW4\n8wrmSC/IF+xlXE6eKCy81BKlsUGDLUjHtH884mwuTZ5K/RoH0QfRDKvWY3jmCgKU\ngv0digh2b5fHNAwcwrYigxWrZ0f30sgzifAX+6CUD9qD5sWNChIZ03v0zHodQlHi\nP5xJqS1sP384wQIimMhnqf6mirG/NtnvuAaJOgY8mibiQXNCKiwe69MuDzvd/GbY\nFwXOfyukVC9guZpQyfwOL6NYMkU6p62tqqzFADlCDyrDGxAiw+Urzlr2n5I3qevd\nNs1TJCvid6HTH8sNuQZY7HR6G+U5EAt94eZQKpztV0DJe4YNiA+2ve5O/0zl7r6g\n+EKl0fci59fduPsUHxXWRm5qI0zJBfZKoGqW310C/0y+mUZlkw6dezNGITgGrbe3\nhhBjGUIkLsoa79jBJBbjSD3CruacECGh1yMa+tcWT2BjAr2ScwxHFyNAEcnmrRnP\nigtkdHE6PVf3Plr4raZOv9gNAu48sZnHBCBw0WQIthOpP2lsA50W6RXRgQ+0fBqM\nUZNnXiJTup7eqY+AxzMX\n=3J/d\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T15:50:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/28c5c00c678b2b01e906b207ec8184a207cbc444","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDI4YzVjMDBjNjc4YjJiMDFlOTA2YjIwN2VjODE4NGEyMDdjYmM0NDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58","sha":"e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58"}],"sha":"28c5c00c678b2b01e906b207ec8184a207cbc444","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/28c5c00c678b2b01e906b207ec8184a207cbc444"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:58:51Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T10:58:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(tool-skills): token-budget skills catalog — every skill visible, priority tiers, tightened descriptions (#63)\n\n* feat(tool-skills): budget-tier skills index — full coverage within a token budget\n\nReplace the alphabetical max_skills_visible cap (which silently dropped every\nskill sorting past position 50) with deterministic tier assembly under a\nconfigurable visibility_token_budget (default 5000, estimate = len//4):\n\n  1. Reserve a name-only index line for EVERY regular skill (full coverage).\n  2. Upgrade index -> one-line summary in rank order, while budget allows.\n  3. Upgrade summary -> full description in rank order, while budget allows.\n\nRank = (-priority, name). priority/summary come from an optional skill\n''visibility:'' frontmatter mapping, read by the hook (cached per path) so no\nmetadata field is added to discovery. Summary falls back to the description''s\nfirst sentence, truncated to 140 chars.\n\nBack-compat: max_skills_visible without a budget keeps the legacy count cap;\nbudget wins when both are set. behaviors/skills*.yaml switch to\nvisibility_token_budget: 5000. User-invoked section unchanged.\n\nAlso: monitor SKILL.md points at the ten-lane-highway skill.\n\n* test(tool-skills): repair two stale pre-existing tests blocking a green suite\n\nNeither test exercises the visibility budget; both fail on base 11f97bc and\nwere asserting against contracts that already changed:\n\n- test_fork_skill_model_resolver_called_with_metadata_fields registered its\n  resolver mock under the old ''routing_matrix'' capability with a sync resolve().\n  Production _execute_fork looks up ''model_role_resolver'' and awaits resolve().\n  Align the mock: register under ''model_role_resolver'', make resolve() async.\n\n- test_skills_visible_in_session matched the CLI''s unknown-option error as\n  ''No such option: --dry-run''; current CLI phrases it \"No such option\n  ''--dry-run''.\". Match the stable ''No such option'' prefix instead.\n\nFull suite from modules/tool-skills now: 304 passed.\n\n* docs(skills): tighten description frontmatter for the token-budget catalog\n\nThe skills index now renders in tiers (name -> one-line summary -> full\ndescription) under a token budget, so every wasted word in a `description:`\ncosts another skill its detail. This is an editorial pass over all 38\nskills/*/SKILL.md descriptions.\n\n- First sentence of every description now stands alone as a <=140-char\n  one-liner, which is exactly what the catalog''s summary tier renders\n  (hooks._first_sentence truncates at 140).\n- Load-bearing routing preserved verbatim or moved earlier: \"Use when\"\n  triggers, quoted trigger strings, slash-command names, MUST/ALWAYS\n  language, and cross-skill pointers (/council, /design-council, personafy,\n  crusty-old-engineer, ten-lane-highway, /verify).\n- Cut repetition, process narration, and over-long persona flavor. The\n  eleven persona lenses keep one load-bearing question, one voice clause,\n  and their triggers; each drops ~40-55%.\n- Literal block scalars (`|`) folded to `>-` so descriptions render as a\n  single line in the catalog instead of ragged multi-line list items.\n- visibility.priority: 5 added to councilify and tester-breaker, plus a\n  curated visibility.summary for councilify (its first sentence is a long\n  compound clause that would truncate badly).\n- code-review, mass-change, and session-debug left untouched: already clean,\n  standalone one-liners with no flab.\n\nTotal: 17,479 -> 13,389 chars (-4,090, -23%; ~4,369 -> ~3,347 est. tokens).\nNo name/version/shortcut/user-invocable/disable-model-invocation/license or\nbelow-frontmatter content changed; verified per-file against HEAD.\n\n* chore(councilify): drop visibility priority — hand-invoked in practice, curated summary suffices\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"022aa1862c528cddb7bc39854fb32b9d5e6bd1f1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/022aa1862c528cddb7bc39854fb32b9d5e6bd1f1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58","verification":{"payload":"tree 022aa1862c528cddb7bc39854fb32b9d5e6bd1f1\nparent 11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1788087531 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788087531 -0700\n\nfeat(tool-skills): token-budget skills catalog — every skill visible, priority tiers, tightened descriptions (#63)\n\n* feat(tool-skills): budget-tier skills index — full coverage within a token budget\n\nReplace the alphabetical max_skills_visible cap (which silently dropped every\nskill sorting past position 50) with deterministic tier assembly under a\nconfigurable visibility_token_budget (default 5000, estimate = len//4):\n\n  1. Reserve a name-only index line for EVERY regular skill (full coverage).\n  2. Upgrade index -> one-line summary in rank order, while budget allows.\n  3. Upgrade summary -> full description in rank order, while budget allows.\n\nRank = (-priority, name). priority/summary come from an optional skill\n''visibility:'' frontmatter mapping, read by the hook (cached per path) so no\nmetadata field is added to discovery. Summary falls back to the description''s\nfirst sentence, truncated to 140 chars.\n\nBack-compat: max_skills_visible without a budget keeps the legacy count cap;\nbudget wins when both are set. behaviors/skills*.yaml switch to\nvisibility_token_budget: 5000. User-invoked section unchanged.\n\nAlso: monitor SKILL.md points at the ten-lane-highway skill.\n\n* test(tool-skills): repair two stale pre-existing tests blocking a green suite\n\nNeither test exercises the visibility budget; both fail on base 11f97bc and\nwere asserting against contracts that already changed:\n\n- test_fork_skill_model_resolver_called_with_metadata_fields registered its\n  resolver mock under the old ''routing_matrix'' capability with a sync resolve().\n  Production _execute_fork looks up ''model_role_resolver'' and awaits resolve().\n  Align the mock: register under ''model_role_resolver'', make resolve() async.\n\n- test_skills_visible_in_session matched the CLI''s unknown-option error as\n  ''No such option: --dry-run''; current CLI phrases it \"No such option\n  ''--dry-run''.\". Match the stable ''No such option'' prefix instead.\n\nFull suite from modules/tool-skills now: 304 passed.\n\n* docs(skills): tighten description frontmatter for the token-budget catalog\n\nThe skills index now renders in tiers (name -> one-line summary -> full\ndescription) under a token budget, so every wasted word in a `description:`\ncosts another skill its detail. This is an editorial pass over all 38\nskills/*/SKILL.md descriptions.\n\n- First sentence of every description now stands alone as a <=140-char\n  one-liner, which is exactly what the catalog''s summary tier renders\n  (hooks._first_sentence truncates at 140).\n- Load-bearing routing preserved verbatim or moved earlier: \"Use when\"\n  triggers, quoted trigger strings, slash-command names, MUST/ALWAYS\n  language, and cross-skill pointers (/council, /design-council, personafy,\n  crusty-old-engineer, ten-lane-highway, /verify).\n- Cut repetition, process narration, and over-long persona flavor. The\n  eleven persona lenses keep one load-bearing question, one voice clause,\n  and their triggers; each drops ~40-55%.\n- Literal block scalars (`|`) folded to `>-` so descriptions render as a\n  single line in the catalog instead of ragged multi-line list items.\n- visibility.priority: 5 added to councilify and tester-breaker, plus a\n  curated visibility.summary for councilify (its first sentence is a long\n  compound clause that would truncate badly).\n- code-review, mass-change, and session-debug left untouched: already clean,\n  standalone one-liners with no flab.\n\nTotal: 17,479 -> 13,389 chars (-4,090, -23%; ~4,369 -> ~3,347 est. tokens).\nNo name/version/shortcut/user-invocable/disable-model-invocation/license or\nbelow-frontmatter content changed; verified per-file against HEAD.\n\n* chore(councilify): drop visibility priority — hand-invoked in practice, curated summary suffices\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqlAzrCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA4NQQAIR8Cjp0ykmL86CW9q88q2wm\n7otByrVvluX82cAjMXnsMvj56rXySECEjfWj5Z4SxI5haIrL+SQ48eNYp3DJMCzX\nR8/UwxA1i60iq3gPzT9TUh5efCnmBIEHZVTrduNggaT+DEds0Snyhg5zxqSazg69\n+Gk5Nn7MDdyTQtAKkD+CsbJrGi13t2XL7kyhSkNOM7Jr6gXalZQmUYfPjDoQdlEb\nkrGMbj1OSgpnrDNhTptVfidCMDqXorSdcesSUqxMUt11QHQWWXsf/otMQ9RoMDw0\npRYaUuOe9uAgzhcfZvdamKoV7Uz3PydXlZi5+xRkbTcg4AfWZwyYs+2JzBAxhH6I\nZobwY2eHKbqE0Ki79K3J3utaB4DfpHKLiw+kI1jMysMHDJRquDidrExCrc7yqkNx\n13gBERBUI0xOZtdR7v05+MFNfvNbLdML2S9wtTVw5nSIOYJYsvK9RMizX8W5hlD+\nREGiCz2UfQ2/WdwTdgsuj4gfCdX01EnivQaeLKL84LVjsyOnxUFFx90JrB4UigR1\n+Bd7/uU1uyhWp6NKPGHddcdL+yRxyGvA9ISbu5XWXm3Y/AK1cbEvjE+vYbdR6KPY\nMAKzlsyEPRNTB2VJoqbUs4hbU5H0MISDnCv4JVdhYCOMJdY9T8lMSJjFkMcZBJBm\nIISpY+izhpRkBzy9DFbh\n=Dp39\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-30T10:58:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGU0NjVmNWVkMDkwMDYxNjE3ZmFkZTA3YjA1MGM2ZjhiZjIxOTFlNTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a","sha":"11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a"}],"sha":"e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/e465f5ed090061617fade07b050c6f8bf2191e58"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T02:14:55Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T02:14:55Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(context): remove contradictory/duplicated skills instructions, point bundle-author material at skills-assist (#62)\n\nC4: modules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/__init__.py''s SkillsTool\ndescription told the model to \"Start tasks by listing or searching skills to\ndiscover relevant domain knowledge\" -- contradicting this bundle''s own\nskills-instructions.md (\"You don''t need to call load_skill(list=true) first\n- skills are made visible automatically through the visibility hook\") and\nthe actual runtime behavior (the visibility hook injects the full catalog\nevery turn regardless). Deleted the contradictory line.\n\nD1: deleted the fabricated <available_skills> example block in\nskills-instructions.md (wrong wrapper tag, fake skill names, missing the\nreal ''User-invoked skills (available via /command):'' section and truncation\nmarker) in favor of a two-sentence statement of the one load-bearing fact.\n\nD2: deleted the second, verbatim-duplicate copy of load_skill''s\noperations/usage in skills-instructions.md (already fully present in the\ntool''s own description, which is in the payload''s tool schema every turn).\n\nT3: deleted the bundle-author-only material (discovery paths/precedence,\ntool-skills config schema, config.skills source types, the silently-ignored\ntop-level skills: footgun) from skills-instructions.md in favor of a pointer\nto the skills-assist skill''s authoring-guide.md, which already documents all\nof it.\n\nD1+D2+T3 all touch skills-instructions.md and are applied as one combined\nchange to that file (two blocks), matching the source edit set''s own\nsequencing note.\n\nTest suite: modules/tool-skills/tests/ 285 passed, 2 failed -- both\npre-existing and confirmed via stash-compare to be present identically\nbefore this patch (test_enhanced_discovery.py''s mock-resolver assertion and\ntest_real_session.py''s CLI --dry-run flag mismatch; neither test references\nany of the content these items remove). Root tests/ + skills/skillify/ +\nskills/image-vision/ tests: 48 passed, 0 failed.\n\nValidated by the 1e2 context-hygiene DTU A/B treatment: 12/12 runs\ntask-correct on both providers at n=3/arm; wire audit confirmed every\ndeleted string absent in all treatment runs and present in all controls;\nmeasured -5,860 chars/turn system prompt (-11.3%) and -1,277 chars/turn tool\ncatalog (-4.5%) reduction across the full treatment set; no YAML corruption\nin mounted agent catalogs. (openai arm showed -45% cost but is noise-inflated\nat this sample size; the defensible claim is the wire-byte reduction.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"1cdbf87e6245bd2ae203bed0ed3ffa07a6215fce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/1cdbf87e6245bd2ae203bed0ed3ffa07a6215fce"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a","verification":{"payload":"tree 1cdbf87e6245bd2ae203bed0ed3ffa07a6215fce\nparent bceac5f175f1dde452856431668616bbbb5c678b\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1787969695 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787969695 -0700\n\nchore(context): remove contradictory/duplicated skills instructions, point bundle-author material at skills-assist (#62)\n\nC4: modules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/__init__.py''s SkillsTool\ndescription told the model to \"Start tasks by listing or searching skills to\ndiscover relevant domain knowledge\" -- contradicting this bundle''s own\nskills-instructions.md (\"You don''t need to call load_skill(list=true) first\n- skills are made visible automatically through the visibility hook\") and\nthe actual runtime behavior (the visibility hook injects the full catalog\nevery turn regardless). Deleted the contradictory line.\n\nD1: deleted the fabricated <available_skills> example block in\nskills-instructions.md (wrong wrapper tag, fake skill names, missing the\nreal ''User-invoked skills (available via /command):'' section and truncation\nmarker) in favor of a two-sentence statement of the one load-bearing fact.\n\nD2: deleted the second, verbatim-duplicate copy of load_skill''s\noperations/usage in skills-instructions.md (already fully present in the\ntool''s own description, which is in the payload''s tool schema every turn).\n\nT3: deleted the bundle-author-only material (discovery paths/precedence,\ntool-skills config schema, config.skills source types, the silently-ignored\ntop-level skills: footgun) from skills-instructions.md in favor of a pointer\nto the skills-assist skill''s authoring-guide.md, which already documents all\nof it.\n\nD1+D2+T3 all touch skills-instructions.md and are applied as one combined\nchange to that file (two blocks), matching the source edit set''s own\nsequencing note.\n\nTest suite: modules/tool-skills/tests/ 285 passed, 2 failed -- both\npre-existing and confirmed via stash-compare to be present identically\nbefore this patch (test_enhanced_discovery.py''s mock-resolver assertion and\ntest_real_session.py''s CLI --dry-run flag mismatch; neither test references\nany of the content these items remove). Root tests/ + skills/skillify/ +\nskills/image-vision/ tests: 48 passed, 0 failed.\n\nValidated by the 1e2 context-hygiene DTU A/B treatment: 12/12 runs\ntask-correct on both providers at n=3/arm; wire audit confirmed every\ndeleted string absent in all treatment runs and present in all controls;\nmeasured -5,860 chars/turn system prompt (-11.3%) and -1,277 chars/turn tool\ncatalog (-4.5%) reduction across the full treatment set; no YAML corruption\nin mounted agent catalogs. (openai arm showed -45% cost but is noise-inflated\nat this sample size; the defensible claim is the wire-byte reduction.)\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkkCfCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAQz0QAJqvdfr69xmYLn13y+oslL8h\n55O7tOst5X+tR2MH/vSVbudzgjrf7EIC3vIuarJF9TqRweUje17NQIdEKFtxPsDD\nfnoUFYL13z8A2O4peWhSAh1CeL64x2j4PoomfZiwag/tv5uAijkkf5O6C4piZjFU\nl3L+2u4Lav8gIQ/DNXFZGvCONPMGGxOMKxSB5+ZXWaAZwvsLhVAk9N+YFQQxjkyj\nvPpKWGW12jpaQwNY5nWDw4FyBBPEnRHqNJf3yKi0lY+cxlvwAEf5JMonrqARorkE\nDHbJqHOEpEXVLKrf1fZbIURd0RuDrRGQTA+eX9UcMY6uPNX+2CZ5sjc74pjPqXb9\n/ZGMak/rxxEBypM7rqJjev+0bW9SntzWNMuA/sh05aKZTK2pXSRup49xEWQuv54J\nlou+VYaiEH9gfR2Nzz1lypIlfyIxwKho+YeM7NmliKWp1kOlu7RjnSm7n12ZonVN\njfoMDre5bIE2PUV6CgroQpKoEOojby6LRO+Y02zbsdihGrkS16oPAYYVAxcSyZ0B\nUQwY6DZI5fpPb2wYODSnpTSGzdMM2ZWJRL0yp8EmRiQofm77jOp1lEQ6RZzMwP12\naWds42Y0zvvU+sISwMQN4pri1VU2YZ3zc4YuMDssLgYtNnaatVisU+TqQ/ZU9QLj\n26pUXPewFJnG77fX+oeW\n=YBeJ\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T02:14:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDExZjk3YmNjZDA1ZjU0YmMzY2M0MzJkMzUzNzJkNjFlNThkNGJmN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/bceac5f175f1dde452856431668616bbbb5c678b","sha":"bceac5f175f1dde452856431668616bbbb5c678b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/bceac5f175f1dde452856431668616bbbb5c678b"}],"sha":"11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/11f97bccd05f54bc3cc432d35372d61e58d4bf7a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11658960?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/sadlilas","id":11658960,"login":"sadlilas","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNjU4OTYw","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sadlilas","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/bceac5f175f1dde452856431668616bbbb5c678b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:23:50Z","email":"sadlilas@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Salil Das"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:23:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: make the remote-skills cache honour AMPLIFIER_HOME (#61)\n\nDEFAULT_SKILLS_CACHE_DIR was hardcoded to ~/.amplifier/cache/skills, making it the one cache path in the skills tool that ignored the variable the rest of the stack respects (amplifier_foundation.paths.get_amplifier_home).\n\nAn application that relocated its Amplifier home still had remote skill clones written into ~/.amplifier, shared with and indistinguishable from every other Amplifier app on the machine. Not reachable via config either: __init__.py:177 calls resolve_skill_sources(sources) with no cache_dir.\n\nReplaced with default_skills_cache_dir(), resolved per call rather than at import so a caller that sets AMPLIFIER_HOME during startup is not defeated by import order. Behaviour is unchanged when AMPLIFIER_HOME is unset.","tree":{"sha":"eeb73773424fed39684226e88e4e0c8b17c79859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/eeb73773424fed39684226e88e4e0c8b17c79859"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/bceac5f175f1dde452856431668616bbbb5c678b","verification":{"payload":"tree eeb73773424fed39684226e88e4e0c8b17c79859\nparent c2e204965f652657ec34d5f6918c9004032b1a6a\nauthor Salil Das <sadlilas@users.noreply.github.com> 1787603030 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787603030 -0700\n\nfix: make the remote-skills cache honour AMPLIFIER_HOME (#61)\n\nDEFAULT_SKILLS_CACHE_DIR was hardcoded to ~/.amplifier/cache/skills, making it the one cache path in the skills tool that ignored the variable the rest of the stack respects (amplifier_foundation.paths.get_amplifier_home).\n\nAn application that relocated its Amplifier home still had remote skill clones written into ~/.amplifier, shared with and indistinguishable from every other Amplifier app on the machine. Not reachable via config either: __init__.py:177 calls resolve_skill_sources(sources) with no cache_dir.\n\nReplaced with default_skills_cache_dir(), resolved per call rather than at import so a caller that sets AMPLIFIER_HOME during startup is not defeated by import order. Behaviour is unchanged when AMPLIFIER_HOME is unset.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqjKhWCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8loQADZIcmmNBsODFnm/wknwY4y9\nihtAw6D/gjIy5P+waFSjZQI1Xa5tviyJDDjUx1ELOQ7359ts6YDd19QZEpesN8qk\nHCphJL+DYlRo1lvT2NFX+TiauUXSN/I8O0jJIaqtkR1ASsrYnwr0XK2KjG0yFyE3\ntBT666AkrTbhFMWTFb+GrTl903v6gpM5G5G1Y2FpvFlQIaacip4T3u+ILSnyC075\njaprOKqLnN9fkHaOGNf2KToDa3xLucAZdSYccvV6odtEA3tUsFTohHfe0Me5/jbA\nNtm1SC0Or+TuESspIHMQs1Ih22e58rmK4VqyaovgnHqdq9UAxCdzF9onHUG5mXSJ\nx7o1yrvZUeDF0c4Zpe6zOUA1IxvT0bva4jG+XOFKpCFaEETLyIQosJVByVhV6GJB\nfRmeZA9tDhfHVsVjQV2FM7MKXvxiqj35hplK/dtlC6RiAr6bJuOO50Wv8C6M8kvr\n3ceRxWWlWx3PPyOnMJiMaSB+2bnijFOVwFJ+k64HXRNwvS+O/77Z6L1czy2V+/2m\nyvoPEb+fHXS0qs+OI/7OLhvBU6iFgYdk9DchwT3XIWeQvS3gD9Iw97dlCicJhrqd\n4zFkF36dQJ1/KVsksLJcoXWSczJsUWIjEuVNFIiGAroplV4/QfAy/BUrQqBY6W7H\n1Xjk1jUHt36E7MwlfcSJ\n=pP1s\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-24T20:23:51Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"h