scriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/44bd261b3af7bf15f1e48ced2c642dd69325f710/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:33:49Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-18T19:33:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: heal read-only .tmp so skill clone doesn''t jam forever on Windows (#58)\n\nReplaces the silent `shutil.rmtree(ignore_errors=True)` cleanup of the temp clone directory with a robust removal that clears the read-only bit and retries, then raises with a precise diagnostic if removal genuinely fails.\n\nRoot cause: git writes pack files (.idx/.pack/.rev) read-only. On Windows the read-only attribute blocks unlink, so the ignore_errors cleanup silently left the .tmp directory on disk. The next resolution attempt then found a non-empty .tmp and git clone aborted with ''destination path already exists'' -- jamming that skill source permanently.\n\nThe raised OSError is contained: it propagates to resolve_skill_source, which logs a warning and returns None, degrading exactly one skill source to ''not resolved'' while leaving all others unaffected.","tree":{"sha":"9bd013b8b36c1f5085e671a36142d2d40d95bec3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/9bd013b8b36c1f5085e671a36142d2d40d95bec3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/44bd261b3af7bf15f1e48ced2c642dd69325f710","verification":{"payload":"tree 9bd013b8b36c1f5085e671a36142d2d40d95bec3\nparent 16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1787081629 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787081629 -0700\n\nfix: heal read-only .tmp so skill clone doesn''t jam forever on Windows (#58)\n\nReplaces the silent `shutil.rmtree(ignore_errors=True)` cleanup of the temp clone directory with a robust removal that clears the read-only bit and retries, then raises with a precise diagnostic if removal genuinely fails.\n\nRoot cause: git writes pack files (.idx/.pack/.rev) read-only. On Windows the read-only attribute blocks unlink, so the ignore_errors cleanup silently left the .tmp directory on disk. The next resolution attempt then found a non-empty .tmp and git clone aborted with ''destination path already exists'' -- jamming that skill source permanently.\n\nThe raised OSError is contained: it propagates to resolve_skill_source, which logs a warning and returns None, degrading exactly one skill source to ''not resolved'' while leaving all others unaffected.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqhLOdCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAH50QAAsCg5+P9PmVD52akFkXqloX\nnCqeVlrwhb3V2aDd/CqXMLTOk6YVBZKjuYY8eoJOFmc3fsgb7pWFdB75AM5U9jQ4\nIR7g2f+fSUbipb7C9L0WroXuEYJVd69XpI3WoyjD7Slmj55h6IHXEDvWKfqKtYCq\nGF2DT3EQyJUGrsqTiKt054CyVnSWbrFyRBk3jtg0m96j87q1MlEQSW8v7/UGna0k\nMiDBnAA/xXWA/77eSSBOdaqCVYKn+t3DYKTUzC0pn0KlU/IyfpMYin98LndYvbc5\n3EaxhP8ZsHSnB6YWUHorwVEQX0dBpOm9xDvpTrBPU2BvRA3cXl5DPGLhupk6nvLU\nbXj7vEzsCMkTG47yU07y0i425laBp/MOMVFbOGhNIpHEvAi2N3xtxE0k8dQmDcBl\nrfqlbSu+175jTho4dX+j1kMnrcB95x1tZp6q9MLR8i782m3pyqYE6dwCxGzvR00w\nekiLfP7XKVQGp0Qtan5MRd38GMJ56MJUxMT8vdRDP+LTmBmvyjFop/14P1Y6BFuq\nkgcl3FDKXjFyqT5NcHkdPbUNzay0G4QALo0AGKnwYbddoGCQi2GRqEEnOC07PMAu\nR+ekDtuMV9vNtIXc40vwRg2D3/UQwFC3b4KbkjSokY2sbwEr1RzMWYAOIEinGn+X\nhGbteWhZc2MBBy2NV0tP\n=NKlN\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-18T19:33:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/44bd261b3af7bf15f1e48ced2c642dd69325f710","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDQ0YmQyNjFiM2FmN2JmMTVmMWU0OGNlZDJjNjQyZGQ2OTMyNWY3MTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b","sha":"16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b"}],"sha":"44bd261b3af7bf15f1e48ced2c642dd69325f710","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/44bd261b3af7bf15f1e48ced2c642dd69325f710"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T22:32:28Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T22:32:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: goal-batch — stop requiring a git remote, and correct the misattributed failure behind it (#57)\n\n* fix: goal-batch — stop requiring a git remote, and correct the misattributed failure behind it\n\nTwo corrections, both prompted by the skill owner questioning a rule.\n\n1. The preflight gate required every lane repo to have a reachable remote and refused to launch otherwise. That gate blocked a legitimate workflow for a reason that was never true.\n\nVerified by direct test: local-only git works through the entire lane lifecycle. A lane commits to its own branch; those commits live in the main repo''s object store, so they survive `git worktree remove` intact, remain reachable, and merge normally with no network at all. The only degradation is that batch_status.sh''s `pushed` column reads 0 — `git ls-remote` exits nonzero to stderr, it does not crash the probe.\n\nThe gate is now: every lane''s output must be COMMITTABLE, not pushable. A remote is recommended (lanes push as they commit, so a crash costs minutes rather than machine-loss risk) and is stated once, but it never blocks the batch.\n\n2. The justification for that gate was factually wrong and is corrected in place. The rule cited ''a real run produced 47MB of genuine output into a remoteless repo and landed nothing in git.'' That repo had TWO remotes configured. The actual loss was that the lane''s entire output sat under gitignored paths (input/, originals/, clean/, runs/, decisions/, *.log) — so it was never committed, and pushing would have saved none of it.\n\nThe preflight now checks the thing that actually loses work: will each lane''s deliverables land in a commit at all? If a lane''s real product is a gitignored artifact directory, that is surfaced at the approval gate as a batch that cannot deliver — a condition no remote fixes.\n\n3. Also clarified headless invocation: in a one-shot `amplifier run`, direct the assistant in natural language (''Use the goal-batch skill and ...'') or call load_skill outright. Naming the skill is what loads it; the bare slash token is not.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: goal-batch — mechanical tmux guard and lane-env preflight\n\nTwo safety mechanisms adopted from a parallel implementation of the same technique that has run ~185 lanes, plus three findings from its written retro.\n\n1. TMUX GUARD (safety hole in what shipped). goal-batch launches lanes into the shared tmux server with no protection. A lane that runs `tmux kill-server` without -L/-S kills the server it is running in — tmux resolves -S > -L > $TMUX > TMUX_TMPDIR, and $TMUX is set in every process descended from an attached client, so TMUX_TMPDIR is NOT isolation. This destroyed 73 live sessions on 2026-08-08 and 81 more on 2026-08-12. The second incident''s own retraction notes the lane had the precedence rule documented in its context when it ran the command — documentation does not stop this.\n\nlaunch_lane.sh now installs a PATH shim into the lane''s environment only (not the orchestrator''s) that refuses any tmux invocation lacking an explicit -L or -S, exits 78, and names the incidents. Verified: the plain `tmux kill-server` and the exact `TMUX_TMPDIR=... tmux kill-server` form from the 08-12 incident are both refused with exit 78; `tmux -L <name> new-session` is allowed through; the real server''s 72 sessions survived every test.\n\n2. LANE-ENV PREFLIGHT. A lane inherits the TMUX SERVER''s environment, not the orchestrator''s shell. When a variable the settings interpolate is missing there it resolves to empty — `base_url: ${ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL}` becomes \"\" and every LLM call dies with \"Connection error\" that looks exactly like a network outage. That killed three lanes twice in one day while the API was reachable throughout. Same class as the amplifier-not-on-PATH bug fixed earlier: the environment inherited into tmux is not the environment you tested in.\n\nlaunch_lane.sh now discovers interpolated variables from the settings files themselves (not a hardcoded provider list, so unknown providers are covered), diffs the current shell against `tmux show-environment -g`, and refuses to launch when a variable is set here but empty there — printing the exact `tmux set-environment -g` fix for each. Verified against a simulated missing variable.\n\n3. Three findings folded into SKILL.md from that implementation''s RETRO-parallel-lanes.md:\n- Inherited artifacts are the single biggest source of false signals. A lane''s worktree starts as a copy of the base commit, so pre-existing status files and evidence directories look like the lane''s own output. Three false alarms in one day came from this, including a BLOCKED.md byte-identical to main whose first line read \"The lane is not blocked\" being read as a real block, and \"23 evidence files\" where 20 were inherited. Phase 6 now requires proving a lane wrote an artifact before reading it as a signal.\n- Phase 7 now specifies three-dot diff (`git diff main...HEAD`). Two-dot compares against main''s current tip, so commits main gained while the lane ran appear as the lane''s work — that produced a near-miss ownership accusation against a lane that touched none of the files.\n- Phase 7 now requires reading diffs ACROSS lanes, not only within them. File ownership does not catch two lanes inventing the same abstraction at different paths — two lanes once created separate ThreadVisibility singletons, one written by one lane and read by the other, and both lanes'' tests passed while the behavior was silently broken.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"5f5fa388940bdef18d46128a30f9e94ad372137e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/5f5fa388940bdef18d46128a30f9e94ad372137e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5f5fa388940bdef18d46128a30f9e94ad372137e\nparent ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1786746748 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786746748 -0700\n\nfix: goal-batch — stop requiring a git remote, and correct the misattributed failure behind it (#57)\n\n* fix: goal-batch — stop requiring a git remote, and correct the misattributed failure behind it\n\nTwo corrections, both prompted by the skill owner questioning a rule.\n\n1. The preflight gate required every lane repo to have a reachable remote and refused to launch otherwise. That gate blocked a legitimate workflow for a reason that was never true.\n\nVerified by direct test: local-only git works through the entire lane lifecycle. A lane commits to its own branch; those commits live in the main repo''s object store, so they survive `git worktree remove` intact, remain reachable, and merge normally with no network at all. The only degradation is that batch_status.sh''s `pushed` column reads 0 — `git ls-remote` exits nonzero to stderr, it does not crash the probe.\n\nThe gate is now: every lane''s output must be COMMITTABLE, not pushable. A remote is recommended (lanes push as they commit, so a crash costs minutes rather than machine-loss risk) and is stated once, but it never blocks the batch.\n\n2. The justification for that gate was factually wrong and is corrected in place. The rule cited ''a real run produced 47MB of genuine output into a remoteless repo and landed nothing in git.'' That repo had TWO remotes configured. The actual loss was that the lane''s entire output sat under gitignored paths (input/, originals/, clean/, runs/, decisions/, *.log) — so it was never committed, and pushing would have saved none of it.\n\nThe preflight now checks the thing that actually loses work: will each lane''s deliverables land in a commit at all? If a lane''s real product is a gitignored artifact directory, that is surfaced at the approval gate as a batch that cannot deliver — a condition no remote fixes.\n\n3. Also clarified headless invocation: in a one-shot `amplifier run`, direct the assistant in natural language (''Use the goal-batch skill and ...'') or call load_skill outright. Naming the skill is what loads it; the bare slash token is not.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: goal-batch — mechanical tmux guard and lane-env preflight\n\nTwo safety mechanisms adopted from a parallel implementation of the same technique that has run ~185 lanes, plus three findings from its written retro.\n\n1. TMUX GUARD (safety hole in what shipped). goal-batch launches lanes into the shared tmux server with no protection. A lane that runs `tmux kill-server` without -L/-S kills the server it is running in — tmux resolves -S > -L > $TMUX > TMUX_TMPDIR, and $TMUX is set in every process descended from an attached client, so TMUX_TMPDIR is NOT isolation. This destroyed 73 live sessions on 2026-08-08 and 81 more on 2026-08-12. The second incident''s own retraction notes the lane had the precedence rule documented in its context when it ran the command — documentation does not stop this.\n\nlaunch_lane.sh now installs a PATH shim into the lane''s environment only (not the orchestrator''s) that refuses any tmux invocation lacking an explicit -L or -S, exits 78, and names the incidents. Verified: the plain `tmux kill-server` and the exact `TMUX_TMPDIR=... tmux kill-server` form from the 08-12 incident are both refused with exit 78; `tmux -L <name> new-session` is allowed through; the real server''s 72 sessions survived every test.\n\n2. LANE-ENV PREFLIGHT. A lane inherits the TMUX SERVER''s environment, not the orchestrator''s shell. When a variable the settings interpolate is missing there it resolves to empty — `base_url: ${ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL}` becomes \"\" and every LLM call dies with \"Connection error\" that looks exactly like a network outage. That killed three lanes twice in one day while the API was reachable throughout. Same class as the amplifier-not-on-PATH bug fixed earlier: the environment inherited into tmux is not the environment you tested in.\n\nlaunch_lane.sh now discovers interpolated variables from the settings files themselves (not a hardcoded provider list, so unknown providers are covered), diffs the current shell against `tmux show-environment -g`, and refuses to launch when a variable is set here but empty there — printing the exact `tmux set-environment -g` fix for each. Verified against a simulated missing variable.\n\n3. Three findings folded into SKILL.md from that implementation''s RETRO-parallel-lanes.md:\n- Inherited artifacts are the single biggest source of false signals. A lane''s worktree starts as a copy of the base commit, so pre-existing status files and evidence directories look like the lane''s own output. Three false alarms in one day came from this, including a BLOCKED.md byte-identical to main whose first line read \"The lane is not blocked\" being read as a real block, and \"23 evidence files\" where 20 were inherited. Phase 6 now requires proving a lane wrote an artifact before reading it as a signal.\n- Phase 7 now specifies three-dot diff (`git diff main...HEAD`). Two-dot compares against main''s current tip, so commits main gained while the lane ran appear as the lane''s work — that produced a near-miss ownership accusation against a lane that touched none of the files.\n- Phase 7 now requires reading diffs ACROSS lanes, not only within them. File ownership does not catch two lanes inventing the same abstraction at different paths — two lanes once created separate ThreadVisibility singletons, one written by one lane and read by the other, and both lanes'' tests passed while the behavior was silently broken.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqf5d8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+/UQAJ5swOOggMhqjcdaT+l1h7B4\nVnRfEXzSaszUl4bNTdGkedyb9rBmF3IHLUy80q04C9RAWDA/pjxtJJQAiVv8xf83\n4lZUapDZr6uA76XsJOf0J1Qk5ssygiGJaJlY9rFSgCSk98L7toME40J2jZeJRjJp\nzlPXMcqhUlSVFHPZHmoY2rpZrWbGi9ntYqBqtpvWr5tZkp3EYpdBum5/nIbZhPDG\nQnNyx599X3HVI4eV5P7fvlTZ0aqKcKgdCILGrofvf2H3j/y3Pd4oJcDD5ChIcC4D\nvkYwTmSBEXHEZh52HL9BZtrg1sOejgvzabay9jkTgpWfY2+wZXsnykgDOeAalIFK\nY7UqLdjtHMXTqDW9KjHA1Go7qgk5X2ZLHuYqzB3W7pEfSMzvhs1XiWiw4OBNvHsP\n7mvRoVM9xRHLH2I390b1bs5iocEN4k4lAwU/U5iDZPSx9hYwQ8ZBCKSGH5NBJTWv\nTR8RQIFgbeRlkaOsC29QE1E/e+LSpUzCTMz9S06KtLRvbuOW/PQkLr4ovHNhIGlo\neYdf/ecICr4zamo1tnNVjIMtYgdDjPHtpificvXjDLd5jRwErt9xE80/bidu7iaZ\nBdOKM5Z9dDK4/guslKLtqx8hUSWeMtlhVZ9285xU2JOp4dns0jEEt3FEdcN36K0i\nZzdLpqBL2AOuzES+t4Tk\n=XuFr\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T22:32:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDE2ZmI3MGQ1NGM0Zjg0ZTBmOTlkMjhmNTZiMzU1ZDliNDVmYTBhOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038","sha":"ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038"}],"sha":"16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/16fb70d54c4f84e0f99d28f56b355d9b45fa0a8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-14T19:59:02Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-14T19:59:02Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: goal-batch v2 — repair the launcher/status contract, harden against real-run failures (#56)\n\ngoal-batch v2.0.0. Five days of real team use (3 operators, ~45 lanes) surfaced defects that a single-operator proving run structurally could not catch. Every change below traces to a specific observed failure.\n\nSCRIPT FIXES (mechanisms, not guidance):\n- launch_lane.sh now OWNS the manifest end-to-end — writes the header and appends one 8-column row per lane. v1 emitted 5 columns while batch_status.sh read 7; the two never agreed, so no batch could actually use both tools as shipped. Both real users independently hand-wrote manifests to work around it.\n- Manifest now records the lane PID. batch_status.sh determines liveness from `kill -0 <pid>` first, tmux only as corroboration. The tmux server has died mid-batch in three separate runs, leaving healthy lanes running as orphans while tmux-keyed probes went blind.\n- launch_lane.sh purges any inherited DONE.json before launch, and batch_status.sh cross-checks DONE.json''s session_id against the manifest — reporting STALE-DONE-IGNORED on mismatch. A DONE.json carried in through the base commit otherwise reads as an already-finished lane.\n- `setsid --wait` (was bare `setsid`) — bare setsid launched ZERO of five lanes on another operator''s machine while working here.\n- launch_lane.sh resolves `amplifier` via plain PATH then login PATH, pins the absolute path into the wrapper, and aborts immediately with a clear message if unresolvable. Previously a non-login-shell PATH produced a confusing 60-second wait for a Session ID that could never arrive.\n- batch_status.sh prints BATCH_ELAPSED from the manifest header and renames the per-lane column to LANE_IDLE. A watcher read lane idle-seconds as batch elapsed time and terminated a watch at 30 minutes actual while claiming 95.\n- batch_status.sh normalizes the DONE.json verdict enum. Two lanes in one batch wrote \"PASS\" and \"success\"; no parser reads those the same way.\n- tmux session name and log path are now DERIVED from batch/lane, so the gb__* convention the orphan sweep and pane-viewer match strings depend on cannot drift.\n\nSKILL.md CHANGES:\n- Phase 2 gate now opens with what the batch will NOT deliver. In a real run the fact that the batch would not produce a working component was disclosed as the third bullet inside a code block, and the user found out only afterwards.\n- Phase 2 requires each lane to trace to something the user asked for. A run invented a lane from the orchestrator''s own scratch notes and got 32 minutes into the gate before the user caught it.\n- Phase 2 honors explicit pre-authorization: plan is always shown, stopping is what a user may waive.\n- Phase 3 requires gitignoring DONE.json before writing it (four of five lanes in one run committed theirs and the merge pass collided on that file), pins the verdict enum to COMPLETE/BLOCKED/PARTIAL, and requires session_id in DONE.json.\n- Phase 6 rewritten around evidence-bound monitoring: every claim about a lane must come from a probe just run; wait on state change, not on a clock. The lowest-overhead run measured (7% of spend) probed for everything it said; watchers that narrated from memory fabricated in multiple runs.\n- Handles empty $ARGUMENTS explicitly — a fork-skill invocation without arguments silently killed a real run.\n- Added `version: 2.0.0` to frontmatter.\n\nVERIFICATION (all run, not asserted):\n- 7 local tests pass: crossed manifest pipe, stale-DONE detection, tmux-death survival, verdict enum normalization across 5 inputs, idempotent relaunch, dead-lane detection, guard rejections.\n- DTU end-to-end with two REAL amplifier lanes: launch_lane.sh wrote the manifest, batch_status.sh read it correctly (the seam that was broken in v1), a seeded stale DONE.json was purged, `tmux kill-server` was executed mid-run and both lanes continued to report WORKING via PID, both reached COMPLETE with matching session_ids, both branches pushed to a real remote, zero DONE.json tracked in any commit, full teardown clean.\n\nKNOWN: SKILL.md grew 258 → 336 lines. Every addition traces to a measured failure, but length is worth watching on the next revision.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"49d7770b10948da75a9060aedd13fd38225e3aaf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/49d7770b10948da75a9060aedd13fd38225e3aaf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038","verification":{"payload":"tree 49d7770b10948da75a9060aedd13fd38225e3aaf\nparent b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1786737542 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786737542 -0700\n\nfix: goal-batch v2 — repair the launcher/status contract, harden against real-run failures (#56)\n\ngoal-batch v2.0.0. Five days of real team use (3 operators, ~45 lanes) surfaced defects that a single-operator proving run structurally could not catch. Every change below traces to a specific observed failure.\n\nSCRIPT FIXES (mechanisms, not guidance):\n- launch_lane.sh now OWNS the manifest end-to-end — writes the header and appends one 8-column row per lane. v1 emitted 5 columns while batch_status.sh read 7; the two never agreed, so no batch could actually use both tools as shipped. Both real users independently hand-wrote manifests to work around it.\n- Manifest now records the lane PID. batch_status.sh determines liveness from `kill -0 <pid>` first, tmux only as corroboration. The tmux server has died mid-batch in three separate runs, leaving healthy lanes running as orphans while tmux-keyed probes went blind.\n- launch_lane.sh purges any inherited DONE.json before launch, and batch_status.sh cross-checks DONE.json''s session_id against the manifest — reporting STALE-DONE-IGNORED on mismatch. A DONE.json carried in through the base commit otherwise reads as an already-finished lane.\n- `setsid --wait` (was bare `setsid`) — bare setsid launched ZERO of five lanes on another operator''s machine while working here.\n- launch_lane.sh resolves `amplifier` via plain PATH then login PATH, pins the absolute path into the wrapper, and aborts immediately with a clear message if unresolvable. Previously a non-login-shell PATH produced a confusing 60-second wait for a Session ID that could never arrive.\n- batch_status.sh prints BATCH_ELAPSED from the manifest header and renames the per-lane column to LANE_IDLE. A watcher read lane idle-seconds as batch elapsed time and terminated a watch at 30 minutes actual while claiming 95.\n- batch_status.sh normalizes the DONE.json verdict enum. Two lanes in one batch wrote \"PASS\" and \"success\"; no parser reads those the same way.\n- tmux session name and log path are now DERIVED from batch/lane, so the gb__* convention the orphan sweep and pane-viewer match strings depend on cannot drift.\n\nSKILL.md CHANGES:\n- Phase 2 gate now opens with what the batch will NOT deliver. In a real run the fact that the batch would not produce a working component was disclosed as the third bullet inside a code block, and the user found out only afterwards.\n- Phase 2 requires each lane to trace to something the user asked for. A run invented a lane from the orchestrator''s own scratch notes and got 32 minutes into the gate before the user caught it.\n- Phase 2 honors explicit pre-authorization: plan is always shown, stopping is what a user may waive.\n- Phase 3 requires gitignoring DONE.json before writing it (four of five lanes in one run committed theirs and the merge pass collided on that file), pins the verdict enum to COMPLETE/BLOCKED/PARTIAL, and requires session_id in DONE.json.\n- Phase 6 rewritten around evidence-bound monitoring: every claim about a lane must come from a probe just run; wait on state change, not on a clock. The lowest-overhead run measured (7% of spend) probed for everything it said; watchers that narrated from memory fabricated in multiple runs.\n- Handles empty $ARGUMENTS explicitly — a fork-skill invocation without arguments silently killed a real run.\n- Added `version: 2.0.0` to frontmatter.\n\nVERIFICATION (all run, not asserted):\n- 7 local tests pass: crossed manifest pipe, stale-DONE detection, tmux-death survival, verdict enum normalization across 5 inputs, idempotent relaunch, dead-lane detection, guard rejections.\n- DTU end-to-end with two REAL amplifier lanes: launch_lane.sh wrote the manifest, batch_status.sh read it correctly (the seam that was broken in v1), a seeded stale DONE.json was purged, `tmux kill-server` was executed mid-run and both lanes continued to report WORKING via PID, both reached COMPLETE with matching session_ids, both branches pushed to a real remote, zero DONE.json tracked in any commit, full teardown clean.\n\nKNOWN: SKILL.md grew 258 → 336 lines. Every addition traces to a measured failure, but length is worth watching on the next revision.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqf3OGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAYpcQAD077TzA6Xzb8BOYbbQHylaJ\nQ8uZ3slx0613LViV7AwxEBDsj9tvgCsX6EDjiBKyz7JopTrzgH6sJrF39i7trtcP\n8E/VxXgHjfcd3MO/JGsMHRSKS1FdBU6JhLOQ0CxV8WzvGic7CGqwbXHKxz5/8W+X\nG/iO9gZC0JY175YRKvGSN80X1dFmfSwF+51CGp6QjDSDBnHD9u9WB2levklOV7he\nYF+AmCdvLC02j7TFoLWODG03wQR1Fq+shaFkM9KSOE9mefJQdaDIiGhcDPRfKTwb\nWE0gEpEAm284CQKgsCeZzk35pn1333MCXdOdBBu6cOPxoUMPKdH/2mspawDnaHqu\nH/AuAg4O4g6LzpqN4/XIRxFUbCKoySJ6DfJ4pGc8g/DHd7itN90JXlUTLOVzpnKb\nbJ88Ht/lAAfXPwvN5uGqNjcZk7ekuQrvCzqwt27WI+g37US04nC1GczA/rwDvb/U\n5aN/rlsGHqAkhQBuIyMkgwJq0Jo1Xo4DYaa36ci9eow9KFqCMkt8iST8ouRvlltH\nNHx6drvEyaS3WmDxckaUnXsDSRC/y/bmRyfLjWXl1fahQeG0aSKUoeLlM5/oE3jU\ndIw7NzRJAl1AquCrC+3hK7cU4KU8TBgkpdCXo3s408wkPlf11Tao8w5Zx8khFDt3\ntLBeCvBEL3M7q1tCQwum\n=0rSw\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-14T19:59:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGRkZmMxNGNlNDYwMzExMjhjM2EyNjhmZmU2MTA5NDk3NmFlNTkwMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28","sha":"b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28"}],"sha":"ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/ddfc14ce46031128c3a268ffe61094976ae59038"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T19:01:09Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-10T19:01:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add goal-batch skill (#55)\n\nAdds the goal-batch skill: plan a batch of independent work into isolated\nlanes, get user approval, then run each lane as its own autonomous /goal\nsession (one git worktree + branch + tmux session each), watch them, and\nverify-and-merge the results with the full suite re-run after every merge.\n\nIncludes companion scripts (launch_lane.sh, batch_status.sh, lane_turns.sh),\nexamples, and comprehensive documentation.\n\nEvidence base: derived from ~33 lanes of production use across 4 repos and\nproven end-to-end in an isolated Digital Twin Universe container\n(2 lanes, real nested sessions, 2 --no-ff merges, test suite 6 -> 27,\nfull teardown verified).\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"d4f4c8dda39436b8b472f17705a5a63f7e7e16f3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/d4f4c8dda39436b8b472f17705a5a63f7e7e16f3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28","verification":{"payload":"tree d4f4c8dda39436b8b472f17705a5a63f7e7e16f3\nparent cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1786388469 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1786388469 -0700\n\nfeat: add goal-batch skill (#55)\n\nAdds the goal-batch skill: plan a batch of independent work into isolated\nlanes, get user approval, then run each lane as its own autonomous /goal\nsession (one git worktree + branch + tmux session each), watch them, and\nverify-and-merge the results with the full suite re-run after every merge.\n\nIncludes companion scripts (launch_lane.sh, batch_status.sh, lane_turns.sh),\nexamples, and comprehensive documentation.\n\nEvidence base: derived from ~33 lanes of production use across 4 repos and\nproven end-to-end in an isolated Digital Twin Universe container\n(2 lanes, real nested sessions, 2 --no-ff merges, test suite 6 -> 27,\nfull teardown verified).\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.co