/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGIyNTNmNmM1ODFjYzAzMGQ4OWVkODEzNDA3YWMzNWJhOTE5MWZjMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982","sha":"cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982"}],"sha":"b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b253f6c581cc030d89ed813407ac35ba9191fc28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T04:23:34Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T04:23:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: never let a skill git-clone prompt on the terminal (#54)\n\nA `git clone` for a skill source, issued from inside the REPL against a\nremote that demands credentials, freezes the entire CLI.\n\ngit opens /dev/tty BY PATH -- not the inherited stdin -- and blocks reading\nit. The descriptor is held by `git-remote-http`, which is NOT the process\nthe timeout kills: CPython''s subprocess.run() kills only the direct child.\nThe orphan survives (measured: 140.6s past the 120s timeout, 1406/1406\nticks, 24/24 trials), keeps holding the terminal, and races prompt_toolkit''s\nstdin reader. That reader runs on the asyncio event-loop thread via\nloop.add_reader, so when its os.read parks, run_forever cannot advance and\nno timer fires. The session hangs until a keypress.\n\nMeasured at a gate-satisfying baseline (12/12 trials firing):\n\n  baseline                    50 park events, 12/12 trials\n  stdin=DEVNULL (rejected)    51 park events  <- closes the WRONG channel\n  GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0        0 park events, 0/12   p=7.4e-07\n  tree-reap on timeout         0 park events, 0/12   p=7.4e-07\n  both (this change)           0 park events, 0/12   p=7.4e-07\n\nPooled across five candidate arms: 241 events / 72 baseline trials -> 0 / 60\ncandidate trials, Fisher p=2.9e-33. All 241 baseline events were BY-PATH\nreads on /dev/tty fds 6,7. Zero candidate-arm events in any channel.\n\nEnd-to-end against the really-installed module, real timeout=120:\n  amplifier tool invoke load_skill source=git+https://<auth-required>\n    before: 121.69s (frozen)   after: 1.83s\n  REPL-level: 37 events / 12/12 -> 0 events / 0/12 with 69% more exposure\n  Public-clone regression: 1.89s -> 1.80s, unchanged\n\nFull evidence: github.com/bkrabach/amplifier-tty-freeze-siteeval (REPORT.md,\n~6,000 trials, 16 append-only rounds).\n\nCredential helpers, tokens embedded in the URL, and GH_TOKEN-style auth are\nunaffected -- only INTERACTIVE prompting is disabled. The tree-reap is\ndefence in depth: if anything in the tree ever blocks on the terminal for\nanother reason, the leak stays bounded by the timeout.\n\nThe clone tests were re-seamed onto `_run_clone` because this fix moves the\ncall off `subprocess.run`, which the existing mocks patched; without the\nre-seam they silently stopped intercepting and hit the network.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"55e7108e1e661f7744c73b0e4222b90f683c10b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/55e7108e1e661f7744c73b0e4222b90f683c10b3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982","verification":{"payload":"tree 55e7108e1e661f7744c73b0e4222b90f683c10b3\nparent af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785731014 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785731014 -0700\n\nfix: never let a skill git-clone prompt on the terminal (#54)\n\nA `git clone` for a skill source, issued from inside the REPL against a\nremote that demands credentials, freezes the entire CLI.\n\ngit opens /dev/tty BY PATH -- not the inherited stdin -- and blocks reading\nit. The descriptor is held by `git-remote-http`, which is NOT the process\nthe timeout kills: CPython''s subprocess.run() kills only the direct child.\nThe orphan survives (measured: 140.6s past the 120s timeout, 1406/1406\nticks, 24/24 trials), keeps holding the terminal, and races prompt_toolkit''s\nstdin reader. That reader runs on the asyncio event-loop thread via\nloop.add_reader, so when its os.read parks, run_forever cannot advance and\nno timer fires. The session hangs until a keypress.\n\nMeasured at a gate-satisfying baseline (12/12 trials firing):\n\n  baseline                    50 park events, 12/12 trials\n  stdin=DEVNULL (rejected)    51 park events  <- closes the WRONG channel\n  GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0        0 park events, 0/12   p=7.4e-07\n  tree-reap on timeout         0 park events, 0/12   p=7.4e-07\n  both (this change)           0 park events, 0/12   p=7.4e-07\n\nPooled across five candidate arms: 241 events / 72 baseline trials -> 0 / 60\ncandidate trials, Fisher p=2.9e-33. All 241 baseline events were BY-PATH\nreads on /dev/tty fds 6,7. Zero candidate-arm events in any channel.\n\nEnd-to-end against the really-installed module, real timeout=120:\n  amplifier tool invoke load_skill source=git+https://<auth-required>\n    before: 121.69s (frozen)   after: 1.83s\n  REPL-level: 37 events / 12/12 -> 0 events / 0/12 with 69% more exposure\n  Public-clone regression: 1.89s -> 1.80s, unchanged\n\nFull evidence: github.com/bkrabach/amplifier-tty-freeze-siteeval (REPORT.md,\n~6,000 trials, 16 append-only rounds).\n\nCredential helpers, tokens embedded in the URL, and GH_TOKEN-style auth are\nunaffected -- only INTERACTIVE prompting is disabled. The tree-reap is\ndefence in depth: if anything in the tree ever blocks on the terminal for\nanother reason, the leak stays bounded by the timeout.\n\nThe clone tests were re-seamed onto `_run_clone` because this fix moves the\ncall off `subprocess.run`, which the existing mocks patched; without the\nre-seam they silently stopped intercepting and hit the network.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqcBfGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACsYQAE14UQRhETjqYiAIUQ4cDPoq\nJJKmvk1PaCpCW10Sa1lM3w6paHKOVrV4jvDxAaxGR52AsThNAqgTb9Xap4SQPrqH\nV3w3EFTYcOzgaSp1Rids/+PfEq9RkJUvcOxfusm680F7EMF82k4L/k9N/9RPkEDc\no1f9U3q4d1AqUu6nnjtrPpLGi3v1l2nbcpgtHldIYj3hyrfpyCQW00nN8x933NJG\nBuLVSZTHNsIm4T5JLe1/wVRcDA/lOlf2ENnWaDGDoE2f2noQ2Tj+LnlGKCtPNZiJ\nWLPgE2Bu46punipaEzcpSdpSiND+Q6/aRbn49HSViLtWgFcSyQAFuWdd4/yH6IBq\nqqmAe/2oPkIfxKqigC6am3as+41yGTbAX0In6XKIKRyQn0eE36cOPLB2myS1iyLu\nsuuHY2QwUlUZmorg3czMggoQoUnHcrMP+Q3p+dgfQwsKfvq7SAGw+Ey7J5KmLHDI\ndE3MwxG5IBGg7nFiccNZ7wCIR5rxqqjQJ119jIl6Bqp4EXRk9l/ffqR5jTIYxhTh\nJhtMy5cHiv1daQT5BZoWU94Y9bP8Vs+6AGMqRU/Ml7OlKy+JmCRCvQurUXlj9Ojo\nchK0ZKNfF74LIG6pXbiugXSM9fyQ23DKNAM+KBU/3dwqfHDIpZVAWc6OqNNjYJSl\nptikd+L8mYYQSrcNFTwr\n=wMcO\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T04:23:35Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGNmYTlmMmE2ZjgyMDAyMTE0YzFiZGZiNzI3ODk3ODQxMWQ0MDQ5ODI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c","sha":"af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c"}],"sha":"cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/cfa9f2a6f82002114c1bdfb7278978411d404982"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:23:59Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T02:23:59Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore: remove graphify skill (lost 5/5 evals to grep baseline) (#53)\n\nThe graphify skill, added in PR #51, wrapped Graphify-Labs'' graphifyy PyPI\npackage. Before publication, it had been evaluated in five fair A/B tests\nagainst grep/read baselines on real corpora — code call-chain queries,\ncross-document synthesis, cross-author synthesis, semantic oracle queries,\nand structural analytics. It lost all five.\n\nThe skill''s central routing claim was disabled before publication; its\ndescription was rewritten to tell agents NOT to route ordinary queries\nthrough it. But it remained model-invocable (user-invocable: true, no\ndisable-model-invocation), so it stayed in the always-visible skills\nindex — roughly 731 characters of description in every session for every\nconsumer — while explicitly telling the model not to use it.\n\nA hands-on evaluation run against this repo''s 46-skill corpus reproduced\nthe known failure modes (god nodes were template headings and test helpers\nrather than real abstractions; 84 duplicate node labels from template\nsection headings; structural and semantic extractors emit inconsistent\nsource paths for the same file, causing self-connections to be reported\nas cross-repo links).\n\nUsage has been zero since the June evaluation. The one case where it\ndemonstrably produced value was one-time orientation on a large unfamiliar\ncodebase — a narrow and rare use case that does not justify a permanent\nper-session context cost in a curated collection.\n\nThe skill remains recoverable from git history. The upstream graphifyy\npackage remains independently installable for anyone who wants it.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6aed8e0d6e2b052b7c5fa91a4beb96a704d63f74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/6aed8e0d6e2b052b7c5fa91a4beb96a704d63f74"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c","verification":{"payload":"tree 6aed8e0d6e2b052b7c5fa91a4beb96a704d63f74\nparent 935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785723839 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785723839 -0700\n\nchore: remove graphify skill (lost 5/5 evals to grep baseline) (#53)\n\nThe graphify skill, added in PR #51, wrapped Graphify-Labs'' graphifyy PyPI\npackage. Before publication, it had been evaluated in five fair A/B tests\nagainst grep/read baselines on real corpora — code call-chain queries,\ncross-document synthesis, cross-author synthesis, semantic oracle queries,\nand structural analytics. It lost all five.\n\nThe skill''s central routing claim was disabled before publication; its\ndescription was rewritten to tell agents NOT to route ordinary queries\nthrough it. But it remained model-invocable (user-invocable: true, no\ndisable-model-invocation), so it stayed in the always-visible skills\nindex — roughly 731 characters of description in every session for every\nconsumer — while explicitly telling the model not to use it.\n\nA hands-on evaluation run against this repo''s 46-skill corpus reproduced\nthe known failure modes (god nodes were template headings and test helpers\nrather than real abstractions; 84 duplicate node labels from template\nsection headings; structural and semantic extractors emit inconsistent\nsource paths for the same file, causing self-connections to be reported\nas cross-repo links).\n\nUsage has been zero since the June evaluation. The one case where it\ndemonstrably produced value was one-time orientation on a large unfamiliar\ncodebase — a narrow and rare use case that does not justify a permanent\nper-session context cost in a curated collection.\n\nThe skill remains recoverable from git history. The upstream graphifyy\npackage remains independently installable for anyone who wants it.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb/u/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA8esQAE/aM2Vq3HJS0nh6c5c/TJzP\n7Held5Z7TBCjO/r0KTf6NcVnZqwEtDbYbtYg9UAx7o2gycHyw3c49YUtT2KBXeBs\nV8MOylG1sUQe6Umas97XJLUtcQMNK0Hwu/yx5z/TGP4bufPzdamqYh/SAmQmoBWF\n+tT2iald8CFXHbYyjOqdSa9vk0iQ3cTbFx0xU9SAgjvTewKyOvK5ORfc0r9HCMdL\n3+/gZWc1WCqHVnwc57tRueUVLdsbYpm7DfHS0bXCJwqvQQDcgwlNes/B+j7UONEK\nsKHfxcUaM3ZmQ4oFLkrAvMpC5nQzVHOjnjhtpxwDB2M9cOMl0DbqBdJk+3RWUZ2Z\nvp57/ySwl+/jhhc7x28mB+QSSqz/Fktwb3rdf5iOL1/ag4rkat/1XXlUiwIJJN+9\nx7s08g4mop0yW/65BSvBe9sbDlwVpz97nlWH+J4JEpPq21227YL4KPtXB93GMwWi\n+qBIbhfjUy4970aPa14l1ngtNiUd7Z+JhHpdTeMawgVUAYPGukb0Q53UIC4E0uqd\n+M4fJ+iC9nNXN38ujHCF6kQI/4eZXoaicMRvnXFlE8tB4YjpwdKKoshMeF1OZkzQ\nYHDRX9cnBlmwx/8CPdQkBUuQAxAHrF1uvdGlvIuTV2cxhuFPyEU9jpw4cqRUb4g3\niKsLGOon2vJDqmC5vXJT\n=rubU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T02:24:00Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGFmMzkwNmI5OWYyOWI1ZDg5NmFlZGE3YmEyMjEyOTIzYzU2OTAxM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961","sha":"935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961"}],"sha":"af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/af3906b99f29b5d896aeda7ba2212923c569013c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:05:47Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-03T00:05:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve @namespace:path skill sources from config.skills (#52)\n\nThe docs (context/skills-instructions.md) promise that config.skills\naccepts a bundle reference like \"@mybundle:skills\", but the mount-time\nresolver (_resolve_skill_sources) only handled git+ URLs and literal\npaths: an @-entry fell into the local-path branch, failed Path.exists(),\nand was silently dropped at debug level. Bundles that register their own\nskills this way (e.g. design-council''s \"@design-council:skills\") never\nloaded them.\n\nA naive mount-time resolve cannot work: the mention_resolver capability\nis registered by the app layer AFTER session.initialize() (which is when\nmounts run) in both production session paths, so get_capability(\n\"mention_resolver\") during mount returns None in every path today.\n\nFix (deferred one-shot resolution, module-local):\n- _resolve_skill_sources partitions @-entries out of the path/git logic\n  and returns them as pending (resolving eagerly if a resolver is\n  already present, for embedding hosts and tests)\n- mount() registers a dedicated one-shot provider:request hook\n  (priority 10, before the visibility hook''s 20) that resolves pending\n  sources at first request -- by which point the resolver exists --\n  and unregisters itself; registered unconditionally so the fix does\n  not depend on visibility being enabled\n- skills merge with the same first-match-wins in-place mutation pattern\n  as execute(source=...), so SkillsVisibilityHook and SkillsDiscovery\n  (which hold references to the same dict) see them immediately\n- failures are now LOUD: any dropped @-source is named in a\n  logger.warning instead of vanishing at debug level\n- a config listing ONLY @-sources no longer falls back to default skill\n  directories (the sources ARE configured; pre-fix that fallback only\n  happened because the entry was dropped)\n\nDocs updated: mount() docstring (stale \"local paths or git URLs\") and\nskills-instructions.md note that @-source skills register at first\nrequest.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb5abd27b5f9462477be7e2ad099cfc5757a80ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/fb5abd27b5f9462477be7e2ad099cfc5757a80ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961","verification":{"payload":"tree fb5abd27b5f9462477be7e2ad099cfc5757a80ef\nparent 6e1843fa59dae868eca19387c9865e07586f9627\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785715547 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785715547 -0700\n\nfix: resolve @namespace:path skill sources from config.skills (#52)\n\nThe docs (context/skills-instructions.md) promise that config.skills\naccepts a bundle reference like \"@mybundle:skills\", but the mount-time\nresolver (_resolve_skill_sources) only handled git+ URLs and literal\npaths: an @-entry fell into the local-path branch, failed Path.exists(),\nand was silently dropped at debug level. Bundles that register their own\nskills this way (e.g. design-council''s \"@design-council:skills\") never\nloaded them.\n\nA naive mount-time resolve cannot work: the mention_resolver capability\nis registered by the app layer AFTER session.initialize() (which is when\nmounts run) in both production session paths, so get_capability(\n\"mention_resolver\") during mount returns None in every path today.\n\nFix (deferred one-shot resolution, module-local):\n- _resolve_skill_sources partitions @-entries out of the path/git logic\n  and returns them as pending (resolving eagerly if a resolver is\n  already present, for embedding hosts and tests)\n- mount() registers a dedicated one-shot provider:request hook\n  (priority 10, before the visibility hook''s 20) that resolves pending\n  sources at first request -- by which point the resolver exists --\n  and unregisters itself; registered unconditionally so the fix does\n  not depend on visibility being enabled\n- skills merge with the same first-match-wins in-place mutation pattern\n  as execute(source=...), so SkillsVisibilityHook and SkillsDiscovery\n  (which hold references to the same dict) see them immediately\n- failures are now LOUD: any dropped @-source is named in a\n  logger.warning instead of vanishing at debug level\n- a config listing ONLY @-sources no longer falls back to default skill\n  directories (the sources ARE configured; pre-fix that fallback only\n  happened because the entry was dropped)\n\nDocs updated: mount() docstring (stale \"local paths or git URLs\") and\nskills-instructions.md note that @-source skills register at first\nrequest.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqb9tbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA930QAItKrPHjzV2JHx0lETaJGCda\nHa4f7VJ65/w5U0XkCqRIFPCO/76RHJZ6F5Lcqdnz7Y1bVO3MjCbR6qTzp36h9Bou\nr9hah8WH9rnwN4/YIB71wS4hj8lJA8lwPCJ3orYMRLr16Ku+J/f/shqiRPt40ApE\n6G1mSZczU+ZK8d7UH3nm3fIhllmFUquJw8PawAa9QlaffNBFIUXl60YFprrULzJ4\n7/GYcF14dvjUm2HEk9WMZ8U0dGbOMq8WDYW7MS3sQkjukJoxoRCZFLA7tICQeWz0\nclfH4VOkNobeGRi3uRcvQTOcMWlctsdCYVBiXuecX/3GxzWtr1UJ36J8E4LtWLXs\nCRGBkQTFuG73HfF4iBLT58XhtW1wfa4+Vp+M0MRH/BPj9j+yVGwS9pEYbY42ayUN\nQHhChQPOLoCczYxPL4uIvxaiUMophu2ScYifoDI+eumCCqDAZfx5neDvjJ/EZL1C\nprIOTkB3m5MgcuxNg0c3hz4OTrQUzZbg9zgDBc3V1orFZ52WqnCf0N5uUtARAzpp\naMJWHrguagSeV98ZUaHA4CPtEp62rz1a7caKtRJbI9o7TWRrVP0Kl4YXokKPks+f\ngmBJ5Xg8hvu4xElu0JhmC7JF54dEEgIp3SuPAqaZnSPuWaY9m0vMC3uLHNFs6ypE\nOZeLjUwbiT821pNyGqLv\n=OG2J\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-03T00:05:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDkzNWJjYTIzZWVjYjgzNzc2OTE5ZTlhZTkwOTljOGJmNjM3OTQ5NjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/6e1843fa59dae868eca19387c9865e07586f9627","sha":"6e1843fa59dae868eca19387c9865e07586f9627","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/6e1843fa59dae868eca19387c9865e07586f9627"}],"sha":"935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/935bca23eecb83776919e9ae9099c8bf63794961"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/6e1843fa59dae868eca19387c9865e07586f9627/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-31T14:09:10Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-31T14:09:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add graphify skill for building queryable knowledge graphs (#51)\n\nAdds the graphify skill — a user-invoked skill (/graphify) that transforms\nany folder of files (code, docs, papers, images, video) into a queryable\nknowledge graph with community detection and an honest audit trail\n(EXTRACTED / INFERRED / AMBIGUOUS confidence labels).\n\nOutputs:\n- Interactive HTML view for human exploration\n- GraphRAG-ready JSON for downstream indexing\n- GRAPH_REPORT.md audit trail\n\nKey design point: Explicitly scoped as a ONE-TIME orientation artifact for\nhuman consumption — NOT a retrieval or Q&A layer. The skill instructs the\nagent NOT to route ordinary codebase questions through the graph; grep/read\nare faster and more accurate for those. This guardrail is deliberate and\ndocumented in the skill description.\n\nImplementation:\n- Builds on public PyPI package ''graphifyy'' (verified)\n- Optionally uses GEMINI_API_KEY/GOOGLE_API_KEY for semantic extraction\n- Falls back to Amplifier delegate agents when provider keys unset\n- No other provider keys are read\n\nNo bundle.md registration changes required — skill description is 731 chars,\nwell under the 1024-char Agent Skills ceiling.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6de5763e4f68ff0d2d1f809fb62068d05a161d08","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/6de5763e4f68ff0d2d1f809fb62068d05a161d08"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/6e1843fa59dae868eca19387c9865e07586f9627","verification":{"payload":"tree 6de5763e4f68ff0d2d1f809fb62068d05a161d08\nparent f5ea2a05ccb265e24d4afc07c045df41aff117b6\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785506950 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785506950 -0700\n\nfeat: add graphify skill for building queryable knowledge graphs (#51)\n\nAdds the graphify skill — a user-invoked skill (/graphify) that transforms\nany folder of files (code, docs, papers, images, video) into a queryable\nknowledge graph with community detection and an honest audit trail\n(EXTRACTED / INFERRED / AMBIGUOUS confidence labels).\n\nOutputs:\n- Interactive HTML view for human exploration\n- GraphRAG-ready JSON for downstream indexing\n- GRAPH_REPORT.md audit trail\n\nKey design point: Explicitly scoped as a ONE-TIME orientation artifact for\nhuman consumption — NOT a retrieval or Q&A layer. The skill instructs the\nagent NOT to route ordinary codebase questions through the graph; grep/read\nare faster and more accurate for those. This guardrail is deliberate and\ndocumented in the skill description.\n\nImplementation:\n- Builds on public PyPI package ''graphifyy'' (verified)\n- Optionally uses GEMINI_API_KEY/GOOGLE_API_KEY for semantic extraction\n- Falls back to Amplifier delegate agents when provider keys unset\n- No other provider keys are read\n\nNo bundle.md registration changes required — skill description is 731 chars,\nwell under the 1024-char Agent Skills ceiling.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqbKyGCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAKrgQAFOZsGw+KrWaT7BrRWHfzGju\nvlfxheOELyI+Ukn8EmQYBUQlnA+tm3NJuVWw1os2GrEbOJGTd0LovAdpxEecSFQt\n3iqezxQoDGRxBHdhYi0q6vxRTNoazkecVa0RvSoqXEf6aFL1nQXMqpnlcb9tERO2\n+VoBSE9txc8/bOtljnswVocOcLrRNzE+oOhyQOhcZy9gi77TEmAm7G//1qVIFfpR\ntvTVkQSwZCtFEz3nN28wC978e4gQLGWo7wrT7baEY4RwXv6npLiH08mgAUhd61op\n8DFr6/84CsZ8kl/vH3LZGh9FRZUzsrSNhKSVezURlPStHRn77d2Uxzh84OKY2m2h\n+ofPrFlD16iAbIkjzHTvkjMrFyiPk1cJXiax4jAQ8JWHXJIn94Ouk/epv+LypIfb\nVBUct81E/6VNhFCPvEtFFQesfZEsqe8YAra7X7wZ2Fv8zZDtjxRrflaj3ZWHtXKW\nJE8ZJigBTKOZkiA20svIOkVBqjCFMielpud+pJkVYaWvWTUBIFNBYbvQDsH/ApJb\n+9+C54BGjr9P8i6afOx+zWeCQtSwg6d7rZjH4o2nxdE4glrubqJYzowmZh7rQlBm\ngR065im0Me7PSWM3z5JEocLCe