r-bundle-skills/commit/f5ea2a05ccb265e24d4afc07c045df41aff117b6","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGY1ZWEyYTA1Y2NiMjY1ZTI0ZDRhZmMwN2MwNDVkZjQxYWZmMTE3YjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7","sha":"7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7"}],"sha":"f5ea2a05ccb265e24d4afc07c045df41aff117b6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/f5ea2a05ccb265e24d4afc07c045df41aff117b6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T21:20:09Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T21:20:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat!: default visibility.placement to \"prefix\" (system-prompt skills index) (#49)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE (default only — no capability removed): the skills index\nnow defaults to the stable system-prompt prefix instead of per-request\ninjection. `visibility.placement: \"request\"` remains fully supported as\nan explicit opt-out and is byte-identical to the pre-flip behavior.\n\nWHY: measured 32-39% root-session cost reduction with identical quality\nand 100% skill recall in controlled ablation (parity-eval E2 arm (iii)\nrun 20260728T114548Z vs arm (i) run 20260728T050320Z; skill-recall probe\nrun 20260728T203351Z: request 6/6 recalled+correct, prefix 5/5, with\nper-trial wire-level delivery verification and non-guessable planted-\ntoken grading). Per-request injection re-sends the full index (~3.5k\ntokens) as fresh input on every provider call; prefix placement bills it\nonce into the provider''s cached system block and cache-reads it after.\n\nAlso in this change:\n- No-factory fallback softened ERROR -> WARNING (once per instance):\n  prefix is the default path now, so sessions that legitimately lack a\n  system-prompt factory (static prompts, minimal embedded coordinators)\n  are not user misconfiguration. Fallback behavior itself unchanged —\n  request-mode injection, skills stay visible, misplacement detectable.\n  Static-prompt refusal behavior unchanged.\n- Defensive coordinator lookup: a coordinator without .get() is treated\n  as \"no surface\" (fallback) instead of raising from the hook.\n\nTests: default-behavior tests now assert prefix placement (factory-\nequipped context); explicit request-mode opt-out covered incl. factory-\nuntouched assertion; fallback test asserts exactly ONE WARNING and zero\nERRORs across repeated requests. Suite: 4 failed, 265 passed — the 4 are\npre-existing on origin/main (test_discovery symlink x2,\ntest_enhanced_discovery resolver, test_real_session). README documents\nthe new default, the opt-out, and the measured rationale.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"0bc7b723efedf84714f7082c15fb8459b86e8ba2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/0bc7b723efedf84714f7082c15fb8459b86e8ba2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7","verification":{"payload":"tree 0bc7b723efedf84714f7082c15fb8459b86e8ba2\nparent 05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785273609 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785273609 -0700\n\nfeat!: default visibility.placement to \"prefix\" (system-prompt skills index) (#49)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE (default only — no capability removed): the skills index\nnow defaults to the stable system-prompt prefix instead of per-request\ninjection. `visibility.placement: \"request\"` remains fully supported as\nan explicit opt-out and is byte-identical to the pre-flip behavior.\n\nWHY: measured 32-39% root-session cost reduction with identical quality\nand 100% skill recall in controlled ablation (parity-eval E2 arm (iii)\nrun 20260728T114548Z vs arm (i) run 20260728T050320Z; skill-recall probe\nrun 20260728T203351Z: request 6/6 recalled+correct, prefix 5/5, with\nper-trial wire-level delivery verification and non-guessable planted-\ntoken grading). Per-request injection re-sends the full index (~3.5k\ntokens) as fresh input on every provider call; prefix placement bills it\nonce into the provider''s cached system block and cache-reads it after.\n\nAlso in this change:\n- No-factory fallback softened ERROR -> WARNING (once per instance):\n  prefix is the default path now, so sessions that legitimately lack a\n  system-prompt factory (static prompts, minimal embedded coordinators)\n  are not user misconfiguration. Fallback behavior itself unchanged —\n  request-mode injection, skills stay visible, misplacement detectable.\n  Static-prompt refusal behavior unchanged.\n- Defensive coordinator lookup: a coordinator without .get() is treated\n  as \"no surface\" (fallback) instead of raising from the hook.\n\nTests: default-behavior tests now assert prefix placement (factory-\nequipped context); explicit request-mode opt-out covered incl. factory-\nuntouched assertion; fallback test asserts exactly ONE WARNING and zero\nERRORs across repeated requests. Suite: 4 failed, 265 passed — the 4 are\npre-existing on origin/main (test_discovery symlink x2,\ntest_enhanced_discovery resolver, test_real_session). README documents\nthe new default, the opt-out, and the measured rationale.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaR0JCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAwpIQAAe2ZVkM5GJYEW1Df1oJYWQq\nPgFoV3/i5EzRp3y9pKirrsZKLjr/ExuqBrDfJ5+pQBd5UzXZ2HuoavDGH/ZO6mE0\nnMaZa6RaarAIoq5ffXMFa7No0GMGA9eN6rF3qGmjCp0o9RIvmlvUpZrx327WuAF+\nk/nIfYpzM5s0W17D6JpoVV25KVFxuGmn44+epm50mb8KWjRRVF6goebKJaVFc5HM\nD4b8nOjKo1hLwCNeVvYEgkXYqQJs1W4tXW0+OxPf5BymZHhtN8wQ/TMfG1NqXwOF\nR5K5mQlksgWX7SyfoCglSx3IaR2Rkl16ZmleCkzAkIkOQEbuWXqGJINBafHQDhO8\njaIvm84bMF++DHGsIUVI3iJzg2oCasdpRmmKtfzD53RveDTa/nJIWioqvR+9xlLI\n+Xi7NnCOtDGl1WnBbZge/Y9cGhgFWya44ToD2yjuwETid9SBkFtf3cgvD07+1i2l\nuDeesiLcNxVYZTzXVqqA6UEa+2SMOuRGfmDG5ncu4UzORKwmNMCFv0wzfJa69tJ8\nlxla9UvxYOi5P+LnBRo43tkA42UxhW2lRJRFVeS1M+m351lKJPyb2W6qtxeBQA47\nSoeDLtdichBLXFnky0dZbBg+1k9OJcPfcd7rSEzdIpk5DpbsNp6+0ALkKlPj+7MH\nSf2iZkpox+8/RxopAmte\n=uSTj\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-28T21:20:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDc3NDY2ODJkOWIzMjY0ZDFkM2I3ZDU2NjAwOTM1MzVlYTA2ZWRkZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20","sha":"05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20"}],"sha":"7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/7746682d9b3264d1d3b7d5660093535ea06eddd7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T19:48:09Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T19:48:09Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: visibility.placement — skills index in the stable system-prompt prefix (#48)\n\nNew config visibility.placement: \"request\" | \"prefix\" (default \"request\" —\ntoday''s behavior byte-identical; prefix is opt-in; unknown value fails\nloudly at construction).\n\nWHY: the per-request injection re-sends the full skills index (~3.5k\ntokens) as fresh input on EVERY provider request. Providers hoist\nrole=system content into their cached prefix (anthropic: single system\ncontent block carrying the first cache breakpoint), so system-prompt\nplacement bills the index once and cache-reads it afterwards.\n\nMECHANISM (discovered, not assumed): inject_context on provider:request\nCANNOT express prefix placement — the hook registry merges all same-event\ninjections into ONE result with the FIRST hook''s role/ephemeral\n(amplifier-core hooks.rs merge_inject_context_results), so a system-role\ninjection would either hijack other hooks'' mutable content into the\ncached prefix or be flattened to the merged role. The surface that CAN:\nthe context module''s system-prompt factory (registered by\namplifier-foundation _prepared.py via context.set_system_prompt_factory;\ncontext-simple invokes it on EVERY get_messages_for_request). In prefix\nmode the hook lazily (first provider:request — guaranteed after session\nprepare) wraps the registered factory: output = base + skills block.\n\nStaleness: the wrapper renders from the CURRENT effective skill catalog\neach call, cached by a cheap catalog hash — re-render only on change, so\nmid-session skill changes (mode overlays) refresh the prefix with exactly\none current copy (one cache bust per change; never a stale copy). Re-wrap\ndetection: if a new base factory is registered after ours, the next\nrequest wraps it (identity check).\n\nFallbacks are loud: no context module / no factory surface → ERROR log +\nrequest-mode injection (agent keeps skill visibility; the misplacement is\ndetectable). A session with a static system prompt (no factory) is left\nuntouched — wrapping would REPLACE the static prompt in context-simple''s\nfactory mode.\n\nTests (tests/test_prefix_placement.py, 11): default-mode byte-identical\nregression, explicit-request identical, invalid-value rejection, prefix\nplacement in factory output, stable-across-requests (cached render\nobject), refresh-on-catalog-change (add + remove, exactly one copy),\nre-wrap after factory re-registration, fork-context filtering in prefix\nmode, loud fallback without surface, static-prompt refusal, enabled=false\nprecedence.\n\nSuite: 4 failed, 261 passed — the 4 failures are PRE-EXISTING on the base\ncommit (verified: clean base = 4 failed, 250 passed; same four:\ntest_discovery symlink x2, test_enhanced_discovery model resolver,\ntest_real_session). Zero regressions. ruff + pyright clean. README\ndocuments the new key.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"f309ce09948393a5529eea900a2bb4ede58cd01a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/f309ce09948393a5529eea900a2bb4ede58cd01a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20","verification":{"payload":"tree f309ce09948393a5529eea900a2bb4ede58cd01a\nparent b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785268089 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785268089 -0700\n\nfeat: visibility.placement — skills index in the stable system-prompt prefix (#48)\n\nNew config visibility.placement: \"request\" | \"prefix\" (default \"request\" —\ntoday''s behavior byte-identical; prefix is opt-in; unknown value fails\nloudly at construction).\n\nWHY: the per-request injection re-sends the full skills index (~3.5k\ntokens) as fresh input on EVERY provider request. Providers hoist\nrole=system content into their cached prefix (anthropic: single system\ncontent block carrying the first cache breakpoint), so system-prompt\nplacement bills the index once and cache-reads it afterwards.\n\nMECHANISM (discovered, not assumed): inject_context on provider:request\nCANNOT express prefix placement — the hook registry merges all same-event\ninjections into ONE result with the FIRST hook''s role/ephemeral\n(amplifier-core hooks.rs merge_inject_context_results), so a system-role\ninjection would either hijack other hooks'' mutable content into the\ncached prefix or be flattened to the merged role. The surface that CAN:\nthe context module''s system-prompt factory (registered by\namplifier-foundation _prepared.py via context.set_system_prompt_factory;\ncontext-simple invokes it on EVERY get_messages_for_request). In prefix\nmode the hook lazily (first provider:request — guaranteed after session\nprepare) wraps the registered factory: output = base + skills block.\n\nStaleness: the wrapper renders from the CURRENT effective skill catalog\neach call, cached by a cheap catalog hash — re-render only on change, so\nmid-session skill changes (mode overlays) refresh the prefix with exactly\none current copy (one cache bust per change; never a stale copy). Re-wrap\ndetection: if a new base factory is registered after ours, the next\nrequest wraps it (identity check).\n\nFallbacks are loud: no context module / no factory surface → ERROR log +\nrequest-mode injection (agent keeps skill visibility; the misplacement is\ndetectable). A session with a static system prompt (no factory) is left\nuntouched — wrapping would REPLACE the static prompt in context-simple''s\nfactory mode.\n\nTests (tests/test_prefix_placement.py, 11): default-mode byte-identical\nregression, explicit-request identical, invalid-value rejection, prefix\nplacement in factory output, stable-across-requests (cached render\nobject), refresh-on-catalog-change (add + remove, exactly one copy),\nre-wrap after factory re-registration, fork-context filtering in prefix\nmode, loud fallback without surface, static-prompt refusal, enabled=false\nprecedence.\n\nSuite: 4 failed, 261 passed — the 4 failures are PRE-EXISTING on the base\ncommit (verified: clean base = 4 failed, 250 passed; same four:\ntest_discovery symlink x2, test_enhanced_discovery model resolver,\ntest_real_session). Zero regressions. ruff + pyright clean. README\ndocuments the new key.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaQd5CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAu+wQAGpdkNc8lGkf/4FtHBTDFNdk\n5L1uEulRKsqE5juRa4vDahzonbYbi++zjdDi8RM0Xa2vrSoLKwHPh6VJ5peLuExu\nqOeD0AAOWr3c4rfS0L4wX/KBjZjh73TsgOg7voZIyEerNBguuBGcuvdIjfXYQD3c\n/30NpUK+OjadH/+1Dt1XcixSPuyDeHlbMIzo9Bv3VGBkRBhG4C0HLdgFR2X4npcs\nnQfceefRMCtf7Vsukl6YUjXLT0qP8wDtKTgn6ACsFRswQgO+OSZ9owebMPC1T1qo\nbwv6UmgvEYCFmfa4Pr/wY8GTdx1EjWN1twNa35pEkqe22UicqIR7+B3JWQgZnQPY\n8tQIWBzP6YQth8r/efPcJNMCrl2tlSa3cyPa8q7sVUEQaqpPKRhoCv1/tJpkMsjA\nZRstw+QuCKc2kAdhAiJuRnbmfe297LH2CbCjZxiJu1uO2h5obpDd/c+Cnm8Q0Mwv\nxza4K/dLozMz6X5yCtIf/JXXHqSkifCC2+3sZMPcSfWx9HKdOfPpchBSNZNxo4OU\nkZdOd/O704orO+HJTTs8wj74R1JPV9K1F/A1GuAmjDr8c4mr/TMMmA0Hthr/I1ik\nnViEuG/+eAkpQJZka0C7feEXfTaGC1CRncnLmnXuvic+sCbX4XrijcuZa1LzjfJh\naV7Brk5v6Fo/HNlvRJYs\n=f63f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-28T19:48:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDA1MjkzNDY2ZjJkOWY0NDU2OGEzZmU0NDdiYTYzZTdhMDhhYTZmMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb","sha":"b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb"}],"sha":"05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/05293466f2d9f44568a3fe447ba63e7a08aa6f20"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:56:42Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T18:56:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: add sequential execution guard to monitor skill (#47)\n\nAdd explicit documentation and detection guidance for a critical bug found\nduring cost/performance evaluation: delegated monitoring loops can issue all\nN checks as parallel tool_use blocks in a single turn, defeating the entire\npurpose of a monitor.\n\nThe fix includes:\n- SEQUENTIAL ONLY requirement with verbatim text for every delegated instruction\n- Explanation of why condition-driven loops are self-protecting vs count-driven\n- Cost/duration sanity check for detecting when parallel batching occurred\n\nMeasured evidence:\n- A child asked for 15 checks emitted 15 simultaneous tool_use blocks in one\n  assistant turn. All 15 date calls returned identical timestamps. It reported\n  success but had monitored nothing.\n- A genuine 13-check monitor: 14 LLM calls, 100s wall time, $0.162 total\n- The parallel 15-check imposter: 2 LLM calls, 18s wall time, $0.026 total\n  (cheaper and faster — the tell that batching occurred)\n\nCloses: Reference PR #46\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"945a102846c40f7cc9adbc2f3a31b7f5d68bbcc8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/945a102846c40f7cc9adbc2f3a31b7f5d68bbcc8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb","verification":{"payload":"tree 945a102846c40f7cc9adbc2f3a31b7f5d68bbcc8\nparent 33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785265002 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785265002 -0700\n\nfix: add sequential execution guard to monitor skill (#47)\n\nAdd explicit documentation and detection guidance for a critical bug found\nduring cost/performance evaluation: delegated monitoring loops can issue all\nN checks as parallel tool_use blocks in a single turn, defeating the entire\npurpose of a monitor.\n\nThe fix includes:\n- SEQUENTIAL ONLY requirement with verbatim text for every delegated instruction\n- Explanation of why condition-driven loops are self-protecting vs count-driven\n- Cost/duration sanity check for detecting when parallel batching occurred\n\nMeasured evidence:\n- A child asked for 15 checks emitted 15 simultaneous tool_use blocks in one\n  assistant turn. All 15 date calls returned identical timestamps. It reported\n  success but had monitored nothing.\n- A genuine 13-check monitor: 14 LLM calls, 100s wall time, $0.162 total\n- The parallel 15-check imposter: 2 LLM calls, 18s wall time, $0.026 total\n  (cheaper and faster — the tell that batching occurred)\n\nCloses: Reference PR #46\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABC