tps://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b","sha":"33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b"}],"sha":"b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b334c9d593e709584c39a14deb2c279747819ddb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3732858?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/danshapiro","id":3732858,"login":"danshapiro","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MzI4NTg=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/danshapiro","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T16:01:37Z","email":"3732858+danshapiro@users.noreply.github.com","name":"danshapiro"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T16:01:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: don''t warn about directory-name mismatch for SKILL.md at the source root (#45)\n\nWhen a skill source has SKILL.md at its root (e.g. a git repo whose root IS\nthe skill), the containing directory name is harness/user-controlled — such\nas hash-suffixed git cache clone directories — never author-controlled. The\nAgent-Skills-spec directory-name check can therefore never be satisfied by\nthe skill author, making the warning an unfixable false positive.\n\nSkip the directory-name check in discovery when SKILL.md sits at the source\nroot itself. Nested skills keep the check unchanged.\n\nAdds 3 tests to tests/test_discovery.py: source-root skip, local-root skip,\nand nested-mismatch-still-warns. Verified: pytest tests/test_discovery.py\n→ 14 passed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"8e776195f828465e5ef80475ad630ec04c385b7d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/8e776195f828465e5ef80475ad630ec04c385b7d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8e776195f828465e5ef80475ad630ec04c385b7d\nparent e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c\nauthor danshapiro <3732858+danshapiro@users.noreply.github.com> 1785254497 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785254497 -0700\n\nfix: don''t warn about directory-name mismatch for SKILL.md at the source root (#45)\n\nWhen a skill source has SKILL.md at its root (e.g. a git repo whose root IS\nthe skill), the containing directory name is harness/user-controlled — such\nas hash-suffixed git cache clone directories — never author-controlled. The\nAgent-Skills-spec directory-name check can therefore never be satisfied by\nthe skill author, making the warning an unfixable false positive.\n\nSkip the directory-name check in discovery when SKILL.md sits at the source\nroot itself. Nested skills keep the check unchanged.\n\nAdds 3 tests to tests/test_discovery.py: source-root skip, local-root skip,\nand nested-mismatch-still-warns. Verified: pytest tests/test_discovery.py\n→ 14 passed.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaNJhCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANmMQAAN/9riy167qil4GUMLQ+17X\n79d6AqE51AhOi2alN4pC5maETO21EBHvFuOyN1gMxIjIDstlPfrW9b3+s9KsfXMG\nVDURV6TD39phq1s3IlstssyCaPmbmwsIhfGGKEQDh7ajr+z/ANk0+B0xWmu+eFem\n0v9ECOfl47gUhHRYdHWs+ZABBz+iYzviqpF+5YuTW0b8kC12R8+oYuYI+OYaFQvs\ngTbGoxkTnYiNfIHH4twmd+bi7RRbTlBr6QGKOptBsAG7crcoYFyLKs1gc5+KVbU0\neeNDG2aoy1qXryK1Jd/zCq0CpFyPpW0WCg7XfwiMWhqgxQQJ7b2E1xfxsSvZ/Afm\nS8p0c3qeP7kw8k/YyI0jN3GMVZIoeiv1ZSL11vtHEVU4R+Dh9ZzA6nkFBUHljYq6\nbqr7sSB9KAkzxBX2wtbywyapoDm+U+IdjPTrAAQgTlMKSYhwGRTlfY5t8WYqwtsg\nZAYXe1AEyLXzKYnKST8eiEuwyyxPdfGbsoqoL8X7MrdKCndUSSFvh1wQdMI18k0H\n9XCbQbv0wZZskdHVe7YFD9kbWGiqb6tVJjhOZnRCijtHrAQvItFFdsF6VDmf2XQu\nJtta7TrvVXjiK2gMytDe1BDJ9nVyHvFnUWuxySiepUGLhyeR1rBXSEz51U1aEpFP\naFsJgb+E57ZCUQAEaWnx\n=zo4Y\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-28T16:01:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDMzYzZlYTJjMTg2NWIzMTU5ZDdhMDczYTI4ZDA4MGQxNTU4MDBkOGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c","sha":"e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c"}],"sha":"33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/33c6ea2c1865b3159d7a073a28d080d155800d8b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-28T10:22:44Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-28T10:22:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add monitor skill for bounded polling loops (#46)\n\nAdd the monitor skill, a bounded sleep→check→decide polling loop that holds\nthe current turn open until the watched thing is DONE, FAILED, or NEEDS YOU.\nThis enables the end-of-turn notification to fire honestly instead of having\nthe agent promise follow-up it has no mechanism to deliver.\n\nThe skill runs inline by default (using existing tools), and decides inline-vs-delegated\nper invocation to balance context cost (each poll re-sends the entire session\nto the model) against progress visibility and steering.\n\nRegistered as `/monitor` slash command, also available for model self-invocation\nwhen about to make a promise to check something.\n\nEvidence from live runs:\n- Inline loop: held discipline across 5 iterations on a real 110-source pipeline\n- Delegated loop: verified 3 notyet checks then FOUND, on claude-haiku-4-5\n- Dispatch latency: ~40s from delegate() to first check, measured twice\n- Turn-completion notification: confirmed arriving at correct moment\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"c57c5c471770b42f7ad440274cbc5a864a29dc55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/c57c5c471770b42f7ad440274cbc5a864a29dc55"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c","verification":{"payload":"tree c57c5c471770b42f7ad440274cbc5a864a29dc55\nparent 50b8863746742cc68ba5e52190557529734baaba\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1785234164 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1785234164 -0700\n\nfeat: add monitor skill for bounded polling loops (#46)\n\nAdd the monitor skill, a bounded sleep→check→decide polling loop that holds\nthe current turn open until the watched thing is DONE, FAILED, or NEEDS YOU.\nThis enables the end-of-turn notification to fire honestly instead of having\nthe agent promise follow-up it has no mechanism to deliver.\n\nThe skill runs inline by default (using existing tools), and decides inline-vs-delegated\nper invocation to balance context cost (each poll re-sends the entire session\nto the model) against progress visibility and steering.\n\nRegistered as `/monitor` slash command, also available for model self-invocation\nwhen about to make a promise to check something.\n\nEvidence from live runs:\n- Inline loop: held discipline across 5 iterations on a real 110-source pipeline\n- Delegated loop: verified 3 notyet checks then FOUND, on claude-haiku-4-5\n- Dispatch latency: ~40s from delegate() to first check, measured twice\n- Turn-completion notification: confirmed arriving at correct moment\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqaIL0CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAvMAQAHo9N7T1n0uv3rwGbMRwu6ce\nWjpQFVqXBNtxOBpdDFeEwhAcOW4tbL8r+zdcl9SLnCbtoB9fgGiEnKwu3HGUlMuT\nnVl5dyE/qDvGDk5icnfrfRDlEwZHwfm3E1kGoeQjQwBjSAkmkxBMfL6Leu0omnju\n9gBmPiJyG3dM/K8TtqxyJ1h/XbnnIor1PayzrphHWQ0rkKo9PANOzIDeLRxpywKI\n33k/dPI0qQz+315REbTsQ3sOrUtntDSbvK7CoPFN78sMB2XVEWBhGj92mbc4TiN/\nz2jBKktWVXlH3CfNOieFpLm2M5B/w8+jK2yemoDwF9mI1UpTwKtm+BqHO92vM8Jq\nZNrp4987qrfTGq8TX7MK0TDp3E1Oiv+kRTc1mQjLW/TYEC0CqYB5LsGs/FMQEvKL\n5ARCi/NGA60ZiWOiqfzFk9tJVU6bnNg6wlu3aQMF2KnTUsVvbyCA1iAjbuBP9Tfj\n0B0V//3z/lOzyStkVkIHbOObdaIG9ihd9XCmMKJuTEXlRDtmJZK5Xo9v0iCkBifS\n/WIGADGovV+k5TgpG3z1NPy1BABKCEmNb7+unP42QXdKwZhgzfLzgl1H/1RLiM/K\nYKJPny8EHMFmasfJN2ILrAJxmlujM/uXw6qjC3Zw54osVsrKYDgRj4P8bsAyPyPf\n5QtBLwCCmbl7l2vDyJ1D\n=xLnt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-28T10:22:44Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGU1YTgzN2U3MWQyODRjYTU1NzNmM2M4MzMwOGFjMTU2NDQ3YzUyMWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/50b8863746742cc68ba5e52190557529734baaba","sha":"50b8863746742cc68ba5e52190557529734baaba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/50b8863746742cc68ba5e52190557529734baaba"}],"sha":"e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/e5a837e71d284ca5573f3c83308ac156447c521c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/50b8863746742cc68ba5e52190557529734baaba/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-14T00:04:46Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-14T00:04:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Councilify meta-skill + verdict decision rule, description-length check (#44)\n\n* feat: add councilify meta-skill for building complete new council review panels\n\nAdds councilify, a new meta-skill sibling to personafy/skillify that automates\nthe construction of orthogonal review panels (councils) for any domain. Following\nthe proven /council → /design-council pattern, councilify:\n\n- Reuses existing orthogonal lenses where an axis is already owned\n- Builds only genuinely-missing lenses via personafy''s methodology\n- Assembles them into an invocable fork-orchestrator + inline-here pair\n\nIncludes ready-to-fill templates for:\n- council-orchestrator.SKILL.md.tmpl (fork runner with parallel fan-out)\n- council-here-orchestrator.SKILL.md.tmpl (inline counterpart for live conversation)\n- council-native-lens.SKILL.md.tmpl (new lens implementation template)\n- bundle.md.tmpl (council bundle entry point)\n- behavior.yaml.tmpl (reusable behavior composition)\n- awareness.md.tmpl (thin discovery pointer for root sessions)\n\nNo scope bleed: each new lens owns exactly one decision axis; duplicative or\noverlapping lenses are refused in favor of complementary expertise that makes\nindependent judgments.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: add bench-size guidance to councilify skill Step 3\n\nAdds grounded minimum/maximum lens-count guidance (hard floor ~4, typical 5-7,\nsoft ceiling ~8) to the councilify skill, derived from confirmed real bench sizes\nacross this ecosystem: council (6), adversarial-review (6), design-council (7),\nand product-council (7→8). Frames as a strong default and judgment aid for\nStep 3 of the councilify workflow, not a hard gate.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* refactor: reorder councilify derivation and document inventory-bias guard\n\nSteps 2 and 3 reordered: domain''s ideal roster is now derived BLIND to the\nexisting skill inventory first (Step 2, ''Derive the domain''s ideal roster —\nblind to the existing inventory first''), with reconciliation against what\nalready exists happening only afterward (Step 3, ''Reconcile against the\ninstalled inventory''). This guards against the installed inventory biasing\nwhat ''ideal'' looks like.\n\nAdded honest, directly-verified limitation: a delegate-spawned sub-session,\neven with context_depth=''none'', was confirmed by direct test to still receive\nan unconditional hooks-skills-visibility system-reminder listing the full\nskill inventory. True technical isolation from the inventory is NOT achievable\nvia delegate alone on this platform. The ''derive blind'' instruction is now\nexplicitly documented as a policy constraint the model is asked to honor, not\nan architectural guarantee, with verified evidence cited inline.\n\nAdded explicit guidance against fixing a target lens-count in advance of\nderivation — the count is an output of the roster-derivation steps, not an\ninput to them.\n\nThis reorder was itself informed by running the proposal through /council\nand /product-council for review before implementing — both independently\nflagged that a literal ''internal multi-proposal-and-debate'' mechanism\n(informally ''council-council'') was NOT worth building as specified (no\nbounded N, no stopping criterion, no dissent-recording protocol comparable\nto /council''s own), so that part was deliberately NOT implemented.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: add verdict decision rule to intent-keeper, description-length check to personafy\n\nEnhances two core council reviewer skills with specific, empirically-tested rules:\n\nintent-keeper: Add ''Verdict Decision Rule'' section that closes verdict instability\n(the same finding was being scored PASS vs CONCERN on repeated identical runs).\nThe rule ties the verdict to whether the target TEXT ITSELF acknowledges limitations\n(PASS), or whether YOU as the reviewer surfaced them (CONCERN/default). Verified via\ntrue-OS-process-isolation replication testing (3+ replicates). The rule eliminates\nthe ambiguity between ''the team has resolved this'' vs ''a threshold exists but doesn''t\nacknowledge the gap'' — establishing PASS only on team''s own explicit acknowledgment.\n\npersonafy: Add explicit sub-check to Step 7 (''Reduce & refine'') that validates the\nfrontmatter ''description:'' field length against Agent Skills 1024-char guidance.\nVerifies that an over-long description (like bet-sizer''s measured 1043 chars) is\ncaught at creation time. Documents that this is a soft token-cost warning (not\nblocking), provides concrete measurement command, names the highest-value compression\ntarget (the negation-identity clause), and targets 700-800 chars — matching compliant\nsibling skills. This fixes a real, permanently-recurring cost since skill descriptions\nare injected into every turn''s visibility context.\n\nBoth fixes were validated during an extensive evaluation project (multiple rounds of\nsizing sweeps, roster candidates, debate-loop testing, replication testing) that built\nand tested a ''Product Development Council'' — a 6-8 lens panel for product plans —\nas the proving ground for the councilify meta-skill.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"98bc329a006fdc3010a0097d3447fadb894a2a3e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/98bc329a006fdc3010a0097d3447fadb894a2a3e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/50b8863746742cc68ba5e52190557529734baaba","verification":{"payload":"tree 98bc329a006fdc3010a0097d3447fadb894a2a3e\nparent 9c1f14c9f2622b2bf192d7d4d09f39f142555f5b\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1783987486 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783987486 -0700\n\nCouncilify meta-skill + verdict decision rule, description-length check (#44)\n\n* feat: add councilify meta-skill for building complete new council review panels\n\nAdds councilify, a new meta-skill sibling to personafy/skillify that automates\nthe construction of orthogonal review panels (councils) for any domain. Following\nthe proven /council → /design-council pattern, councilify:\n\n- Reuses existing orthogonal lenses where an axis is already owned\n- Builds only genuinely-missing lenses via personafy''s methodology\n- Assembles them into an invocable fork-orchestrator + inline-here pair\n\nIncludes ready-to-fill templates for:\n- council-orchestrator.SKILL.md.tmpl (fork runner with parallel fan-out)\n- council-here-orchestrator.SKILL.md.tmpl (inline counterpart for live conversation)\n- council-native-lens.SKILL.md.tmpl (new lens implementation template)\n- bundle.md.tmpl (council bundle entry point)\n- behavior.yaml.tmpl (reusable behavior composition)\n- awareness.md.tmpl (thin discovery pointer for root sessions)\n\nNo scope bleed: each new lens owns exactly one decision axis; duplicative or\noverlapping lenses are refused in favor of complementary expertise that makes\nindependent judgments.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* docs: add bench-size guidance to councilify skill Step 3\n\nAdds grounded minimum/maximum lens-count guidance (hard floor ~4, typical 5-7,\nsoft ceiling ~8) to the councilify skill, derived from confirmed real bench sizes\nacross this ecosystem: council (6), adversarial-review (6), design-council (7),\nand product-council (7→8). Frames as a strong default and judgment aid for\nStep 3 of the councilify workflow, not a hard gate.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* refactor: reorder councilify derivation and document inventory-bias guard\n\nSteps 2 and 3 reordered: domain''s ideal roster is now derived BLIND to the\nexisting skill inventory first (Step 2, ''Derive the domain''s ideal roster —\nblind to the existing inventory first''), with reconciliation against what\nalready exists happening only afterward (Step 3, ''Reconcile against the\ninstalled inventory''). This guards against the installed inventory biasing\nwhat ''ideal'' looks like.\n\nAdded honest, directly-verified limitation: a delegate-spawned sub-session,\neven with context_depth=''none'', was confirmed by direct test to still receive\nan unconditional hooks-skills-visibility system-reminder listing the full\nskill inventory. True technical isolation from the inventory is NOT achievable\nvia delegate alone on this platform. The ''derive blind'' instruction is now\nexplicitly documented as a policy constraint the model is asked to honor, not\nan architectural guarantee, with verified evidence cited inline.\n\nAdded explicit guidance against fixing a target lens-count in advance of\nderivation — the count is an output of the roster-derivation steps, not an\ninput to them.\n\nThis reorder was itself informed by running the proposal through /council\nand /product-council for review before implementing — both independently\nflagged that a literal ''internal multi-proposal-and-debate'' mechanism\n(informally ''council-council'') was NOT worth building as specified (no\nbounded N, no stopping criterion, no dissent-recording protocol comparable\nto /council''s own), so that part was deliberately NOT implemented.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* fix: add verdict decision rule to intent-keeper, description-length check to personafy\n\nEnhances two core council reviewer skills with specific, empirically-tested rules:\n\nintent-keeper: Add ''Verdict Decision Rule'' section that closes verdict instability\n(the same finding was being scored PASS vs CONCERN on repeated identical runs).\nThe rule ties the verdict to whether the target TEXT ITSELF acknowledges limitations\n(PASS), or whether YOU as the reviewer surfaced them (CONCERN/default). Verified via\ntrue-OS-process-isolation replication testing (3+ replicates). The rule eliminates\nthe ambiguity between ''the team has resolved this'' vs ''a threshold exists but doesn''t\nacknowledge the gap'' — establishing PASS only on team''s own explicit acknowledgment.\n\npersonafy: Add explicit sub-check to Step 7 (''Reduce & refine'') that validates the\nfrontmatter ''description:'' field length against Agent Skills 1024-char guidance.\nVerifies that an over-long description (like bet-sizer''s measured 1043 chars) is\ncaught at creation time. Documents that this is a soft token-cost warning (not\nblocking), provides concrete measurement command, names the highest-value compression\ntarget (the negation-identity clause), and targets 700-800 chars — matching compliant\nsibling skills. This fixes a real, permanently-recurring cost since skill descriptions\nare injected into every turn''s visibility context.\n\nBoth fixes were validated during an extensive evaluation project (multiple rounds of\nsizing sweeps, roster candidates, debate-loop testing, replication testing) that built\nand tested a ''Product Development Council'' — a 6-8 lens panel for product plans —\nas the proving ground for the councilify meta-skill.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqVX0eCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAl/IQAIxySiCzjWhocQkMPeEaZRbv\n96UBi2SvxgLSkkYdxwoP3zgLGOuQApABddLKeIcHNZ0he1BH0lk697VFm81W2blD\nmx9FSNBMQQ4T9lJMIxdUXnNtPVrxVkKb0YUH+x6DvK6XtU0PZSXpSe9wZxbV235P\neBreJYrc1EuOZTSZQCJ2Fm+YXSw9QgzZ7C2alBIsUE1EpUYfAMGJMBxc/ZsI4+d9\nqdKqKyl2uJNZ4NmxMGbwBgWr/ij0YURR58RU2zXk9NAG59/nyjHkg/1GgI+fZpKj\nhbYKITQPsoU+LRMcJSdv5z60+X54z5Dscb6Oz57IOLbp2IsYpMNq8cBIhG76SgeW\nHx5XXWsgXQizYsp216m3kP39dCsvVTjXuVY7DTW2eeoL2rw0DhEXNNXtM9hhs/k8\nJS9zHpBSNkrJ5aZ8R8rsams+lvkA64J29eWQ5PMwB7DS0JbH/jAQhszXo7Vb082S\nSYwZ1OIHUlqZkBODfoM9zucfFwAgrwxuGzo8Dy4OVPGzYOzWg/kZ4AeH3keNAXsO\nxNrMOTsfF0cgei6ThZNy427ZF2JGB8LdE14vBAICdKfjjB/fGcleyc8a4kuPzd1f\n9Vf5wJXNCZ4Hv0E/srOOikrK6Q+vjsO25ik3E2HCJasJ3nEF6pdpspyYuCuv2xFj\neodP+foegX+W6NEY9vzk\n=gbZ9\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-07-14T00:04:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followe