com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/276d336f72dba3da11088391e19910bfd62c0893/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-09T08:31:42Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-09T08:31:42Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: extend amplifier-tool-leverage-patterns with attractor-only specialization (#41)\n\nDocuments the target shape for Amplifier bundles where an attractor .dot\npipeline is the SOLE home of logic by construction, with five thin consumption\nsurfaces backed by that one file:\n  - Standalone .dot runnable in any attractor engine, zero Amplifier coupling\n  - Dot-graph resolver sidecar in Amplifier Resolve (DTU/Team Pulse hosted use)\n  - Lite engine-wrapper lib usable by any Python project, zero Amplifier dependency\n  - Amplifier tool module (thin mount() wrapper)\n  - Click-based CLI (thin wrapper)\n\nExplicitly names the anti-pattern to avoid (.dot files requiring compile-time\ntemplating before an engine can run them) and flags this as target/aspirational\nshape, not yet proven end-to-end anywhere. Cites microsoft/amplifier-app-wiki-weaver\nas the closest real-world reference, but clearly notes it has not reached this\ntarget yet (tokenized .dot files, missing resolver sidecars, engine wrapper still\ncoupled to Amplifier''s PreparedBundle machinery, argparse not Click).\n\nInstructs future readers not to copy wiki-weaver''s current coupling forward as\nif it were the pattern.\n\n🤖 Generated with Amplifier\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"42263c1014c8936da441e30a3ca148fff025bf3b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/42263c1014c8936da441e30a3ca148fff025bf3b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/276d336f72dba3da11088391e19910bfd62c0893","verification":{"payload":"tree 42263c1014c8936da441e30a3ca148fff025bf3b\nparent 6176ab8b32e660c8ac8b6f3cec1512cde99de63f\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1783585902 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1783585902 -0700\n\ndocs: extend amplifier-tool-leverage-patterns with attractor-only specialization (#41)\n\nDocuments the target shape for Amplifier bundles where an attractor .dot\npipeline is the SOLE home of logic by construction, with five thin consumption\nsurfaces backed by that one file:\n  - Standalone .dot runnable in any attractor engine, zero Amplifier coupling\n  - Dot-graph resolver sidecar in Amplifier Resolve (DTU/Team Pulse hosted use)\n  - Lite engine-wrapper lib usable by any Python project, zero Amplifier dependency\n  - Amplifier tool module (thin mount() wrapper)\n  - Click-based CLI (thin wrapper)\n\nExplicitly names the anti-pattern to avoid (.dot files requiring compile-time\ntemplating before an engine can run them) and flags this as target/aspirational\nshape, not yet proven end-to-end anywhere. Cites microsoft/amplifier-app-wiki-weaver\nas the closest real-world reference, but clearly notes it has not reached this\ntarget yet (tokenized .dot files, missing resolver sidecars, engine wrapper still\ncoupled to Amplifier''s PreparedBundle machinery, argparse not Click).\n\nInstructs future readers not to copy wiki-weaver''s current coupling forward as\nif it were the pattern.\n\n🤖 Generated with Amplifier\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqT1xuCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA/wUQADq7j3jTsOxl91tjeKtUmeGx\nGtyXtQcJpPxI3rYFrLNm0eRxJv1VNyOC0gX8TrLYGYBemlNGdxzJvjFOJztrrJCF\nhEuz5Qh8vedkcLtU07NQTGEcXtNBZ6XIdr3QvwkwVhDXO/dLbyhDivYBIE3dSqz0\nTyPvBldB0WCDAaq+eA3gmeCrjJKk709xJKXx4P/AZ7eytMSWMZsrXtjS2uD+dTLK\n1JTV88