gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/92e4e0e18706e449e7d800e1007d9126856ccebb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-27T02:41:31Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-27T02:41:31Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: council-here — prevent context-elaboration-bleed in the review brief (#37)\n\ncouncil-here builds a brief of the current conversation for the cold lenses. It was\nfolding the in-session assistant''s OWN prior elaboration — invented \"concerns\",\nnumbered \"tensions\", a non-existent \"Known Tensions section\" — into that brief and\nthe lenses then quoted it back as the user''s design''s own specification (fabrication).\nWorst on low-signal invocations. Fix adds two Phase-0 rules: (1) SOURCE DISCIPLINE —\nthe brief states only what the design actually IS as specified; never fold prior chat\ndiscussion/concerns/elaboration into it or quote chat-derived commentary as the\ndesign''s own words; (2) FAIL LOUD — if there is no concrete design to review, do not\nmanufacture one; say so and ask. Validated in pinned-model DTUs, graded from events.jsonl:\non a deterministic recreation (assistant invents 5 numbered concerns, then /council-here)\nthe lenses attributed 0/8 of those concerns to the design (was up to ~50%); fail-loud\nfired 6/6 on a no-design conversation; a grounded-design control still convened cleanly\n6/6 with no over-refusal.\n\nSigned-off-by: Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com>\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"6c9ec670c9a84ff30bdaf71847db125df922f028","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/6c9ec670c9a84ff30bdaf71847db125df922f028"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/92e4e0e18706e449e7d800e1007d9126856ccebb","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c9ec670c9a84ff30bdaf71847db125df922f028\nparent b1bcc29ffc2b07fae7644b79ea72686bb87f4572\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1782528091 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782528091 -0700\n\nfix: council-here — prevent context-elaboration-bleed in the review brief (#37)\n\ncouncil-here builds a brief of the current conversation for the cold lenses. It was\nfolding the in-session assistant''s OWN prior elaboration — invented \"concerns\",\nnumbered \"tensions\", a non-existent \"Known Tensions section\" — into that brief and\nthe lenses then quoted it back as the user''s design''s own specification (fabrication).\nWorst on low-signal invocations. Fix adds two Phase-0 rules: (1) SOURCE DISCIPLINE —\nthe brief states only what the design actually IS as specified; never fold prior chat\ndiscussion/concerns/elaboration into it or quote chat-derived commentary as the\ndesign''s own words; (2) FAIL LOUD — if there is no concrete design to review, do not\nmanufacture one; say so and ask. Validated in pinned-model DTUs, graded from events.jsonl:\non a deterministic recreation (assistant invents 5 numbered concerns, then /council-here)\nthe lenses attributed 0/8 of those concerns to the design (was up to ~50%); fail-loud\nfired 6/6 on a no-design conversation; a grounded-design control still convened cleanly\n6/6 with no over-refusal.\n\nSigned-off-by: Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com>\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqPzhbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyQIQAIkYwFOeoqAAqPHJHDH8UjxY\na36it8RE56A1wBzo5UWbJ7PKyle8L+svkhEYwuwFWsbGsnh15Pt5vfJKV8cx5u+V\n7Jnvplr2VLCoHxAbZG3tiN3GRSPIN72fHdkNZhuVqPANHUjxVx8Ck1cj+w4V5QWf\nQOrn+yEMrQBgkRtxfjM+Inu5DrwCzJQy9D5lDUojYSxZ9Z9eeIUqFbMhnN/Jo5tL\n8fIMxl3OZEvvXOC7Mayvy/IchIEcwQaUPcXmu+kF4xAzn+nkLqnOZAPFI9w8APCK\nd62E9c74rGO6SMK7sXQ+2D/7s5d4sH/Y/GKyd1xB1ciMd8erfRRgq4QZ5k7BGHN/\nUMz5uTsywXnHwv7RblzgwTe0XCWoSX8ntPvpL97BIT/1TnpnJFYTqjcN2BKQx/9Y\nZf0p2Lhd4I5RccZ0cZ3SkObuXecl3QrrbSZsVvtQij2ydcfUMxezdwQuDAfpdSHm\n9xqY5Db0hcpplB7Q3SEliUOgmJRX7s7hpqPOF/S93y0FLgXxxmd6PV0c3aIx42kG\nkp0tPPQ/S85ZNvhiYJPzolQu2Gvl/OcQGZ/9uKrc5tQn0yH6e4DYDbeN8TBdK6qY\nXcAHiJZwU1HLUQPzksl+50gB+mjXH+Bh6UbQNs+r5eETatBSBjCOTHfYRUBsCdPe\nW/zlKaQ078qlKltwWViM\n=pmzW\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-27T02:41:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-b