MmIxYjA3YzNhMzVjM2VjYjdlZmIyM2M4NzIzYjcyMmE2MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/6e0f42ece5a72be453789e7c7028ffb536216c58","sha":"6e0f42ece5a72be453789e7c7028ffb536216c58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/6e0f42ece5a72be453789e7c7028ffb536216c58"}],"sha":"6dc6e2b1b07c3a35c3ecb7efb23c8723b722a619","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/6dc6e2b1b07c3a35c3ecb7efb23c8723b722a619"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/6e0f42ece5a72be453789e7c7028ffb536216c58/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T20:36:28Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T20:36:28Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: remove incorrect Claude-Code tool names from allowed-tools frontmatter (#31)\n\nThe /council, /council-here, and related persona lens skills were hallucinating\nreviews and fake delegation because their ''allowed-tools:'' frontmatter listed Claude\nCode tool names (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Agent) instead of Amplifier module IDs\n(tool-filesystem, tool-search, tool-bash, tool-delegate, tool-skills).\n\nAmplifier matches allowed-tools VERBATIM against module IDs. When the names\ndon''t match, a forked skill gets an EMPTY tool surface, can''t read files or\ndelegate, and the model fabricates <tool_call>/<tool_response> text blocks\ninstead of making real calls — resulting in hallucinated target documents and\nsimulated panel reviews with zero real delegation.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove allowed-tools from council, council-here, mass-change, session-debug\n  and all five persona lens skills (intent-keeper, user-advocate, tester-breaker,\n  crusty-old-engineer, cranky-old-sam). Forked skills now inherit the parent''s\n  real tool surface. Council and council-here bodies are unchanged.\n- Correct authoring docs (README, spec-reference, skills-vs-agents, authoring-guide)\n  to teach module-ID semantics, not Claude-Code names. This removes the recurrence\n  source for the bug.\n- Update personafy to stop emitting the incorrect allowed-tools line into new personas.\n\nVerified in clean-room DTU:\n  /council <file>      BEFORE: 0 real calls, hallucinated unrelated doc, 22 fake blocks\n  /council <file>      AFTER:  1 read_file, 12 delegate spawns (6 lenses × 2 rounds),\n                               12 child sessions, grounded in target file, 0 fake blocks\n  /council-here        unchanged (inline skill; allowed-tools was inert)\n\nNote: council-here still simulates its six \"independent\" lenses (they run sequentially\nin a delegated worker that cannot inherit the delegate tool). This pre-existing design\nissue is left out of this PR for the skill''s author to address separately.\n\nFixes: #31\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"84846094c0fc990bee33d2311653ad93f4d20fba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/84846094c0fc990bee33d2311653ad93f4d20fba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/6e0f42ece5a72be453789e7c7028ffb536216c58","verification":{"payload":"tree 84846094c0fc990bee33d2311653ad93f4d20fba\nparent 09f8be7c3ab8d76ab57f828e705d14808265e138\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1782160588 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1782160588 -0700\n\nfix: remove incorrect Claude-Code tool names from allowed-tools frontmatter (#31)\n\nThe /council, /council-here, and related persona lens skills were hallucinating\nreviews and fake delegation because their ''allowed-tools:'' frontmatter listed Claude\nCode tool names (Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Agent) instead of Amplifier module IDs\n(tool-filesystem, tool-search, tool-bash, tool-delegate, tool-skills).\n\nAmplifier matches allowed-tools VERBATIM against module IDs. When the names\ndon''t match, a forked skill gets an EMPTY tool surface, can''t read files or\ndelegate, and the model fabricates <tool_call>/<tool_response> text blocks\ninstead of making real calls — resulting in hallucinated target documents and\nsimulated panel reviews with zero real delegation.\n\nChanges:\n- Remove allowed-tools from council, council-here, mass-change, session-debug\n  and all five persona lens skills (intent-keeper, user-advocate, tester-breaker,\n  crusty-old-engineer, cranky-old-sam). Forked skills now inherit the parent''s\n  real tool surface. Council and council-here bodies are unchanged.\n- Correct authoring docs (README, spec-reference, skills-vs-agents, authoring-guide)\n  to teach module-ID semantics, not Claude-Code names. This removes the recurrence\n  source for the bug.\n- Update personafy to stop emitting the incorrect allowed-tools line into new personas.\n\nVerified in clean-room DTU:\n  /council <file>      BEFORE: 0 real calls, hallucinated unrelated doc, 22 fake blocks\n  /council <file>      AFTER:  1 read_file, 12 delegate spawns (6 lenses × 2 rounds),\n                               12 child sessions, grounded in target file, 0 fake blocks\n  /council-here        unchanged (inline skill; allowed-tools was inert)\n\nNote: council-here still simulates its six \"independent\" lenses (they run sequentially\nin a delegated worker that cannot inherit the delegate tool). This pre-existing design\nissue is left out of this PR for the skill''s author to address separately.\n\nFixes: #31\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqOZzMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAZZoQAAH+7TZcfNau29wSDmIgPeBO\nm7qOgjd7HsMae3Z0M3udIOyyBbwKaqbzy/Zhl5PxQelvdvFmLJydR91BNqe4EQPT\nyyckn7NxePGO4GskHqWkE2LwtL9AXLqHEEIs5ALyLUa6bDLlTLpT4q4wQkJ0m1Hx\nzKXIdVgdhNICXIMBdKcEhHGNAUYJxMBs0J1KZnQPnuzvmb7sowcx6oldyu0BiF8A\nizD06wyDoLkAbzLCOrPNX7jE/xFfojM9cQkOkEi+LIAfAMjOKNbE/OuAUXEsIjve\n9oC48o/WMT4ohVZp9TYjl31d4nGhnd8jdwFJiZFSTM+2p9SYizZipDGj7WY/J0jS\neNwN74w0gnRVqY/OswcrE8w2xZ1i4mxuXzR2tcbFqh22hu0a2ef904KODsu/vBuw\nfSFgeP7J9b0qzvk3tSqg93Z2w0uodHlp6NC6oJfXuQNysz5c5eMHE4qKAOEAp7yC\nkHuAKo5zD7YmCmfQXVqLqdZOrA5hKkuURydmDQ06bG8hidLWOHF8xkJO+J1O0v71\nrNEelgInqUMmH0x88EYQHONL2KTBpR+H+iHbjtV/XKJ297ARgrJUHkmIHAVgdCWw\nvQyOn6oBfZtZTYyeX2Jy6KJbdjA8ImswU5BEdiqQyL5sbOZv4YI9A/pPdDd9FzMT\n1zC2mHbxXeFq8UZP0hEu\n=Jq6/\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-22T20:36:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node