ubscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/8380be4f466dbcd428b982613ff1c42c39265935/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T23:34:40Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T23:34:40Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"message":"feat(tool-skills): deliver $ARGUMENTS to fork skills (fixes council)\n\nFork skills run in a child session and cannot see the parent conversation context.\nWhen a user types /skillname <args>, the argument text must be threaded through\nthe load_skill tool''s arguments parameter so it reaches the fork skill''s\n$ARGUMENTS substitution. Previously _execute_fork hardcoded arguments=None,\nso $ARGUMENTS was always empty inside forks, which caused council''s\n''empty arguments -> print usage and stop'' guard to fire on every invocation.\n\n- Added ''arguments'' parameter to load_skill input schema (clear description\n  that it is required for fork skills to receive /command arguments)\n- Threaded arguments through all code paths: execute -> _load_skill ->\n  _execute_fork -> preprocess(arguments=...) for both inline and fork skills\n- Added 3 new tests proving real $ARGUMENTS substitution inside _execute_fork\n  end-to-end (test_fork_arguments.py)\n\nFull tool-skills test suite: 252 passed, 2 pre-existing failures unrelated to\nthis change (verified against clean baseline).\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"2f6981d6073cb28c008f483804c700f7b6e00c56","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/2f6981d6073cb28c008f483804c700f7b6e00c56"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microso