g_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/hazamarek","id":14955735,"login":"hazamarek","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE0OTU1NzM1","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/hazamarek","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/e2a844b4e04b63373cffe8de1b2c43adc8beb7cc","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGUyYTg0NGI0ZTA0YjYzMzczY2ZmZThkZTFiMmM0M2FkYzhiZWI3Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036","sha":"d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036"}],"sha":"e2a844b4e04b63373cffe8de1b2c43adc8beb7cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/e2a844b4e04b63373cffe8de1b2c43adc8beb7cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/a10d8a3af134176b4e7a5890cbf33790b9eacc7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T22:13:20Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T22:13:20Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"message":"feat(tool-skills): add optional parent-conversation context inheritance for fork skills\n\nAdds caller-side context inheritance to FORK skills, bringing them to parity with the\n`delegate` tool. Previously, `context: fork` skills always spawned sub-sessions with a\nclean slate (no parent conversation). Now callers can opt in using the same two-axis model:\n\n- context_depth: \"none\" (default) | \"recent\" | \"all\"\n- context_scope: \"conversation\" (default) | \"agents\" | \"full\"\n- context_turns: int (default 5), used when depth=\"recent\"\n\nDefault is \"none\", preserving historical clean-slate fork behavior with zero regression.\nWhen opted in, parent messages are sanitized (same filtering as delegate: conversation\nstrips tool/thinking blocks; agents adds delegate/task results; full includes all tool\noutput truncated) and prepended as [PARENT CONVERSATION CONTEXT] ... [YOUR TASK] ...\nbefore the skill body, using identical injection approach to delegate.\n\nChanges:\n- modules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/context_inheritance.py (NEW)\n  Pure, self-contained transforms mirroring delegate''s logic (no cross-bundle deps)\n- modules/tool-skills/amplifier_module_tool_skills/__init__.py\n  Added context params to input schema (marked \"FORK SKILLS ONLY\"); threaded through\n  execute -> _load_skill -> _execute_fork; added _get_parent_messages(); gated prepend\n  on context_depth != \"none\"\n- modules/tool-skills/tests/test_fork_context_inheritance.py (NEW)\n  10 tests covering transforms and _execute_fork wiring: default-none no-injection,\n  opt-in prepend, empty-parent clean path\n\nVerified: 10 new tests pass; full module suite 249 passed (2 pre-existing failures in\ntest_enhanced_discovery.py and test_real_session.py remain unchanged). Module import\nand logic verified against local source.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"df3ddac35d1e22b09c3c4dc8b5640516d9dcd16a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/df3ddac35d1e22b09c3c4dc8b5640516d9dcd16a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/a10d8a3af134176b4e7a5890cbf33790b9eacc7f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/a10d8a3af134176b4e7a5890cbf33790b9eacc7f","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGExMGQ4YTNhZjEzNDE3NmI0ZTdhNTg5MGNiZjMzNzkwYjllYWNjN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036","sha":"d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036"}],"sha":"a10d8a3af134176b4e7a5890cbf33790b9eacc7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/a10d8a3af134176b4e7a5890cbf33790b9eacc7f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-19T05:09:17Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-19T05:09:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(tool-skills): resolve race condition in concurrent remote skill-source resolution (#28)\n\nWhen a bundle configures tool-skills with multiple skill sources pointing at\nthe same git repo+ref but differing only by #subdirectory fragments, the cache\nkey (derived from url@ref, excluding subdirectories) collapsed them to a single\nshared cache path. The concurrent resolve_skill_sources gather cloned this path\n5 times simultaneously against an empty cache (the state after ''amplifier reset'').\n\nA race condition ensued: one task won the clone race while others observed\n''directory exists but no .amplifier_cache_meta.json'', logged warnings, and\nshutil.rmtree''d the in-progress clone before re-cloning. This symptom manifested\nas ~4 ''Removing corrupt skills cache (no metadata)'' warnings on every ''amplifier''\nstartup post-reset, plus a latent partial-clone failure mode.\n\nThis fix:\n- Deduplicates remote sources by resolved cache_path before the concurrent\n  gather, ensuring each unique repo@ref is cloned exactly once\n- Per-cache_path asyncio lock as defense-in-depth against residual races\n- Atomic clone-to-temp-then-rename strategy: clone into a .tmp directory,\n  write .amplifier_cache_meta.json, then atomically rename into place; a\n  half-clone is never observed as ''corrupt''\n- Fast-path for already-resolved cache (no lock), double-checked slow-path\n  (lock + re-check) for concurrent first-call win\n\nPublic function signatures and return contracts remain unchanged.\n\nVerified with regression test reproducing the race deterministically:\n- Before: 5 clones, 4 warnings, test fails\n- After: 1 clone, 0 warnings, test passes\nFull suite: 239 passed (2 pre-existing unrelated failures)\nDTU validation: A/B contrast confirms 0 warnings, valid metadata, no temp leftovers\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"151740b1a183bec12a380b01e18796bb69e1f090","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/151740b1a183bec12a380b01e18796bb69e1f090"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036","verification":{"payload":"tree 151740b1a183bec12a380b01e18796bb69e1f090\nparent ccd988c1cad68595306fcf9d294241d4defe4f9f\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1781845757 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781845757 -0700\n\nfix(tool-skills): resolve race condition in concurrent remote skill-source resolution (#28)\n\nWhen a bundle configures tool-skills with multiple skill sources pointing at\nthe same git repo+ref but differing only by #subdirectory fragments, the cache\nkey (derived from url@ref, excluding subdirectories) collapsed them to a single\nshared cache path. The concurrent resolve_skill_sources gather cloned this path\n5 times simultaneously against an empty cache (the state after ''amplifier reset'').\n\nA race condition ensued: one task won the clone race while others observed\n''directory exists but no .amplifier_cache_meta.json'', logged warnings, and\nshutil.rmtree''d the in-progress clone before re-cloning. This symptom manifested\nas ~4 ''Removing corrupt skills cache (no metadata)'' warnings on every ''amplifier''\nstartup post-reset, plus a latent partial-clone failure mode.\n\nThis fix:\n- Deduplicates remote sources by resolved cache_path before the concurrent\n  gather, ensuring each unique repo@ref is cloned exactly once\n- Per-cache_path asyncio lock as defense-in-depth against residual races\n- Atomic clone-to-temp-then-rename strategy: clone into a .tmp directory,\n  write .amplifier_cache_meta.json, then atomically rename into place; a\n  half-clone is never observed as ''corrupt''\n- Fast-path for already-resolved cache (no lock), double-checked slow-path\n  (lock + re-check) for concurrent first-call win\n\nPublic function signatures and return contracts remain unchanged.\n\nVerified with regression test reproducing the race deterministically:\n- Before: 5 clones, 4 warnings, test fails\n- After: 1 clone, 0 warnings, test passes\nFull suite: 239 passed (2 pre-existing unrelated failures)\nDTU validation: A/B contrast confirms 0 warnings, valid metadata, no temp leftovers\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNM79CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAANj8QAIIDNUEnOYKbLvFfHVXYcuiO\ny8RZkZOO89xMOTJ0Fr2zNvQiYWbVplG8RxZs2a1RQkPkocDSoqIilT4rDlrFQjsu\nPja4PsPlfVW9vB8SAvccSIPcIubBnDEOGeqlqiRStFgfkhFGJCkPtu1+h/rFAwWS\n2Y3+3Y75mZkMM7jKXhyZSguooU4kVU2k84LDDf4qp3IX0tc/9ickUFzdZCy0cEQX\n/H2awcHvlOVKFtr7vEeEODKA+b16jArZN9MPrAEjl1ZwTerzmP5P3w6U0U/nwr3q\nb7OPsseqcQL4ZLrqCTGBJ4TuuIkLsIJrRR+8d7k/Dx8B5PZPNDLcT1N7mp9q9vn8\npozYZI1slZx9DG//ibel5QcFsMe8/yrLo5TsHnkRV7ROHyAotVzwYOL/rvVunq1a\nOZicaWKIaX2U62Y+N+mLvKbq0aLtYyozxqaz2opxf0RuMlxJVTWwuXgVlwTA3+Jt\nN8n5qCxUv78UCpnqkPwEsXSYRmHOTUvTHuzApMPC7yrEXegx6tX2CkwagcFzCMe7\npUt5osD0p5Fgvtlxzmz3A1j6E4MUk4Tc+KksDT3H9xO3NrT9pvFC+r36V5/T9yWQ\nothzLmRmC5qz8yLEu6u8+bplOqEOuazZ00Y3vMRkQx/P0Ywjd2IufFdYuAnQ2Da8\nI9JfpiKGKSekTnWbBvUu\n=P13X\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-19T05:09:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGQ2NmNlYzE5NjM1ZDllNjViMTU1N2FmMDRiNjE5ZTY0ZmJhNjgwMzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/ccd988c1cad68595306fcf9d294241d4defe4f9f","sha":"ccd988c1cad68595306fcf9d294241d4defe4f9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/ccd988c1cad68595306fcf9d294241d4defe4f9f"}],"sha":"d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/d66cec19635d9e65b1557af04b619e64fba68036"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1099912?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ramparte","id":1099912,"login":"ramparte","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTk5MTI=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ramparte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/ccd988c1cad68595306fcf9d294241d4defe4f9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-18T16:39:51Z","email":"sam@schillace.com","name":"Sam Schillace"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-18T16:39:51Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(skills): add persona council — intent-keeper, user-advocate, tester-breaker lenses + /council panel (#27)\n\nAdds three opinionated reviewer ''lens'' skills as first-class peers to the existing cranky-old-sam / crusty-old-engineer family:\n  - intent-keeper — ''Is the goal clear, consistent, and still the real goal?''\n  - user-advocate — ''Does the person we serve actually need/want this, and can they live with it?''\n  - tester-breaker — ''How do I make this fail? Where are the edges?''\n\nAdds /council, a user-invocable fork power-skill modeled on the built-in /code-review. It convenes the six lenses on a target, runs a cold independent fan-out + debate-to-consensus, and synthesizes a verdict with a roster manifest and per-lens attribution.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Sam Schillace <sam@example.com>\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"76b040aab86866d09fc663662fc5e9008af21951","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/76b040aab86866d09fc663662fc5e9008af21951"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/ccd988c1cad68595306fcf9d294241d4defe4f9f","verification":{"payload":"tree 76b040aab86866d09fc663662fc5e9008af21951\nparent a4f743678d41b12397ad00ed1b6982a1e87cf9d5\nauthor Sam Schillace <sam@schillace.com> 1781800791 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781800791 -0700\n\nfeat(skills): add persona council — intent-keeper, user-advocate, tester-breaker lenses + /council panel (#27)\n\nAdds three opinionated reviewer ''lens'' skills as first-class peers to the existing cranky-old-sam / crusty-old-engineer family:\n  - intent-keeper — ''Is the goal clear, consistent, and still the real goal?''\n  - user-advocate — ''Does the person we serve actually need/want this, and can they live with it?''\n  - tester-breaker — ''How do I make this fail? Where are the edges?''\n\nAdds /council, a user-invocable fork power-skill modeled on the built-in /code-review. It convenes the six lenses on a target, runs a cold independent fan-out + debate-to-consensus, and synthesizes a verdict with a roster manifest and per-lens attribution.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-authored-by: Sam Schillace <sam@example.com>\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqNB9XCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA1MYQAGz3MXVPwN8OJUoVv6nNJZwd\ncK5G+YFQNOcOjt5q7AnoFXsRdATW1Sb58KXbPGgkjDI8hSTTqm0Ssjmj0QvObFz/\n7oAt0P7s21d6Lz5cMrBLAwuL+/uunWhekDxCyj+Yl3hYdFAGelSuqgyFkZwVS/+U\nZxj2MFq2N8M7AVF3KGxNyjedXU41o4ApyrWL0lHWTCZE/KNPGDMaQqnDl+Bfll3B\nPbPcWLQnCT7cDcrPXrqOLxQgdnLXglZO4wnLLlsjsK84RnG95kMFKKqXENiz4NwE\neCtS/b5q5jD5oysCLtqdEMQvAxNod2MbBZEZIadZsYgkWchxQ9FQ4MAO33b60azX\nDaabPi7mskLjicpqIJo5t5ZJICpFin0MsX9qMg7XEqAjCGMAL5Fqd4Gaf1Eqypna\nsKKFtp7cSYLNCIuOqX9Y/gJrtNWQRnCl0XKQH/XXYCIqaZI9EzIcTT3cBxS2qmUu\nd6LnElSd777bzlReZUIOapSlyhqoHgRn/GSdBaBMOFuITjPXl1lShd4DzD6AbZ/V\nIctNxUSxhuf5TEyNykMY65yS1AIIZ5/19Qe2Qg+1HqHOYeQ1OvtXpAt1g+0vHQLx\nawCq1b7SqPloHWbXswHRC7Ipvk4sRyZsNk+uDjsd12xXbHTpre1ogQMeJfDsUlTA\n3FWCPMpuQGER6NkkL+0z\n=fFqk\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-18T16:39:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_us