b.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/b3cf7cafd1e148af0727b830baba2e1d8386c3e1","sha":"b3cf7cafd1e148af0727b830baba2e1d8386c3e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b3cf7cafd1e148af0727b830baba2e1d8386c3e1"}],"sha":"183e0c0d2c2c3534481174b51872e602b588d069","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/183e0c0d2c2c3534481174b51872e602b588d069"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/b3cf7cafd1e148af0727b830baba2e1d8386c3e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-29T14:55:22Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-29T14:55:22Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"message":"feat(skills): add shortcut alias field for slash-command invocation\n\nSkills can now declare an optional shortcut alias (e.g. `shortcut: COSam`)\nin their SKILL.md frontmatter. The alias becomes an alternate slash-command\nthat resolves to the same canonical skill, while the primary skill name\nremains the advertised invocation in /skills listings, the LLM-visible\nskills block, and skill detail views.\n\nUse case: a skill named `cranky-old-sam` (advertised as such for clarity\nand discoverability) can also be invoked via `/COSam` or `/cosam` (case-\ninsensitive at the CLI input layer) for power users who want a faster\nkeystroke without polluting the discovery surface.\n\nMirrors the modes bundle''s `shortcut:` mechanism so the two surfaces have\nparallel UX.\n\nChanges:\n\n- discovery.py:\n  - Added _SHORTCUT_PATTERN: r''^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$'' (case-tolerant\n    at the YAML-author boundary; lowercased for storage so dispatch is\n    uniform).\n  - SkillMetadata.shortcut: str | None = None new field.\n  - Parsing block: reads frontmatter[\"shortcut\"], validates against the\n    regex, lowercases on storage, warns on invalid values (skill remains\n    invokable via its canonical name).\n\n- __init__.py: get_shortcuts() rewritten to:\n  - Always include \"name\": <canonical> in each value dict so the CLI\n    knows what to load regardless of which key matched.\n  - Add a second entry keyed by metadata.shortcut when set, pointing at\n    the same value dict (i.e., both `cranky-old-sam` and `cosam` resolve\n    to the canonical skill).\n\nlist_skills(), the LLM-visible skills block, and skill detail views are\nunchanged — aliases are invokable but never surfaced. This is the\n\"hidden alternate\" model the user asked for.\n\nBackward compatible with the CLI: old CLI versions that ignore the\n\"name\" key will dispatch using the lookup key (canonical names work\nunchanged; aliases would no-op until the CLI is updated).\n\nValidation: smoke-tested SkillMetadata field shape and regex behavior\nstandalone. Full pytest suite to be exercised by CI.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":