yNDU1Njg3Y2I4YzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a","sha":"9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a"}],"sha":"87960e8c1045e19e66800a2538862455687cb8c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/87960e8c1045e19e66800a2538862455687cb8c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-29T15:38:18Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-29T15:38:18Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: add one-line-installer-patterns skill and cross-link from cli-packaging-patterns (#12)\n\n* feat: add one-line-installer-patterns skill\n\nThis new skill documents the curl-piped install.sh pattern for use cases\nwhere uv tool install (Python CLI), npm publish (Node CLI), Docker Compose\n(containerized multi-service), or static binary download (Go/Rust) are not\nthe right answer.\n\nCovers:\n- When this pattern is the right tool (narrow set of use cases)\n- Security trade-off (trust model, documented attack class)\n- Community convention (curl -fsSL | bash, not sh)\n- What the installer should do (set -euo pipefail, detect OS/arch, no bootstrapping)\n- What the installer should NOT do (wizard, sudo without consent, auth from stdin)\n- Post-install: survey of major CLIs'' first-run commands\n- Real installers to read (deno, rustup, ollama, fly, bun, supabase, coolify)\n- Known failure modes (caching, shell rc edge cases, stdin conflicts)\n- Multi-service truth (almost always Docker Compose)\n- Cross-references to cli-packaging-patterns for pure Python CLIs\n\nAuthored through crusty-old-engineer lens: direct, evidence-linked, anti-hype.\n\n* refactor: update cli-packaging-patterns with cross-references and post-install survey\n\nAdds:\n- §1: ''When this skill is NOT the right answer'' table pointing readers to\n  one-line-installer-patterns for non-Python-CLI cases (multi-language stacks,\n  raw TS/React, system bootstrapping, Docker Compose)\n- §6: ''Post-install configuration: init, login, or nothing?'' with a survey of\n  major CLIs'' first-run commands (rustup, bun, deno, ollama, gh, vercel,\n  heroku, fly, supabase, aws, gcloud, terraform, firebase, git, npm, cargo)\n- Explicit note that init for tool-wide config is a minority pattern. The\n  dominant patterns are: login/auth-login for auth, configure for tool config,\n  init for per-project setup, or sensible defaults + lazy prompts\n- Footer ''Related skills'' cross-linking to one-line-installer-patterns,\n  config-state-patterns, and http-service-patterns\n\nThis refactor addresses the finding from crusty-old-engineer that the Amplifier\necosystem''s init convention, while internally consistent, does not match the\nbroader community expectation. The updated skill documents this honestly,\nreferences the full survey in one-line-installer-patterns, and encourages\ndeliberate choice rather than cargo-culting.","tree":{"sha":"d015fb11675336aaf48a5999aa661d16b5faaff6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/d015fb11675336aaf48a5999aa661d16b5faaff6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a","verification":{"payload":"tree d015fb11675336aaf48a5999aa661d16b5faaff6\nparent f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1777477098 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1777477098 -0700\n\nfeat: add one-line-installer-patterns skill and cross-link from cli-packaging-patterns (#12)\n\n* feat: add one-line-installer-patterns skill\n\nThis new skill documents the curl-piped install.sh pattern for use cases\nwhere uv tool install (Python CLI), npm publish (Node CLI), Docker Compose\n(containerized multi-service), or static binary download (Go/Rust) are not\nthe right answer.\n\nCovers:\n- When this pattern is the right tool (narrow set of use cases)\n- Security trade-off (trust model, documented attack class)\n- Community convention (curl -fsSL | bash, not sh)\n- What the installer should do (set -euo pipefail, detect OS/arch, no bootstrapping)\n- What the installer should NOT do (wizard, sudo without consent, auth from stdin)\n- Post-install: survey of major CLIs'' first-run commands\n- Real installers to read (deno, rustup, ollama, fly, bun, supabase, coolify)\n- Known failure modes (caching, shell rc edge cases, stdin conflicts)\n- Multi-service truth (almost always Docker Compose)\n- Cross-references to cli-packaging-patterns for pure Python CLIs\n\nAuthored through crusty-old-engineer lens: direct, evidence-linked, anti-hype.\n\n* refactor: update cli-packaging-patterns with cross-references and post-install survey\n\nAdds:\n- §1: ''When this skill is NOT the right answer'' table pointing readers to\n  one-line-installer-patterns for non-Python-CLI cases (multi-language stacks,\n  raw TS/React, system bootstrapping, Docker Compose)\n- §6: ''Post-install configuration: init, login, or nothing?'' with a survey of\n  major CLIs'' first-run commands (rustup, bun, deno, ollama, gh, vercel,\n  heroku, fly, supabase, aws, gcloud, terraform, firebase, git, npm, cargo)\n- Explicit note that init for tool-wide config is a minority pattern. The\n  dominant patterns are: login/auth-login for auth, configure for tool config,\n  init for per-project setup, or sensible defaults + lazy prompts\n- Footer ''Related skills'' cross-linking to one-line-installer-patterns,\n  config-state-patterns, and http-service-patterns\n\nThis refactor addresses the finding from crusty-old-engineer that the Amplifier\necosystem''s init convention, while internally consistent, does not match the\nbroader community expectation. The updated skill documents this honestly,\nreferences the full survey in one-line-installer-patterns, and encourages\ndeliberate choice rather than cargo-culting.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJp8iXqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzpkQAG9w5xezaCzlqzfpRbpN7ElC\n0SiIgIQI5LzJpuOK2+X4g60EGztiwX13ES4WcNpj2u9iFNCtxSnbFCMkdWGnjmYI\nKNC0Usrvc1CzKXJ4WgNkpyXTKK/FPsUExf4TwGepEARmQ/9+229M6+P4VBbRXrtA\npXvpt+MAg/yzJlRUn0GvFVaHuYMmI/6GGLGOxh1fBhXOzsoiKlwKqVQ19WvCOuo/\ndvTKEmvs6GfcJB7CKJgBR0zpS0jHLml0iah6oxeNcYjF2RUiohVNqcETj0F9Y7N6\n+ppfkXej7EUAwbmsVGNr8XRkroVyYLEn9anPFXuvjc8UElpxQCBgEnGbYl1cSFp6\nQrg3Ra7Gh3r3hTgGZJb8WMWHjcrIU0Jb4AXP7WSPatmVSBBoBED3o6YlWC0cF1g+\nk2HljKkPhp+r6ba83jJQqTS69l8f5o94r5boDJCIwhFHtOGpuCSJCG4qR6KhJSYo\njG04eoKUDTEKoYBuJqysbHksfemzpPsP6KVuPuWQCYUTonTFKnb3zx1EkQud/zZB\nrteCxQNO8CzodeOLRvJ17hFxMBHHgZJRkJhpWKPfcbFvtJJzycNdqgz0YGtSteZk\nNkSjbHEVf3nchihznLVXvQjocLUUEuM1Zmqs3VilADQPWkwCM5xImYe3aadlpXD2\n+qccZ0gpRIwYzoUzTSnV\n=WA0i\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-04-29T15:38:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKDljZGVhZjBjYzg1NDg0YmRjZTVmODI1ZjA5NzM2ZjZmYjYzZDE0NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2","sha":"f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2"}],"sha":"9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/9cdeaf0cc85484bdce5f825f09736f6fb63d145a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-23T15:50:05Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-23T15:50:05Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"message":"refactor: eliminate orchestrator-config fork marker, consolidate to session metadata\n\nReplace double-writing pattern with single source of truth via session metadata.\nThe fork-session marker was written to both orchestrator config (semantically wrong)\nand session metadata (correct), causing mount() to read from the wrong place.\nThis commit:\n\n- Adds _detect_fork_session(coordinator) helper that checks the in-session\n  capability first, then falls back to session.metadata.is_forked_skill_session\n  with isinstance guard for non-dict metadata.\n- Replaces ~20-line detection block in mount() with helper call. Keeps\n  coordinator.register_capability(\"skills.fork_context\", True) inline.\n- Removes orchestrator_config={\"_is_forked_skill_session\": True} kwarg from\n  spawn_fn() call in _execute_fork(). Fork marker now travels via session_metadata\n  exclusively (no behavior change to spawner — metadata was already being set).\n- Updates comments to document the single source of truth.\n- Rewrites test_mount_config_shapes.py to verify metadata-path detection,\n  deprecate the old orchestrator_config path, and defend against non-dict metadata.\n- Renames test_execute_fork_passes_orchestrator_config_fork_marker to\n  test_execute_fork_passes_session_metadata_fork_marker.\n\nFollows up commit 0f00d19 (guard orchestrator config chaining against string values).\n\nDiff: 151 insertions, 68 deletions across 3 files.\nAll 224 tests pass. No behavior change to end users.\n\nGenerated with Amplifier\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"44d81b6858a1e09f5b00da8526414795777ef3ec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/44d81b6858a1e09f5b00da8526414795777ef3ec"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2","node_id":"C_kwDORWWbQtoAKGYxMzA1ZDhjMzk1ODExYWU4ZjJmNjlmOTliOWJhZmRmNTg3YWU1ZTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commit/0f00d19287bbc2ba86dc74adf1367aef5e4255a9","sha":"0f00d19287bbc2ba86dc74adf1367aef5e4255a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/0f00d19287bbc2ba86dc74adf1367aef5e4255a9"}],"sha":"f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/f1305d8c395811ae8f2f69f99b9bafdf587ae5e2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/0f00d19287bbc2ba86dc74adf1367aef5e4255a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-23T13:48:34Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-23T13:48:34Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"message":"fix: guard orchestrator config chaining against string values in mount()\n\nCommit 408131a added fork-session detection to tool-skills mount() that chained\n.get() calls through coordinator.config[\"session\"][\"orchestrator\"]. This\nassumed the value was always a dict, but MockCoordinator (and production sessions\nwith simple orchestrator IDs) store it as a plain string.\n\nWhen the string key exists, the {} default never kicks in — .get(\"orchestrator\", {})\nreturns the string, causing .get(\"config\", {}) to crash with ''str'' object has no\nattribute ''get'' during protocol_compliance validation.\n\nSolution: Check isinstance(value, dict) before chaining further .get() calls.\nHandles both production string orchestrator IDs and spawner-based dict config with\nfork flag safely.\n\nTest coverage: Added test_mount_config_shapes.py with 4 regression tests covering\nstring orchestrator, dict without flag, dict with flag, and empty config cases.\nAll 48 existing tests continue to pass.\n\nGenerated with [Amplifier](https://github.com/microsoft/amplifier)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Amplifier <240397093+microsoft-amplifier@users.noreply.github.com>","tree":{"sha":"a293fc7dcd44b19ccb3f316b710054fbf42b8bd8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/a293fc7dcd44b19ccb3f316b710054fbf42b8bd8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/0f00d19287bbc2ba86dc74adf1367aef5e4255a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/702425?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bkrabach","id":702425,"login":"bkrabach","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMjQyNQ==","organizations_url":"ht