6df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-23T01:19:10Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-23T01:19:10Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Skills bundle consolidation -- module absorption, skills-assist, strategic docs (#5)\n\n* feat: absorb tool-skills module into bundle (copy from standalone repo)\n\n* feat: update behavior YAMLs to reference local module (modules/tool-skills)\n\n* fix: update BUNDLE_SKILLS_DIR paths for tests inside bundle\n\n* feat: add skills-assist context-sink skill\n\n* docs: add skills authoring guide companion file for skills-assist\n\n* docs: add Agent Skills spec reference companion file for skills-assist\n\n* docs: add compatibility matrix companion file for skills-assist\n\n* docs: add skills-vs-agents companion file for skills-assist\n\n* test: add acceptance tests for skills-assist power skill\n\n* style: apply ruff formatting to test files\n\n* docs: update README with vision, skills-assist, and modules architecture; add skills-vs-agents guidance to context\n\n* fix: remove unused imports and apply ruff format to test files\n\n- Remove unused ''import pytest'' and ''import json'' from test_real_session.py\n- Apply ruff format to pre-existing test files for consistent formatting baseline\n  (test_auto_load.py, test_code_review_power_skill.py, test_coordinator_integration.py,\n   test_mass_change_power_skill.py, test_multi_source.py, test_real_session.py)\n\nAll 212 module tests pass.\n\n* fix: use ${SKILL_DIR} for companion file paths in skills-assist\n\n* fix: update stale module URLs to bundle subdirectory paths\n\n* docs: update module README URLs to reference bundle repository\n\n* fix: add foundation include to bundle.md for standalone use\n\n* fix: remove amplifier-core from runtime dependencies (host-provided)\n\n* fix: remove dead if-coordinator guard in mount()\n\n* chore: add .gitignore to exclude generated files\n\n* docs: classify allowed-tools and hooks as experimental in spec references\n\n* chore: track uv.lock for reproducible builds\n\n* docs: clarify #path= vs #subdirectory= URL fragment distinction\n\n* docs: distinguish expert skills from power skills in README\n\n* refactor: move deferred stdlib imports to module top in sources.py\n\n* refactor: standardize dict merge strategy in model_resolver.py\n\nReplace filtering comprehension with simple dict spread for effective_hints.\nThe ''gemini'' hint in the original test was replaced with ''gpt'' because\n''gemini'' contains ''mini'' (a default hint substring), which would be found\nfirst under the new defaults-first iteration order.\n\n* docs: document insertion-order sensitivity in model_resolver effective_hints\n\nThe substring-match loop iterates in insertion order, so config-only hints\n(new keys not in defaults) are checked after all default hints. Add a\ncomment that makes this behavior explicit and guides maintainers on when\nto use config overrides (existing keys) vs. new keys.\n\nAlso expand the test comment explaining why ''gpt''/''gpt-4'' is used instead\nof ''gemini''/''gemini-pro'' — with defaults-first iteration, ''mini'' would\nmatch before ''gemini'', returning ''fast'' instead of the intended ''reasoning''.\n\n* refactor: use direct attribute access instead of getattr in hooks.py\n\n* test: add gitignore pattern verification test\n\nAdds tests/test_gitignore.py which was created as part of Task 7\n(add .gitignore at bundle root) but was not included in the Task 7\ncommit (e844023). The test verifies:\n- .gitignore exists at the bundle root\n- All 9 required patterns are present\n- Exactly 9 patterns total (no extras)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@example.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@example.com>","tree":{"sha":"ef21eda1f4b6bd0325d686ab877f454efd94ceae","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/ef21eda1f4b6bd0325d686ab877f454efd94ceae"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/b0215888d843f07ec8c59981ad8d1b847b2046df","verification":{"payload":"tree ef21eda1f4b6bd0325d686ab877f454efd94ceae\nparent dac4eec93e8c06e0e922f65c391408f01b9ea828\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1774228750 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774228750 -0700\n\nfeat: Skills bundle consolidation -- module absorption, skills-assist, strategic docs (#5)\n\n* feat: absorb tool-skills module into bundle (copy from standalone repo)\n\n* feat: update behavior YAMLs to reference local module (modules/tool-skills)\n\n* fix: update BUNDLE_SKILLS_DIR paths for tests inside bundle\n\n* feat: add skills-assist context-sink skill\n\n* docs: add skills authoring guide companion file for skills-assist\n\n* docs: add Agent Skills spec reference companion file for skills-assist\n\n* docs: add compatibility matrix companion file for skills-assist\n\n* docs: add skills-vs-agents companion file for skills-assist\n\n* test: add acceptance tests for skills-assist power skill\n\n* style: apply ruff formatting to test files\n\n* docs: update README with vision, skills-assist, and modules architecture; add skills-vs-agents guidance to context\n\n* fix: remove unused imports and apply ruff format to test files\n\n- Remove unused ''import pytest'' and ''import json'' from test_real_session.py\n- Apply ruff format to pre-existing test files for consistent formatting baseline\n  (test_auto_load.py, test_code_review_power_skill.py, test_coordinator_integration.py,\n   test_mass_change_power_skill.py, test_multi_source.py, test_real_session.py)\n\nAll 212 module tests pass.\n\n* fix: use ${SKILL_DIR} for companion file paths in skills-assist\n\n* fix: update stale module URLs to bundle subdirectory paths\n\n* docs: update module README URLs to reference bundle repository\n\n* fix: add foundation include to bundle.md for standalone use\n\n* fix: remove amplifier-core from runtime dependencies (host-provided)\n\n* fix: remove dead if-coordinator guard in mount()\n\n* chore: add .gitignore to exclude generated files\n\n* docs: classify allowed-tools and hooks as experimental in spec references\n\n* chore: track uv.lock for reproducible builds\n\n* docs: clarify #path= vs #subdirectory= URL fragment distinction\n\n* docs: distinguish expert skills from power skills in README\n\n* refactor: move deferred stdlib imports to module top in sources.py\n\n* refactor: standardize dict merge strategy in model_resolver.py\n\nReplace filtering comprehension with simple dict spread for effective_hints.\nThe ''gemini'' hint in the original test was replaced with ''gpt'' because\n''gemini'' contains ''mini'' (a default hint substring), which would be found\nfirst under the new defaults-first iteration order.\n\n* docs: document insertion-order sensitivity in model_resolver effective_hints\n\nThe substring-match loop iterates in insertion order, so config-only hints\n(new keys not in defaults) are checked after all default hints. Add a\ncomment that makes this behavior explicit and guides maintainers on when\nto use config overrides (existing keys) vs. new keys.\n\nAlso expand the test comment explaining why ''gpt''/''gpt-4'' is used instead\nof ''gemini''/''gemini-pro'' — with defaults-first iteration, ''mini'' would\nmatch before ''gemini'', returning ''fast'' instead of the intended ''reasoning''.\n\n* refactor: use direct attribute access instead of getattr in hooks.py\n\n* test: add gitignore pattern verification test\n\nAdds tests/test_gitignore.py which was created as part of Task 7\n(add .gitignore at bundle root) but was not included in the Task 7\ncommit (e844023). The test verifies:\n- .gitignore exists at the bundle root\n- All 9 required patterns are present\n- Exactly 9 patterns total (no extras)\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@example.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@example.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEG