subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bkrabach","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/commits/9b44d6d5ceeaf69a56ac9a06286136ed32d270e7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-20T17:27:23Z","email":"brkrabac@microsoft.com","name":"Brian Krabach"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-20T17:27:23Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: Add /simplify, /batch, and /debug power skills (#2)\n\n* feat: add /simplify power skill with parallel review agents\n\n- Orchestrates 3 parallel review agents: Code Reuse, Code Quality, Efficiency\n- context=fork, disable-model-invocation=true, model_role=critique, user-invocable=true\n- Supports optional $ARGUMENTS focus area to narrow review scope\n- 3-step process: git diff to find changes, spawn parallel agents, aggregate by impact\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@microsoft.com>\n\n* feat: add /batch power skill for parallel batch execution\n\nAdds the /batch power skill that decomposes large changes into\nindependent work units and executes them in parallel via delegate agents.\n\nFrontmatter:\n- context: fork\n- disable-model-invocation: true\n- user-invocable: true\n- model_role: reasoning\n\nThe 5-step orchestration process:\n1. Understand the change by researching the codebase\n2. Decompose into 5-30 independent work units\n3. Present plan for approval\n4. Execute in parallel via delegate agents on batch/<unit-name> branches\n5. Integration summary of successes/failures with next steps\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@microsoft.com>\n\n* feat: add /debug power skill\n\n* fix: replace /simplify with battle-tested review prompt\n\n* fix: replace /batch with battle-tested orchestration prompt\n\n* fix: replace /debug with session-analyst-powered diagnostics\n\n* fix: add explicit user-invocable: true to power skills\n\nSkills that should be slash-command accessible must now explicitly opt in\nsince the default changed to False. Added user-invocable: true to:\n- skills/simplify/SKILL.md\n- skills/batch/SKILL.md\n- skills/debug/SKILL.md\n\n🤖 Co-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@sourcegraph.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@microsoft.com>","tree":{"sha":"a315f4aaf9a8c05d181ecf0099e13787a61d580d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/trees/a315f4aaf9a8c05d181ecf0099e13787a61d580d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/amplifier-bundle-skills/git/commits/9b44d6d5ceeaf69a56ac9a06286136ed32d270e7","verification":{"payload":"tree a315f4aaf9a8c05d181ecf0099e13787a61d580d\nparent 388616680979ece14ec5a486a3b93fecdede8cba\nauthor Brian Krabach <brkrabac@microsoft.com> 1774027643 -0700\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1774027643 -0700\n\nfeat: Add /simplify, /batch, and /debug power skills (#2)\n\n* feat: add /simplify power skill with parallel review agents\n\n- Orchestrates 3 parallel review agents: Code Reuse, Code Quality, Efficiency\n- context=fork, disable-model-invocation=true, model_role=critique, user-invocable=true\n- Supports optional $ARGUMENTS focus area to narrow review scope\n- 3-step process: git diff to find changes, spawn parallel agents, aggregate by impact\n\nCo-authored-by: Amplifier <amplifier@microsoft.com>\n\n* feat: add /batch power skill for parallel batch execution\n\nAdds the /batch power skill that decomposes large changes into\nindependent work units and executes them in parallel via delegate agents.\n\nFrontmatter:\n- context: fork\n- disable-model-invocation: true\n- user-invocable: true\n- model_role: reasoning\n\nThe 5-step orchestration process:\n1. Understand the change by researching the codebase\n2. Decompose into 5-30 independent work units\n3. Present plan for approval\n4. Execute in parallel via delegate agents on batch/<unit-name> branches\n5. Integration summary of successes/failures 